window.FWN_FEY_EVOLUTION_MERCHANT_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_FEY_EVOLUTION_MERCHANT_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2101,"title":"Chapter 2101 Lost the Hearts of the People!","paragraphs":["2101 Lost the Hearts of the People!","The angry roar came from an elderly woman. She was dressed in a dignified purple and red fur jacket, and it was clear that she was a respected member of a tribe.","Both men and women in the Iron Hammer Federation needed to participate in mining activities. Thus, many women’s hands were also covered in calluses.","The elderly woman’s hands were slightly wrinkled but otherwise soft. There were no calluses on the surface at all. This meant that she had not worked a day of hard labor in her life.","The elderly lady was so enraged that her eyes had turned red. Her roar lacked any sort of deportment.","The elderly woman had been conversing with the other five pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters. This meant that she was also a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master.","Pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters could use their spiritual energy and soul power to concoct spirit fluids. They possessed much more spiritual power and soul power than regular people.","The more spiritual energy and soul power one possessed, the greater control one would have over one’s emotions.","The elderly woman was not the only one filled with bitter resentment, but the other five pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters also could not help but scream in a fury, “I always felt that there was something off about the previous king’s death! Ever since Luo Cai took the throne, he hasn’t held a single formal imperial meeting, nor has he worn the crown to greet the snow beast!","“He even issued an order that forces all the tribes to walk to their deaths. He’s despicable! If you ask me, he doesn’t even have the crown!”","The angry scream from the middle-aged man wearing black armor was immediately rebuked by the elderly woman, “He Zhan! All of us were opposed in some manner to Luo Cai’s order. You’re the one who went against us and supported him. How can you say something like this now? If not for you, I would have asked Luo Cai what the meaning behind his order is!”","He Zhan’s jaw fell open, and he was at a loss for words for a few moments.","He had his own motive for helping Luo Cai and going against the other Black Gold tribes.","He Zhan was from the Giant Peak Tribe, which was considered one of the weaker tribes of the seven Black Gold tribes in the Iron Hammer Federation.","It was inevitable that there would be fights over resources amongst a federation’s top factions.","The Giant Peak Tribe always drew the shortest sticks during such fights.","But the Guard Mountain Tribe had supported Luo Cai early on and provided him with significant aid.","Thus, he immediately raised their status when he became ruler of the Iron Hammer Federation. This allowed the Guard Mountain Tribe to surpass the other six Black Gold tribes.","As a result, He Zhan also had the idea of currying favor with the Iron Hammer Federation’s king.","But now, He Zhan saw this idea as ridiculous.","In order for the Giant Peak Tribe to rise in rank in the Iron Hammer Federation, the Iron Hammer Federation first needed to improve and develop.","But now, Luo Cai did not care at all about the Iron Hammer Federation’s benefits and gave such a ridiculous order.","Just the thought of it caused He Zhan to boil with rage.","If He Zhan could stand in front of Luo Cai now, he might not be able to hold himself back from reaching out and cutting down Luo Cai’s head.","He Zhan never liked to be reprimanded.","But now, he had nothing to say against the elderly woman’s admonishments.","The longer He Zhan looked at the five people around him, the guiltier he felt. He bowed deeply to each of them.","“I’m sorry, everyone! I didn’t think things through. If we’re ever able to escape from the sea of flowers, I am willing to lay down the entire Giant Peak Tribe to compensate all of you.”","He Zhan’s words caused the other five pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters’ expressions to become less sour. None of them continued to reprimand him.","A man holding a large ax patted He Zhan’s shoulder.","“We Black Gold tribes should stick together!”","“Now, you’ve cleared the air with us.”","“If we’re able to escape, we six Black Gold tribes will still be brothers!”","“However, the Gilt Iron Tribe will never forgive the Guard Mountain Tribe!”","The elderly woman wearing the purple and red fur jacket looked at the ax-holding man and said, “The Guard Mountain Tribe is now Luo Cai’s claws. They helped Luo Cai to reassign the experts in the tribe and did a purging of imperial guards. All the imperial guards who weren’t obedient to Luo Cai were killed. I’m sure all of you know this.”","The elderly woman paused before she continued. “I heard that the Guard Mountain Tribe has been leading the imperial guards in helping Luo Cai to hunt down Princess Luo Lan. I was always suspicious of whether the previous king truly passed down the throne to Luo Cai. The previous king was an Immortal expert, and he was in the pink of health during the imperial meeting two months ago.”","The elderly woman sighed.","When she first heard the news, she had believed in this possibility.","However, she did not want to act before the other Black Gold tribes did.","It was well known that no good could come from sticking one’s head out.","But if she had known that they were going to befall the fate they were experiencing today, she would have led her tribe in sticking their head out.","Every Black Gold tribe in the Iron Hammer Federation occupied a piece of fertile land in the Iron Hammer Federation.","Every Black Gold tribe would build a city with their tribe at the center.","In order to ensure that every tribe had access to sufficient resources and attain sufficient expansion, the Black Gold tribes were very far from each other and the royal capital.","As a result, much of the information from the royal capital did not make it to the Black Gold tribes.","The tribes of the Iron Hammer Federation spent their days fighting, mining resources, and gathering food. Thus, they did not wage as much psychological warfare on each other like the factions of the Divine Wood Federation did.","Nonetheless, Luo Cai’s actions had been too impactful.","Besides the elderly woman, several others had also heard of this rumor, and just like her, none of them had wanted to stick their heads out first.","But now that the elderly woman had mentioned the matter and all of their collective displeasure with Luo Cai, all of them were dying to kill Luo Cai.","The ax-wielding man picked up where the elderly woman left off and said, “Luo Cai is mediocre, and the previous king was only nurturing him to be a Guard Captain. All his hopes had been in Princess Luo Lan. Regardless, he shouldn’t have passed on the throne to Luo Cai.”"]},{"number":2102,"title":"Chapter 2102 Forehead that Popped Out From the Ground!","paragraphs":["2102 Forehead that Popped Out From the Ground!","He Zhan could not help but nod instinctively when he heard what Ling Chenxiong said.","Luo Cai had been nurtured by the previous king, and the leaders of all the Black Gold tribes had seen him often.","It was not just the leaders of Black Gold tribes, but even the leaders of the Platinum tribes agreed that Luo Cai did not possess any distinctive talent.","He had been nurtured by the previous king because his father was the cousin of the previous king, meaning that they were blood relatives.","Luo Cai’s father had died whilst trying to stop a carcinoma fey disaster. Thus, the previous king felt indebted to Luo Cai.","Additionally, the previous king was probably planning for Luo Cai to assist Luo Lan when she ascended to the throne.","But never would the good and wise previous king have expected that Luo Cai would end up betraying him.","He Zhan never understood how Luo Cai had been able to ascend to the throne, given his capabilities.","The Truth Association had been hiding in the shadows. Thus, the leaders of the Black Gold tribes, who rarely came to Cold Frost City, were completely unaware of the existence of the Truth Association.","The six pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters who were present all preferred Luo Lan to take the throne over Luo Cai.","The elderly man who stood off to the side silently looked into the distance and sighed.","“We might have spirit qi professionals who can produce food, but they can only feed 60,000 people. Furthermore, they will only be able to do so for a short period. If they do so for a prolonged period of time, their roots will be affected.","“We have already given the order that cannibalism is forbidden even if they end up starving to death. However, as time drags on, even we won’t be able to hold down the fort. With more and more tribe members being rounded up by the sea of flowers. it’s likely that the border area is already in a mess. The future of the Iron Hammer Federation will be destroyed at the hands of this sea of flowers!”","At that moment, all the tribe members from the Iron Hammer Federation felt the ground below them start to shake. It was as though something large was traveling underground.","All of them were instantly filled with panic and fear.","This sudden occurrence caused hysteria to break out among the previously relatively calm members of the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe.","Normally, it would be very easy for Lin Yuan to transport Luo Lan to the center of the area where the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members were trapped.","The Source Sand’s aura could not be hidden from the six pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters, but it could be hidden from most emperor-class experts.","Lin Yuan had instructed the Source Sand to cause such a commotion because he wanted to challenge Luo Lan and stimulate her growth, as well as test to see if the Iron Hammer Federation had an attitude that was worth nurturing.","Besides the underground tremors, Lin Yuan had already created a shocking scene from which Luo Lan could appear.","The endless sea of flowers was terrifying, and unknown lifeforms were hidden within it.","The lifeform that could cause such serious tremors had to be strong.","The pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters even commanded the experts in their tribes to attack the ground.","But at that moment, the aura of danger suddenly appeared. It contained endless deadliness that seemed to target everyone present.","The nine Immortal experts narrowed their eyes. They could sense that the lifeform releasing its aura around them also had Immortal power.","The aura from this lifeform was full of deadliness but lacked carnage. It seemed to be a warning and suppression.","From this lifeform’s aura, the nine Immortal experts knew that the lifeform would not attack them as long as they did not attack it.","As such, the Immortal experts immediately halted the experts who had not reached Immortal to stop.","At the same time, they became even more fearful of this sea of flowers.","The Immortal experts had accepted Shadow’s warning after receiving it because they were unable to locate Shadow despite being able to sense it. An invisible enemy was all the more terrifying.","If they angered this lifeform, carnage would be added to its aura, and there would be no way for them to stop it based on the direction it was coming from. At that time, these tribe members would be killed by the lifeform before they had the chance to starve to death.","As the spirits of the experts fell, a pool of quicksand appeared and started swirling in the hard earth.","The pool of quicksand started to widen.","Since the quicksand had appeared at the center of the six Black Gold tribes, the experts hurriedly ordered their comrades to move.","The Black Gold tribes had very large egos.","As all the tribes moved together, it was easy to reach the center. However, it would be difficult to move away from the center.","Luckily, the pool of quicksand had stopped expanding once it reached a certain size. Otherwise, many members of the Black Gold tribes would have fallen into the quicksand.","The members of Black Gold tribes were usually very haughty when they encountered members of Platinum tribes, much fewer members from Yellow Gold and White Silver tribes.","But now that the entire Iron Hammer Federation was in crisis, the members of the Black Gold tribes retracted all of their arrogance.","There was no bloodshed even as they pushed the other tribe members to move.","Lin Yuan had noticed this.","As the Source Sand’s power increased, its intelligence grew.","Since Lin Yuan’s spiritual energy was attached to the Source Sand, he could sense the environment around the Source Sand.","This sight gave rise to a good impression of the Iron Hammer Federation in Lin Yuan.","There was no way that such a sight could be seen in the Divine Wood Federation.","The members of the Black Gold tribes were staring unblinkingly at the quicksand.","This was when they saw something solid rising from within the quicksand.","At first, the members of the Black Gold tribes, including the six pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters, could not tell what the emerging item was.","But slowly, as more of the item was revealed, the Black Gold tribe members recognized the item that was now round 12 centimeters tall to be a forehead."]},{"number":2103,"title":"Chapter 2103 I Have Something More Important to Say!","paragraphs":["2103 I Have Something More Important to Say!","As more of the forehead emerged from the quicksand, the leaders of the Black Gold tribe and the pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters let out gasps of astonishment.","Luo Lan might be the First Princess of the Iron Hammer Federation, but she was not haughty. From a young age, she had been traveling around the tribes providing medical aid as a means of training.","After more than a decade of training as a healing-type spirit qi professional, she had saved at least tens of thousands of the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members.","Each day she worked, she only stopped when she was completely exhausted of spiritual power.","Luo Lan’s actions made her a known face amongst the tribes.","The head that had emerged from the sand was around 50 to 60 centimeters, and there was no way that all of the almost ten million tribe members who had been captured could see it.","But those who could see it immediately recognized the head as belonging to Luo Lan.","With the Source Sand’s current power and the exquisite composition of the sand granules, the patterns on the granules were also extremely clear.","The six pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters who stood at the front of the group exchanged looks of shock.","A sand carving of Luo Lan had appeared at the center of the sea of flowers at such a time. This was astonishing and even a little thrilling.","But since it was Luo Lan, the six pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters felt relaxed, and a flame of hope sparked to life within them.","However, this was just a statue of Luo Lan’s head and not actually her.","The experts from the Black Gold tribe went on full alert. After all, there was still a terrifying lifeform hiding and watching from the shadows.","As the sand continued to move, the appearance of the head was just the beginning. It was followed by a neck, and upper body until a 500-meter-tall statue rose into the sky.","The statue of Luo Lan was depicted to be wearing a silk dress, with her head slightly hung and her hands held in Buddha’s Mudra. It was as though she was expressing pity for all the creatures of the world.","With the 500-meter-tall statue rising into the sky, even the Black Iron tribe members at the periphery of the group could make out its image.","Almost all, if not all those still alive in the sea of flowers, could see the statue.","The voice of Luo Lan reverberated through the crowd, and some granules of sand fell from the statue’s hands.","The radium boards had been combined with the falling granules, and Luo Lan, dressed lavishly and wearing the Iron Hammer Federation’s crown, appeared on the statue’s hands.","She opened her eyes to see that she was up in the air and immediately realized why Lin Yuan had asked her if she was afraid of heights.","If someone who was afraid of heights found themselves more than 500 meters in the air, they would immediately lose all strength in their legs, as well as their ability to speak.","There were many high-class spirit qi professionals who were afraid of heights. There were numerous king-class experts who only levitated one or two meters off the ground despite being able to circulate their spirit qi to fly.","In actuality, Luo Lan was slightly afraid of heights.","When she looked back at the statue behind her, she immediately understood Lin Yuan’s intention. He wanted to turn her into the faith of the Iron Hammer Federation.","This was not the time for her to be showing her weak side.","It was now absolutely imperative that she ensured the survival of as many people as possible and efficiently distributed rations.","Luo Lan knew that Lin Yuan had sent an expert to accompany her. This was for her safety and to carry out any orders she had to control the situation.","Luo Lan hoped that she would not have to use this strength as it would mean that more of the Iron Wood Federation’s citizens’ lives would be lost.","Luo Lan calmed herself down and took a deep breath before she called down with a steady voice, “I am Luo Lan. I’m sure all of you know me! My father was the king of the Iron Hammer Federation until he was killed by Luo Cai, who has conspired with a faction from the Great Lush Federation. Luo Cai has also been secretly trying to hunt me down and kill me!”","Luo Lan circulated her spiritual power while she spoke. She was an A-rank spirit qi professional and could project her voice thousands of meters away by channeling her spiritual power.","As a result, at least 100,000 people around the statue heard what she said.","Luo Lan’s words caused a stir among the crowd.","The leaders of the Black Gold tribes and the pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters had only made guesses about the matter, but Luo Lan’s words shone a light on the current Iron Hammer Federation imperial court’s biggest secret.","As a result, the new king now appeared to be an ingrate who committed regicide. He had even turned his back on the Iron Hammer Federation to collude with another federation.","Given that Luo Lan had been groomed from young to take over the throne, she knew what the impact of saying such words to people who hated would have on Luo Cai.","He not only did not have a claim to the throne, but even if he did, Luo Lan’s words would have shaken its legitimacy.","As the experts gazed at Luo Lan, they saw that she was wearing the crown that represented the leadership of the Iron Hammer Federation.","All of the Black Gold tribe leaders and pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters instantly believed what she said.","This was partly due to Luo Lan’s image in the Iron Hammer Federation.","The previous king of the Iron Hammer Federation had made it clear that he wanted Luo Lan to replace him. Furthermore, the crown of the Iron Hammer Federation could only be passed on to someone it had acknowledged with blood.","The previous holder of the crown had to let his blood drip onto the crown to remove the imprint in order for it to be contracted by a new contractor.","When the previous king died, the only person who had been around was Luo Cai. He had assumed the throne immediately after declaring that the previous king was dead.","Luo Lan had not had any time to enter the imperial court to take the crown. This meant that the previous king had given Luo Lan the crown long ago.","Luo Cai had fully earned the ire of the public. Many people had died as a result of his order, and he was carrying many sins.","Although only 100,000 people heard what Luo Lan said, the contents of her speech quickly traveled to every corner of the crowd.","The crowd was now completely riled up.","Luo Lan was not only the First Princess of the Iron Hammer Federation but had also saved many tribes. Her appearance had pulled the fraying crowd together.","The leaders of the Black Gold tribe and pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters planned on asking Luo Lan detailed questions about what was going on.","This was when Luo Lan said sternly, “Now is not the time to talk about such things. I have something more important to say!”"]},{"number":2104,"title":"Chapter 2104 Do Your Best to Continue Surviving!","paragraphs":["2104 Do Your Best to Continue Surviving!","What could be more important at such a time?","From Luo Lan’s perspective, she would benefit more if she attacked Luo Cai now.","Now, all the tribe members were stuck in the sea of flowers while Luo Cai was seated firmly in the imperial court.","Luo Lan had to ruin Luo Cai’s image and expose his sins in order to take back the throne.","While everyone was guessing what Luo Lan was thinking, what she said next stunned them all.","“I have rations that will sate your hunger. Pay attention! Do your best to continue surviving before I get to you!”","She started to call out the names of the Black Gold and Platinum tribes’ leaders’ names. Once she had called out almost 100 names, she said in a woeful voice, “Your lives are the most precious things to the Iron Hammer Federation! The people who I just called out are the leaders of the Black Gold and Platinum tribes. I hope that you will disseminate the rations as quickly as possible during this time of suffering.”","The leaders whose names had been called out by Luo Lan looked touched.","She had made it clear that the lives of the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members were more important to her than getting her revenge on Luo Cai.","At that moment, she lived up to exactly the image they had formed of her in the past.","When all of them were helpless, she had appeared like a goddess and promised to give them enough rations to ensure all their survival.","Her words had given all of them renewed hope, and many of their dimmed eyes lit up in an instant.","In order for them to be the leaders of Black Gold and Platinum tribes, they had to have reached king-class at least, and it was easy for them to fly at low altitudes.","The leaders of the Black Gold and Platinum tribes flew up to Luo Lan and bowed to her.","Luo Lan did not give them a chance to offer pleasantries and started handing out the Item-Storing Walnuts filled with the Soldier Ration Radishes.","“You can pluck off a leaf to taste for yourselves! Each person only needs to be given one leaf, and they’ll be full of energy for the next week. Once everyone is full, I’ll take you out of the sea of flowers. I am giving you these Item-Storing Walnuts because I trust you. What you do with them will determine the future of the Iron Hammer Federation. Form pairs and ensure that the leaves are quickly handed out to the tribe members!","“I’m sure you know that if you hand them out slowly or if any tribe procures too many leaves, the consequences will be calamitous! You can deal as you see fit with any tribe member who tries to selfishly hog the leaves and refuses to pass them down. Time is of the essence. Go now!”","Ever since Luo Lan received the Item-Storing Walnuts containing the Soldier Ration Radishes from Lin Yuan, she had been trying to come up with the best way to distribute the resources.","After mulling over the issue, she decided that the fastest way would be to trust the Black Gold and Platinum tribes to distribute the rations.","If she could not even trust her own people at such a time, there would be no future for the Iron Hammer Federation.","She had also set up a failsafe by asking them to form pairs. This would allow them to keep each other in check and prevent any one person from occupying too many of the Solder Ration Radishes.","Frankly, she should not have told the crowd that she could solve their hunger because this would immediately cause a commotion to flare up.","However, she truly hoped that these people who had already given up would be able to endure and find the courage to continue surviving.","When one was in a desperate situation, their willpower could carry them far and enable them to find the strength to keep living.","This was not a joke, as Luo Lan herself had experienced it.","When she had been floating down the river, feeling the iciness of the water penetrating her starving body, she would have eventually become a corpse floating on the surface of the river.","However, she had managed to enter the meeting amongst the constellations. With the Astronomical Parliament as her hope, she managed to boost her spirits enough to carry on.","Luo Lan did not say how she wanted to disseminate the rations. Thus, the people at the edges were trying their best to squeeze toward the center.","Luo Lan looked at the seemingly endless ocean of people and knew that it would be a colossal task to give out the Soldier Ration Radishes. At the very least, it would take close to a day.","Normal people could not even stand going hungry for a day, and much less, people from the tribes who had already gone hungry for an unimaginable amount of time.","The current arrangement was the best one that Luo Lan could have made. She did not have any better ideas.","Faced with a lack of manpower and people dropping like flies at the edges, all Luo Lan could do was watch and feel helpless.","The leaders of the Black Gold and Platinum tribes Luo Lan had called out first thought that the Item-Storing Walnuts contained the Usnea, just like she did when she saw the vines.","However, she did not appear to be joking.","Each of the leaders of the Black Gold and Platinum tribes pulled out a branch and plucked out a leaf.","At the instant that the leaves entered their mouths, they started to tremble with excitement.","Luo Lan’s miraculous discovery had indeed brought new hope to the Iron Hammer Federation.","The leaders of the tribes chattered excitedly, “First Princess! We definitely won’t let your efforts go to waste!”","After bowing to Luo Lan, the leaders of the tribes immediately returned to their own tribes and started distributing the Soldier Ration Radishes’ vines.","They ensured that each of their tribes received ten vines before handing down the rest of the leaves.","In an instant, a green light spread out from the 500-meter-tall statue.","Every area that could be reached by the green light was suddenly brimming with life.","The least concrete thing in the world was human nature.","The green light would definitely be stopped at some point.","Nonetheless, the experts from the Black Gold and Platinum tribes kept their promise to Luo Lan.","If there was even a hint of bloodshed or congestion, they would be removed to make way for the green light.","Before, Luo Lan did not rejoice at the appearance of the green light or grieve for those who had to be put down because she knew that she had more important things to do."]},{"number":2105,"title":"Chapter 2105 Sudden Strange Occurrence!","paragraphs":["2105 Sudden Strange Occurrence!","The most important matter at hand was to stabilize the conditions of the almost 10,000,000 people present.","Luckily, while the Soldier Ration Radishes were being distributed, those who could sense it knew that they would be able to benefit soon. Otherwise, the crowd would have already descended into chaos.","Luo Lan remembered Lin Yuan saying that she could give commands to the powerful being hiding in the shadows.","She did not instruct Shadow to deal with the tribe members who had caused trouble but left the job to the Black Gold and Platinum tribes instead.","But now, she needed to trouble Shadow to do something.","She hoped that Shadow could help her to project her voice further.","If her voice could not reach far enough to be heard by the Black Iron tribes at the edges, it should at least be heard by the Light Bronze and White Silver tribes.","Luo Lan knew that her saying such things at such a time would be able to calm the hearts of the crowd. It was what she needed to do as the First Princess of the Iron Hammer Federation.","Shadow was a dimensional lifeform and could not understand Luo Lan’s actions at all. It could not figure out why a ruler like Luo Lan needed to pity these weaklings.","In the abyssal world, only the strong were respected, while the weak did not even have the right to live.","Nonetheless, Shadow still followed Lin Yuan’s order and cooperated with Luo Lan the best it could.","Shadow released its aura.","As an Apostle, it could help to carry Luo Lan’s voice further when it released its source-type power and faith power.","Luo Lan did not understand this Immortal expert’s power, but it was much more effective to use source-type power and faith power to project one’s voice than spirit qi.","This allowed the spirit qi professionals at the edge of the area to hear Luo Lan’s voice clearly.","Luo Lan encouraged the starving tribe members while she made them sincere promises and mapped out a glorious future that was awaiting them.","The promises that she made to them were the same as the ones that Lin Yuan had made to her.","There was no better encouragement than these promises.","But it went without saying that once she voiced the promises, she would be held accountable to them.","However, Luo Lan did not fear this.","Even if she could not fulfill these promises and was hounded by them, she was still willing to save as many lives as she could now.","Furthermore, Luo Lan came to trust Lin Yuan after she got to know him. She believed that he would make good on his promises, just like how he was giving her the chance to save these tribe members.","Luo Lan’s passionate speech, full of hope and sincerity, had indeed been extremely effective.","Lin Yuan had been watching everything from the underground palace.","He could not help but marvel at her benevolence and decision-making power, as well as the unselfishness of the Black Gold and Platinum tribes.","Lin Yuan felt that it would be much more worth it to nurture the Iron Hammer Federation than the Divine Wood Federation.","After a moment of silence, Lin Yuan confirmed his decision. He planned on helping Luo Lan and the Iron Hammer Federation even more.","In the midst of her passionate speech, Luo Lan suddenly noticed that the sand beside her had turned into a pool of quicksand.","The figure of a young man dressed in white robes appeared next to her.","Lin Yuan did not immediately speak to Luo Lan but gave an order to the Source Sand instead.","The Source Sand had been creating sand continuously ever since it was at the underground palace.","With so much sand, it would be easy to create as large of a scale of commotion as he wanted.","It was akin to treating the Source Sand like an animal.","The movement of the sand was just like an animal rolling over, and it did not take up too much spiritual power.","Once Lin Yuan was done communicating with the Source Sand, a quicksand that contained all of the Iron Hammer Federation’s members appeared.","Lin Yuan tossed out 50 Diamond Item-Storing Walnuts.","The Item-Storing Walnuts were squeezed by the Source Sand and released the Soldier Ration Radishes that were within.","The quicksand became the best vehicle for transport that helped to deliver the Solder Ration Radishes.","The grains of sand flicked the leaves down from the Soldier Ration Radishes and pried the leaves into the mouths of the tribe members who had collapsed from hunger.","It was inevitable that they would end up feeding sand to the collapsed tribe members as well, but they would still be alive nonetheless.","After the quicksand that encompassed the 10,000,000 people appeared, everyone cast their gazes at Luo Lan.","This was because she had also appeared out of a pool of quicksand.","The experts who looked at her, as well as the nearby tribe members, all saw Lin Yuan next to Luo Lan. They also saw him instructing the pool of quicksand to deliver the Soldier Ration Radishes.","Uncontrollable tears welled up in Luo Lan’s eyes when she saw what Lin Yuan did.","The tears were a sign of her deepest sincerity as well as her gratitude to Lin Yuan on behalf of Lin Yuan.","Luo Lan did not forget her duty because of Lin Yuan.","With her voice magnified by Shadow, Luo Lan told the people who had the Soldier Ration Radishes not to forget to hand out the vines to the others after they ate a leaf.","Everything was progressing nicely, and more and more citizens of the Iron Hammer Federation were being saved. Suddenly, something strange occurred.","A man dressed in a dark red half-armor appeared in the air not far from Luo Lan and Lin Yuan.","His hair was slightly white, which meant that he did not have much of his lifespan left despite having a middle-aged appearance.","The middle-aged man could clearly sense Shadow’s aura but was not concerned.","He glanced at Lin Yuan before focusing on Luo Lan.","His gaze was complex as he looked at Luo Lan.","Lin Yuan and Luo Lan both noticed this expert who had suddenly appeared.","...","When the man dressed in dark red half-armor entered the sea of flowers, Lin Yuan received a warning from Silver Corona.","Silver Corona calculated that it was no match for this expert and so had not tried to stop him.","Lin Yuan knew that this man in dark red half-armor was either a local expert from the Iron Hammer Federation or a member of the Truth Association.","All the members that Lin Yuan had seen or heard of from Jin Qianxun wore red-gray cloaks.","This man in dark red half-armor did not try to hide. It was more likely that he was an expert from the Iron hammer Federation."]},{"number":2106,"title":"Chapter 2106 You’re Right, I’m Here to Kill You!","paragraphs":["2106 You’re Right, I’m Here to Kill You!","Regardless of where he was from, he had to be an enemy from the way he had appeared without warning in the sea of flowers!","As Lin Yuan grew, he became increasingly merciless to his enemies.","However, Lin Yuan was not in a rush to kill this expert wearing dark red half-armor.","This expert was indeed more powerful than Shadow, but not by much.","!!","The advanced Immortal power could indeed exert pressure on Shadow. Thus, it was to be expected that the expert wearing dark red half-armor would be unbothered by Shadow’s presence.","If this expert was from the Iron Hammer Federation, his power was top class in the Iron Hammer Federation, and he could be called an expert that guarded his federation.","Lin Yuan was curious why such an expert had not stopped Luo Cai’s moronic order but instead came to see Luo Lan.","Could he be here to kill Luo Lan?","Lin Yuan was not making wild guesses.","He had been observing the mood in the man’s eyes, and that was what sealed Lin Yuan’s guess.","It was likely that this man dressed in dark red armor was familiar with Luo Lan.","Luo Lan had appeared on the statue without warning and had used the fastest method to disseminate the Soldier Ration Radishes that also had not caused a stir among the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members.","This sight allowed Lin Yuan to see how the Iron Hammer Federation came together during crises, as well as Luo Lan’s ruling and decision-making abilities.","There was no question that Luo Lan had grown from this incident.","This expert’s intent to kill could be a gift to Luo Lan to allow her to grow even faster.","This expert dressed in dark-red half armor could be unbothered by Shadow because he was indeed stronger than Shadow.","Lin Yuan could also be unbothered by this expert because he had Begin Lady.","All experts who had not awakened their birth horoscopes were nothing more than ants to experts who had set their spirit fires alight.","The experts who had reached Eternal were considered at the peak of the main world but were only slightly stronger ants to experts who had set their spirit fires alight.","Luo Lan looked at the man wearing dark red half-armor and called out, “Fang Ke, you”","The moment she called out to him, she was stopped by her rationality.","Her father’s death had to be linked to Fang Ke.","He was her father’s personal guard, yet he was still alive after her father had died.","Moreover, if her father had been murdered, Fang Ke should have sought revenge against Luo Cai.","Why was he allowing Luo Cai to hunt her despite being alive?","Furthermore, Luo Cai had seen the killing intent in Fang Ke’s eyes that was the same as that in the eyes of the men who were hunting. They were all equally bone-chilling.","Luo Lan smiled bitterly and said, “Are you here to kill me?”","Luo Lan knew that many people had died while trying to help her flee from the Iron Hammer Federation.","Thus, her heart had not fully hardened.","However, Fang Ke’s killing intent was the final straw that fully stonified her heart.","As she looked at Fang Ke now, there was no panic in her eyes, only coldness. It was the gaze of a ruler placing judgment on one of her subjects who had plotted against her.","Fang Ke felt a twinge of panic when he saw Luo Lan’s gaze shift.","Fang Ke had been loyal to her father, but the hand pulling the strings behind the Iron Hammer Federation was too powerful. There was no way for anyone to even think of resisting.","Eventually, Fang Ke made the selfish decision of choosing to live while becoming the claws for this hand.","Although Luo Lan was currently in the midst of saving the Iron Hammer Federation, Fang Ke still decided to kill her.","Luo Lan’s eyes had been the same as her father’s. These eyes had been haunting Fang Ke’s dreams.","Fang Ke frowned when he saw her gaze.","In his mind, he would be able to kill Luo Lan with a slight twitch of his hand.","Thus, he was not going to let his guard down when he spoke. He went on to reply honestly, “You’re right. I’m here to kill you. Rather than you leading these people back to their deaths in the Iron Hammer Federation, they might be able to survive once you’re dead.”","Luo Lan snorted and stared down Fang Ke as she said in a low voice, “If I didn’t appear and hand out the vines, these millions of Iron Hammer Federation citizens would have died of starvation!","“Did you think about how you’re going to find a way for them to survive then? Why didn’t you stop Luo Cai when he made such a stupid decision? If you only betrayed my father, I can see you as just a traitor to the Freezing Hammer Tribe. But by not stopping Luo Cai, you have turned your back on all the tribes in the Iron Hammer Federation. I want to know if the present you is fit to say something so contradictory!”","Luo Lan’s words rendered Fang Ke speechless.","Fang Ke knew that he was on the losing side when it came to a battle of logic, and Luo Lan had just exposed his sins in front of millions of citizens of the Iron Hammer Federation.","The last of his pride crumbled. He felt both guilty and furious.","He seemed to want to stand up for himself and said, “Rather than being killed, smart people would choose another way to continue surviving!”","Luo Lan could not help but smirk with amusement.","“Both smart and dumb people have their dignity. Regardless of whether the Iron Hammer Federation is strong or weak, they have their dignity! For the past century, you have enjoyed life in the Iron Hammer Federation. I’m sure you’re able to understand such simple logic!”","Luo Lan’s words cut deep into Fang Ke, and he attacked her in a fit of guilty rage.","He did not summon any feys.","As a Sovereign expert, he could still produce significant effects when he used his feys’ abilities without summoning them.","Fang Ke had carefully aimed this attack at an area that Shadow could not block.","He intended to end it all with this one attack.","Fang Ke was even more powerful than the leaders of Black Gold tribes and pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters.","The leaders of Black Gold tribes and pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters were weaker than Shadow.","...","However, Fang Ke had not expected the experts on the ground to leap into the air toward Luo Lan just as he was about to attack her."]},{"number":2107,"title":"Chapter 2107 Blood Claw Charging Wolf!","paragraphs":["2107 Blood Claw Charging Wolf!","The experts with defense-type feys applied their shields onto Luo Lan.","It was clear that by helping Luo Lan at this moment, they were making it clear that they were siding with her.","For the sake of Luo Lan, these people attacked Fang Ke despite knowing that they were no match for him.","This was proof of what Luo Lan had just declared to him.","!!","Apparently, these people were the dumb people with dignity, while he was the smart person without dignity.","This immediately caused Fang Ke to seethe, and he bellowed, “Charge ahead! Blood Claw Charging Wolf!”","With Fang Ke’s roar, a man with long hair the color of blood appeared next to him.","This man’s face was strangely vile and emanated cruelty. He looked at everyone as though they were delicious meals.","Feys were only obedient to their masters.","Fang Ke had been around Luo Lan often when she was young. As such, the Blood Claw Charging Wolf was very familiar with her.","But now that Fang Ke’s will had changed, the Blood Claw Charging Wolf’s attitude toward her and the other experts from the tribes had also changed.","The Blood Claw Charging Wolf raised its claw-tipped hand and let out a fearsome howl.","Soon, the image of blood-red wolves appeared in the sky.","The wolves started charging wildly about in the sky, kicking up a blood-colored gust that was tinged with the metallic flavor of blood.","As was his habit, Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the Blood Claw Charging Wolf.","This was when he saw that the Blood Claw Charging Wolf was one of the rare feys that had four typesblood-type, dark-type, gold-type, and wind-type.","Apparently, the Blood Claw Charging Wolf had already gone through three elemental mutations.","Elemental mutations were the rarest type of mutation.","The Floating Island Whale was distinct from the Island Whale because it had gone through an elemental mutation.","Although the Blood Claw Charging Wolf’s elemental mutations were clearly not as complete as that of Universe, it was considered a historical miracle for it to have gone through four slight elemental mutations.","Lin Yuan was fully capable of using another method to obtain feys with such strong potential.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had been an obedient puppy recently while it worked on increasing its power. Currently, it had already reached Diamond X/Legend and was about to reach Fantasy Breed.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee lived off of Red Thorn but was not restricted by Lin Yuan’s spirit qi professional rank.","Once the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee evolved to Fantasy Breed, Lin Yuan could use his resources to continue increasing its power.","The Acid Corpse Poison Bee could be hosted within other feys, and the Blood Claw Charging Wolf was the best potential host.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s control over lifeforms that the Acid Corpse Poison Bee had hosted was not restricted by the freshness of the target. It would not face any resistance from the target’s spiritual energy and soul power when it was hosted in corpses.","Thus, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was fully capable of taking control of powerful lifeforms through the Acid Corpse Poison Bee.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee could produce around six of the Acid Corpse Poison Bee.","By calculations, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee could produce another Acid Corpse Poison Bee each time it evolved by a significant extent. Even when it reached Immortal, it would only be able to produce nine of the Acid Corpse Poison Bee at most.","Thus, Lin Yuan wanted to prioritize quality and carefully pick each fey that the Acid Corpse Poison Bee hosted.","At that moment, Fang Ke was clearly intent on killing Luo Lan and the tribe members who were protecting her. He wanted to use his power to catch all his prey in one net.","Although the tribe members had hesitation in their eyes as they faced the Blood Claw Charging Wolf, they eventually decided against retreating and chose to stick by Luo Lan.","In the midst of a crisis, Luo Lan had appeared to save all of them. Thus, there was no reason for them to abandon her in her time of need.","All the tribes who were present already saw Luo Lan as the true ruler of the Iron Hammer Federation.","Luo Lan looked relieved and glad when she saw the tribe members shielding her.","Ever since Fang Ke appeared, Luo Lan had not expressed any fear of him.","This was because Lin Yuan had placed an expert by her side to protect her and because he was right next to her as well.","As the First Princess of the Iron Hammer Federation, Luo Lan was well aware of what kind of power the leader of the Yang family had possessed when he was ruling the Divine Wood Federation.","Lin Yuan was capable of completely transforming the Divine Wood Federation with ease. How could Fang Ke, who had not even reached pinnacle Immortal, be of any concern to him?","Although Fang Ke had summoned the Sovereign/Immortal VIII Blood Claw Charging Wolf, Luo Lan was not afraid.","Lin Yuan was touched by the willingness of the Iron Hammer Federation’s experts to protect Luo Lan when she was threatened.","Now was the time to settle this sudden commotion.","Lin Yuan watched as Fang Ke’s fey swiped a dark red claw at Luo Lan and the tribe experts and he reached out a finger to point at it.","The pink gem at the corner of Lin Yuan’s eye turned into a stream of water.","The stream of water swirled around Lin Yuan’s finger before shooting over to Fang Ke.","The stream of water’s attack on Fang Ke appeared weak, but at the moment it made contact with his attack, it released an explosion of power that completely negated his attack.","The stream of water turned into sprays of water that rained down, each moving toward the Blood Claw Charging Wolf’s claws.","Once the water negated the Blood Claw Charging Wolf’s attack, it gathered back together and shot through Fang Ke’s temple, dragging out a fountain of blood with it as it emerged from the other side of his head.","None of the blood stained the stream of water.","The large net trapped the Blood Claw Charging Wolf and was soon alight with the faint glow of flames.","The glow of flames locked away the Blood Claw Charging Wolf’s power and prevented it from activating its Immortal body.","This sudden occurrence shocked not only the experts who had been willing to lay down their lives to protect Luo Lan, but even Luo Lan, who already knew that Lin Yuan was capable of solving the problem.","Luo Lan had not expected it to be so effortless for Lin Yuan to solve the issue.","At that moment, Luo Lan suddenly felt that becoming a member of the Astronomical Parliament was an even luckier opportunity than being born as the First Princess of the Iron Hammer Federation.","..."]},{"number":2108,"title":"Chapter 2108 The Legend Shrouded in Moonlight!","paragraphs":["2108 The Legend Shrouded in Moonlight!","Lin Yuan did not stay after solving the issue but returned to the underground palace instead.","However, he did not know that he had just cemented himself as a legend in the Iron Hammer Federation.","The legend would say that after the Iron Hammer Federation’s goddess saved the citizens, a godly being even more powerful than the goddess had wrapped himself in moonlight in the middle of the blazing day and used sand and vines to save the entire Iron Hammer Federation. When the goddess was later threatened by a traitor, the godly being had used a stream of water to protect her.","The Iron Hammer Federation had always worshiped the snow beast on the snowy mountain.","!!","But ever since this event, a statue of a god shrouded in moonlight and wielding a stream of water and sand appeared in the snow beast’s temple. This statue represented rich fertility. There was a statue of the goddess next to the godly being, who was only one head shorter than the godly being.","The shrine in the depths of Lin Yuan’s soul started to change.","He had not had a chance to investigate the changed shrine yet, but the faith power continued to accumulate.","Lin Yuan believed that it would be better to possess as much faith power as possible. Thus, he also yearned to accumulate it. He was always thinking of ways to gather as much faith power as possible.","Lin Yuan did not think about faith power with this appearance.","But once he returned to the underground palace, he noticed that there were many more dots of light in the shrine in his soul.","He realized that the tribe members of the Iron Hammer Federation were good sources of faith power.","Lin Yuan intended to give Luo Lan some instructions once she returned.","Now that he had made good on his promise to her, he had the right to request anything of her.","With help from Luo Lan, who was currently the First Princess of the Iron Hammer Federation but was soon going to be its ruler, Lin Yuan would eventually be able to attain the faith of every tribe member from the Iron Hammer Federation.","But it went without saying that these were all just hypothetical plans at this stage.","The most important thing that Lin Yuan needed to do now was come up with a way to combat Fifth Page Truth.","Luo Lan had appeared and used her own means to control the situation.","The tribe members who had traveled all the way here and had managed to keep from starving to death while being held captive by the sea of flowers were the most elite combat power that the tribes could offer.","With these people loyal to Luo Lan, she would be able to take back the throne from Luo Cai as long as the Truth Association did not step in to help him.","With the crown on her head, Luo Lan had a much more legitimate claim to the throne than Luo Cai.","Although Luo Lan had been shocked by Lin Yuan’s methods, she was not shocked when he left.","Rather, she turned to the experts around her who had wanted to shield her and said, “Go and continue handing out the vines. Once everyone has eaten a leaf, each of them can keep two leaves and one vine for themselves. After eating one leaf, they won’t have to eat again for the next five to ten days. With the vines, they won’t have to worry about food for the next month!”","Luo Lan jumped down from the statue made of sand and started to heal the injured tribe members just like she did before.","Not all the tribes of the Iron Hammer Federation had arrived at the border at the same time. Thus, there were still more who were entering the sea of flowers under orders of the imperial guards.","Silver Corona gathered them within the sea of bone lotus flowers, and the members of the Black Gold tribes immediately handed the Soldier Ration Radishes to them to save those who were on the brink of starvation.","Lin Yuan knew that he had ruined the Truth Association’s plan for the Iron Hammer Federation to start a war and that news of this would soon reach Fifth Page Truth and Luo Cai.","At that time, both parties would jump into action.","What Lin Yuan needed to do next was wait.","For the next two days, Lin Yuan’s life was abnormally quiet. But he knew that this was just the calm before the storm.","Luo Lan had already returned to the underground palace.","She had not had a single night of good rest ever since she found out that her father was dead and she had to flee from the Iron Hammer Federation.","She had just been working non-stop for two days.","But when she returned to the underground palace, she looked extremely excited.","Lin Yuan could see gratitude brimming in her eyes.","He did not give her the chance to thank him and said, “You should have done all you needed to do in the past two days. You’ve done well! Much better than I imagined! What are you planning on doing next with the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members?”","Luo Lan was silent for a moment before she said, “Lord Lin Yuan, none of the experts from the Iron Hammer Federation need to keep their heads low out of hunger anymore. I want to bring some of them with me to take back the imperial court!","“I know that you are almighty. I can’t deal with the Truth Association, so please provide your protection! However, Luo Cai killed my father and ruined the future of the entire Iron Hammer Federation. It will take more than 20 years for the population of the Iron Hammer Federation to recover. I want to personally lead these tribe members who are lucky enough to survive into the imperial court to seek revenge against Luo Cao.”","Lin Yuan looked at Luo Lan with surprise.","He had not expected her to be so hot-blooded.","Luo Lan wanted to lead the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members back to the Iron Hammer Federation.","With the Soldier Ration Radishes, they did not have to fear going hungry.","However, things were not as simple as Luo Lan thought.","Lin Yuan did not know what Fifth Page Truth was capable of.","His goal was to reduce the entire Startling Lines Continent into a mayhem of bloodshed until all the citizens from the three federations lost their lives to war.","Lin Yuan had saved these tribe members who had been slated to be collected by the grim reaper.","It was likely that Fifth Page Truth would still find a way to claim their lives.","Thus, it was a very dangerous decision for Luo Lan to lead the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members back to the imperial court at such a time.","Ta Lei’s city was still in the process of being built. Although there was help from the Land Imps, there were not enough Spirit Craftsmen or manpower to start carving into the scaffolding that the Land Imps had set up.","Ever since the construction of Ta Lei’s city began, Lin Yuan saw it as the core of the entire Startling Lines Continent as well as the largest customer for Sky City’s resources.","Hence, the size and scale of the city were comparable to that of Sacred Forest City. In fact, it was even larger than Sacred Forest City.","This was why construction was still not done despite having help from so many Land Imps."]},{"number":2109,"title":"Chapter 2109 Sudden Embrace!","paragraphs":["2109 Sudden Embrace!","It was Ta Lei’s city to take in more than a hundred million people.","It would be a good decision for Luo Lan to lead the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members to Ta Lei’s city and help to set it up.","With so many helpers, Ta Lei’s city would likely be done in a few weeks.","It would not be too late for Luo Lan to lead the tribe members back to the Iron Hammer Federation’s imperial court after the dust had settled.","“Luo Lan, I understand you want to get your revenge, but this is clearly isn’t the right time. I’m sure you know about how Seventh Page War conquered the Seven States of Darkness and caused all the lifeforms there to be in utter misery.","“Fifth Page Truth is also one of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon, so he definitely won’t be more merciful than Seventh Page War. If you take the tribe members back now, you might be stopped by Fifth Page War before you even make it halfway back.","“You’ve seen Ta Lei and been to the city he’s building. You should settle the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members back in Ta Lei’s city for now and help him with the construction of the city. Don’t worry. Once everything is settled, I will leave the handling of Luo Cai to you.”","When Luo Lan heard what Lin Yuan said, she knew that she had been overzealous about revenge.","She had heard about Tower Canon from Su Yiren. But when the time came for her to seek revenge, she forgot about Tower Canon’s terrifying might.","If she could not take the tribe members back to the Iron Hammer Federation, she would have an issue with finding a place for them to settle down.","Although the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribes were united, they also fought frequently.","Once they were all full but were still stuck in the sea of flowers, Luo Lan could not guarantee that they would not stop fighting amongst themselves.","Luckily, Lin Yuan had already come up with a place they could stay.","Ta Lei had joined the Astronomical Parliament earlier than her. He might just be a member from one of the Iron Hammer Federation’s Black Iron tribes while she was the First Princess of the Iron Hammer Federation, but she dared not underestimate him.","This was because she had heard Ta Lei call Lin Yuan ‘master’ more than once. Lin Yuan had not agreed to being addressed in such a way, but he had not stopped Ta Lei either.","If these tribes with growing populations settled down in Ta Lei’s city and helped him to build it, the tribe members would gain a better-than-average safe haven as well as be doing a favor for him.","Luo Lan bowed to Lin Yuan before she said, “Lord Lin Yuan, I won’t express my gratitude in words. From now on, use me as you please!”","Luo Lan suddenly felt as though there were two pairs of eyes on her. She turned and saw that the gazes were coming from the silver armor-wearing young man who was always by Lin Yuan’s side and Wen Yu, who also occupied a golden throne in the Astronomical Parliament.","Both Wen Yu and Liu Jie were looking at Luo Lan with slightly flustered eyes.","Luo Lan also noticed that her words were slightly inappropriate and quickly explained, “Lord Lin Yuan, what I mean is that I’ll do whatever you want me to do.”","Lin Yuan smiled and shook his head as he said, “These are all the deals we have already made. You don’t need to thank me. But since you already did, keep the bracelet. There are hundreds of the Diamond Item-Storing Walnuts inside the bracelet. You don’t just eat to fill your stomach. There isn’t much taste to the Soldier Ration Radish. The bracelet is spatial equipment. When you wear it, you can control it using your spiritual energy. There are various ingredients inside the Diamond Item-Storing Walnuts.","“Once you reach Ta Lei’s city, you can distribute the ingredients and give everyone a few feasts. The Soldier Ration Radish’s leaves and vines that you’ve already given out can act as an emergency food supply. The Soldier Ration Radish’s leaves and vines contain an immense amount of vitality. On top of that, they don’t go bad for a long time, so you don’t have to worry when storing them.","“The food inside the Diamond Item-Storing Walnuts were obtained from a chamber of commerce in the Divine Wood Federation. When the two federations start to exchange resources in the future, the Iron Hammer Federation won’t have to worry about the risk of starvation during winter. With this, I’ve fulfilled my promise to you.”","Luo Lan bowed deeply to Lin Yuan again.","She had not known him for long, but her impression of him was slowly deepening.","Since she was a member of the Astronomical Parliament, she was technically Lin Yuan’s subordinate.","Normally, a superior would not make promises to a subordinate.","However, Lin Yuan did not take his promise to her lightly. Rather, he had fulfilled it in a short span of time.","Moreover, Lin Yuan was a very gentle person and was more than willing to spare a thought for her and the tribe members of the Iron Hammer Federation.","An example of this was when he used the Source Sand to deliver the Soldier Ration Radishes to the tribes at the periphery.","If the Soldier Ration Radish had been planted in the Iron Hammer Federation, the tribe members would not have been bothered by hunger during winter.","Lin Yuan had given her such a large amount of the Soldier Ration Radishes without hesitation.","It was difficult to gauge the value of the Soldier Ration Radish.","To a federation, such a large amount of the Soldier Ration Radish could stabilize a faction when it was in danger.","Every leaf of the Soldier Ration Radish could save a life.","Even without the Soldier Ration Radishes, the over 600 Diamond Item-Storing Walnuts that Lin Yuan had given her were valued at over 10,000,000 Great Lush dollars","Apart from Lin Yuan, Su Yiren was also very kind to her. Ta Lei, Bei Xu, and the rest were also very friendly to her. She did not feel awkward when she communicated with them through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Luo Lan’s heart warmed as she looked at Lin Yuan.","She ignored Wen Yu and Liu Jie, who were looking at her, and went up to Lin Yuan to wrap her arms around him.","It was not a strong hug, and Luo Lan drifted out of the underground palace like a light breeze once the hug was over to organize the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members.","Lin Yuan’s eyebrow twitched after Luo Lan hugged him.","He did not think much of the hug and attributed it to her being overly happy.","However, Lin Yuan felt he had been hugged too many times in the past six months."]},{"number":2110,"title":"Chapter 2110 Black-Hearted Thunder!","paragraphs":["2110 Black-Hearted Thunder!","In the next few days, the tribes of the Iron Hammer Federation were gathered under the flag of Luo Lan as she led all of them into Ta Lei’s city.","Ta Lei had long become the pride of the Horseshoe Tribe.","Despite being the City Lord, Ta Lei personally ushered Luo Lan and the other leaders of tribes and Creation Masters into the city.","A few months ago, Ta Lei had only been a young boy in a faction.","Although he had become a Creation Master after joining the Astronomical Parliament, his heart was just as pure as it had always been.","His pure-heartedness was reserved for the Astronomical Parliament.","But in a way, he had already become a black-hearted maggot that was sufficiently merciless.","This was all due to Su Yiren.","If Ta Lei’s city was small, it would be fine.","However, his was a metropolis that was even larger than Sacred Forest City. If he did not grow quickly into his role as the City Lord, he would eventually be replaced.","Su Yiren had seen how stiff competition was amongst the Astronomical Parliament’s members. However, this was not intentional but was because the members were individually too outstanding.","If she did not work hard to improve himself, she would eventually lose her presence among the ever-increasing members.","Su Yiren could clearly feel that she had not improved as much when she had been a Dark Envoy as during the few months since she had joined Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan not only had members of the Astronomical Parliament beside him.","People like Liu Jie and Listen were shining in their own way.","Her heart had not been set when she first arrived at the underground palace.","Ta Lei was the one who had spent the longest time by her side.","Su Yiren did not want him to end up replaced.","Luo Lan dared not think lightly of Ta Lei.","But ever since she found out about his background, she understood why the experts from the Black Gold and Platinum tribes had not thought much of him.","Ta Lei experienced such an attitude against him when a member of a Platinum tribe provoked him.","At that time, he sent out the expert Lin Yuan had assigned to him to kill that expert from the Platinum tribe.","Through this, he had demonstrated his prowess as a City Lord.","He planned out the residences for the tribe members in Luo Lan’s stead.","At first, Ta Lei did not feel a sense of belonging to the Iron Hammer Federation.","Luo Lan had helped many tribes in the Iron Hammer Federation, but the Horseshoe Tribe had not been one of them.","Rather, the Horseshoe Tribe had almost been killed by a tribe with a Class 2 Creation Master.","If he had not encountered Lin Yuan, his entire family would be dead.","Thus, Ta Lei was not afraid in the slightest of these legendary large factions as well as the First Princess of the Iron Hammer Federation.","Ta Lei and Su Yiren had maintained contact through the Thoughts Letter Paper, and she had given him a lot of advice.","Through this, Ta Lei found out that Lin Yuan was the one who had saved these tribe members of the Iron Hammer Federation.","Ta Lei knew that Lin Yuan would not permit any of these tribe members to lay a hand on him.","Ta Lei’s attitude took Luo Lan by surprise.","Luo Lan first thought that Ta Lei would act friendly and respectful when he found out who she was.","Nonetheless, she suppressed this sense of inappropriateness.","This enormous city belonged to Ta Lei. It was still somewhat acceptable for him to make arrangements in her stead.","When many tribe members did not move after hearing about Ta Lei’s arrangements, Luo Lan immediately rebuked the tribe leaders.","She had just saved the lives of all the tribe members, and all of them now saw her as a goddess.","Thus, no matter how indignant the tribe members felt, they started moving according to Ta Lei’s arranged residences.","Ta Lei knew that these tribe members of the Iron Hammer Federation had come to his incomplete city to help with construction.","It was reasonable for him to assign jobs to them as the City Lord of this giant city.","However, he did not do so.","Ta Lei was aware of how these tribe leaders saw him.","He had decided on the residences in Luo Lan’s stead because he wanted to maintain his pride and duty as the City Lord.","If he could not keep up his pride or carry out his duty, he would be sending Lin Yuan a sign that he was incapable.","After he did this, he could take a backseat to other matters and leave them to Luo Lan.","Ta Lei did not have to worry about how much effort the tribe members put into helping out in the city.","He could just send out assessors and inform Luo Lan of the results.","If anyone slacked off and did not put effort into building the city, Luo Lan would take care of them.","Ta Lei knew how important the city’s construction was to Lin Yuan.","In the past, Ta Lei had been a clueless young boy from a small tribe.","But after his time with Su Yiren, Ta Lei understood what kind of position he held as the core of the three federations.","It was clear that Lin Yuan intended to use the city to nurture his affiliated factions. All the people who had benefited from Lin Yuan would move into the city.","Besides carrying out his duty as the City Lord, Ta Lei needed to invest more of his effort into increasing his power.","...","Everything was calm over the next few days.","But deep in the palace of the Iron Hammer Federation’s imperial court, a young man with hard features and sly eyes currently had his brow deeply furrowed as he listened to the anxious report from the elderly man standing below him. His fist made grinding noises as he squeezed it tighter and tighter.","All of a sudden, the young man’s patience ran out, and he slammed a hand down on the armrest of his seat and yelled, “Useless! You’re all useless! Why hasn’t Fang Ke returned?”","The elderly man started trembling when Luo Cai slammed his hand down on the armrest.","When Luo Cai had been by the previous king’s side, he had always appeared formal and professional. Apart from his mediocrity, no one could find any issues with him.","But ever since he became the king of the Iron Hammer Federation and had numerous powerful experts at his beck and call, he started acting unreasonably and recklessly."]},{"number":2111,"title":"Chapter 2111 Luo Cai Coughs Blood!","paragraphs":["2111 Luo Cai Coughs Blood!","The elderly man was an emperor-class expert and a butler within the imperial court who was in charge of delivering information.","He was afraid that Luo Cai would vent his ire on him.","There was already another butler who Luo Cai had killed while he was delivering information.","That butler had died an unnecessary death.","Luo Cai had been the one who requested to receive the reports, but he lost his temper when the content of the reports did not meet his satisfaction, threatening the lives of everyone in the imperial court.","However, Luo Cai had asked him a question, and he could not leave him hanging.","“Your Majesty, Lord Fang Ke hasn’t returned.”","Luo Cai picked up something and tossed it at the elderly man.","At that moment, an almost negligible aura emerged from the depths of the palace.","Luo Cai’s entire demeanor changed when he sensed this aura.","“You’re dismissed! If Fang Ke returns, send him to my room immediately!”","The elderly man was an emperor-class expert and had also sensed the aura from the depths of the imperial court. He knew that the person this aura belonged to had saved him.","Yet, he did not feel a shred of happiness.","The elderly man noticed a few times while he was giving his report that there had been a person wearing a red-gray robe standing next to Luo Cai.","Luo Cai’s gaze would flicker toward this person before he gave any order, as though he was seeking this person’s opinion.","This told the elderly man that an unknown faction was controlling Luo Cai.","The elderly man was extremely sorrowful, but there was nothing he could do with the power he had.","He could tell that many servants in the imperial court had lost their respect for Luo Cai, despite many of them having been promoted to their positions by him.","Most of the servants within the imperial court came from Yellow Gold tribes.","Luo Cai had dispatched all of the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribes in the middle of winter, with rampant food scarcity.","The reason for invading the Divine Wood Federation in order to obtain food to tide them over this crisis was not convincing.","He had even sent all of the weak women and elderly to the Divine Wood Federation as well.","Luo Cai had met with immediate opposition after giving out this order.","However, all those who had opposed him had disappeared in the night and were never to be seen again.","As such, no one else dared to stand against him.","Even if these people’s disappearance was not related to Luo Cai, it had to be caused by the faction controlling him. Luo Cai had to be aware of this.","The more the elderly man thought about it, the sadder he became. He wondered how many of his family members in the tribe were still alive.","After the elderly man left, a figure dressed in a gray-red robe walked out from within the palace.","Luo Cai jumped to his feet when he saw this figure leave his seat empty as he said respectfully, “My lord, please take a seat!”","The figure dressed in the gray-red robe did not stand on ceremony and planted himself on the throne that was supposed to be reserved for the ruler of the Iron Hammer Federation.","Luo Cai bowed and asked tentatively, “Lord, when will I be able to officially join the Truth Association?”","The moment the last word left Luo Cai’s lips, a withered hand reached out from underneath the robe and closed its fingers around his neck before lifting him up from the ground.","Luo Cai had also done the same to other servants when he lost his temper. He had not expected being choked and struggling to breathe would bring with it such discomfort and misery.","Luo Cai knew that the possibility of him being killed by this person was very high, just like how he had helped him kill his uncle.","Luo Cai’s brain was so lacking in oxygen that he was already feeling dizzy. But he never stopped struggling.","The withered hand forcefully tossed him away a moment later, and he crashed to the ground below the platform.","Although he was an A-rank spirit qi professional, this fall had broken most of his bones, and all of his internal organs were in pain.","At that moment, a hoarse voice said, “Didn’t you say nothing would go wrong with the plan? Your plan has ruined Lord Truth’s plan. Do you think I should let you live? After messing up everything, you dare to ask to join the Truth Association?”","Luo Cai was not clear on what was happening, but it was obvious that the Truth Association knew more than him.","He said in a low voice, “Lord, please tell me straight. If I’ve done anything wrong, I will do my best to make up for it!”","The figure vanished from the throne, and in the next moment, Luo Cai felt himself being kicked to the stone pillar at the center of the hall.","A low voice was accompanied by the sound of Luo Cai spitting out a mouthful of blood.","“Make up for it? Your cousin Luo Lan has already gathered all of the tribe members you sent out. There is a way for you to make up for it. The leaders of the tribes pleaded with you and managed to leave 20% of each of their tribes’ members at home to upkeep the tribe. Go and deal with them!”","Luo Cai had been coughing violently while lying in a crumpled heap on the ground.","His eyes filled with blood when he heard what the figure said, and he replied anxiously while coughing, “Lord, it was agreed that these people”","Before he could finish speaking, the hoarse voice interrupted him. “When I promised to let these people live, it was because you assured me that nothing would go wrong with the plan. Now that your plan is riddled with issues and affected Lord Truth’s plan, the deaths of these people is just a small way of compensating Lord Truth.","“Luo Cai, you know what Lord Truth’s plan is. You were willing to send out 80% of the tribe members. Why are you trembling in fear now? If Lord Envoy hears of this, he will definitely be enraged! If he’s angry, you will not continue to live on this earth!”","The figure wearing red-gray robes walked over to Luo Cai and grabbed his short hair, lifting him off the ground. The words that came next were all enunciated slowly. “If you don’t do this properly, I’ll get someone to take your place. Don’t forget how you managed to become king of the Iron Hammer Federation! The Truth Association can place you in this seat and just as easily give it to someone else instead. I’m sure your replacement will be able to do this well.”"]},{"number":2112,"title":"Chapter 2112 Best of Luck to You!","paragraphs":["2112 Best of Luck to You!","A deep resentment floated to the surface of Luo Cai’s gaze.","He knew that if he shook his head, his life would immediately come to an end.","He did not have a rightful claim to the Iron Hammer Federation’s throne.","The Freezing Hammer Tribe had always been the ruler of the Iron Hammer Federation.","Although Luo Lan was the only direct descendant of the Freezing Hammer Tribe, it had many collateral descendants, such as Luo Cai.","All of his brothers and sisters were equally as ambitious as him. If any of them saw the opportunity to replace him, they would be more than willing to do so.","The only thing he could do was nod and agree.","He had already sinned against the Iron Hammer Federation.","As long as he had the support of the Iron Hammer Federation, the matter could be attributed to an early error as the king of the federation.","But if he laid a hand on the remaining 20% of tribe members of the Iron Hammer Federation, he would never be able to wash his sins away, even with the support of the Truth Association.","He sensed that the hand grabbing his hair had increased in force. He screamed as though he was in extreme grief, “Lord, give me a chance to make reparations! I will definitely perform well! But can I ask what else I’ll have to do after this matter is over?”","The moment Luo Cai was done speaking, the withered hand let go and dropped him.","The figure wearing red-gray robes said mockingly, “Once you’re done with this matter, you won’t need to do anything else! The Truth Association will leave the Iron Hammer Federation tomorrow. Hehe, I want to see the person who dared to ruin Lord Truth’s plan! Once we leave the Truth Association, best of luck to you!”","The figure dressed in red-gray robes walked back into the depths of the palace.","In the expansive hall, Luo Cai struggled to climb to his feet.","He used the sleeve of his lavish clothes to wipe the blood from his chin.","He used to have a group of servants in the imperial court who were loyal to only him. They were sufficient to protect him.","But if he attacked the remaining tribe members on the Truth Association’s order, would those servants still remain loyal to him?","All of these previously loyal servants knew that there was a powerful force behind him.","At that time, even if the people from the Truth Association left the Iron Hammer Federation’s imperial court, he would have to pretend they were still present in order to use scare tactics to protect himself.","The people from the Truth Association rarely showed themselves, and it would be possible for him to keep up the lie.","Luo Cai only hoped that the Truth Association could handle the matter cleanly and for none of the dispatched tribe members to return one day. Otherwise, he would truly have to experience being hunted.","There was a wide room with numerous well-crafted shelves. The material that the shelves were made from had been soaked in spirit qi.","Although they had not become fully jade-textured, it was jade-textured to a significant extent.","In a place like the Startling Lines Continent where there had been no Class 5 Creation Masters, the shelves were representative of one’s elite status.","A man wearing plain robes was sitting at a table and holding a thick volume. There were many pieces of paper sandwiched between the pages of the book, and the pieces of paper were covered with markings.","Clearly, the book’s owner had flipped through it countless times.","Currently, the book’s owner was in serious thought and not concentrating on the book at all.","Ever since Jin Qianxun attended his first Truth Association meeting, he had attended them more frequently on a basis of every two to three days.","Each time he would relay the information he received from the meeting to Su Yiren and Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan had provided Jin Qianxun with enough motivation for him to be willing to do such things.","Jin Qianxun knew that he could not rely on his First Brother for information.","He was not the type to be hung up on such things. He would immediately attract suspicion if he suddenly became interested in them.","Since he could not obtain information from home, he went out and participated in many social events despite usually disliking such gatherings.","It was not an exaggeration to say that the Great Lush Federation was full of scholars.","The stronger the faction, the more they would push their younger generation to garner more knowledge.","Knowledge could be passed on, and an ocean of information had been recorded in bound volumes.","Only true successors could read these books.","Thus, gatherings meant to discuss, and research academia almost only consisted of the Great Lush Federations elite.","Jin Qianxun dared not stand out too much. As such, he had only attended four such gatherings.","He learned that the other elites had the same guesses as he and his Second Brother.","A few of them had been too hasty and went to feedback the matter to the heads of their families. As a result, they had been tamped down to different extents.","There was a rumor that the youngest young master of the Sheng family, who had been beloved by his family, had even lost his life because of this.","This confirmed Jin Qianxun’s guess.","There was currently only one topic being addressed during the Truth Association’s meetings, which was that all the families of the Great Lush Federation were to lead their members to the border between the Iron Hammer Federation and Divine Wood Federation tomorrow.","The faction members found out from the Truth Association about how the Iron Hammer Federation had invaded the Divine Wood Federation.","But because of his link to Lin Yuan, Jin Qianxun knew that the Iron Hammer Federation’s invasion of the Divine Wood Federation had not been successful.","The Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members had suffered heavy losses on the long journey but were eventually saved by Lin Yuan.","Given the Truth Association’s impressive means, there was no way they were unaware of this.","Yet, they were hiding the truth from the Great Lush Federation’s secret aristocratic families, who were the main sources of power in the Great Lush Federation.","What could be the goal of instructing the families to lead their members in an all-out attack?","Jin Qianxun could not make an accurate prediction.","However, his prediction was inconsequential.","All he needed to do was relay all the information he received to Lin Yuan.","...","Lin Yuan received the information from Jin Qianxun through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","In the past few days, many Immortal experts had entered the flower sea.","Once it was confirmed that these experts were loyal to the Truth Association, Purple Love had killed all of them.","Although Lin Yuan already had his own prediction after reading the information he received from Jin Qianxun, he still felt it necessary to hold a small meeting to discuss the matter."]},{"number":2113,"title":"Chapter 2113 Offering Witch Dappled Spider!","paragraphs":["2113 Offering Witch Dappled Spider!","Wen Yu and Liu Jie had remained by Lin Yuan’s side for the past few days.","Although Lin Yuan had agreed to help Su Yiren reclaim the Dark Continent and fight it out with Seventh Page War after settling the situation in the Startling Lines Continent, the construction of the harbor in the Great Lush Federation had to come first.","The marine route between the Great Lush Federation and Dark Continent that would be opened by Wo Lun leading a fleet from the Violent Wind Federation could be started at a later date. There was no rush for it.","After all, the Ethereal Jellyfish only had three opportunities to build the Space Tunnel.","Although Lin Yuan possessed a large number of the Item-Storing Walnuts and thus did not have to worry about lacking spatial energy to use the Space Tunnel, it was still necessary to use them judiciously.","Once the Space Tunnel was built, any person could only travel inside the Jewelled Cave Golden Toad that Lin Yuan possessed.","It was a huge drain on resources, and Lin Yuan had already decided where the next Space Tunnel would be built.","Lin Yuan intended to construct a Space Tunnel between the Return from Faraway Mansion and Universe once it took to the air. This would allow the people on Universe to return to the Return from Faraway Mansion in an instant.","No matter how many external factions and territories Lin Yuan set up, his home was the Return from Faraway Mansion.","Once the matters in the Startling Lines Continent were settled, Universe would have been nourished by sufficient pure water-elemental energy and pure spirit qi for it to evolve to Fantasy Breed and Myth Breed.","Once Universe evolved to Myth Breed, Lin Yuan could start building Sky City on its back.","After Universe evolved to Diamond/Legend, it had no obstacles blocking its comprehension of Willpower Runes.","Now was the time for Universe to comprehend a Willpower Rune.","Almost all of the white-clothed followers who Lin Yuan had nurtured first already had two feys who were stuck at Diamond X/Fantasy V.","These feys were the high-quality Bronze feys that Lin Yuan had gifted them for becoming white-clothed followers.","It would not be long before Lin Yuan would be able to obtain a large amount of spirit qi crystals from the white-clothed followers.","Before the spirit qi crystals were used to increase the power of the Perfect Touch Wisteria, they could be used to evolve Universe to Myth Breed.","Lin Yuan had been waiting for a long time to start building Sky City on Universe’s back.","Universe’s exclusive skill Floating Island Secret Realm would not only enable it to build a special space on its back after consuming wind-elemental energy but would also allow its flesh to have powerful fusion ability. Any lifeform, dead or alive, could be planted in Universe’s fat and become its nourishment.","Both the space created and the fusion ability were related to the purity of the elemental energy.","With the Element Well, Lin Yuan could create maximum space on Universe’s back and increase the fusion ability to the greatest extent.","With Floating Island Secret Realm, it would not be difficult for Lin Yuan to build Sky City on Universe’s back.","Lin Yuan had a clear plan for what he was going to do next. Wen Yu and Liu Jie were aware of his intentions.","As such, both of them had been helping with matters in the Startling Lines Continent for the past few days to take some of the load off Su Yiren’s back.","Lin Yuan did not invite many people to attend his war meeting. He only invited Wen Yu, Liu Jie, Su Yiren, Purple Love, and the Mother of Bloodbath.","When Purple Love was not killing the members of the Truth Association who had entered the Sea of Flowers, she was spending time with the Mother of Bloodbath.","The Mother of Bloodbath was Jade Sundial’s child, and its name Blood Love was a derivative of Purple Love’s own.","Purple Love felt that she owed the Mother of Bloodbath far too much after all the years of abandonment it had to endure.","But now, Purple Love finally had a chance to spend an extended period with the Mother of Bloodbath. Thus, she could not lather enough love on the Mother of Bloodbath.","The Mother of Bloodbath had gone with Lin Yuan to the Divine Wood Federation to train.","Besides not being aware of the Astronomical Parliament, it knew almost everything that Lin Yuan did.","The Mother of Bloodbath did not have a shred of talent when it came to strategic planning, but it had a unique way of seeing things.","Listen was one of the main members of Sky City.","The impending fight with the Truth Association would involve the future of the Iron Hammer Federation.","Lin Yuan had not invited Listen and Luo Lan to attend because Listen’s talents lay in networking and business management. He was preparing to build a new system of commerce in the Startling Lines Continent with the Prosperous Chamber of Commerce at the center. For this, he had contracted a Vitality Sloth and was so busy every day that he had not even had time to sleep.","At this time, Luo Lan needed to settle the tribe members who had just moved into Ta Lei’s city.","People did not feel many other emotions when they were starving. But once they were fed and free, they would be bombarded by emotions anew.","By Luo Lan’s calculations, more than 400,000,000 tribe members from the Iron Hammer Federation had managed to survive. However, almost all of them had lost at least one loved one to the havoc.","Grief permeated the air in Ta Lei’s territory.","The sorrow would only deflate after enough time had passed.","Luo Lan was doing all she could to soothe these tribe members as well as tend to the spirit qi professionals who were injured.","At the start of the meeting, Lin Yuan explained the entire situation.","After listening to what Lin Yuan said, both Wen Yu and Su Yiren fell into deep thought.","Purple Love was flummoxed.","As a Heavenly Family Fey, Purple Love had never participated in the squabbles between humans. If not because of Lin Yuan, she would never have allowed the Heavenly Family Cottage to form an alliance with the human-led Radiance Federation.","Nonetheless, she could tell that something was wrong from the content of Lin Yuan’s explanation.","Fifth Page Truth’s goal was likely to gather all of the humans in the Startling Lines Continent and force the three federations to go to war with each other.","There was no way that the Great Lush Federation would emerge as the victor of the war.","Could it be that Fifth Page Truth’s motive was not to gain something from the result of the war but just to ensure that the war took place?","At that moment, the Mother of Bloodbath, who had not spoken since the meeting began, said with a twinge of fear, “I’m sure all of you have heard of the fey called the Offering Witch Dappled Spider! I encountered one once when I was still maturing. If it had not been caught by the Spirit Guards, both Sister Summer and I would have lost our lives!”","Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, Wen Yu, Purple Love, and Su Yiren’s eyes widened."]},{"number":2114,"title":"Chapter 2114 Possibility of being Devoid of a Conscience!","paragraphs":["2114 Possibility of being Devoid of a Conscience!","The Offering Witch Dappled Spider was far too famous for its own good.","Firstly, the Offering Witch Dappled Spider had one of the most elite spider-species fey bloodlines.","The carcinoma feys were fearsome in their destruction of the environment and feys around it.","They had low intelligence and only acted on instinct.","Hence, they were never described as evil.","However, the Offering Witch Dappled Spider was always described as evil.","It was blood-, dark-, and poison-type. It was skilled at using blood-, dark-, and poison-type energy.","After the Offering Witch Dappled Spider laid its eggs, it would hide them in the stone cracks under fallen leaves.","The Offering Witch Dappled Spider’s maternal duties were done the moment it laid its eggs.","There was even a high chance that it would eat its own eggs.","The Offering Witch Dappled Spider’s eggs had concentrated blood-, dark-, and poison-type energy. Thus, they were very nourishing for the Offering Witch Dappled Spider.","Because of this, it was very rare for an egg to hatch successfully.","Even if the eggs were not eaten by their mothers and managed to hatch, they would immediately launch into a bloody fight with each other after hatching.","The young Offering Witch Dappled Spiders killed their siblings in order to consume their flesh and strengthen their feeble newly-hatched selves.","Only one of the Offering Witch Dappled Spiders would be able to leave alive. It would do its best to flee as far from its birthplace as possible.","There was a predisposition in the Offering Witch Dappled Spider’s genes for it to flee from its birthplace in order to hide from its mother.","Once the Offering Witch Dappled Spider had fled far enough away, it would dig up or rob the nest of a spider-species fey and begin weaving its cocoon there.","Then, it would fall into a decade-long slumber.","While it was sleeping, it was very vulnerable, making it ideal food for many underground lifeforms.","But if the Offering Witch Dappled Spider was able to make it through its child stage, it would start to leave a horrible bloody trail behind it.","The Offering Witch Dappled Spider would use one of the three types of energy in its body to concoct a special venom.","When the venom was injected into a target, the target would go mad with hunger and attack any and all lifeforms that were near it.","There was a high chance that the lifeforms attacked by the starving target would end up poisoned by the venom as well.","The Spirit Guards had decided to capture the Offering Witch Dappled Spider because it killed all the lifeforms in a 1,000-meter radius wherever it went.","The Offering Witch Dappled Spider poisoned so many lives so it could activate the venom in their bodies when it was no longer able to evolve itself. It would then sacrifice the vitality in the poisoned lifeforms to earn a breakthrough for itself.","Although the Mother of Bloodbath had not made its prediction clear, it could only have brought up the Offering Witch Dappled Spider to compare it to Fifth Page Truth.","During their discussion, Lin Yuan, Wen Yu, and Liu Jie had not considered it from this perspective.","It was blasphemy to nature to sacrifice all the lifeforms in a continent for oneself. Not even those who were devoid of conscience would do so.","However, from the example of what had happened to the Dark Continent, it showed that Tower Canon was only ever self-serving. Thus, it was actually conceivable for Fifth Page Truth to do such a thing.","Purple Love was silent for a moment before she said, “I have also been wondering what Fifth Page Truth’s reason could be for pushing the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members on such a long journey that resulted in the death and injury of so many. After hearing what Little Love said, I was reminded of something.","“The Heavenly Family Cottage has interacted with Tower Canon before. Fifth Page Truth is much more unhinged than Seventh Page War. Seventh Page War had the courage to attack the Dark Continent but would never dare to lay a hand on the members of the Heavenly Family Cottage.","“Yet, Fifth Page Truth did so and has been trying to cover this deed up ever since. He is not afraid of the Heavenly Family Cottage hunting him down at all. As such, it’s absolutely likely for him to sacrifice the entire Startling Lines Continent for his own benefit.”","The more she spoke, the deeper she furrowed her brow, and the more difficult it became for her to hide her look of utter loathing.","Although the Heavenly Family Cottage was a faction that was meant for Heavenly Family Feys to lie low, they had always done what they could to protect feys and maintain the balance between feys and humans.","The Heavenly Family Cottage had played a big role in the signing of the agreement between the various federations and the sea clans.","Purple Love always saw her grudge against Fifth Page Truth as personal.","However, if Fifth Page Truth was really aiming for such a thing, he would be doing harm to the entire main world.","For the sake of the entire main world, Fifth Page Truth had to die.","Liu Jie, Wen Yu, and Lin Yuan shared a look when they heard what Purple Love said before casting their gazes at Su Yiren.","When Su Yiren saw Lin Yuan looking at her, she bit her lip and was silent for a few moments before she said, “My urgency to seek revenge on Seventh Page War did not just come from my desire to avenge my grandmother, but also because she saw all the lifeforms in the Dark Continent as weeds after taking over.","“Everyone in the imperial court who was linked to the Seven States of Darkness was killed. I’m sure the Radiance Federation also wants to nurture its young experts and provide them with resources. The Seven States of Darkness had become one body but were still seven different entities. Every entity wanted to nurture its outstanding young experts. But the young elites were also killed by Seventh Page War because they had been nurtured by the imperial court.","“This was why I so badly wanted to kill Seventh Page War and put an end to all this. But now that I think back to it, it was too childish of me to put my life on the line just because my Absolute Love Poppy is special.","“Seventh Page War might be human, but with the gap between our powers, I won’t even be able to influence her thoughts, much less take control of her!”","Su Yiren fixed her resolute eyes on Lin Yuan before she continued. “Given what Seventh Page War did, nothing Fifth Page Truth does will be surprising. But I think what we need to find out now is how Fifth Page Truth will benefit by using such a method.”","Lin Yuan rarely held such small meetings.","Everyone present was smart and only brought up important points.","Lin Yuan felt that he could hold more such small meetings to discuss matters in the future."]},{"number":2115,"title":"Chapter 2115 Lin Yuan’s Sense of Powerlessness!","paragraphs":["2115 Lin Yuan’s Sense of Powerlessness!","Su Yiren had made an important point, but it was not going to be easy to dig up any information about Fifth Page Truth.","Even until now, Jin Qianxun had not even seen what Fifth Page War looked like, much less be able to find out information about him. This was despite his position as a main member of a secret aristocratic family.","Lin Yuan only found out the Truth Association’s existence from the Truth Association’s envoy in the Divine Wood Federation.","If the situation was truly as the Mother of Bloodbath guessed, there was no way they could continue waiting for Fifth Page War to come to them because they felt secure in having Purple Love and Begin Lady on their side.","One could only imagine what Fifth Page Truth would do in order to achieve this goal.","Lin Yuan looked at Purple Love and asked, “Auntie Purple, since the Heavenly Family Cottage had interacted with Tower Canon, you must know a fair amount about Fifth Page Truth. Did you guess something, which is why you became so certain after Blood Love spoke of the Offering Witch Dappled Spider?”","The inheritance that the Heavenly Family Cottage had been passing down for a millennium was their wealth. But the most precious of their treasures were the secrets they knew about experts.","If the question had come from anyone else, Purple Love would absolutely not have answered.","However, she saw Lin Yuan as one of her own.","Purple Love started to reveal everything she knew about Fifth Page Truth, “More than two centuries have passed since I last crossed paths with Fifth Page Truth. During our last encounter, he had just started walking down heaven’s path and had not awakened his birth horoscope yet.","“It is very likely that he has now. I can be certain that he is not human. But I am not sure what he actually is. All I know is that he spends all his free time hidden in a ball of flesh. The ball of flesh seems to be an entity of its own and not a precious instrument. My guess is that it is either a sacred source lifeform or linked to Fifth Page Truth’s main body.","“I only know of one of Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeforms. I don’t know its name, but it can control laws. The entire world was composed of laws. Fifth Page Truth can strip laws using this sacred source lifeform. Once he does this, lifeforms with the same type of laws that are within the sacred source lifeform’s range won’t be able to use them.","“Fifth Page Truth managed to touch Jade Sundial because she was in labor and her weak body was unprepared. Another reason was that Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeform had taken control of many fire- and light-type laws. After stripping those laws, Jade Sundial became severely restrained and would have been even if she possessed other types of laws. She was the Heavenly Family Fey that controlled the sun. Thus, her roots had been affected.","“I can only wonder what level of power Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeform has reached. I might be a Heavenly Family Fey and thus cannot be considered in the same way as regular feys, but I am also fearful of Fifth Page Truth. This sacred source lifeform can manipulate laws, which are connected to souls and willpowers. Fifth Page Truth has definitely contracted more than one sacred source lifeform. If Fifth Page Truth intends to sacrifice the Startling Lines Continent’s lifeforms as ingredients, there is a high chance that it is related to a sacred source lifeform I’m unfamiliar with.”","Purple Love paused before continuing. “I am certain of what Blood Love said because Fifth Page Truth’s methods are similar to the Offering Witch Dappled Spider in some ways. The Offering Witch Dappled Spider will first prepare its nest before it poisons other feys with its venom.","“If Fifth Page Truth is really behind the Truth Association, the Truth Association’s appearance has stunted the entire Great Lush Federation’s development. This must mean that he has already started scheming centuries ago.","“Lin Yuan, I remember hearing a conversation between Wen Yu and Luo Lan where Luo Lan mentioned that there were some tribe members who had been left at home because they were far too unsuitable for the long journey. They must be part of the firewood that Fifth Page Truth prepared for his flames. If our guess is correct, he will definitely make a move on those people.”","Lin Yuan’s chest tightened, and he immediately said, “Su Yiren, go and contact Luo Lan and tell her to inform all the tribes to contact their members who were left at home. I want to receive reports immediately! If everything is fine”","Lin Yuan froze at this moment, and a heavy sense of powerlessness overcame him.","He had already silently agreed with the guess that the group had landed on.","The tribe members who had been left at home had to be harboring heart-wrenching sadness as they waited for their family’s safe return. Lin Yuan badly wanted to save them.","Alas, the Iron Hammer Federation was too large.","The Iron Hammer Federation was in the middle of winter. While the tribe members who had relocated to Ta Lei’s city had been fed, those who had been left at home still had to grapple with hunger.","The tribes had given away most of their rations to those who left on the journey.","Hence, expecting these people to head to the border between the Iron Hammer Federation and Divine Wood Federation was unrealistic. Even if Lin Yuan asked them to do so, they would never make it.","In order to ensure their survival, they had to be fetched one by one.","Even if Begin Lady, who had awakened its spirit fire, went to carry out this task, it would take far too long. When it reached the tribes, it also needed time to distribute the food.","However, he still hoped there was a chance to save them and thus immediately instructed Luo Lan to contact them.","If Fifth Page Truth truly tried to make a move on them, he would want to gather them together.","That would be the best time to flee.","As long as the tribe members found a way to flee or hide, the imperial court would be momentarily incapacitated.","Luo Cai had promised that nothing would go wrong with killing the remaining tribe members because he wanted to fulfill Fifth Page Truth’s goal.","There were two imperial guards assigned to every Yellow Gold and above tribe.","There were probably no imperial guards left to spare in the imperial court."]},{"number":2116,"title":"Chapter 2116 Chance for the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen to Evolve!","paragraphs":["2116 Chance for the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen to Evolve!","The servants who were left could not search the entire area because of a lack of manpower.","But as long as they made enough noise, Fifth Page Truth would still come to them.","To Fifth Page Truth, the tens of millions of tribe members in Ta Lei’s territory were no different from a delicious piece of meat.","From what Purple Love said, Su Yiren knew that the situation was critical.","!!","The experience in the Dark Continent had been harrowing, and Su Yiren had watched it all unfold.","Although Su Yiren had no attachment to the Startling Lines Continent, she did not want to see it crumble like the Dark Continent had.","Moreover, ever since she joined Lin Yuan, this was the first time that she was seeing him give her instructions in such an anxious manner.","Luo Lan and Su Yiren were used to communicating through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","In order to relay the information as quickly as possible, Su Yiren did not communicate through the Thoughts Letter Paper, which was the most secure method. Instead, she chose to call, which was the quickest method.","Luo Lan had been leading a team of 500 healing-type spirit qi professionals from the tribes and went around healing the tribe members.","Luo Lan had maintained a good relationship with the leaders of the tribes.","Not long ago, she heard from many tribe members that the king had given the order for all the tribe members to gather at the Freezing Hammer Tribe. Those who could not reach the Freezing Hammer Tribe should gather at the larger tribes nearby.","Luo Cai had already lost all of his authoritative aura. Almost every tribe member saw him as a traitor of the Iron Hammer Federation.","When they received the order from Luo Cai, they complained about him while wondering what he was trying to achieve.","However, none of the tribe leaders disobeyed Luo Cai’s order.","The people left in the tribes who had been unable to fight huddled together so they could better keep warm.","But when she heard what Su Yiren said in the call, Luo Lan immediately became frantic.","Su Yiren did not lie to Luo Lan. Since she was a member of the Astronomical Parliament, Lin Yuan had said that Luo Lan was trustworthy.","Luo Lan could manage the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members perfectly and calmly.","But now, she was in full panic mode.","But Luo Lan knew that under no circumstances could she tell the tribe leaders about this. If they found out, chaos would ensue.","This was because the people who had remained were their loved ones.","Since she could not mention it, she had to find another way to convince the tribe leaders to call their members who had been left at home to pack up quickly and come over.","Although some of them might lose their lives to the harsh winter weather during the journey, it would be better than all of them being slaughtered.","The people who had lived in the Iron Hammer Federation for decades had experience enduring the winter there. These people had the intelligence to help others who were not as experienced to survive.","In spite of her lack of rest, Luo Lan sprang into action.","The small meeting that Lin Yuan called came to an end.","Lin Yuan thought back to how there had been almost no Law Crystals from Myth Breed feys in the Yi family’s treasure vault.","Even the treasure vault of the Yang family, who presided over the imperial court, was greatly lacking in Law Crystals.","Lin Yuan learned from Yi Huailong that the Yang family had a great appetite for Law Crystals and World Crystals. Yet, they had almost none in their treasure vault.","This meant that the Yang family had given all of the World Crystals and Law Crystals they had collected to the Truth Association.","Purple Love had mentioned that Fifth Page Truth had a sacred source lifeform that could manipulate laws. It was likely that all of the Law Crystals and World Crystals had gone to it.","This made Lin Yuan see similarities between Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeform and the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen could also absorb World Crystals and Law Crystals continuously.","However, Lin Yuan did not use his sacred source lifeform to limit others from using their laws. Instead, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen used the laws it absorbed to protect him.","Lin Yuan remembered Morbius saying that if they encountered sacred source lifeforms that were similar to the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen in the future, Morbius could use some of its root power to fuse that sacred source lifeform with the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen and increase the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Stars.","If this was in the past when Morbius’ root power had been weak, Lin Yuan would not have wanted Morbius to help to raise the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Stars and cause it to fall asleep.","But now, for some reason, Morbius had a much larger store of root power.","Morbius was the fey that had Lin Yuan’s heart, and increasing his power would also be beneficial for Morbius.","Lin Yuan had been discussing with Morbius how its root power should be used.","Lin Yuan could easily contract a second sacred source lifeform now. However, it was not easy for him to pick one.","Since he knew how sacred source lifeforms were created, he could guess what abilities the sacred source lifeform would have from the Apostle’s abilities.","Now, Lin Yuan needed to carefully consider his next choice of sacred source lifeform.","But rather than thinking about what his second sacred source lifeform should be, it was more important to Lin Yuan to increase the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Stars.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was currently 4 Stars. A few months had passed, and it had not improved by much, even after all the Law Crystals and World Crystals it had absorbed.","The abilities gained by both of the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s forms had impressed Lin Yuan.","Previously, everyone thought that Lin Yuan had used all of his secret weapons in the fight against Qian Yu. But in actuality, he had not used the new ability that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had gained when it reached 4 Stars.","This new ability had always been Lin Yuan’s secret weapon.","He understood what the strong points of the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s two forms were.","Lin Yuan was looking forward to the new ability that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen would gain when it reached 7 Stars.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s improvement was not as astounding as Lin Yuan’s own amongst the younger generation.","When Lin Yuan attended the Major Federation Meeting, he would be in the same generation as Qian Yu.","Even if Qian Yu’s 7 Stars sacred source lifeform was disregarded, even Gao Feng’s sacred source lifeform had reached 6 Stars. Two years later, Gao Feng’s sacred source lifeform would definitely have reached 7 Stars.","It could be said that increasing the Stars of the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had become the most pressing task Lin Yuan needed to accomplish on the road to increasing his power.","..."]},{"number":2117,"title":"Chapter 2117 Thick Soil City","paragraphs":["2117 Thick Soil City","The giant city built on Ta Lei’s territory had been named Thick Soil City by Lin Yuan.","The soil had to be solid in order for Sky City to float securely in the sky.","For the past day, Luo Lan had done all she could to urge the tribe leaders discreetly.","The tribes were immediately thrown into an entanglement of sorrow and fury.","From the moment they stepped foot into Thick Soil City, the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members started missing home.","The people of the Iron Hammer Federation were very simple and honest.","After any tribe was established, the members were always together, even if the entire tribe needed to move.","Although there were also collateral and direct descendant bloodlines amongst the Platinum tribes, and the direct descendant bloodlines were more elite than the collateral bloodlines, the gap in status was not as large as in the Divine Wood Federation.","The direct and collateral disciples of the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribes all lived together and had close relationships.","The tribe members who managed to survive had just experienced the pain of having to leave their families. But now, they were about to experience the pain of their families dying. How could these people who were already in the depths of despair hold on?","When a person’s emotions were about to bubble over, they needed a way to vent.","The heart-wrenching wails of desperation could be heard all over the Iron Hammer Federation.","However, venting did not do the tribe members any good.","Not even the leaders and Class 4 Creation Masters from the Black Gold tribes had any way of preventing all of this from happening.","The only thing they could do was tell their tribe members who had remained at home to do their best to hide.","The tribe leaders knew what kind of people had been left at home.","It was unknown if these people would be able to flee successfully in the middle of winter. It was not only the humans who had to go hungry but the feys as well.","The young, old, and weak with no combat abilities not only had to survive the cold weather in order to survive in the wild but so did their starving feys.","There was no need for Luo Lan to do anything, and every tribe member in Thick Soil City now hated Luo Cai with every fiber of their being.","While Lin Yuan was talking to Luo Lan, he had clearly told her that he needed faith power.","Lin Yuan had saved the Iron Hammer Federation and rescued the lives of the tens of millions of tribe members who were now living in Thick Soil City.","Luo Lan could not repay the debt she owed Lin Yuan.","Thus, she had advertised what Lin Yuan needed throughout Thick Soil City.","In the moment of crisis, Lin Yuan had given Luo Lan the Soldier Ration Radishes and saved the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members. This was because he wanted to make the Iron Hammer Federation see Luo Lan as a goddess.","He had been successful in doing so.","However, the image of the goddess was still a rung lower than the god that Lin Yuan was seen as.","Thus, Lin Yuan could clearly sense that the dots of light in the shrine were increasing with every second.","The moment one dot of light appeared, it would start to grow rapidly.","Each of these dots of light was already larger than those that Lin Yuan had collected in the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan’s shrine looked different after it had been burned by the spirit fire.","The amount of faith power in the shrine increased continuously and was about to fully occupy the space.","Lin Yuan had a feeling that his shrine was about to undergo another transformation.","He had been confused about the situation within the shrine, but he had a slightly clearer idea about it ever since the last transformation.","Each new glowing dot of light that became stronger and represented an even larger amount of faith power was because Lin Yuan had instructed Begin Lady to transform into a stream of water and killed the Blood Claw Charging Wolf.","The Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members saw Fang Ke as virtually undefeatable. All regular people without power and those who only possessed a small amount of it admired the strong.","However, they could not even begin to fathom the power of this expert who had saved them. To them, he was no different from a god.","Lin Yuan sensed the changes within the shrine as he prepared to face the final battle in the Startling Lines Continent.","According to the information from Jin Qianxun, many of the secret aristocratic families from the Great Lush Federation had already led their experts out in full strength.","The Truth Association had far greater control over the Great Lush Federation than they had over Luo Cai and the Iron Hammer Federation.","If Jin Qianxun had never met Lin Yuan, he would have immediately gone to his brother to contest such a ludicrous decision.","But now, Jin Qianxun saw himself as a bystander.","After all, Lin Yuan had promised to let him take over as the head of the Jin family and for the Jin family to replace the Truth Association as the rulers of the Great Lush Federation.","As such, everything that was happening now was just temporary pain that the Jin family had to endure. No matter how many members of the Jin family lost their lives, Jin Qianxun did not mind as long as it led to a bright future.","Jin Qianxun understood the situation, but his two brothers were completely left in the dark.","Jin Qianxing had become much more subdued after he was slapped by Jin Qianding and dared not act as recklessly as he did before.","But when Jin Qianding gave the order for all to set off, Jin Qianxing had attacked him in order to safeguard the Jin family’s future.","In the end, Jin Qianding ordered his fey to kill Jin Qianxing.","This was not just happening in the Jin family. Any member of a secret aristocratic family who had spoken in opposition to the decision ended up killed.","Killing one as an example to send out a warning to the rest was a tried and tested method.","After they were killed, there were no longer any voices of opposition within the secret aristocratic families.","Jin Qianxun never stopped sending reports to Lin Yuan as he followed Great Lush Federation’s team out.","If the scheme unfolding in the Startling Lines Continent was truly related to helping Fifth Page Truth increase his power, it was likely that Fifth Page Truth would seek Lin Yuan out personally.","Yesterday, Lin Yuan had already instructed Listen, Li Wan, and the rest to flee to the underground palace for safety.","Lin Yuan did not want his subordinates to fall into any harm.","...","Besides people like Lin Yuan and Li Wan, who worked hard directly under him, Lin Yuan also sent word through the Thoughts Letter Paper to Yi Huailu and Yi Huailong."]},{"number":2118,"title":"Chapter 2118 Stop Hiding, Come Out and Fight!","paragraphs":["2118 Stop Hiding, Come Out and Fight!","Yi Huailong was now the joystick that Lin Yuan manipulated to control the Divine Wood Federation.","As long as Yi Huailong was around, Lin Yuan could just let him know of any resources that he needed.","Yi Huailong would never turn down any of Lin Yuan’s requests.","Hence, Yi Huailong was just as important to Lin Yuan as Luo Lan was.","Yi Huailu, who was Sky City’s first living Class 5 Creation Master, was even more important.","When Lin Yuan started building Sky City atop the Floating Island Whale, he intended to assign all jobs that could only be accomplished by Class 5 Creation Master to Yi Huailu.","From a strategic significance standpoint, Yi Huailu was more important than all the resources that the Startling Lines Continent could offer.","Before Lin Yuan left, he had left enough of the Ethereal Jellyfish’s tentacles with Yi Huailu and Yi Huailong. With the Ethereal Jellyfish’s tentacles, Yi Huailong and Yi Huailu could transport themselves all the way to the underground palace.","Currently, the Ethereal Jellyfish had reached Diamond X. As such, each one of its tentacles could transport targets by around a distance of 700 kilometers between two nodes.","Lin Yuan had left hundreds of the tentacles, which was more than enough for Yi Huailong and Yi Huailu to reach the underground palace.","Lin Yuan did not understand Fifth Page Truth’s methods.","Although Begin Lady had set its spirit fire alight, it still could not travel thousands of kilometers to reach the Divine Wood Federation’s imperial court.","Although Little Peach could summon Begin Lady using its bloodline power, the most important thing when facing experts on Fifth Page War’s level was strategy.","Hence, the situation would only be considered safe when Yi Huailu and Yi Huailong arrived at the underground palace.","The two of them had sought refuge in the Hollowed Tamarix tree castle before. This was not the first time that Lin Yuan was providing shelter for them.","The construction of the underground palace was not complete yet.","However, with help from Hu Tian, who had the Scary Claw Rock Bear, and the hundreds of Spirit Craftsmen from Heavenly Craft Pavilion, the construction had entered its final phase.","Hu Quan had already broken through past Class 5 Spirit Craftsman.","If the floating carvings on the walls were preserved, people from centuries and millennia in the future would assume that the underground palace was actually the sacred palace of a god.","Hu Quan had thought too much about the patterns he carved on the walls as there had not been many options for him as a Class 5 Spirit Craftsman.","But everything was different once he became a Class 6 Creation Master.","Although Class 6 Creation Masters could not give souls to their carvings, they could inject emotions.","Because of his abilities as a Class 6 Spirit Craftsman, Yi Huailong and Yi Huailu could see the growth, warmth, and unity of Sky City from the moment they laid eyes on the wall.","Besides the carvings on the wall, Hu Quan had also dug out four large lotus ponds in the four corners of the underground palace. There was one of the Sunlight King Lotus planted in each lotus pond.","Hu Quan asked for Lin Yuan’s help to nurture a large number of the Platinum Spirit-Siphon Goldfish.","The army of Hundred Questions Beasts had tired themselves out nurturing the Platinum Spirit-Siphon Goldfish.","However, with their help, they managed to hand over 200 of the Spirit-Siphon Goldfish to Hu Quan.","Hu Quan had asked Lin Yuan to nurture so many of the Platinum Spirit-Siphon Goldfish because he had embedded various jade-textured wood in the walls.","When the Spirit-Siphon Goldfish released spirit qi, the jade-textured wood would start to glow.","The light from the jade-textured wood was very warm. When it was matched with the light produced by the Sunlight King Lotuses, it would seem as though it was daytime in the underground palace all day.","As the leader of one of the Divine Wood Federation’s veteran elite families, Yi Huailong felt that he had his fair share of experience.","But once he arrived at the underground palace and saw all the furnishings that had been made with jade-textured wood, Yi Huailong felt as though he had actually been a country bumpkin all this while.","After all, these were not regular jade-textured pieces of wood but treasures that almost had 100% purity.","Yi Huailong had only seen such treasures in Sky Creation’s tree castle, where there had been a few pieces of furniture made of jade-textured wood.","The furniture made of jade-textured wood was what removed all suspicion from Yi Huailong and the other disciples of veteran elite families who came to the tree castle to trade with Lin Yuan.","At the time, Yi Huailong assumed that it was just as difficult for Lin Yuan to come across furniture made of jade-textured wood.","Lin Yuan looked at Yi Huailong and said, “If you’re interested in the jade-textured wood, I can give you ten tons of them. The situation in the imperial court should have been settled before you came over, right?”","Yi Huailong was delighted when he heard the first part of what Lin Yuan said. But the second half caused his heart to sink.","“Lord Lin Yuan, I have settled everything in the imperial court. I instructed the Yi family’s younger generation to open a new shelter within the imperial court. As for the members of the veteran elite families, I instructed all of them to stay at home and not go out under any circumstances. If there’s any danger, the safest place for them will be at home where they have the shelters that they built in advance.”","Lin Yuan nodded.","Yi Huailong’s arrangement was the right one. Given the circumstances, this was the best arrangement that could be made.","Lin Yuan was about to speak with Yi Huailu when several masses of powerful aura shot out from the sea of flowers.","Silver Corona was instantly overcome by a sense of helplessness, and it immediately alerted Lin Yuan.","Frankly, there was no need for Silver Corona to alert Lin Yuan as the latter and the rest had already sensed the uncontrolled auras.","The experts had not released their auras in order to locate their enemies, as they could have done so by releasing their spiritual energy. There was no need for them to use such an excessive method.","The incoming experts had done so in order to declare war.","They were standing out in the open and announcing that they had arrived. They were also trying to scream at their enemy to come out of hiding and fight it out."]},{"number":2119,"title":"Chapter 2119 Interested in Silver Corona!","paragraphs":["2119 Interested in Silver Corona!","Lin Yuan was both surprised and happy with the attitude of the Truth Association’s experts.","Lin Yuan was never afraid of an enemy being open.","It was said that an arrow shot from the dark was the hardest to dodge. Lin Yuan was most afraid of enemies who stood in the shadows and carried out their schemes.","If the people from the Truth Association went directly to slaughtering the people in Thick Soil City without even announcing themselves, there was nothing that Lin Yuan could do about it.","Purple Love sensed the auras before she said softly, “Three of the experts have reached Eternal, and one of them has reached advanced Eternal. There shouldn’t be experts of such caliber in the Startling Lines Continent. It looks like there’s no doubt that they are from the Truth Association.","“Fifth Page War’s methods are always bizarre and dominant. He had attacked Jade Sundial with a scheme because he had not been certain if he was her match. He had been afraid that she would give up on giving birth and using her Eternal Heart to die alongside him. Clearly, he doesn’t see us as a real threat. This is good. I will launch a sneak attack on him today just like he did to Jade Sundial.”","Lin Yuan bit his lip lightly.","He could hear the hatred punctuated in each of the words that Purple Love spoke. It could be said that Purple Love resented Fifth Page War to the core.","Otherwise, she would not have to launch a sneak attack on experts who were only Eternal when she had clearly already surpassed Eternal.","Since it was time to fight, Lin Yuan did not intend to hide.","With Purple Love and Begin Lady around, he was confident that he would be able to kill Fifth Page Truth.","Lin Yuan remembered the Moon Empress and Purple Love mentioning that the Eight Pages of Tower Canon were not ranked according to their power.","Since they were both part of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon, the gap in power between First Page Fate and Fifth Page Truth should not be large.","Before Purple Love had awoken her birth horoscope, she had been able to kill First Page Fate while sustaining serious injuries herself.","Now that they had Begin Lady, which had set its spirit fire alight, there would be no issues in eliminating Fifth Page Truth.","Lin Yuan walked out of the underground palace.","Lin Yuan had mentioned that he only needed Purple Love with him to take on the experts from the Truth Association.","But when Lin Yuan started walking out of the underground palace, Wen Yu and Liu Jie did not hesitate to follow him.","To Liu Jie and Wen Yu, it was only natural for them to follow Lin Yuan at such a dangerous moment.","This was why Liu Jie had not hesitated to take the attack on Lin Yuan’s behalf in the evolving water world dimensional rift.","Liu Jie was just as prepared this time.","Wen Yu was ready to use the Dragon Pearl Embryo that Mystic Moon had given her if the situation seemed to be leaning toward the enemy.","After she absorbed the Dragon Pearl Embryo that Mystic Moon had produced, there was now a fraction of Mystic Moon’s bloodline in her body.","She could activate the weak bloodline and sacrifice the Dragon Pearl Embryo in order to channel the energy within to attack an enemy or for defense.","The Dragon Pearl Embryo could not only increase Wen Yu’s power but also act as a life preserver.","When Liu Jie, Wen Yu, and Liu Jie were standing at the entrance of the underground palace, Lin Yuan could sense through Silver Corona that the four figures in the sky were 50 meters diagonally above him.","Clearly, the fog produced by the sea of bone lotus flowers could not block the sight of these four experts from the Truth Association.","The four experts had already arrived at the entrance of the underground palace and were waiting for the people within to show themselves.","Lin Yuan instructed Silver Corona to clear the fog above the sea of flowers.","Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, and Wen Yu looked up to meet four gazes of mocking.","The four experts were of various sizes but were all wearing gray-red robes.","This was not the first time that Lin Yuan was seeing experts wearing gray-red robes.","The people that Yang Hanxian had called out to for help in Sacred Forest City had also been dressed in the same attire.","But it was evident that these four experts were stronger than the people who had come to save Yang Hanxian. Apparently, these people were nearer to the core of the Truth Association.","While the four experts from the Truth Association were looking at them mockingly, Lin Yuan was also observing them.","He did not feel pressured in the slightest by the expressions exhibited by these four experts.","This was unsurprising.","By common knowledge, it was already shocking enough for there to be a beginner Eternal expert in the Startling Lines Continent.","One of the four experts from the Truth Association was advanced Eternal, and there was no way he was bothered in the slightest by the beginner Eternal experts.","However, he had already killed one of the Truth Association’s envoys in Sacred Forest City and obtained the Pilgrimage Corpse Bird as a result. It allowed him to become aware of the existence of a sixth dimensional world.","The four experts from the Truth Association should be acting cautiously at this moment.","Could it be that they did not know what had happened?","At that moment, one of the experts with feet-length hair said with amusement, “Your fairy that can create the sea of bone flowers isn’t bad. If you dissolve your contract with the fairy and give it to me, I can allow one of the two people next to you to live.”","There was no point in sparring tongues with this expert from the Truth Association.","Even if all of them were about to die, there was no way they would reveal the existence of Fifth Page Truth or provide any more information about him.","Although Lin Yuan had Genius and could use Connected Tails to learn what another lifeform was thinking and learn what they knew, Genius was only at Diamond/Fantasy at the moment.","Lin Yuan could instruct Genius to use Connected Tails to forcefully link up with an emperor-class target to look through their memories and knowledge.","However, even if thearch-class and above experts were comatose, Genius would experience resistance from the target’s soul if it tried to use Connected Tails to steal their memories and knowledge.","There was no way that Genius could survive the resistance put up by a soul of an expert that was thearch-class and above.","Lin Yuan not only saw Genius as his fey but also as a member of his family.","Under no circumstances would he risk Genius’ safety."]},{"number":2120,"title":"Chapter 2120 Goddess of Mercy Arrives!","paragraphs":["2120 Goddess of Mercy Arrives!","When Liu Jie and Wen Yu heard what this female expert said, they both looked enraged.","The cruelest thing that a spirit qi professional could do to another spirit qi professional was not to threaten them but to forcefully break their contract with their fey.","Spirit qi professionals would experience backlash when they cut their contracts with their feys. The impact from this was even more serious than if the enemy killed their feys.","Furthermore, when a spirit qi professional dissolved a contract with their fey, it was essentially breaking an important relationship link.","The female expert from the Truth Association not only wanted to steal the fairy that Lin Yuan had contracted but was also trying to hold two of them hostage.","If not for the fact that they knew that they would not be able to defeat this enemy, Wen Yu and Liu Jie would have already attacked.","It would not be suitable for Purple Love to immediately kill the first wave of enemies. This would prevent the Truth Association from sending out more experts in the future.","After he summoned White Speak, Lin Yuan would boost White Speak using faith power and instruct it to fight as hard as it could against the four experts from the Truth Association.","This was the right decision to make.","But before Lin Yuan could summon White Speak, the entire space was immediately filled with rolling waves. Gold and red colors started spreading throughout the water.","The water-elemental energy was so expansive that Lin Yuan thought for a moment that Begin Lady had acted without his permission and attacked.","However, Begin Lady was clearly still attached to his face and had not moved in the slightest.","So, where had the water-elemental energy come from then? Could it have come from the Truth Association’s experts?","Just as Lin Yuan was about to instruct Begin Lady to attack, he felt a familiar aura from the water-elemental energy.","It was the aura of a pure mermaid king bloodline.","Lin Yuan had only felt mermaid king bloodline power from Qian Yu and the Goddess of Mercy.","However, the mermaid king bloodline from Qian Yu had not been this concentrated. Furthermore, he had already been killed by Lin Yuan.","If the person who came was the one Lin Yuan was familiar with, it had to be the Goddess of Mercy.","Lin Yuan did not understand why the Goddess of Mercy had come, but she was definitely more of a foe than a friend in his eyes.","The Goddess of Mercy did not have ties to any of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon.","As such, it was likely that she had come to see him.","Lin Yuan could not be certain what she was plotting, but she had to have a motive for treating him so well.","Just as he guessed, a woman with a gold and red fishtail appeared in the sky.","The woman was holding an umbrella, and a light rain was falling within the umbrella.","The woman’s long red hair was charming, and the spots on her tail looked extremely dignified.","The weaved skirt hung around the fishtail.","Lin Yuan remembered that the Goddess of Mercy liked to expose her perfect figure with whatever she wore.","Yet, her outfit today wrapped her figure up completely.","Once the Goddess of Mercy appeared, she fixed her eyes on Lin Yuan.","She had come to see him.","When she last saw him in the Divine Wood Federation, she had left a mark on his body so she would be able to find him no matter where he was.","Although she already knew that she was about to see him, she could not help but let her mind wander and indulge when she finally did lay eyes on him.","The Mirror God had used his spirit fire to leave two scars on the Goddess of Mercy’s body. They were permanent blemishes on the body she had been proud of","The Mirror God’s insult caused the Goddess of Mercy’s heart to become as dark as the depths of the sea.","When she looked at Lin Yuan now, the Goddess of Mercy felt as though all her troubles had melted away.","But soon, she noticed that there was something wrong with Lin Yuan’s situation.","This change was not due to a change in the purity of the mermaid emperor bloodline power.","The purity of his mermaid emperor bloodline power had clearly increased from the last time she saw him.","The only reason for his bloodline power to be weakened was that the roots had been injured.","The Goddess of Mercy was most afraid of something happening to Lin Yuan.","She had been disappointed countless times before she met him.","It could be said that he was her only hope.","But now that she was in front of Lin Yuan and his mermaid emperor bloodline power, she felt an immense attraction to him.","The four experts next to her were clearly at odds with Lin Yuan. Three of them had reached beginner Immortal while one had reached advanced Immortal.","There was no way that a young man like Lin Yuan could have the power to take on experts of that level.","No matter how outstanding Lin Yuan was, he was still a young man of not even 20 years old.","The Goddess of Mercy was very glad that she came before the battle broke out.","If the four of them attacked Lin Yuan together, the consequences would be unimaginable.","The Goddess of Mercy thought that Lin Yuan was the apple of the Moon Empress’ eye. But now, she no longer thought so.","If the Moon Empress did treasure Lin Yuan that much, why would she allow him to take on such a powerful enemy?","The Goddess of Mercy did not think of what could have happened for Lin Yuan to end up taking on such a powerful enemy but immediately started blaming the Moon Empress.","The four experts from the Truth Association had not expected such a mighty expert to arrive.","The Goddess of Mercy was at the height of her fury and did not try to cover her aura at all.","The female expert who had threatened Lin Yuan said to the Goddess of Mercy gingerly, “Are you the Goddess of Mercy from the Freedom Federation? We are members of the Truth Association, a native faction of the Startling Lines Continent. We belong to Tower Canon and are under Fifth Page War. We are here on a task from Fifth Page War to kill the faction that has been ruining Fifth Page War’s plans in the Startling Lines Continent.”","...","The female expert from the Truth Association spoke to the Goddess of Mercy in a completely different tone than she had taken with Lin Yuan.","It was clear that she had recognized the Goddess of Mercy.","The Goddess of Mercy was one of the Freedom Federation’s members of royalty, and the Truth Association could not afford to get on the wrong side of the Freedom Federation.","Not even Fifth Page Truth dared to make an enemy of the entire Freedom Federation.","Furthermore, the Goddess of Mercy’s bad temper was famous far and wide.","It was unlikely that Fifth Page Truth would make an enemy out of her even if she ended up killing all of them there and now. So, if they died at that moment, their deaths would be in vain!"]},{"number":2121,"title":"Chapter 2121 Blue Sail and Sailfish!","paragraphs":["2121 Blue Sail and Sailfish!","The female expert from the Truth Association had introduced them because she hoped that the Goddess of Mercy would decide not to cause trouble for them on account of Tower Canon and Fifth Page Truth.","Fifth Page Truth did not want to make an enemy out of the Goddess of Mercy, and it was likely that the feeling was mutual.","The stronger the expert, the less willing they would be to enrage a powerful enemy, lest they bring about undesirable consequences on themselves.","However, the female expert did not expect her words to not only fail to achieve her desired effect but to even have the opposite effect.","The Goddess of Mercy was the most afraid of something happening to Lin Yuan.","However, the female expert said that she wanted to kill Lin Yuan.","The Goddess of Mercy was relieved that she had arrived in time. If she had been slightly later, he would have been killed by these experts who Fifth Page Truth had sent.","Others might be afraid of Fifth Page Truth, but the Goddess of Mercy was not.","The Freedom Federation had deep ties with Tower Canon.","The Goddess of Mercy was well aware of the capabilities of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon.","She had also interacted with Fifth Page Truth before. The impression she had was that Fifth Page Truth was no match for her.","Even if Fifth Page Truth was stronger than her, she would still fly into a rage and attack him if he killed Lin Yuan.","The Goddess of Mercy not only wanted to kill these four experts but wanted to claim Fifth Page Truth’s life as well.","Since Fifth Page Truth wanted to lay a hand on Lin Yuan, her appearance must have ruined his plan.","In the future, he would continue coming after Lin Yuan.","The only sustainable solution was to kill Fifth Page Truth.","The Goddess of Mercy had decided that she would use the lives of these pathetic four experts to force Fifth Page Truth out.","Once he appeared, she would kill him even if it meant she ended up with injured roots.","She could recuperate and recover her roots. Thus, that was preferable to Lin Yuan forever being under threat from Fifth Page Truth.","The Goddess of Mercy waved her hand, and a girl with long horns and long light green hair that resembled kelp appeared in front of her.","The Goddess of Mercy swished her fishtail, and water elements formed a towering wave in the sky.","“Blue Sail, eliminate the three weaklings! I will handle the stronger one myself!”","Feys and their contractors could influence each others’ feelings.","With an owner like the Goddess of Mercy, her feys were all brutal and ferocious.","The Goddess of Mercy rarely used Blue Sail.","Blue Sail flipped her kelp-like hair and let out a peal of laughter that resembled twinkling bells.","The long horns on her head gleamed uncannily, and the color deepened continuously.","Blue Sail did not move immediately after receiving the order from the Goddess of Mercy.","Instead, it released its aura to give the four members of the Truth Association time to prepare.","The Goddess of Mercy did not use Blue Sail often.","As a Class 5 Creation Master, the Goddess of Mercy had still provided Blue Sail with the best nurturing.","Lin Yuan did not expect the Goddess of Mercy to attack the four Truth Association members immediately upon arrival.","Purple Love was a Heavenly Family Fey and could hide within the constellations.","If Purple Love did not do anything to affect the situation, it would be difficult for the Goddess of Mercy to notice her presence.","The Goddess of Mercy had no idea that Lin Yuan had come prepared.","Begin Lady sensed the Goddess of Mercy and the light green-haired girl she had summoned before it immediately communicated with Lin Yuan through its soul to tell him about the girl he could not use True Data to sense. This allowed him to find out that it was a pinnacle Eternal fey.","The four experts from the Truth Association had not expected the Goddess of Mercy to attack them without hesitation after she found out who they were.","Four of them summoned all of their feys.","The weakest of their feys had reached Creation Breed while the strongest had reached Eternal. All of them were considered magnificent treasures in the Startling Lines Continent and could turn the tide of a federation.","But now, even if they were Eternal feys that had activated their Eternal Hearts, they were no match for the long light green-haired girl.","This allowed Lin Yuan to learn of the huge gaps in power between the 12 sublevels of Eternal.","The Goddess of Mercy was a Class 5 Creation Master and had her pick of the best feys.","It was likely that her feys could roll grades, which was why it was able to cause such a stir with one attack.","While the sailfish shadow was moving back and forth, it let out a loud wail. The wail was as deep as an ocean.","Right after the wail, silver scales appeared all over the sailfish’s shadow.","The silver scales were not just for show.","There was no way that the Creation Breed and Immortal Breed feys could evade the attack from the sailfish shadow.","However, the three beginner Eternal feys that had activated their Eternal Hearts were able to avoid being pierced through by the sailfish shadow.","The silver scales on the sailfish shadow were like files. If the beginner Eternal feys made contact with it, they would end up bloody and scratched up.","The silver scales could not only cause physical damage but also had cursing effects.","The wounds would become infected and start to smell and cause the entire body to slow down.","The experts from the Truth Association did not have any time to react before the sailfish shadow flipped over and pierced through the three Eternal feys that had been cursed. The three Eternal feys were immediately split into two.","The blood from the three feys rained down on the sea of Bone Lotus Flowers.","This was a big gift to Silver Corona.","...","Silver Corona raised its small head and looked longingly at Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan was about to turn Silver Corona down but eventually nodded vexedly."]},{"number":2122,"title":"Chapter 2122 What Pride Does Fifth Page Truth Have With Me Here?","paragraphs":["2122 What Pride Does Fifth Page Truth Have With Me Here?","Normally, the Eternal feys should belong to the Goddess of Mercy after she had killed them.","If Silver Corona was at Gold or Silver grade, it would not be able to take in such an opportunity.","But if Silver Corona could absorb the flesh and souls of Eternal feys, it had a high chance of being able to evolve to Myth Breed. More importantly, there was also a high chance it would enable Silver Corona’s fairy bloodline to break through.","Evolving their bloodline was very important to any fairy.","The relationship between Lin Yuan and the Goddess of Mercy was special.","After all, Lin Yuan would not instruct Silver Corona to touch the Eternal feys’ Eternal Hearts.","Silver Corona saw Lin Yuan nodding and excitedly nudged his face.","It was so riled up with excitement that the entire sea of bone lotus flowers started to shake.","Soon, Silver Corona lay down calmly in Lin Yuan’s arms and fell asleep.","High-grade feys usually experienced a bloodline breakthrough when they were at their weakest. Thus, they always found a safe environment before they let their guard down.","Silver Corona felt that there was no place safer than in Lin Yuan’s arms.","Lin Yuan silently held Silver Corona and waited for the moment it opened its eyes.","If Silver Corona could gain its fourth pair of wings before it evolved to Myth Breed, it would become a legend in the history of fairies, just like Red Thorn was.","After the girl with long light green hair that the Goddess of Mercy had summoned killed the Creation Breed, Immortal Breed, and three beginner Eternal feys as well as their contractors, it returned to stand dutifully by the Goddess of Mercy’s side.","Its gaze landed on Lin Yuan.","As a fey that the Goddess of Mercy had contracted, the girl with long light green hair could sense the intense emotions the Goddess of Mercy felt for him.","When a contractor had many feys, the feys would compete amongst themselves for favor from the contractor. This was because the favored feys always received more resources than the others.","The girl with light green hair thought darkly, Anyone who can help the Goddess of Mercy obtain Lin Yuan will definitely become the Goddess of Mercy’s most beloved fey.","The last expert from the Truth Association who was left looked at the Goddess of Mercy with uncontrollable fury and bellowed, “Goddess of Mercy, can’t you leave some of Fifth Page Truth’s pride intact?”","The Goddess of Mercy’s anger had been lessened slightly after the three experts from the Truth Association were killed.","But when she heard the question from the last expert, her rage exploded again.","She forcefully waved her hand in the direction of the expert, and the water-elemental energy formed a palm that sailed toward the expert.","The expert wanted to dodge the slap, but his body had been frozen by the Goddess of Mercy.","The palm made of water-elemental energy hit the expert from the Truth Association’s face and left him in utter pieces.","The expert with an advanced Eternal fey was very respected in the Truth Association. There was no way he could take such humiliation lying down.","The Goddess of Mercy’s anger had not decreased in the slightest after the slap.","Soon, another palm formed from water-elemental energy appeared in the sky. It sailed towards the expert from the Truth Association like a hurricane.","While she attacked, she sneered, “What pride does Fifth Page Truth have with me around? Anyone who touches one of my people deserves to die!”","The Goddess of Mercy’s eyes flashed, and she looked at the place behind the expert from the Truth Association.","It saw that a throne made of bones had suddenly appeared.","A large ball of flesh was pulsating on the throne made of bones. It looked as though a living fetus was growing within it.","“Goddess of Mercy, who is one of your people? Can it be that you’re referring to the young man below you? Hehe, this is so interesting! I heard from Second Page Revival that you have been urgently collecting the mermaid bloodline for the past few years. Because of this, you even got in a conflict with the God of Fools and the Mirror God. Aren’t you interested in this young man and calling him one of your people because of the mermaid bloodline within him? But is the young man aware of this?”","Fifth Page Truth had been guessing Lin Yuan’s identity and the faction he came from.","Fifth Page Truth had spent the past few decades trying to evolve his sacred source lifeform, the Divine Order Evil Fetus, to 11 Stars. As such, he was unaware of events that took place in the outside world and had not interacted much with the other Eight Pages of Tower Canon either.","Although there were at least four of the Eight Pages who knew of Lin Yuan’s background, Fifth Page Truth had been completely left out of the loop.","With the Goddess of Mercy’s support, it was no wonder that this young man had the confidence to act as he pleased and stir up as much trouble as he wanted in the Startling Lines Continent.","Fifth Page Truth’s words caused the Goddess of Mercy’s expression to change in an instant.","He had revealed her secret.","There was sure to be trouble if the other members of royalty from the Freedom Federation found out about this.","Both the Mirror God and the God of Fools were trying to get in her way.","Once they found out, it was likely that they would try to kill Lin Yuan.","In the past, the Goddess of Mercy had not been afraid of the Mirror God.","But now that the Mirror God had set his spirit fire alight, the Goddess of Mercy no longer had the capabilities to stand up to him.","Rather than this matter spreading far and wide, the Goddess of Mercy was only afraid of Lin Yuan finding out.","Even if she could not stop the God of Fools and Mirror God from laying a hand on Lin Yuan, he should be safe as long as he remained in the Radiance Federation where that old man was.","But once Lin Yuan found out her motive, not only would she be unable to gain his affection, but the negative emotions he felt towards her might increase.","The Goddess of Mercy, who was in a middle of a stand-off with Fifth Page Truth, felt her imposing aura weaken.","Her eyes naturally drifted to Lin Yuan.","He had actually guessed long ago that the Goddess of Mercy had a motive involving him and that her intentions were likely related to the mermaid bloodline.","Fifth Page Truth’s words and the Goddess of Mercy’s reaction had only confirmed these.","When the Goddess of Mercy’s loftiness diminished, a crack appeared on the ball of flesh on the throne of bones.","A young boy with chestnut-colored hair stepped out from the crack. He was holding a staff made of bones."]},{"number":2123,"title":"Chapter 2123 It’s Time for the Coronation, Law Church!","paragraphs":["2123 It’s Time for the Coronation, Law Church!","At the center of the staff was a crystal ball the size of an infant’s fist, and within the crystal ball were the auras of various laws.","Once Fifth Page Truth appeared, he raised the staff and shook it gently at the sky, saying in a chillingly sonorous voice, “It’s time for the coronation, Law Church!”","There were tens of thousands of torches in the sky, each of them emanating the aura of a law.","Six statues formed in the territory, each the image of a nun that was dressed in long robes.","The statues assembled the laws within the torches and affected the entire territory.","After he activated his sacred source lifeform, the Law Staff’s ability Law Church, a wicked smile appeared on Fifth Page Truth’s face.","The wicked smile on such an innocent boyish face looked extremely creepy.","“Goddess of Mercy, the devil and fey you contracted are related to the elements. My sacred source lifeform is the most capable of countering people like you. The person you’re interested in ruined my plan. Because of him, I won’t be able to achieve my goal even if I forcefully carry on with the plan. But if I’m able to refine you, I will not only be able to achieve my goal but will also allow my collection of laws to become enriched. Goddess of Mercy, don’t assume that you’re the only one who has awakened your birth horoscope.”","Fifth Page Truth’s words caused the Goddess of Mercy’s expression to turn solemn.","The Goddess of Mercy was not afraid of Fifth Page Truth. Fifth Page Truth only had a rough understanding of her power. This was just like how the Goddess of Mercy only knew that Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeform could control laws.","They would not find out about each other’s secret weapons unless they crossed swords.","Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeform’s ability had astonished the Goddess of Mercy. However, the Goddess of Mercy was not helpless like Fifth Page Truth had said.","The Goddess of Mercy was now worried about Lin Yuan’s safety.","Regardless of what Lin Yuan thought of her after hearing what Fifth Page Truth said, she would save him no matter what.","Fifth Page Truth was very despicable.","When Fifth Page Truth dealt with her, he would try to distract her and use a sneak attack to try and kill Lin Yuan.","The Goddess of Mercy could fight on par with Fifth Page Truth.","But with Lin Yuan present, she would be at a disadvantage when having to protect him at the same time.","This might even allow Fifth Page Truth to catch the opportunity to deal her a deadly hand.","The Goddess of Mercy did not intend to bother with what Fifth Page Truth said. She was going to use her most vicious attacks against Fifth Page Truth.","She could only occupy Fifth Page Truth if she released an endless barrage of fierce attacks, thereby protecting Lin Yuan.","Crimson red devil tattoos appeared all over the Goddess of Mercy’s beautiful face as four curved horns curled out from her red hair.","Two of the four horns intertwined at the back of her head while the other two stretched toward the sky.","The gold and red patterns made it appear as though the black horns were stained with blood.","The nails on the Goddess of Mercy’s hands also started to grow longer, and they were so red that it made it seem as though the world had lost all of its colors.","The red of the Goddess of Mercy’s nails suppressed even the brilliance from various laws.","Her fishtail also started growing until it looked more like a snake’s tail.","The already large tail started to grow wider and red spikes grew out from the two sides of the fishtail. When the Goddess of Mercy swished her tail, she resembled a poisonous snake flicking its tongue.","After the Goddess of Mercy transformed, she pointed at Fifth Page Truth and activated her higher devil.","A black and red silhouette appeared behind the Goddess of Mercy. The silhouette seemed to be hiding an extremely evil lifeform.","But the envious eyes of a femme fatale could be seen in the silhouette.","Black blood dripped out from the black eyes.","It was as though an innocent young girl had seen something which caused envy to bloom within her and was instantly turning into a monster.","Fifth Page Truth noticed that the Law Staff’s ability Law Church was still in effect,","Yet, once the crying silhouette appeared behind the Goddess of Mercy, Fifth Page war immediately lost his connection to the Law Staff.","Fifth Page Truth was now no longer able to take on the Goddess of Mercy.","When Fifth Page Truth appeared, the Goddess of Mercy had recalled the young girl with light green hair that she had used to kill the experts from the Truth Association. This was because a pinnacle Eternal fey would be far from enough to take on an opponent like Fifth Page Truth.","The Goddess of Mercy did not want a fey she had put a lot of effort into nurturing to die, even if it was not one of her main feys, as it would still result in her spiritual energy experiencing backlash.","This could give Fifth Page Truth the chance to trip her up.","When she fused with her devil and used her devil abilities, she had summoned the two feys that had surpassed Eternal.","The two main feys who the Goddess of Mercy had summoned had maintained human form and had similar appearances. Both had long black hair that reached their waists and red eyes. They were also wearing purple-red leather armor and holding long spears made of dark red water.","When feys were in human form, their features would not stand out as much as when they were feys, but it was still clear that they were different from the human form.","Given the similar appearances of these two feys, it was likely that they were the same type of fey and that they had undergone the same type of mutation during their nurturing process.","Lin Yuan was not afraid at all of Fifth Page Truth, who was determined to kill him.","Lin Yuan was more focused on the two main feys that the Goddess of Mercy had summoned.","Normally, a spirit qi professional would not nurture two of the same type of fey unless they had complementary abilities. An example was Lu Pinru, who had nurtured numerous of the Glowing Silkworm Weavers."]},{"number":2124,"title":"Chapter 2124 Constellation Decree!","paragraphs":["2124 Constellation Decree!","It was likely that these two similar feys were able to work very well in tandem.","From the moment the two feys appeared, they used their long spears to attack Fifth Page Truth.","The Goddess of Mercy’s nails scratched at Fifth Page Truth’s face.","With such ferocious oncoming attacks, Fifth Page Truth hurriedly retreated back into the ball of flesh.","As a result, the Goddess of Mercy’s nails made contact with the pulsating ball of flesh instead.","Five bloody streaks were left on the surface of the ball of flesh.","The Goddess of Mercy’s two feys raised the spears they were holding and plunged them into the ball of flesh.","The two long spears started to twist within the ball of flesh, letting out the sounds of tendons and bones being sliced through.","The Goddess of Mercy did not stop her attacks there and continued to slash violently at the surface of the ball of flesh.","It also used its snake-like tail to inject poison into the ball of flesh.","The ball of flesh was left battered and injured all over. There were even some holes in parts of it, revealing Fifth Page Truth within.","Fifth Page Truth had not expected the Goddess of Mercy to launch such a barrage of attacks on him, nor had he expected her to be able to lock his sacred source lifeform by fusing with her devil.","Luckily, he was sufficiently strong. Otherwise, he would have sustained serious injuries from the Goddess of Mercy’s full-powered attacks.","Currently, it seemed as though Fifth Page Truth had no way of countering the Goddess of Mercy’s attacks.","But the longer she attacked Fifth Page Truth, the grimmer her expression became.","Fifth Page Truth’s defensive abilities surpassed the Goddess of Mercy’s expectations.","The Goddess of Mercy was certain that Fifth Page Truth was unaware of what her devil ability after fusing with her higher devil was. Because of this, she was able to take him by surprise.","However, her attacks had only resulted in him sustaining light injuries.","It was clear that Fifth Page Truth had acclimated to her attacks.","As her feys continued to attack him, she sensed that the surface of the ball of flesh had released a large amount of absorption power that had consumed a portion of her energy to recover itself.","A minute had passed since she started leading her feys in the attack.","When she fused with her higher devil and used the higher devil ability, her sacred source lifeform would only be able to use its ability for almost six minutes.","Thus, there was a high chance that she would fail to break through Fifth Page Truth’s defenses.","At that time, she would be restrained by Fifth Page Truth’s Law Staff.","With this thought, the Goddess of Mercy’s heart sank, and she yelled, “Mad Leaving and Mad Return, inject your birth horoscope into the Eternal Heart and activate it. Sacrifice some things to use Constellation Decree.”","The two spear-holding girls released a tsunami of aura toward Fifth Page Truth and changed into their fey forms.","When Lin Yuan saw their fey forms, he immediately knew what their types were.","Both of them now had long and slender fishtails.","From the moment they transformed, they summoned all of the water-elemental energy around them.","The inflated blood aura was proof that these two feys were Blood Ritual Witch Fishes which were rarer than mermaids.","There was a rumor that the Goddess of Mercy had gotten her hands on the Blood Ritual Witch Fish.","Lin Yuan had not expected the Goddess of Mercy to have nurtured the two Blood Ritual Witch Fishes to such an extent. Both had already unlocked their birth horoscopes.","Lin Yuan had given Bei Xu the Blood Ritual Witch Fish to contract. He was aware that the Blood Ritual Witch Fish was full of potential but had not expected its potential to be so outstanding.","The Blood Ritual Witch Fish needed to absorb its contractor’s blood to grow.","The Jasmine Lily had used the Mountain Jade Imprint on Bei Xu. Thus, it could now recover Bei Xu’s vitality even if they were thousands of miles apart.","This allowed Blood Ritual Witch Fish to have endless blood energy to supply the Blood Ritual Witch Fish to grow quickly.","Now that Bu Po had become a reserve disciple of the Spirit Mother, he had clearly left Bei Xu in the dust.","But with the Blood Ritual Witch Fish, it was possible for Bei Xu to one day surpass Bu Po.","When the Goddess of Mercy’s two Blood Ritual Witch Fishes turned back into fey form and summoned their Eternal Hearts, Fifth Page Truth bellowed from within the ball of flesh, “Goddess of Mercy, you’re crazy! You actually instructed your feys to use Constellation Decree? Don’t you know that injecting the birth horoscope into the Eternal Heart will cause unimaginable damage to a fey?”","The Goddess of Mercy did not react at all to what Fifth Page Truth said. She did not do as he said to stop the two Blood Ritual Witch Fishes from injecting their birth horoscopes into their Eternal Hearts.","“Fifth Page Truth, you haven’t summoned a fey yet. It must be true that you aren’t human! A fey will indeed sustain damage when it injects its birth horoscope into its Eternal Heart, but the injury can be healed with time! The damage won’t be irreparable! Spending time to heal my feys is a very worthy price in exchange for killing you.”","The two Blood Ritual Witch Fishes could clearly be seen thrashing rapidly within the two Eternal Hearts.","Suddenly, the lustrous energy within the two Blood Ritual Witch Fishes emerged from their heads.","Two dice-shaped objects the color of blood and with the image of the Blood Ritual Witch Fish carved on each of them shot out from the Blood Ritual Witch Fishes’ foreheads and into the Eternal Hearts.","The Eternal Hearts melted into fluids that were absorbed by the dice-shaped objects.","At that instant, the two Blood Ritual Witch Fishes seemed to be connected.","Purple Love looked at the Goddess of Mercy in shock before glancing back at Lin Yuan.","She was very surprised to see the Goddess of Mercy step in to help Lin Yuan.","Purple Love knew how tenuous the relationship between the Radiance Federation and Freedom Federation was.","However, she had not expected the Goddess of Mercy to go so far for Lin Yuan, to the point that she was willing to let two of her feys inject their birth horoscopes into their Eternal Hearts to produce the spirit-harming Constellation Decree."]},{"number":2125,"title":"Chapter 2125 The Divine Order Evil Fetus Shatters!","paragraphs":["2125 The Divine Order Evil Fetus Shatters!","Feys that used Constellation Decree could heal after recuperation.","But if their spirits were damaged, they would not be able to set their spirit fires alight again in the future.","Purple Love saw Lin Yuan as her junior and was also grateful to him.","Given Lin Yuan’s current level, there was no way he knew the cost of using Constellation Decree.","By doing something so monumental, Lin Yuan now owed the Goddess of Mercy a big favor.","However, this might not be a good thing for Lin Yuan.","If Purple Love joined forces with the Goddess of Mercy, it would not be difficult to take down Fifth Page Truth. There was no need to pay such a large price.","Purple Love did not say anything to Lin Yuan in advance.","If she tried to communicate with him now, it would definitely catch the attention of Fifth Page Truth.","This would prevent her from launching a sneak attack on Fifth Page Truth.","Presently, both of the Goddess of Mercy’s feys had injected their birth horoscopes into their Eternal Hearts, but they had not triggered the constellations with their spirit to unleash Constellation Decree. There was still hope to turn back.","When the Goddess of Mercy saw her, she would know that the situation was advantageous. Then, she would not allow her two feys to sacrifice their futures to continue and continue on to unleash Constellation Decree.","Purple Love used her ability as a Heavenly Family Fey to call out to the constellations.","Although it was still daytime, the constellations illuminated the sky with a faint glow.","As a result, the constellations now shared the same sky as the sun.","Purple Love was always skilled at making use of spatial energy.","She appeared behind Fifth Page Truth’s ball of flesh, and 12 tails sprouted from behind her.","They slammed onto the ball of flesh like they were nails hammering into a wall.","The attack from the tails left clear marks on the ball of flesh.","Although the ball of flesh had terrifying recovery abilities, it could not immediately recover the parts that had been damaged by the tails.","Next, the tails went on to pierce the ball of flesh.","Under the constant attack from the tails, the ball of flesh was sundered, revealing Fifth Page War who was hiding within.","Purple Love glared at Fifth Page Truth with furious hatred as all the constellation power gathered on her body","This was when she released a meteor of fox fire.","Long ago, Purple Love had used this method to claim First Page Fate’s life.","Fifth Page Truth had not sensed Purple Love’s existence.","Purple Love was a Heavenly Family Fey, a lifeform most affiliated with nature in the world.","If Purple Love wanted to hide, Fifth Page Truth would have to plow through the area using his spiritual energy to search for her. Otherwise, there was no way he would detect her presence.","When Fifth Page Truth attacked Jade Sundial, he was most afraid of bringing about retribution from the Heavenly Family Cottage.","This was why he had been hiding for all these years.","Purple Love’s attack allowed Fifth Page Truth to know that he would have to give up the Divine Order Evil Fetus as a shield if he wanted to survive.","After the Goddess of Mercy appeared, she shot a look at Lin Yuan.","The Goddess of Mercy had heard that Heavenly Family Cottage and the Radiance Federation had formed an alliance and knew there was a blood grudge between Heavenly Family Cottage and Fifth Page Truth.","The Goddess of Mercy saw Lin Yuan as a talented and capable young man. A person like him should not be exposed to danger.","It seemed that Lin Yuan dared to take on Fifth Page Truth because he had Purple Love protecting him from the shadows.","The Goddess of Mercy had instructed the two Blood Ritual Witch Fishes to inject their blood horoscopes into the Eternal Heart and to use Constellation Decree in order to protect Lin Yuan and prevent Fifth Page Truth from attacking him.","With this thought, the Goddess of Mercy stopped the two Blood Ritual Witch Fishes from using Constellation Decree.","Instead, she ordered them to attack Fifth Page Truth at the same time that Purple Love did.","The Blood Ritual Witch Fishes looked at Purple Love with relief as happiness engulfed them.","They could not disobey the Goddess of Mercy’s orders because they were her feys. But frankly, they were against the order.","If the Goddess of Mercy was in danger, the two of them would not mind using Constellation Decree.","But the Goddess of Mercy was trying to save a young lad who she had not even had much interaction with.","Any fey that had awakened its birth horoscope wanted to use its spirit to set its spirit fire alight and enter a new world.","But thankfully, the Goddess of Mercy did not use her sacred source lifeform when instructing the two Blood Ritual Witch Fishes to attack.","The Goddess of Mercy’s sacred source lifeform was defense-type and could not boost her combat abilities.","When she had the advantage in the fight against Fifth Page Truth, there was no need for her to use her sacred source lifeform.","The Goddess of Mercy used her second higher devil ability against Fifth Page Truth, Envy Deepening, on the ball of flesh.","When a target was afflicted by Envy Deepening, the damage sustained by the lifeforms around the target would also increase.","The Goddess of Mercy was afraid that Fifth Page Truth was not dead yet and triggered a violent explosion in the sky.","The Goddess of Mercy intentionally blocked the sea of Bone Lotus Flowers from the explosion in order to get on Lin Yuan’s good side and prevent him from getting a negative impression of her because of what Fifth Page Truth had said.","She also instructed her two main feys to block the energy ripples in the direction of Thick Soil City.","If the ripples of a battle between experts that were beyond Immortal reached Thick Soil City, half of the city would crumble no matter how strongly it was fortified.","If that happened, countless of the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members would die in Thick Soil City.","Both Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy thought that this attack would be enough to put an end to Fifth Page Truth.","...","But it did not take long for them to realize that something was wrong.","This was because the effects of the Law Staff’s ability Law Church had not dissipated yet.","Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy hurriedly looked towards where Fifth Page Truth had been.","This was when they saw Fifth Page Truth clutching his head with both hands as though he was in a wild fit.","Fifth Page Truth’s surroundings were filled with the sounds of pieces of flesh falling to the ground.","It was clear that the pieces of flesh did not come from the ball of flesh around Fifth Page Truth.","Fifth Page Truth endured his violent fit and agony as he started to laugh.","His laughter seemed to be mixed with an inexplicable creepiness.","“You not only ruined my plan to evolve the Divine Order Evil Fetus but even destroyed the Divine Order Evil Fetus itself. That young man must be very important to the two of you!”"]},{"number":2126,"title":"Chapter 2126 The Trapped Lin Yuan!","paragraphs":["2126 The Trapped Lin Yuan!","Fifth Page Truth’s creepy voice paused and suddenly turned ear-piercingly shrill.","“Watch as how I destroy two of you for breaking my sacred source lifeform!”","While he spoke, Fifth Page Truth raised the Law Staff and activated the ability it had gained when it reached 10 Stars, Ruling Settlement.","Neither Purple Love nor the Goddess of Mercy had expected Fifth Page Truth to not only survive their combined attack but also emerge unscathed.","Fifth Page Truth’s defensive abilities had exceeded both of their expectations.","But when they sensed the aura of the falling fragments around Fifth Page Truth, both of them realized that Fifth Page Truth had sacrificed a pinnacle 10 Stars sacred source lifeform to block the attack.","He had essentially cut off his wrist to save his arm.","As a result, Fifth Page Truth’s soul and potential had both taken excruciating hits.","After a spirit qi professional’s fey died, they might have the chance to recover their spiritual energy and contract another fey. They would not be seriously affected.","However, a sacred source lifeform was linked to the contractor’s soul. Once they died, a part of the contractor’s soul would leave with it, and there was no way of making up for the loss.","At this moment, Fifth Page Truth’s expression could only be described as fiercely sinister.","Fifth Page Truth had swapped out the Divine Order Evil Fetus for the Law Staff as his main sacred source lifeform a few decades ago.","The Divine Order Evil Fetus allowed Fifth Page Truth to find a way to live forever using flesh.","In order to evolve the Divine Order Evil Fetus to 11 Stars, Fifth Page Truth had begun plotting a few decades ago.","He had even built the Truth Association and taken control of the Startling Lines Continent for this.","Yet today, the plan that had been in the works for decades had been ruined, and the Divine Order Evil Fetus had been destroyed.","From the moment that the Divine Order Evil Fetus was destroyed, Fifth Page Truth knew that he would lose his position as the Fifth Page of Tower Canon.","His power had not been outstanding amongst the Eight Pages to start with.","Now, he had also lost a pinnacle 10 Stars sacred source lifeform.","If the other Pages found out, the first to take a dig at him would be Third Page Eternal Sin.","Fifth Page Truth placed all the blame and object of his fury on Lin Yuan.","This was because he was no match for Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy.","If Fifth Page Truth was facing either Purple Love or the Goddess of Mercy alone, he would have been able to grievously injure them by using the special abilities of the Law Staff.","The victor would not have been as clear as it was now.","But now that Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy were ganging up on him, they would surely help out one another if any was in trouble.","Given the circumstances, he stood no chance of victory.","Furthermore, Lin Yuan was the cause of this entire incident.","He was the one who had come to the Startling Lines Continent and started targeting the Truth Association. He was the reason that Fifth Page War was in the predicament that he was facing now.","Otherwise, he could have remained safely hidden, and there was no way that Purple Love would have been able to find him.","By tracing the cause back to Lin Yuan, Fifth Page Truth found his target to vent on.","Weren’t both the Goddess of Mercy and Purple Love very concerned about Lin Yuan?","Fifth Page Truth had just experienced loss in the destruction of the Divine Order Evil Fetus.","If the Goddess of Mercy and Purple Love watched Lin Yuan die and could not do anything to stop it, they would feel the same way that Fifth Page Truth was feeling at that moment.","When Fifth Page Truth instructed the Law Staff to use Ruling Settlement, the fire that was produced by setting alight all the laws shot into the sky, creating pillars of fire.","Tens of thousands of colored pillars of fire speared the sky.","All the laws had been triggered to their maximum extent.","The nuns continuously plucked strings of laws from the flaming pillars and swiftly weaved them into a world comprised of laws.","The weaved world of laws encapsulated Lin Yuan and Fifth Page Truth within.","The Goddess of Mercy and Purple Love’s expressions changed when they saw what had happened.","Neither of them had expected the Law Staff to have such an ability.","Now that the small world had closed around Lin Yuan and Fifth Page Truth, it meant that Lin Yuan now had to take Fifth Page Truth on by himself.","Both of them could try to break in, but the attacks might affect the interior of the world and hit not just Fifth Page Truth but Lin Yuan as well.","Unless Lin Yuan was able to kill Fifth Page Truth within the miniature world, Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy could not even attempt to break it.","Liu Jie and Wen Yu’s expressions had changed at the same time that Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy’s did.","They knew that Lin Yuan had protection with him in the form of Begin Lady.","Although they did not know the exact extent of Begin Lady’s power, they had heard about it from Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan was going to have to take Fifth Page Truth on by himself now.","Both of them knew that Lin Yuan was not the type to boast, but no one was more important than Lin Yuan to them. They could not help but be filled with worry for him.","While the two of them knew that Lin Yuan had a secret weapon with him when he took on Fifth Page Truth, the Goddess of Mercy and Purple Love were completely unaware.","The two experts who had already awakened their birth horoscopes were so worried that they faltered in their demeanors.","The Goddess of Mercy had even betrayed Lin Yuan for the sake of the Freedom Federation.","At first, her reasons had been purely selfish.","If Lin Yuan did not possess the mermaid emperor bloodline and allowed the Goddess of Mercy to see an opportunity to boost her power, she might not even have spared Lin Yuan a second thought, even if he was an elite from the Radiance Federation.","But now, the Goddess of Mercy did not notice that when Lin Yuan fell into danger, she was not worried that she had lost the opportunity to increase her power but was concerned for his actual safety.","...","By the time she regained her senses, she found herself dazed.","She did not understand why her thinking had changed.","Purple Love felt exceedingly ashamed.","She had allowed him to fall into danger while by his side.","Not only would she have no way of answering to the Moon Empress, but she had also let down Blood Love, Blood New Moon, and Jade Sundial.","Purple Love had never been the type to hesitate.","Once she was sure that there was nothing she could do against Fifth Page Truth or break the small world built from laws, Purple Love took a deep breath and asked the Goddess of Mercy, “Goddess of Mercy, do have any way of sealing off Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeform’s ability without harming Lin Yuan who’s inside?”"]},{"number":2127,"title":"Chapter 2127 Scared Stupid?","paragraphs":["2127 Scared Stupid?","The Goddess of Mercy shook her head and slapped the sky with her fishtail to express her worry and impending sense of loss.","It was just like how people liked to pace when they were thinking.","When Purple Love realized that there was also nothing that the Goddess of Mercy could do, she flashed over and scooped up the sleeping Silver Corona into her arms.","The Law Staff’s ability Ruling Settlement placed the mark on the aura of Lin Yuan’s vitality. Thus, Silver Corona had not been pulled into the mini world but was left outside.","Purple Love had picked up Silver Corona because it was a fey that Lin Yuan had contracted.","Silver Corona was currently in the midst of transforming its bloodline.","There could only be two reasons for it to have fallen asleep.","The first was that it was successful in increasing its power to become an eight-winged fairy.","The other possibility was that Lin Yuan had died, and his contract with Silver Corona had been broken.","If Silver Corona was forcefully awakened, Purple Love would not be able to get an exact sense of Lin Yuan’s condition, but she would at least be able to tell if he was alive.","Purple Love knew who the Goddess of Mercy was.","Purple Love did not want to interact with someone like the Goddess of Mercy, who was evil and always acted in the most extreme manner.","“The Moon Empress treasures her disciple greatly. He has to have a secret weapon that the Moon Empress prepared for him. The Moon Empress has also awakened her birth horoscope. The secret weapon from her might allow him to break out from the world that Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeform created using laws. Even if the secret weapon isn’t able to break the world, it should allow Lin Yuan to fend off Fifth Page Truth for a few more minutes. Five minutes later, the ability Ruling Settlement will lose effect.”","The Goddess of Mercy was annoyed when she heard what Purple Love said, but she also felt slightly relieved.","She had seen for herself how important Lin Yuan was to the Moon Empress.","The Moon Empress would definitely have given him a safety net.","He just needed to use it, and Fifth Page Truth would definitely have a harder time trying to take Lin Yuan down.","The Moon Empress had to be worried that Na Na would come after Lin Yuan after he stole the young Disaster World Faceless Beast.","With how much trouble Lin Yuan was prone to, the Moon Empress had to have prepared an impressive safety net in order to set herself at ease.","The Goddess of Mercy forced herself to calm down and wait out the agonizingly long five minutes.","Liu Jie and Wen Yu were worried about Lin Yuan and balled their fists up.","Not even Purple Love or the Goddess of Mercy had could do anything to help Lin Yuan out of this danger. It went without saying that Liu Jie and Wen Yu were helpless as well.","Liu Jie and Wen Yu detested feeling helpless. But this was not the first time that they were feeling this way.","The two of them shared a look and prayed that Lin Yuan’s secret weapon would be effective against Fifth Page Truth.","Both of them resolved to become stronger.","In the past, they wanted to become stronger so they could keep up with Lin Yuan’s pace and not be left behind.","But at this moment, they did not just want to be able to keep up with Lin Yuan. They hoped that the next time Lin Yuan was in danger, they would be able to do more than stand off to the side like useless blocks of wood.","Time passed terrifyingly slowly.","Lin Yuan, who was within the small world, could sense that he had lost his connection to most of his elemental energy.","If he had a fey that was beyond Fantasy Breed with him at the moment, he would notice that they could not tap into their laws.","Although the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s main diet consisted of law source crystals, it had also consumed a significant amount of law crystals and world crystals.","He could sense that the laws on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt were clashing against the small world that Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeform had created.","Although the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s laws were currently at a disadvantage, Lin Yuan could still make use of them, albeit their power would be far from their original capabilities.","If Lin Yuan used the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Sword Skills now, it would only produce 10% of its usual power.","But in spite of the treacherous situation, Lin Yuan was not panicked in the slightest but was calmly staring at Fifth Page Truth.","Fifth Page Truth was overcome with fury, and his mind was completely twisted and blurred over.","Yet, Lin Yuan’s expression turned out to be one as calm as a snow-covered landscape.","This only added fuel to the fire of Fifth Page Truth’s fury.","Fifth Page Truth smiled sinisterly.","“What’s wrong? Have you been scared stupid? You shouldn’t have come to the Startling Lines Continent to cause trouble. Today, you will die here, and I’ll use your bones to decorate the throne of bones below me.”","Fifth Page Truth intended to use this terrifying method to see the fear blossom on Lin Yuan’s face.","Yet, he was met with a clear and composed voice, “The throne of bones below you didn’t come with you into the small world made of bones. By now, the Goddess of Mercy should have taken your throne of bones apart! I don’t think you’ll have the chance to use my bones to decorate it. Rather than me thinking about whether my life will come to an end here, you should think about how you’ll be able to handle being surrounded by Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy once we’re back out there!”","At first, Fifth Page Truth had fully underestimated Lin Yuan.","But now, Lin Yuan could say such things to him without a hint of fear.","Even an idiot could tell that Lin Yuan was prepared.","Fifth Page Truth did not believe that a young man could be so calm in the face of death.","However, Lin Yuan’s words had hit a nerve with Fifth Page Truth.","It was true that Fifth Page Truth still did not know how he could take on the Goddess of Mercy and Purple Love.","He knew the Goddess of Mercy was trying so hard because of the bloodline in Lin Yuan’s body. Meanwhile, Purple Love had a grudge against him for killing the Sky Sundial Jade Spider.","Purple Love had killed First Page Fate and ended up with her roots injured. This meant that she was ready to do the same with Fifth Page Truth today.","Fifth Page Truth knew what was waiting for him once he left the small world.","If he had to face either Purple Love or the Goddess of Mercy alone and the Divine Order Evil Fetus had not been destroyed, Fifth Page Truth would have some confidence in finding a way out.","But now that the Divine Order Evil Fetus was gone, it would be difficult for him to escape with just the Law Staff.","Fifth Page Truth had not been willing to admit that his life could possibly come to an end here.","...","But after what Lin Yuan said, Fifth Page Truth had no choice but to face the music."]},{"number":2128,"title":"Chapter 2128 The Smartest Hunters Always Present Themselves as Prey!","paragraphs":["2128 The Smartest Hunters Always Present Themselves as Prey!","Fifth Page Truth scoffed.","“How I’m going to take on Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy is a problem for the future. You don’t have to worry about it. What you need to worry about now is how you will take me on.”","Fifth Page Truth had not expected to hear a cold chuckle after he was done speaking.","“You see me as prey and are so certain that I cannot escape this small world you’ve created. But have you heard that the smartest hunters always present themselves as prey? You’re only so angry and bent on killing me because you lose a pinnacle 10 Stars sacred source lifeform to the Goddess of Mercy and Purple Love’s attacks. I’m very glad that the sacred source lifeform you lost isn’t the one who can control laws. I will think it a pity if the sacred source lifeform that controls laws had died.”","!!","Fifth Page Truth inhaled sharply when he heard what Lin Yuan said.","Fifth Page Truth almost burst out into laughter.","What are you saying? Can it be that an ant like you has the audacity to eye my Law Staff? How arrogant and daring!","Fifth Page Truth felt that Lin Yuan was unbelievably presumptuous at this moment. But before he could say something, Lin Yuan went on to say, “There’s something you said that was wrong. You and I are not the only ones in this world. Begin Lady, put an end to him! Then, capture the Law Staff. Try not to hurt the Law Staff with your attacks!”","The moment Lin Yuan spoke, Fifth Page Truth watched as the pink and gold mole at the corner of Lin Yuan’s eye fell to the ground and turned into a slim girl with black hair.","She was wearing a pink and gold shawl that billowed around her.","However, Fifth Page Truth could not sense even a hint of any aura from the girl Lin Yuan had called Begin Lady.","Fifth Page Truth should be the ruler of this world of laws created by his sacred source lifeform.","He should be able to sense the girl, even if she was a regular person.","There could only be one possibility for her to have escaped his detection, which was that she was more powerful than him and that her capabilities had reached a level that was beyond his understanding.","Fifth Page Truth’s back broke out in cold sweat with this thought.","At first, Fifth Page Truth had been wondering if he should kill Lin Yuan or just kidnap him.","He might be able to flee if he had held Lin Yuan hostage.","Yet, it turned out that the one who threatened his life was not the Goddess of Mercy or Purple Love, but this young man he had pulled into the small world.","Lin Yuan said that the smartest hunters always presented themselves as prey.","Fifth Page Truth thought Lin Yuan was arrogant and egotistical at that time.","But now, he knew that this young man who appeared harmless was a highly intelligent hunter.","After Fifth Page Truth appeared, the young man did not immediately send out the girl wearing the pink and gold shawl. Instead, he allowed Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy to handle him.","This was likely because he did not want to reveal his secret weapon.","It could be that he had done exactly what this young man wanted by instructing the Law Staff to use Ruling Settlement to create this small world.","The young man could now use his secret weapon however he pleased.","Fifth Page Truth did not know how many young men had never experienced this feeling of their life at risk of coming to an end.","A selfish expert who only knew how to think about himself would be obsessed with increasing his power and afraid of dying.","When the Law Staff used Ruling Settlement, it would only pull the lifeform whose vitality it had marked into the small world.","It was clear that this girl was beyond the Law Staff’s reach and was not concerned by the Law Staff’s power at all.","This meant that the girl had definitely set her spirit fire alight.","A sacred source lifeform’s ability could only affect an expert who had set his spirit fire alight if the sacred source lifeform had reached 11 Stars.","If his plan had not been ruined and the Divine Order Evil Fetus had evolved to 11 Stars, he would not be as helpless as he currently was.","But not only had his plan been ruined, but the Divine Order Evil Fetus had also been killed by the Goddess of Mercy and Purple Love.","Even if he had the pinnacle 10 Stars Law Staff and used all of his other secret weapons, he stood no chance of survival in front of the girl who had set her spirit fire alight.","Birth horoscopes appeared to be invincible, but if they were lightly exposed to spirit fire, they would immediately be burnt to ashes. All that would be left would be the power within them.","With this thought, Fifth Page Truth hurriedly said, “I have accumulated substantial wealth these past few years. You can have all of them. See if there’s anything that you want. If you want me to be your Protector, I can swear on my birth horoscope to serve you for a hundred years!”","Lin Yuan looked amused when he heard what Fifth Page Truth said.","Not long ago, Fifth Page Truth said that he wanted to kill Lin Yuan. He had even been ready to grind all his bones to dust.","But once Begin Lady appeared, Fifth Page Truth realized that he was no match for the enemy and decided to try the weak approach. He was now even willing to give up his freedom in exchange for his life.","Clearly, Fifth Page Truth was not one to be stubborn for the sake of it.","Once one swore on one’s birth horoscope, there was no way of backing out.","It could be said that once Lin Yuan nodded his head, he would gain a top expert who had awakened his birth horoscope in his arsenal.","The expression indicated that the young man was not interested in his offer.","Fifth Page Truth hurriedly said, “All of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon are Class 5 Creation Masters. I might not have outstanding Creation Master talent, but I’m definitely more capable than Yi Huailu.”","Fifth Page Truth released a bit of his might.","He felt that by revealing his status as a Class 5 Creation Master, Lin Yuan would set aside their differences and keep him alive for the sake of the value he represented.","Lin Yuan narrowed his eyes slightly when he heard what Fifth Page Truth said.","It seemed that Fifth Page Truth had a good grasp of the situation in the Divine Wood Federation. He even knew that Yi Huailu had become a Class 5 Creation Master.","It was likely that someone in the Divine Wood Federation still had ties to the Truth Association.","Lin Yuan felt that he needed to have a chat with Yi Huailong to ensure that the entire Divine Wood Federation had been properly purged of any traces of the Truth Association."]},{"number":2129,"title":"Chapter 2129 Tower Canon’s Foundation!","paragraphs":["2129 Tower Canon’s Foundation!","Lin Yuan had not expected every single one of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon to be a Class 5 Creation Master.","That meant that there had to be at least eight Class 5 Creation Masters in Tower Canon.","This was the combined number of Class 5 Creation Masters that the three major federations had.","Furthermore, Tower Canon had never been idle.","Whale Ocean Commerce, which used to be one of the top three factions in the Radiance Federation, had been ruined by one of the Pages. As a result, Di Wanmi went down a path of no return.","Tower Canon not only possessed Class 5 Creation Masters of their own but even recruited other experts who had the potential to become Class 5 Creation Masters as well.","This meant that it was very likely that the Eight Pages had more Class 5 Creation Masters working under them or with them.","This allowed Lin Yuan to understand Tower Canon’s power from a new perspective.","Lin Yuan did not reply to what Fifth Page Truth said. Instead, he changed the topic and asked, “If every single one of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon are Class 5 Creation Masters, exactly how many Class 5 Creation Masters does Tower Canon have?”","Tower Canon looked hesitant. He had not been spoken to in such a way for many years.","But he remembered that his life was in this young man’s hands, so he replied honestly, “Each of the Eight Pages works on our own. I don’t know the exact situation of the others. It’ll be seen as a provocation if I try to find out about them.","“None of the Eight Pages want to make an enemy of each other. So, I don’t have an exact answer for how many Class 5 Creation Master Tower Canon has.","“I have about ten Creation Masters who are Class 4 and above. One of them became a Class 5 Creation Master 30 years ago. I have placed him in the Truth Association to act as the representative of the Truth Association. After I become your Protector, the Class 4 and 5 Creation Masters under me will automatically work for you as well.”","Fifth Page Truth’s revelation of his circumstances made Lin Yuan think that Fifth Page Truth might not possess as many Creation Master resources as the three major federations, but the gap was not large.","Lin Yuan believed that Tower Canon had many Class 5 Creation Masters under them.","The Moon Empress had once mentioned to Lin Yuan that Creation Masters were not just a product of talent but also time.","Chef Supreme had been stuck at pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master for 50 years before he became a Class 5 Creation Master.","Once an expert awoke his birth horoscope, his soul power would increase greatly, and it would be much easier for him to use his soul to concoct spirit fluids.","If an expert could reach Class 4 Creation Master before he awoke his birth horoscope, he would be able to find his own unique Creation Master path in a matter of months or a few years at most. There would be no need for him to reach pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master.","Many of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon had to already have been walking the earth for a long time.","Additionally, Fifth Page Truth was not human. Until now, Lin Yuan could not be certain of what Fifth Page Truth’s true form was.","But according to Fifth Page Truth’s aura, Lin Yuan could be certain that Fifth Page Truth did not come from the sixth dimensional world that the Pilgrimage Corpse Bird had come from.","Begin Lady looked at Lin Yuan while Fifth Page Truth was speaking.","Since it had consumed Bai Dong and Su Jian’s souls, it had absorbed their combined experiences.","Begin Lady now had a good grasp of the relationships of the people around him.","It knew that Fifth Page Truth had killed the mother of the Mother of Bloodbath, who was Lin Yuan’s first Path Protector, and thus formed a great grudge between them.","Begin Lady was curious about what Lin Yuan was going to do.","No one on the outside would know if Fifth Page Truth submitted to Lin Yuan in this small world and was kept hidden by Lin Yuan from then on.","Even if Purple Love, the Mother of Bloodbath, and the others found out, it was unlikely that they would make any comment.","Fifth Page Truth’s greatest value lay in remaining alive to act as Lin Yuan’s Protector and serve him for the 100 years he offered.","But selfishly, Begin Lady did not want Lin Yuan to accept Fifth Page Truth’s loyalty.","If Lin Yuan placed profits above his kinship, Begin Lady would not be able to resolve the image it had of him as a young man who had given up everything to save it with this new Lin Yuan who prioritized his profits.","Fifth Page Truth was already prepared to summon his birth horoscope to swear to become Lin Yuan’s Protector.","It knew that once it became Lin Yuan’s Protector, he would no longer have to worry about facing Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy.","If Purple Love and the Goddess of Mercy still tried to attack him, Lin Yuan would definitely protect him.","Just as Fifth Page Truth was about to relax, Lin Yuan looked at him seriously and said solemnly, “You should be in possession of the Sky Sundial Jade Spider’s heavenly family crystal. Give it back to me now.”","Lin Yuan’s solemn words sounded like an accusation to Fifth Page Truth.","Fifth Page Truth hurriedly took out the Sky Sundial Jade Spider’s heavenly family crystal from his spatial equipment.","Fifth Page Truth had a love-hate relationship with the Sky Sundial Jade Spider’s heavenly family crystal.","He had such a treasure in his possession but not the Eternal Heart that came with it, allowing it to be refined.","If he forcefully tried to refine it, he would be burned by the sun power.","Since Lin Yuan wanted it now, there was no harm in giving it to him.","After all, once he became Lin Yuan’s Protector, he would no longer have the chance to attack the Heavenly Family Cottage.","Fifth Page Truth took out Jade Sundial’s heavenly family crystal.","In order to express his humbleness, Fifth Page Truth walked over to Lin Yuan and knelt down on one knee like his servants did as he raised the heavenly family crystal high in front of Lin Yuan.","Fifth Page Truth had considered abruptly attacking Lin Yuan at close quarters, but he quickly dismissed the idea.","If he dared to try to sneak attack Lin Yuan, there would only be two possible results.","Firstly, Begin Lady would notice his intention and kill him before he even made contact with Lin Yuan.","Alternatively, he would be successful in killing Lin Yuan.","But then, he would have to take on Begin Lady himself.","What was the point in attacking if both results ended in his death?","At the moment that Fifth Page Truth took a knee, he noticed that Begin Lady’s body was covered in a layer of pink flames.","Although the pink flames were licking at him, he was not burned. However, they did leave a vest-like layer on him.","Fifth Page Truth thought that this was Begin Lady’s way of limiting him and protecting Lin Yuan.","After Lin Yuan received Jade Sundial’s heavenly family crystal from Fifth Page Truth and checked that nothing was wrong with it, he said something that caused Fifth Page Truth’s jaw to drop but also his anger to rise again."]},{"number":2130,"title":"Chapter 2130 The Lifeform in the Shrine!","paragraphs":["2130 The Lifeform in the Shrine!","“Begin Lady, kill him! Don’t forget that I want his sacred source lifeform to be intact!”","After hearing what Lin Yuan said, a gentle smile spread across Begin Lady’s face.","As it nodded, two pink flames appeared in its eyes.","The vest of fire that had appeared on Fifth Page Truth started to burn more intensely the moment the flames in Begin Lady’s eyes lit up.","“You...”","Before Fifth Page Truth could finish speaking, his original form appeared beneath the flames.","When Lin Yuan saw Fifth Page Truth’s original form, he finally knew what Fifth Page Truth actually was.","It turned out that Fifth Page Truth was actually a mouse-species fey.","According to the features on his body, which was the yellow fur on his abdomen, faint gold strands of hair on his long tail, and patterns of mountains on his back, it was likely that he was the descendant of the River and Mountain-Consuming Mouse and the Golden Tail Greedy Mouse.","The River and Mountain-Consuming Mouse could consume mountains and rivers as its food and had extremely strong defensive abilities.","Meanwhile, the Golden Tail Greedy Mouse was very similar to the Offering Witch Dappled Spider in that it could consume the flesh of other lifeforms to increase its power or even the power of its companions.","The Golden Tail Greedy Mouse was ranked 21st amongst the 100 Most Fiercest Beasts. and was considered a legendary fey.","Spirit fire took the form of flames, but it was not actually a type of fire but a product of insanely concentrated spiritual power.","Experts who had set their spirit fire alight could gain a unique power from their spirit.","If Fifth Page Truth had not let down his guard, Begin Lady would still be able to suppress him but would not have had such an easy time at least.","The vitality, soul power, and spiritual energy within Fifth Page Truth were decreasing rapidly as the spirit fire was burning them up.","Begin Lady intentionally let out a stream of water to wrap around the Law Staff to protect it from suffering damage from the spirit flames.","In the short span of a few seconds, Fifth Page Truth was burned to ashes after drowning in the spirit fire.","Begin Lady had protected the Law Staff and Fifth Page Truth’s spatial equipment.","Begin Lady intended to burn up Fifth Page Truth’s birth horoscope to trigger his spirit attribute.","Fifth Page Truth’s spirit attribute would greatly increase Begin Lady’s power.","But when Begin Lady’s spirit fire burned Fifth Page Truth’s birth horoscope into a mass of purple and brown spirit attribute and was about to start refining the energy within the spirit attribute, the shrine in the center of Lin Yuan’s soul that had been silent for some time started to react violently.","It released a strong craving and started absorbing the mass of purple and brown power.","The shrine’s craving for spirit attribute power exceeded Lin Yuan’s expectations.","Begin Lady thought that Lin Yuan was the one who wanted Fifth Page Truth’s spirit attribute power and did not fight with him, allowing him to absorb the spirit attribute power into the shrine.","During this entire time, Lin Yuan was in shock.","The last time the shrine had transformed due to Begin Lady’s spirit fire had been part of Lin Yuan’s expectations.","But he had not yet had the time to properly investigate the shrine’s transformation.","Now that the shrine had absorbed Fifth Page Truth’s purple and brown spirit attribute power, it once again transformed from the inside out.","At the moment that the shrine at the center of Lin Yuan’s soul was done absorbing the spirit attribute power, its interior exploded.","At first, the shrine had been like a wide field of constellations. The dots of light representing the faith power from other lifeforms were spread all around the shrine.","The explosion seemed to be separating out the environment within the shrine. The clean air floated above while the muddy air sank below.","The large amount of faith power seemed to distinguish the sky and earth within the shrine.","The remaining faith power was stored in the altar at the center of the world and transformed into a fountain of faith that continuously spewed faith power in fluid form.","The changes to the shrine had used up almost 90% of the faith power in Lin Yuan’s shrine.","At the moment, Lin Yuan did not know what the significance of the changes were. All he knew was that everything he wanted to do within the shrine could be accomplished by using up faith power.","Not long ago, he had appeared next to Luo Lan and saved millions of the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members.","After Lin Yuan had plucked them out of despair, all of the tribe members offered him pure faith power.","At first, the water spray from the fountain of faith at the center of the altar had only been about half a meter tall. But now, it was already three meters tall.","After the shrine absorbed the purple and brown spirit attribute power and injected it into the fountain of faith, Lin Yuan could sense that he was willing to sacrifice faith power to patch up the purple and brown faith power and create a new lifeform.","This was a very peculiar feeling.","A feeling arose in Lin Yuan when the fountain water formed from faith power made contact with the purple and brown spirit attribute power. He felt like a starving man at a buffet.","Lin Yuan had not had the chance to investigate the shrine.","Since the shrine’s interior had changed, Lin Yuan intended to check through it properly.","Lin Yuan projected his mind into the world within the shrine and immediately found himself on the altar.","The world around him was empty, and it was not much different from when he was last here.","Lin Yuan knew that he could expand the world’s borders by using up some of the fountain water.","However, he did not choose to do so.","This was because he did not know if he would encounter something he could not handle in the expanded borders.","Additionally, it would be better to use the faith power to begin construction in the world of the shrine rather than using it to expand the size of the world.","The best way to use the faith power would be to combine it with the purple and brown spirit attribute power.","With this thought, Lin Yuan decided to do so.","Although the purple and brown spirit attribute power came from Fifth Page Truth’s birth horoscope, it still retained the unique spirit attribute that Fifth Page Truth’s birth horoscope had comprehended.","However, all of Fifth Page Truth’s spirit and soul had been burned to ruins in the spirit fire.","This just meant that the purple and brown spirit attribute power that came from Fifth Page Truth’s birth horoscope no longer had much to do with him."]},{"number":2131,"title":"Chapter 2131 Holy Spirit?","paragraphs":["2131 Holy Spirit?","As Lin Yuan poured out the fountain water into the purple and brown spirit attribute, the spirit attribute started to pulse gently as though it was a fetus with a heartbeat.","The more fountain water entered the purple and brown spirit attribute, the stronger the pulsing became.","Lin Yuan could hear the sounds within the fetus.","As Lin Yuan continued to use faith power to hatch the fetus, Lin Yuan gained a deeper understanding of how faith power could affect this world.","Lin Yuan gathered a small amount of source-type power at the bottom of the altar.","A stone pillar sprouted to link the altar to the ground.","Lin Yuan could sense that if he was willing to spend more faith power, he could even produce whatever carvings he wanted on the stone pillar.","Lin Yuan had played video games in his previous life.","He felt that the world within the shrine was like a large sandbox game.","However, he did not need to strenuously gather resources on his own for this sandbox game. All he needed to do was spend faith power, and everything could be achieved.","If Lin Yuan wanted, he could even use faith power to create an army within this world.","However, the troops’ strength would depend on how much faith power he was willing to use.","Faith power was the main currency in the world of the shrine.","The more he investigated the world of the shrine, the more interested in it he became.","Lin Yuan thought.","It isn’t easy to collect faith power in the main world. Collecting faith power from dimensional lifeforms in the marsh world is much easier.","Lin Yuan had discussed spirit fire with Begin Lady in the past.","Spirit fire had created a world within Lin Yuan’s shrine.","Thus, the world within the shrine was definitely related to spirit attribute power and spirit fire.","Lin Yuan had asked Begin Lady about what was special about the shrine.","However, Lin Yuan realized that Begin Lady was completely unaware.","It also did not know what level was beyond spirit fire.","While Lin Yuan was thinking, the fetus was done absorbing the faith power.","Lin Yuan could sense that the fetus was communicating with him respectfully and expressing its wish to hatch.","Lin Yuan was the ruler of the shrine world, so the fetus could not hatch naturally without his permission.","If he could control the world, Lin Yuan would be like the father and god of the shrine world.","After Lin Yuan agreed for the fetus to hatch, he was immediately struck by something.","He could sense that he could decide how the hatched fetus looked like if he used up a small amount of faith power.","Fifth Page Truth’s spirit attribute power was a mix of evilness and filth.","This was related to Fifth Page Truth’s true form being a mouse-species fey.","Although Fifth Page Truth looked like a young boy, there was no way that was his true appearance.","When Begin Lady used the spirit fire to burn Fifth Page Truth’s body, and his young face had burned away, it revealed a waxy yellow and flat face underneath.","There were triangular eyes that were iconic of mouse-species feys on the waxy yellow and flat face.","It was common for feys to wear a facade after changing into human form.","If the fetus was allowed to hatch without Lin Yuan interfering with its appearance, it would likely end up looking like Fifth Page Truth did.","When he thought about Fifth Page Truth’s protruding mouth, ape-like chin, and triangular eyes, Lin Yuan decided to spend some faith power to manipulate the fetus’ appearance.","The things that Lin Yuan created using faith power in the shrine world did not come with intelligence, nor could they communicate with Lin Yuan.","Even if Lin Yuan used faith power to create a large army in the shrine, they would all be lifeless.","However, this lifeform birthed from spirit attribute power and faith power could communicate with Lin Yuan before it hatched, meaning that it had intelligence.","Given Lin Yuan’s current power, obtaining an expert who had awoken his birth horoscope would be difficult.","For the time being, there was no way another lifeform with intelligence would appear within the shrine world.","Lin Yuan decided to let this lifeform manage the shrine world on his behalf.","Although Lin Yuan did not expand the shrine world using faith power, the size of the shrine world was not small either. It was about the size of two buildings.","The more faith power Lin Yuan provided, the more water would appear within the faith fountain.","Lin Yuan did not know how the shrine world would be useful to him.","However, there would be no harm in doing some construction.","Because Lin Yuan was not stingy with his faith power as it manipulated the fetus’ appearance.","Soon, a human figure about the same height as Lin Yuan appeared next to him.","This figure had a face that brought about peace and prosperity and was full of holiness.","The figure was dressed in long white and blue robes with cloud patterns on them. It was similar to Sky City’s uniform.","The newly hatched lifeform kneeled respectfully by Lin Yuan’s feet and started to pray as though it was worshipping him.","“My god, I am a holy spirit that came from you. Please gift me a name!”","Lin Yuan was slightly stunned.","God? Holy spirit?","It was clear that this newly hatched lifeform that had been birthed from spirit attribute power and faith power understood its background. However, Lin Yuan was clueless.","At this moment, Morbius said in Lin Yuan’s head, “Partner, ever since the last time when you told me about the change to the shrine’s interior, I have been wondering what happened. My memory is lacking, but do you remember the Moon Empress mentioning that the Freedom Federation called all experts who had awakened their birth horoscope as gods, but they had only taken control of their lifespan?","“It is actually experts who have set their spirit fire alight who are closer to crossing the gate to become gods. Only the experts who have broken through past setting their spirit fire alight can be called gods. The more I think about it, the more I think the shrine world may be linked to the level beyond spirit fire. After all, the spirit fire was what caused the changes to the shrine.”","Lin Yuan nodded. His guess was exactly the same as what Morbius had said."]},{"number":2132,"title":"Chapter 2132 Lin Yuan’s Divine Kingdom!","paragraphs":["2132 Lin Yuan’s Divine Kingdom!","This was the only guess that could explain the changes in the shrine world.","Lin Yuan could not sense all the changes in the world by only using Morbius.","With the holy spirit around, he might learn more than he already knew.","“Since you’re the holy spirit I created, your name shall be Truth!”","Lin Yuan mentioned this name because the holy spirit came partially from his faith power and partially from Fifth Page Truth’s spirit attribute.","There had to be more than one holy spirit in the shrine world.","Thus, it would be easier to give all of them names to make it easier to differentiate and remember them.","After the holy spirit got its name, it bowed to Lin Yuan before climbing to its feet and asking, “God, do you plan on building your divine kingdom?”","Lin Yuan froze.","Divine kingdom? Was this space in the shrine world called a divine kingdom?","The name of the divine kingdom suggested that it was a world created by the divine spirit.","It seemed that he and Morbius’ guess had been right.","The gears in Lin Yuan’s mind started to turn.","Morbius could investigate other feys and dimensional lifeforms. But could it check holy spirits and see their data as well?","With this thought, Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Truth.","What he saw caused his eyes to light up. He could see not only its data but also information about his divine kingdom.","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Grade","[Present Holy Spirits]: One","(Truth): A beginner holy spirit. It can set up the divine kingdom and manage the lifeforms in the divine kingdom in the ruler’s stead.","[Divine Kingdom Role]: Unconfirmed (The derivation rate of the divine kingdom has to reach 10% in order for the divine kingdom role to be confirmed.)","[Divine Kingdom Derivation]: Unactivated (To activate the saturation, the environment comfort level in the divine kingdom has to reach ‘barren’.)","[Environment Confort Level]: Wasteland","From True Data, Lin Yuan now had a general understanding of how he could develop this divine kingdom.","Since the information on True Data stated that Truth could set up the divine kingdom and manage the lifeforms within in the ruler’s stead, it should know how the environment comfort level could be changed from wasteland to barren!","Lin Yuan ordered Truth, “I do have the intention of building the divine kingdom up. How much faith power is needed to change the divine kingdom’s environment comfort level from wasteland to barren?”","Truth looked delighted.","Nothing made a holy spirit happier than a ruler wanting to establish the divine kingdom, as its greatest wish was to be able to serve its ruler.","“Around one-sixth of the current amount of water in the faith fountain is needed to change the environment comfort level from wasteland to barren. However, there are many ways to change the environment comfort level, and each method will also affect the derivation in the divine kingdom differently.”","After communicating with Truth, Lin Yuan now knew what the derivation of the divine kingdom meant.","In plain terms, derivating the divine kingdom was like proliferating the population on earth and causing it to go through different eras of evolution and history.","The environment comfort level was a necessary requirement that had to be met before lifeforms could begin living in the divine kingdom.","In his past life, Lin Yuan had been good at biology and was the biology class representative during high school. Thus, he knew how important water was during the derivation of a world.","This did not mean that lifeforms could not be derived from other environments.","After his conversation with Truth, Lin Yuan knew that as the ruler of the shrine world, he not only had to raise the environment comfort level from wasteland to barren but also had to invest significant effort into the divine kingdom.","This meant that no matter what lifeforms were eventually derived in the divine kingdom, they could all be considered Lin Yuan’s descendants.","Lin Yuan also had the mermaid bloodline in his body.","The beginning of human history started from water. The same went for mermaids.","Eventually, Lin Yuan decided that his main direction for the divine kingdom when changing its environment comfort level from wasteland to barren would mainly be to turn it into an ocean.","However, this did not mean that there would not be a hint of land.","Lin Yuan intended for one-fifth of the area to be land, and it would be situated below the altar.","Once the derivation of the divine kingdom began, it would never stop unless Lin Yuan chose to change the environment comfort level to wasteland or killed all of the lifeforms within it.","Otherwise, the derivation of the divine kingdom would march on.","After a year of evolving feys, Lin Yuan understood the ins and outs of evolving lifeforms.","He could not guess what the derivation of the shrine would end up looking like, but he had not abandoned his original plan.","He respected the miracle of life, and all he could do was his best every step of the way.","If the divine kingdom was what lay beyond experts who had set their spirit fire alight, was the fog on the outskirts of the divine kingdom hiding the divine kingdoms built by other experts?","There were not many experts in the main world who had awakened their birth horoscopes, much less set their spirit fire alight.","This meant that there could be experts not from the main world in the divine kingdoms past the fog.","Lin Yuan seemed to have had his prospectives broadened.","The true beginning of an expert’s journey was when he started to develop his divine kingdom.","After hearing Lin Yuan’s instruction and communicating with him, Truth said, “I am unsure how much time is needed to change the environment comfort level from wasteland to barren. I will inform you immediately once the change is complete!”","Lin Yuan gave Truth the authority to use the water in the truth fountain before he left the shrine world.","After Lin Yuan woke up, he saw Begin Lady looking at him concernedly.","Begin Lady had protected the Law Staff so it was still unscathed even after Fifth Page Truth died.","The Law Staff’s ability Ruling Settlement was still in effect.","Begin Lady said that the effects of Ruling Settlement would only last for five minutes.","Lin Yuan’s exchange with Fifth Page Truth had only lasted three minutes.","The first thing that Lin Yuan did after standing up was to assure Begin Lady that he was fine. Next, he started to take note of the time until Ruling Settlement lost its effect.","Lin Yuan noticed that he had only been in the shrine world for about a second or two."]},{"number":2133,"title":"Chapter 2133 Many Debts of Love!","paragraphs":["2133 Many Debts of Love!","To Lin Yuan’s memory, he had spent more than ten hours in the shrine trying to hatch the fetus.","This meant that time flowed at a different pace in the shrine world than it did in the main world.","Lin Yuan intended on calculating the exact difference the next time he went into the shrine world.","Once Begin Lady saw that Lin Yuan was fine, it turned back into a pink and gold crystal and attached itself to Lin Yuan’s face.","Before Begin Lady fell asleep again, it gave the Law Staff and Fifth Page Truth’s spatial equipment to Lin Yuan.","Fifth Page Truth was an expert who had awakened his birth horoscope and had also been one of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon. Thus, there were countless resources within the spatial equipment.","However, these resources that were exceptionally precious to Lin Yuan were not inviting to Begin Lady at all.","What was really inviting to Begin Lady was the pure spirit qi and water-element energy and those were all in Lin Yuan’s Spirit Lock spatial zone.","There was no place more comfortable for Begin Lady than the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","After the Law Staff’s ability lost effect, Lin Yuan appeared once again at the entrance of the underground palace.","When Liu Jie and Wen Yu spotted Lin Yuan, their expressions of worry immediately morphed into radiant smiles.","Both of them were unable to hold themselves back as they rushed forward to envelop him in a bear hug.","The Goddess of Mercy who had been moving her tail anxiously in the air felt herself relax when she saw Lin Yuan.","But she quickly started to carefully observe him for fear that Fifth Page War had taken hostage of him within his body.","After a thorough examination, she felt certain that Lin Yuan was still himself.","After all, the mermaid bloodline power in Lin Yuan’s body could not be fabricated by Fifth Page Truth.","The Goddess of Mercy knew that Liu Jie was Night Leaning Moon’s disciple and that Wen Yu was Mystic Moon’s disciple. Both of them had to have taught their disciples to be careful.","But once Lin Yuan appeared, neither of them had hesitated to hug him.","This showed how important he was to them.","Such companionship was hard to come by and the Goddess of Mercy herself had never had such relationships in her life.","In the past, the Goddess of Mercy was never jealous of such companionship. But this was because she had never had the chance to feel and witness such ties up close.","But now because of Liu Jie, the Goddess of Mercy was able to see the relationship between him, Liu Jie, and Wen Yu and it made her wish to have such companions as well.","The Goddess of Mercy also wanted to try to be a teammate who was willing to leave her back exposed to her comrades.","She had stopped worrying after she was assured of Lin Yuan’s safety but the anger within her had not been quenched in the slightest.","While she spoke, the Goddess of Mercy looked fearful. She had not expected the Moon Empress to be this powerful that the secret weapon she prepared for Lin Yuan to even be able to kill Fifth Page Truth.","Did this mean that the Moon Empress had set their spirit fire alight?","Begin Lady had not shown itself throughout and was now hidden on Lin Yuan’s body. Thus, neither Purple Love nor the Goddess of Mercy knew of its existence.","They did not believe that a young man like Lin Yuan who was not even 20 years old was capable of using his own power to defeat Fifth Page Truth.","Thus, the attributed his survival to the Moon Empress.","At first, Purple Love wanted to go up to Lin Yuan to check on him. But after she heard what the Goddess of Mercy said, Purple Love turned and asked her, “Where are you going?”","Although the Goddess of Mercy had helped Lin Yuan in the past, Fifth Page Truth’s words allowed Fifth Page Truth to find out that the Goddess of Mercy had intentions for Lin Yuan.","The Heavenly Family Cottage was on good terms with the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","Purple Love had a certain understanding of the mermaid bloodline.","The pressure of more elite mermaid bloodlines on inferior bloodlines was much stronger than that of fairies.","Ever since the Goddess of Mercy who had the mermaid king bloodline set her sights on Lin Yuan who had the mermaid emperor bloodline, her subconscious placed eternal shackles on her from doing anything that could harm Lin Yuan.","However, this did not stop her from causing trouble.","With the Goddess of Mercy’s temper, it was likely that she had not gone over to Lin Yuan and wanted to leave because she wanted to vent her rage.","The Goddess of Mercy believed that slaughter was the best way to vent.","Was the Goddess of Mercy planning on killing the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members who were in Thick Soil City? All of those people had been saved by Lin Yuan.","The Goddess of Mercy caught Purple Love’s eye and immediately guessed that Purple Love was ruminating over something.","She rolled her eyes at Purple Love and said, “I do want to purge the fury within me but my targets will be the people from the Truth Association. Apologize to Lin Yuan on my behalf. I will leave after killing every member of the Truth Association.”","The Goddess of Mercy swished her tail and disappeared along with her two main feys.","She badly wanted to stay with Lin Yuan but she knew that it would not do Lin Yuan any good if her relationship with him was leaked. It would also affect her partnership with the Radiance Federation.","Her reason for coming was to sneak a look at Lin Yuan.","She had only stepped in to help because someone was threatening him. But now that the threat had been neutralized, there was no reason for her to stay.","She hoped Lin Yuan would understand her intentions and any bad impression that Lin Yuan had of her would be erased by her actions today.","When the Goddess of Mercy left, Purple Love looked at Blood Love who had rushed out from the underground palace, she let out a sigh.","This young man did not have many years behind him yet he had already collected many debts of love.","Her niece still did not have the courage to express how she felt and it was possible that she would not have the chance to make it known in the future.","She wondered who Lin Yuan would eventually end up with after his eyes were finally opened.","There were so many beauties hanging around him. Would some conflict arise from his choice?","Purple Love shook her head. This matter was none of her business.","She wondered if the Moon Empress had thought about this issue. If she had not, it meant that she had a headache waiting for her!","Liu Jie and Wen Yu released Lin Yuan from the bear hug.","But before he could say anything to them, the Mother of Bloodbath swooped in to wrap its arms tightly around him.","The Mother of Bloodbath was the heavenly family fey that could communicate with the sun.","Although it had been in the underground palace, it could sense what was happening outside the underground palace through the sun.","At the moment that Lin Yuan had been captured by Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeform, the Mother of Bloodbath was so overwhelmed by worry that it forgot how to breathe."]},{"number":2134,"title":"Chapter 2134 Everything is Fine!","paragraphs":["2134 Everything is Fine!","If it did not know that it was too weak to be of any help in the fight and might end up as a burden, the Mother of Bloodbath would have rushed out of the underground palace.","The Mother of Bloodbath believed that it hid its feelings for Lin Yuan very well. Or rather, it had not even noticed it yet.","It did not know when its feelings for Lin Yuan started to change.","But when he was facing death, the Mother of Bloodbath lost control of its emotions and it finally realized the truth.","This was not the first time that the Mother of Bloodbath was hugging Lin Yuan.","He gently patted its back and said, “Don’t worry, everything is fine.”","The Mother of Bloodbath squeezed Lin Yuan’s hand before letting him go.","It moved to stand off to the side with a conflicted and thoughtful expression.","The Mother of Bloodbath was shocked by its feelings for Lin Yuan.","Wen Yu had noticed all of the changes in the Mother of Bloodbath’s expressions.","Wen Yu was the manager of Sky City who ensured that everything ran smoothly. She was very capable of observing and picking up on how others were feeling.","She could tell that the Mother of Bloodbath’s feelings for Lin Yuan had been buried so deep that it had not even realized it.","But it was clear that it had realized the truth.","But given Wen Yu’s understanding of the Mother of Bloodbath, it would continue to suppress its emotions and not express them.","Purple Love had also noticed the change in the Mother of Bloodbath’s emotions.","She was slightly stunned.","She saw that Lin Yuan had no idea what had brought about the changes to the Mother of Bloodbath’s expression.","Purple Love did not know if it was good news that her niece had finally realized how she truly felt.","As a senior, Purple Love did not broach the topic.","Purple Love remembered what the Goddess of Mercy said and said to Lin Yuan, “The Goddess of Mercy left. Before she left, she said that she would take care of the Truth Association. She probably understood how you felt after she saw the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members in Thick Soil City and found out about their circumstances. So, she probably won’t touch the secret aristocratic families even if they’re currently under the control of the Great Lush Federation.”","Purple Love did not mention the Goddess of Mercy’s concern.","The Goddess of Mercy’s concern for Lin Yuan had been written all over her face.","Given her understanding of Lin Yuan, he was oblivious to matters of the heart but very sharp when it came to everything else.","He must have picked up from what Fifth Page Truth said that the Goddess of Mercy had an ulterior motive.","If Purple Love knew that someone had an ulterior motive for treating her well, there was no way she could be happy about it.","However, Purple Love did not know that Lin Yuan had known all along that the Goddess of Mercy had intentions for him and had even guessed what they were.","Fifth Page Truth’s words only served as evidence for his guess.","Regardless of whether her motives were pure, she had helped him today. This meant that he now owed her a favor.","If not for the Goddess of Mercy, Lin Yuan’s biggest secret weapon, Begin Lady, would have been exposed.","Furthermore, she had been at a disadvantage in her fight against Fifth Page Truth.","The Goddess of Mercy and Purple Love had to work together in order to break through Fifth Page Truth’s defenses.","The Goddess of Mercy had been willing to stand by him and protect him despite knowing that she was no match for Fifth Page Truth.","Lin Yuan had to repay this favor.","It would not be easy to purge the Truth Association after Fifth Page Truth’s death.","Lin Yuan had experts under him but the only combat power he had beyond Eternal was White Speak when it was boosted by faith power.","Lin Yuan could not ask Purple Love to settle the Truth Association for him.","The Goddess of Mercy was doing him a huge service after protecting him.","Now that Fifth Page Truth was dead, Lin Yuan’s name was essentially stamped on the entire Startling Lines Continent.","From now on, the miscellaneous issues in the Great Lush Federation and Iron Hammer Federation could be slowly ironed out.","It was inevitable that obstacles would crop up but they would not be big ones. Lin Yuan had always been a capable person.","Now that Fifth Page Truth had been handled, the most pressing issue was to ensure the safety of the remaining tribe members from the Iron Hammer Federation.","Lin Yuan did not rejoice over Fifth Page Truth’s death. He did not even immediately go to check on what resources were stoned in Fifth Page Truth’s spatial equipment.","Lin Yuan called Luo Lan and said, “Go and check that all the tribes in Thick Soil City still have the Soldier Ration Radishes left. Once you’ve checked that all of them are sufficiently stocked up, you can send them back to their original tribes.”","Luo Lan had been working herself to the bone the past few days. She was not only busy but also filled with worry.","Lin Yuan’s call immediately caused delight to spread across her face as it told her that everything was now fine.","He had even asked if the tribes had sufficient Soldier Ration Radishes stocked up, which showed her just how kind and noble he was.","“Lord Lin Yuan, I have checked every tribe’s store of Soldier Ration Radishes. It is enough for the time being. I will go and inform the tribe leaders to lead their tribe members back home.”","Lin Yuan gave her a few reminders, “On the way back, instruct the Platinum and Black Gold tribes to migrate. Give their leaders more of the Soldier Ration Radishes. If they happen to meet their weaker members who are on the run, they can hand the food out to replenish their energy. If I’m not wrong, they have their own stock of warm clothes. If you don’t have enough of the Soldier Ration Radishes, I will ask Su Yiren to help to send more to you.”","Lin Yuan hung up the call.","He did not know if the members of the Truth Association were aware of Fifth Page Truth’s death. But he knew that there was no way that Fifth Page Truth would have allowed his subordinates to have a clear idea of his personal condition.","If the members of the Truth Association were left in the dark, there was no way that Luo Cai would be aware of it.","It was likely that Luo Cai was still sending out his men to kill the fleeing tribe members, thinking that he was carrying out Fifth Page Truth’s order.","With the Platinum and Black Gold tribes leading the way, they could vent their fury to their heart’s content on Luo Cai’s men who they met along the way. They would also be plucking Luo Cai’s claws and making it easier for Luo Lan to regain control of the imperial court and bring light back into the Iron Hammer Federation."]},{"number":2135,"title":"Chapter 2135 Help Him to His Seat","paragraphs":["2135 Help Him to His Seat","Lin Yuan always placed importance on faith power and had plans to faith power from the Startling Lines Continent.","But now that he wanted to carry out derivation in the divine kingdom, Lin Yuan decided that he would make it his main goal to collect as much faith power as he could from the Startling Lines Continent.","After the dust settled in the Divine Wood Federation, Iron Hammer Federation, and Great Lush Federation, Lin Yuan would leave this task to Yi Huailong, Luo Lan, and Jin Qianxun.","Lin Yuan felt that he would bring about unimaginable opportunities while developing the divine kingdom.","The Mother of Bloodbath, Wen Yu, and Liu Jie did not find anything to be strange when Lin Yuan called Luo Lan. The three of them were well aware of the type of person Liu Jie was.","However, Purple Love, who did not know Lin Yuan as well, looked at him in shock.","Her impression of Lin Yuan improved significantly.","It was to be expected if Lin Yuan was willing to look out for the lives of the citizens of the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan enjoyed glory both as a disciple of royalty and as a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. However, he was also saddled with duty.","But he did not have such a duty to the tribe members of the Iron Hammer Federation.","This world ruled by martial arts was a selfish one.","Thus, the stronger the expert, the more he wanted to take control of his resources.","In such a situation, it was indeed despicable of Fifth Page Truth to try to sacrifice all the lifeforms in the Startling Lines Continent to increase the Stars of his sacred source lifeform.","But in a way, his motives were understandable.","Fifth Page Truth was only carrying out such selfishness to the extreme.","Lin Yuan allowed Purple Love to see the goodness in humans.","Purple Love was the Heavenly Family Fey that was affiliated with the stars. Thus, she possessed a certain level of divine abilities.","This was not the first time Purple Love felt that Lin Yuan was capable of causing quakes to ripple all over the main world. This would definitely break the balance, and many unstabilizing factors would arise.","However, Purple Love felt that if Lin Yuan was the cause behind the disruptions, his shining character would mold the changes into positive ones.","Purple Love handed Silver Corona to Lin Yuan and said, “Now that your secret weapon from the Moon Empress has taken care of Fifth Page Truth, I will go and help you to collect the shattered remains of his sacred source lifeform. The body of a pinnacle 10 Stars sacred source lifeform presents unimaginable wealth. At the very least, the Moon Empress will be able to forge a 9 Stars precious instrument out of it.","“As for the members of the Truth Association killed by the Goddess of Mercy, their own bodies and the bodies of their feys will definitely be reduced to smithereens. I will fetch their Eternal Hearts, Immortal bodies, and world crystals for you. This fairy can have the remnants of their flesh and blood!”","Lin Yuan hurriedly handed Jade Sundial’s heavenly family crystal he obtained from Fifth Page Truth over to Purple Love.","Purple Love received the heavenly family crystal with slightly trembling hands.","Her main reason for coming to the Startling Lines Continent was to get her revenge on Fifth Page Truth and take back Jade Sundial’s heavenly family crystal.","By the time Lin Yuan was out of danger, Fifth Page Truth had already disappeared.","Purple Love could not ask him about Fifth Page Truth at such a time.","She had been afraid that they had lost the opportunity to retrieve Jade Sundial’s heavenly family crystal.","Once they failed to retrieve Jade Sundial’s heavenly family crystal, it would be impossible to recover her body and truly revive her.","Purple Love did not expect Lin Yuan to remember to get Jade Sundial’s heavenly family crystal back from Fifth Page Truth despite being in serious danger himself.","Because of Lin Yuan’s gesture, the entire Heavenly Family Cottage now owed him another enormous favor.","After receiving Jade Sundial’s heavenly family crystal, Purple Love sincerely thanked him and left to collect the resources that would be valuable to the sea of Bone Lotus Flowers.","The Mother of Bloodbath felt overwhelmed by emotions and almost let slip the words that had climbed to the tip of its tongue.","But when it remembered Lin Yuan’s current state, the Mother of Bloodbath forced the words back down.","It was afraid that once it spoke those words, it would never be able to turn back into the small spider that sat contentedly on Lin Yuan’s head.","It had spent some time in the human world and often browsed through forums and participated in meal gatherings. Thus, it knew that once feelings were expressed, the words could never be taken back.","While Lin Yuan was on the phone, Wen Yu had called Su Yiren to deliver resources to Luo Lan.","When Wen Yu was done, she said, “Luo Lan doesn’t need our help anymore. She has garnered considerable prestige after leading the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members in Thick Soil City. Without the support from the Truth Association, Luo Cai can’t stand up to Luo Lan with just the help from the servants in the imperial court who are still loyal to him.","“We just need to wait for the good news from Luo Lan! About one-fifth of the Soldier Ration Radishes that were grown in the marsh world were given to her. With so much of the Soldier Ration Radishes, the tribes will be able to survive winter after returning home. Once most of the Soldier Ration Radishes have been used up, it should be time for the trading route between the Iron Hammer Federation and Divine Wood Federation to be opened.","“Listen started planning out the trading route two weeks ago. Without the robber groups, the merchant groups he recruited can travel for business without worries. Young Master, Jin Qianxun has been continuously providing us with information. I think we should go and meet up with him to fulfill the promise to him.”","Lin Yuan could not help but smile when he heard what Wen Yu said.","With a capable manager like her around, every task became easier.","Lin Yuan knew that Listen had recruited so many merchant groups on his order.","But he had started drawing out the plans for the trading route between the Iron Hammer Federation and Divine Wood Federation two weeks ago because Wen Yu had asked him to do so.","There was actually no need for Lin Yuan to put so much effort into the business of the Iron Hammer Federation.","Jin Qianxun had been providing him with valuable information, and Lin Yuan was very satisfied with his performance."]},{"number":2136,"title":"Chapter 2136 Oh My God! Faeries Have Such an Ability Too?","paragraphs":["2136 Oh My God! Faeries Have Such an Ability Too?","Now that the Truth Association was no more, it was time for a reshuffle of power in the Great Lush Federation.","This was the best time for Lin Yuan to help Jin Qianxun into the sea of power.","Su Yiren was on the way to Thick Soil City to deliver resources to Luo Lan.","As a previous Dark Envoy, Su Yiren knew how precious resources like the Soldier Ration Radish were because they had the potential to ensure the survival of an entire society.","If a similar resource existed in the Seven States of Darkness, Seventh Page War would not have been able to conquer the Dark Continent so quickly.","All the correspondence with Jin Qianxun so far had been from Su Yiren through the Thoughts Letter Paper. It was time for Lin Yuan to contact Jin Qianxun directly.","Purple Love quickly gathered the pieces of the Divine Order Evil Fetus’s corpse.","Compared to the Eternal Heart, the four Eternal Hearts and six immortal bodies were rather worthless.","There was a large gap between a 9 Stars sacred source lifeform and 10 Stars sacred source lifeform.","There was no certainty that even Eternal experts possessed 9 Stars sacred source lifeforms, much less 10 Stars sacred source lifeforms.","Purple Love placed everything she had collected in a scale and handed the glowing yellow scale to Lin Yuan.","“Little Yuan, I have stored everything I collected for you in this scale left by Yellow Rock. Fifth Page War’s sacred source lifeform is preserved in a complete state, which is rare. After you give it to the Moon Empress, she should be able to forge a pinnacle 9 Stars precious instrument out of it. If she’s lucky and adds sufficient aiding ingredients, she might even be able to produce a 10 Stars precious instrument.”","Lin Yuan looked at the yellow scale with shock.","Yellow Stone was a member of the Heavenly Family Cottage and his full name was the Yellow Stone Exquisite Turtle. He was a heavenly family fey that was affiliated with the earth’s core.","His scale was a natural spatial equipment. It was comparable to Lin Yuan’s spatial ring which had been made from one of the Spatial Mother Shellfish’s old shells.","Lin Yuan received the scale with a bright smile and said, “Thank you for collecting these for me. It would have taken me forever to do so myself!”","Lin Yuan was not being insincerely courteous.","Firstly, Silver Corona could not control the sea of flowers when it was asleep.","Even if Lin Yuan used True Data, the pieces of the Divine Order Evil Fetus’ corpse had flown too far after the explosion and it would have taken him very long to collect all of the pieces.","Begin Lady had already protected him. He was apologetic for having absorbed Fifth Page Truth’s spirit attribute power by accident which would also have been beneficial for Begin Lady.","If he said he wanted Fifth Page Truth’s spirit attribute power, Begin Lady would not have hesitated to give it to him.","However, he had taken it from Begin Lady without first asking it. For this, he was very apologetic to Begin Lady.","Begin Lady was a lifeform that had set its spirit fire alight and was now Lin Yuan’s friend and companion.","There was no way Lin Yuan would instruct Begin Lady to do such a menial job.","While he spoke, Lin Yuan used his spiritual energy to look inside the Yellow Stone Exquisite Turtle’s scale.","He saw that there was a large amount of gray and black flesh with flecks of red that was stored within a large iron chest.","After Morbius examined the pieces, it found that only two-thirds of the Divine Order Evil Fetus’ body had been collected. It was not as complete as Purple Love had said.","When Purple Love heard what Lin Yuan said, she hurriedly waved her hands.","“Little Yuan, the last thing I want to hear is you thanking me. If you thank me for every little thing, I don’t know how we’re going to continue living together!”","Purple Love had spoken from the heart.","When she saw that Lin Yuan had more to say, she quickly changed the topic.","She had sensed Lin Yuan using his spiritual energy to look inside the Yellow Stone Exquisite Turtle’s scale and noticed the expression on Lin Yuan’s expression. She started to explain to him, “Little Yuan, are you thinking that not enough of the Divine Order Evil Fetus’ body was preserved? I can guarantee that the Azure Federation’s Sea Divine Nine Spiked Halberd is a beginner 10 Stars precious instrument that was made from a sacred source lifeform body that was even more incomplete than the Divine Order Evil Fetus is.”","Purple Love sighed before she went on to say, “When the Goddess of Mercy was fighting Fifth Page Truth, he did not see her as a threat. Thus, he had not used the Divine Order Evil Fetus’ abilities. When I sneak attacked him, he was in a state of sudden panic and had not reacted in time to use the Divine Order Evil Fetus as a shield. In the end, all he could do was watch as it was exploded to pieces by myself and the Goddess of Mercy. Both mine and the Goddess of Mercy’s attacks had been mainly physical. If our attacks had been mainly elemental, we would be lucky to preserve even 10% of its body.”","Lin Yuan understood the meaning behind Purple Love’s words.","Fifth Page Truth had been floored by Purple Love’s sneak attack.","Otherwise, there was no way that a victor could emerge in a fight between experts who only used physical attacks.","But there was one point that Purple Love had gotten wrong, which was that the Divine Order Evil Fetus’ body was not complete in the slightest.","The one that was truly complete was the Law Staff that Begin Lady had shielded. It was also pinnacle 10 Stars and had been 100% preserved.","Lin Yuan had communicated with Morbius.","When the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen absorbed the Law Staff’s power, it would be absorbing the Law Staff’s willpowers and sacred source lifeform power.","The sacred source power was what kept a sacred source lifeform alive.","After the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen absorbed the Law Staff’s willpowers and sacred source power, its body would still exist.","Lin Yuan wanted to turn it into a precious instrument.","Lin Yuan was affiliated with a sacred source lifeform like the Law Staff and a precious instrument made from it would be suitable for Lin Yuan.","The Fish World Sea Trump Card was only an 8 Stars precious instrument. He had used Frigid’s Cold Season Poisonous Fish to boost it to 10 Stars.","When a Class 6 Creation Master forged a precious instrument out of a fully preserved 10 Stars sacred source lifeform, the results were sure to be impressive.","If Lin Yuan possessed a 10 Stars precious instrument that he later boosted with the Cold Season Poisonous Fish, it should be able to reach 11 Stars.","Even if Lin Yuan could not take on a top expert on his own with an 11 Stars precious instrument, he could pick a side in a fight between two top experts to support them.","At this moment, Lin Yuan heard Begin Lady’s voice.","What it said immediately caused excitement to spread across his face.","Oh my god! Fairies have such an ability too?"]},{"number":2137,"title":"Chapter 2137 Precious Instrument Freedom!","paragraphs":["2137 Precious Instrument Freedom!","“Lin Yuan, you used the blue waist accessory to help me overcome the Heaven’s Trial. If that is a precious instrument, I might be able to create the materials for precious instruments and nourish them to eventually help them become whole.”","Although Begin Lady spoke with hesitation, its tone was level.","It was an intermediate faerie that was well aware of its own abilities.","Since Begin Lady had brought the topic up to Lin Yuan, it meant that it was confident that it would be able to create precious instruments.","However, it had no experience in doing so and dared not give any guarantees.","!!","While Lin Yuan was impressed by the capabilities of faeries, he also started to think.","He had numerous bodies of sacred source lifeforms. First was the Crimson Tentacle Algae which he had obtained after killing Shark Awn. Next were the three gorgons that used to belong to Yan Ling, Cai Huo, and You Changjian. The last were those that came from Yang Hanxian and the Truth Association’s members.","All of these sacred source lifeforms corpses could be turned into precious instruments.","However, the rate at which Di Wanmi was creating precious instruments was much too slow.","While Di Wanmi had been creating precious instruments, Lin Yuan had assigned a new task to her. Thus, she had not even been able to create her first precious instrument.","The same went for Yi Huailu. He had only recently become a Class 5 Creation Master and did not have any advantage over Di Wanmi.","Yi Huailu was in the midst of discovering his potential.","Rather than asking Yi Huailu to create precious instruments, he should be focusing on building up the Divine Wood Federation.","Thus, despite Sky City already having two Class 5 Creation Masters under its wing, Lin Yuan still needed to ask the Moon Empress for help when he wanted to forge precious instruments.","There was no way that he could dump a pile of sacred source lifeform bodies on her and force her to slave away day and night for him.","But now, Begin Lady could take over the burden.","Nonetheless, there was no way that Lin Yuan could ask Begin Lady to create a precious instrument out of a pinnacle 10 Stars sacred source lifeform’s corpse right out of the gate.","He could give it the bodies of some lower Stars sacred source lifeforms to practice with first and see how capable it really was at this.","If Begin Lady happened to be skilled at creating precious instruments, Lin Yuan would then consider giving it the Law Staff.","If the precious instruments that Begin Lady forged fell in Stars severely, Lin Yuan would have no choice but to approach the Moon Empress.","Otherwise, it would be a waste of a 10 Stars sacred source lifeform’s corpse.","Since Lin Yuan and Begin Lady had communicated through their souls, Purple Love was unaware of the conversation.","When Purple Love saw Lin Yuan’s smile, she thought that he was happy about having obtained the complete corpse of the Divine Order Evil Fetus.","She smiled as well.","“Little Yuan, Heavenly Family Cottage has not slacked off in our collection of resources despite having remained below the radar. We have some resources that will be suitable for the Divine Order Evil Fetus’s body. I will ask Blue Lotus to bring them to you.”","Lin Yuan was about to thank Purple Love before he was sternly stopped by one stern look from her.","He just wanted to express his gratitude to her but Purple Love also felt indebted to him because of what he did for Heavenly Family Cottage.","Lin Yuan did not want an expert of Purple Love’s position to bow in thanks to him.","He was never the type to expect returns from others for deeds he had done for them.","However, Lin Yuan indeed needed to ask for Purple Love’s help with something.","She was not an outsider to him so he spoke candidly, “Auntie Purple, besides the Divine Order Evil Fetus’ body, I also obtained the Law Staff’s body. The Law Staff is more suited for me and I am thinking about turning it into a precious instrument. I don’t have many resources on hand that are complementary with turning the Law Staff into a precious instrument. Does Heavenly Family Cottage have such resources in storage? If you do, I would like to trade for some with you.”","When Purple Love heard what Lin Yuan said, she tousled his hair and said, “We definitely have them. However, the Law Staff’s abilities are rather special. Even Heavenly Family Cottage doesn’t have many resources that are compatible with it. When I ask Blue Lotus to search for resources that are compatible with the Law Staff, I’ll also tell her to look for resources that will aid in forging a precious instrument out of it. I’ll tell her to give them all to you. If you ever need any resources from Heavenly Family Cottage, all you have to do is say the word. There’s no need for any trades. If you draw a line with Heavenly Family Cottage when it comes to such matters, we will really be at a loss about how we can thank you for helping Blood Love and saving Jade Sundial.”","From the sincere way that Purple Love spoke, Lin Yuan could tell that she was delighted that she could be of help to him.","After Purple Love participated in the small meeting, she had a general understanding of Lin Yuan’s reason for coming to the Startling Lines Continent.","She also knew that Lin Yuan had started a faction called Sky City and that the Mother of Bloodbath was one of the main members of the faction.","“Little Yuan, if you are planning to head to the Great Lush Federation next, I will go with you. Give me a set of Sky Creation’s uniform and none of Fifth Page Truth’s subordinates will recognize me. It would be bad if news got out that I was killing humans from the Startling Lines Continent. Sky Creation’s mask will help to hide my identity. I can also help with any issues that require martial force to be settled.”","Lin Yuan could tell that Purple Love’s words were full of affection.","As the head of Heavenly Family Cottage, Purple Love held up the pride of the faction.","Yet, she was willing to put on Sky City’s uniform to help him.","This meant that she had already started caring for the Mother of Bloodbath as though she were its mother.","Otherwise, there was no need to go to such an extent just to repay a favor.","“Auntie Love, I don’t have any spare uniforms now but I’ll ask Wen Yu to make one specially for you. All of Sky Creation’s uniforms are handmade by Wen Yu. Let me get in touch with Jin Qianxun first and we’ll set off a day later! It’ll give me a chance to see how he performs during this extra day.”","The Great Lush Federation was in chaos now due to the Truth Association’s order and because of Fifth Page Truth’s death.","Jin Qianxun’s decisions and how he positioned himself given the circumstances would allow Lin Yuan to see what kind of character he had.","Regardless, Lin Yuan would fulfill his promise to Jin Qianxun. However, Jin Qianxun’s character would determine Lin Yuan’s attitude towards him in the future."]},{"number":2138,"title":"Chapter 2138 War Chariot, Judgment, Lover","paragraphs":["2138 War Chariot, Judgment, Lover","Lin Yuan had placed Luo Lan in the middle of the sea of flowers to address the despairing tribe members of the Iron Hammer Federation because he wanted to see what she was capable of.","Now, he was going to test and observe Jin Qianxun in the same way.","He hoped that Jin Qianxun would not end up disappointing him.","On this trip to the Great Lush Federation, he would not only be boosting Jin Qianxun to the throne of the Great Lush Federation to enable the Jin family to become the rulers of the Great Lush Federation but he also intended on opening the harbor. His goal was to turn the harbor into the trading hub of the Startling Lines Continent.","Apart from these two tasks, Lin Yuan also had something more important to do, which was to find out from Fifth Page Truth’s subordinates if there was truly a Class 5 Creation Master among them.","There had never been a Class 5 Creation Master in the history of the Startling Lines Continent. Yi Huailu was the first one.","It could be said that the strategic significance of one Class 5 Creation Master was greater than that of the entire Great Lush Federation.","Lin Yuan had hesitated before he instructed Begin Lady to kill Begin Lady. He was afraid that the Class 5 Creation Master under Fifth Page Truth might have signed a contract with Fifth Page Truth that caused him to die when Fifth Page Truth did.","But after his hesitation, he still decided that it was necessary to kill Fifth Page Truth.","If he caused that Class 5 Creation Master to die by killing Fifth Page Truth, there was nothing that Lin Yuan could do about it.","However, Lin Yuan felt that it was unlikely that a Class 5 Creation Master would willingly work under Fifth Page Truth. He had to have been forced.","Thus, it was very likely that the Class 5 Creation Master was still alive.","It was even possible that he had taken over control of the Truth Association after Fifth Page Truth’s death.","Luckily, the Goddess of Mercy had only helped him to clear the members of the Truth Association who had been around the underground palace instead of going directly to the Truth Association’s headquarters in the Great Lush Federation.","Otherwise, she might have killed the Class 5 Creation Master along with the rest of them.","First, Wen Yu took Purple Love’s body measurements.","At first, she had been nervous about making a set of uniform for an expert like Purple Love.","But when she started taking Purple Love’s measurements, she found herself starting to envy Purple Love.","Damn! How could a fey in human form have such a great figure? My figure has not improved in the slightest even after eating stacks of rainbow fish skin every day. Did her great figure come from her true form being a fox?","After she absorbed Mystic Moon’s Dragon Pearl Embryo, the bloodline in her body had been growing stronger.","Could my figure improve after gaining the dragon-species bloodline? I hope so! It definitely will!","Purple Love’s demeanor was very natural while Wen Yu was taking her measurements.","But soon, Purple Love was increasingly disconcerted by Wen Yu’s gaze. It did not take her long to guess what was running through Wen Yu’s head.","Purple Love instinctively said, “Don’t make the uniform too form-fitting. I don’t like form-fitting clothes.”","Wen Yu was momentarily stunned.","This was likely the pride of a senior!","...","A building affixed with two towers that each had three opulent clocks hanging off them was emitting various fragrances.","When the fragrances intermixed, different flower patterns were produced, making the towers appear even more beautiful.","A Lead Chanter was chanting loudly outside of the tower.","There were 36 chanters who were chanting earnestly alongside the Lead Chanter while kowtowing.","The Lead Chanter and 36 chanters were wearing white robes that all had the word ‘sin’ on the back, making them seem like prison uniforms.","It was a routine for there to be continuous chanting day and night outside of the tower.","A short-haired girl within the tower was sitting quietly by a long table.","Her eyes were flashing sharply and the aura she was emanating caused her earrings to start to move.","A moment later, the short-haired girl mumbled to herself, “The sins that Fifth Page Truth had been carrying have all disappeared. The brand that I left on him has also been erased. Given his capabilities, there’s no way he could have discovered my brand even if his power has increased. I was wondering why all of Fifth Page Truth’s sins had disappeared before he left. It looks like he’s dead!”","At this point, the girl’s sinister smile melted away and was replaced by a different expression.","“The Eight Pages of Tower Canon sure are interesting! I wonder who will succeed the position of Fifth Page now that Fifth Page Truth is dead.”","The expressions on the girl’s face were changing continuously and it looked as though she was going mad.","At this moment, ripples appeared on the silver mirror beside her.","She picked up the mirror and rubbed it gently with her pointer.","Soon, the image of a man appeared.","There were tattoos peppered all over the man’s face. Upon closer inspection, one would realize that the tattoos formed the image of a large war chariot.","“Judgment, Righteousness managed to survive thanks to your information.”","Third Page Eternal Sin frowned when she heard the words of the tattooed man.","“Don’t call me Judgment, I am currently on a mission with no end point in sight and have almost forgotten that codename. I prefer to be called Tenth Sacred Cup.”","War Chariot replied placatingly, “Judgment, I know you are dissatisfied with the mission that World and Restraint gave you. I’m here to tell you that Restraint changed his mind. He thinks that there’s something very wrong with Tower Canon and wants you to return.”","Third Page Eternal Sin started to guffaw in a deranged fit, causing War Chariot to frown at her. But, he did not interrupt her.","After laughing for a full three minutes, Third Page Eternal Sin’s voice became extremely cold, “I prepared for this mission for 30 years and have been undercover in Tower Canon for 400 years. After 400 years, I can’t bring myself to back out. As unwilling as I am to be part of this mission, how can I let the 430 years I’ve already invested into it go to waste? Tell Restraint that in the outside world, I’m Tenth Sacred Cup. In the Sacred Cup Sequence, I have a hold on the Sacred Cup Queen. He doesn’t have the right to order me around. I will remain in Tower Canon until I’ve dug out all of its secrets.”","After hearing what Third Page Eternal Sin said, War Chariot lost his temper and yelled angrily, “Judgment, don’t forget how Lover died! If you insist on acting as you please, you’ll most likely end up with the same destination!”"]},{"number":2139,"title":"Chapter 2139 Seventh Page War Can’t Return to Human Form!","paragraphs":["2139 Seventh Page War Can’t Return to Human Form!","War Chariot could no longer suppress his fury and vitriol spewed forth from him, causing the words he said to give off a bone-rattling sensation.","“Lover died because he was stupid! I won’t let myself be afflicted by even a hint of emotion when I’m on a mission. Let me say it once more, call me Tenth Sacred Cup! We only speak once a month I don’t want to waste time discussing nonsense. First Page Fate is truly dead. But I can’t find anything about First Page Crimson who suddenly succeeded the position.”","Third Page Eternal Sin’s icy tone quelled War Chariot’s rage and silenced him.","His expression turned austere and determined when he heard Third Page Eternal Sin’s report on Tower Canon.","“After Righteousness returned, he reported all of this information. If you can’t find out anything about First Page Crimson, haven’t you tried provoking him to test his skills?”","!!","War Chariot had more to say but kept them to himself.","There were times when power revealed more than one’s background.","The moment he spoke, fear flashed across the face on the other side of the mirror.","This took War Chariot by surprise.","To his memory, the girl in front of him had different expressions every day regardless of when she had been Judgment or even now during her time as Tower Canon’s Third Page Eternal Sin. However, none of her expressions had been fear.","But aside from his shock, War Chariot also realized how serious the situation was.","Given Judgment’s character, her expression meant that she had already tried crossing swords with him and lost.","Otherwise, such an expression would never appear on her countenance.","There was a pause before Judgment went on to murmur, “First Page Crimson has, at the very least, set his spirit fire alight. His appearance is what makes me think that there’s a bigger secret that Tower Canon is trying to hide. Seventh Page War is no longer on the island. Before she left the island, she had a clash against First Page Crimson. Now, she can’t even transform into human form. So tell Restraint not to send out anyone to test First Page Crimson’s power, no matter how curious he is.”","At first, there was more that War Chariot wanted to say. But before he could speak, he watched as the girl on the other side of the mirror gently tapped its surface.","Ripples appeared on the surface of the mirror and their connection came to an end.","Third Page Eternal Sin looked down at her hands as her expression slowly turned maniacal.","I hope that I can find out everything there is to know about Tower Canon and leave before the Sleeper’s Revival begins. Once that plan is set into motion, everything will be over.","...","The jade-textured wooden furniture in the underground palace glowed gently. Under this illumination, one would feel at ease.","Lin Yuan was lying on the bed in his room. Having just woken up, he stretched.","The small white cat beside him had long woken up. When it saw that he was awake, it gently nudged him with its body and swung its long tail happily.","Lin Yuan had not had such restful sleep in a long time.","Recently, he had expended a lot of effort and energy in his crusade against the Truth Association.","He had already spent a considerable amount of time in the Startling Lines Continent.","Now, the entire Startling Lines Continent finally belonged to him.","Lin Yuan picked up Genius, changed clothes, and walked out of his room.","When he pushed open the door of his room, he saw Su Yiren standing outside holding a document.","She would occasionally lift one of her feet to stand on its tips in order to divide the weight between her two legs.","It seemed that she had already been standing here for some time.","Lin Yuan hurriedly said, “In the future, if you need to speak with me, you can just wake me up. You don’t have to stand by the door and wait.”","Su Yiren hurriedly shook her head and said, “Young Master, you haven’t gotten good rest recently. This matter isn’t urgent. It’s just information that came from Jin Qianxun about the Great Lush Federation. In the time that I’ve been waiting, I’ve also given out orders to the 14 Poppy Fruits.”","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow.","He did not know when it started but Su Yiren had stopped calling him by his name but addressed him as ‘Young Master’ instead.","He did not try to correct her and just took the papers that she was holding.","As one of the previous Dark Envoys, Su Yiren was arrogant by nature.","She had started addressing him in such a way because of the promise he had made to recover the Dark Continent. Because of it, she not only felt submissive towards him but also willing to sincerely lay down her pride.","Another reason for the change was that this was how Wen Yu addressed him.","After the cemented Lin Yuan’s position in her heart, she subconsciously raised his importance to her.","Su Yiren could tell that the person Lin Yuan trusted the most was Wen Yu.","Hence, Su Yiren did all she could to compare herself to Wen Yu.","Lin Yuan immediately caught on to all of Su Yiren’s intentions.","He became more impressed by her abilities with each passing day. She had already raised his opinion of her all of her own.","Otherwise, he would never have promised to help her recover the Dark Continent even if it benefitted him.","When he looked over the information from Su Yiren, Lin Yuan gained deeper insight into the current situation in the Great Lush Federation.","There was indeed a group of experts in the Great Lush Federation who had died, including several leaders of top secret aristocratic families.","Jin Qianxun’s oldest brother, Jin Qianding, was among them.","Lin Yuan was now confused about whether the leaders of the top secret aristocratic families had sworn their servitude to Fifth Page Truth directly or to his other subordinates.","Fifth Page Truth’s death had led to an immense chain reaction.","The death of so many of the Great Lush Federation’s top experts and leaders had thrown the entire federation into chaos.","Given the circumstances, almost everyone was in a state of discombobulation.","Jin Qianxun had ventured a guess but he kept it to himself.","He knew that he was not considered strong amongst the Great Lush Federation’s experts.","With the promise from Lin Yuan, there was no need for him to engage in the fight.","Thus, Jin Qianxun chose to remain independent.","He did not influence any of the experts who had distinguished themselves in order to preserve his reputation when he took over the throne of the Great Lush Federation.","Instead, he chose to silently wait for Lin Yuan’s arrival.","Di Wanmi had left a deep impression on Jin Qianxun in Oak City."]},{"number":2140,"title":"Chapter 2140 Virgo Liu Jie!","paragraphs":["2140 Virgo Liu Jie!","In order to instill confidence in Jin Qianxun, Sky City had not hidden the fact that Sky City was the one that had helped the Yi family take over the Divine Wood Federation’s imperial court and enabled Yi Huailong to become its ruler.","Given that Jin Qianxun was one of the main members of the Jin family, which was one of the top-secret aristocratic families in the Great Lush Federation, it was to be expected that he knew of the Yi family’s position in the Divine Wood Federation.","Yet, Lin Yuan managed to raise such an insignificant family like the Yi family to the top of the food chain and enabled Yi Huailong to become a king.","This meant that Lin Yuan could definitely do the same for the Jin family.","Although Jin Qianxun did not participate in the mess, he still did all he could to stabilize the core of the Jin family.","!!","After Lin Yuan learned of all that Jin Qianxun did in the past few days, he came to a decision.","Jin Qianxun was able to guard but was not enterprising. He was wary and very conscious of his duty.","A person like Jin Qianxun was not very suited to be the ruler of a federation.","However, a person like this was just right for Lin Yuan.","He did not need Jin Qianxun to be overly courageous and noble. All he needed to do was manage the Great Lush Federation in the same way that Yi Huailong did for the Divine Wood Federation.","Lin Yuan intended to control the trading system in the Startling Lines Continent himself.","Listen was going to oversee all the chambers of commerce.","This would ensure that the supply of resources flowed smoothly.","When the three federations were no longer fighting amongst each other, the number of bandit groups would decrease by at least half. If any more cropped up, they could be easily dealt with.","When Lin Yuan did not say anything after flipping through the documents, Su Yiren quipped, “Jin Qianxun isn’t a talent by any means, but he is very obedient. He knew to protect the Jin family’s direct descendants in such circumstances and also protected the collateral members rather well as well. This means that he is the type to value relationships. I think that after you help him to assume the throne of the Great Lush Federation, he’ll be easier to control than Yi Huailong.”","Su Yiren did not know that Yi Huailong had sworn his loyalty to Lin Yuan.","When Yi Huailong used the Ethereal Jellyfish’s tentacles to travel to the underground palace for shelter, Su Yiren gained a certain level of understanding of him.","It could be said that she was not fond of him at all.","This was because she could see his ambition.","Although he was useful as Lin Yuan’s main medium of controlling the Divine Wood Federation, ambition was the last quality that a tool needed to have.","Lin Yuan nodded.","“Yiren, come with me to the Great Lush Federation. The construction of the harbor will take precedence after we take control of the Great Lush Federation. If the construction isn’t done well, not only will Wo Lun’s fleet be unable to enter, but we will have no way of sending massive troops to the Dark Continent either. I’m sure that you’ll be able to carry out this task with flying colors.”","Tears welled up in Su Yiren’s eyes.","Lin Yuan had made her the promise but had not mentioned it since then.","“Young Master, don’t worry. Leave the construction of the harbor to me. I definitely won’t allow any slip-ups to take place!”","After Su Yiren left, Lin Yuan went to find Liu Jie.","The Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting was held again yesterday.","Wen Yu, who was the owner of the Astronomical Parliament, had pulled Liu Jie into the parliamentary meeting.","Liu Jie occupied the Virgo throne","Wen Yu was the only one who could direct people to thrones, but the final decision of which throne was picked was left up to the constellations.","Wen Yu and Lin Yuan were both surprised that the Virgo throne had claimed Liu Jie. But it did not take long for them to see the reason behind the decision.","Liu Jie was principled and organized in everything that he did.","When he was cooking, he would ensure that every utensil was washed before he used the next one.","He was also slightly germaphobic.","These were similar traits of a Virgo.","Liu Jie had always been curious about the Astronomical Parliament that Lin Yuan and Wen Yu sometimes mentioned. He had never entered it before and could not understand its magical aspects.","It was only after he entered the Astronomical Parliament and took a seat on the Virgo throne that he understood just how special the Astronomical Parliament was.","He also realized how Lin Yuan had come to know people like Ta Lei, Su Yiren, and Yin Lin.","When the Azure Federation envoy team came to spectate the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Liu Jie had been confused about Yin Lin’s clear siding with Lin Yuan.","But now he knew that the members of the Astronomical Parliament had all been saved by Lin Yuan at their darkest moments, just like he had done for Liu Jie.","However, he was much luckier than the members of the Astronomical Parliament because he got to know Lin Yuan sooner.","Although he was Lin Yuan’s retainer knight and carried out that duty, he actually owed Lin Yuan far more than what he could repay by just providing Lin Yuan with his protection.","Liu Jie had interacted a fair amount with Su Yiren and Luo Lan recently. As such, he was familiar with them.","He had also met Ta Lei a few times.","Ta Lei was very respectful of Liu Jie because he knew that Liu Jie was Lin Yuan’s retainer knight and friend. He addressed Liu Jie as ‘uncle’.","Liu Jie had also met with Yin Lin.","The only members of the Astronomical Parliament who were foreign to Liu Jie were Bei Xu, Bu Po, and Wo Lun.","The members of the Astronomical Parliament usually communicated through the Thoughts Letter Paper. Any issues that they had could be solved by contacting each other.","Not much happened during the parliamentary meeting.","The main purpose of the meeting was for the members who were unfamiliar with Liu Jie to get to know him.","Yin Lin, Su Yiren, and Bu Po’s identities were now very different from when they first joined the Astronomical Parliament.","Bei Xu, Wo Lun, and Ta Lei were still working hard to improve themselves.","In truth, all of them had wondered if they would one day be able to take up one of the 12 golden thrones after they made significant contributions to the Astronomical Parliament.","Although Lin Yuan had never mentioned it, the members all thought that the thrones would be filled by those among them.","Yet, this did not turn out to be the case, and Liu Jie ended up taking one of the 12 thrones.","This caused many of the members to feel slightly discouraged.","By occupying the golden thrones, Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, and Wen Yu were able to sense the changes in emotions of the members who sat on the north-south constellation seats.","Before the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting came to an end, Lin Yuan said, “From now on, there will be no abrupt occupations of the 12 golden thrones. There will also be more participants in the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meetings besides the nine of us. More people will be taking up the seats around you. The people who will eventually occupy the remaining nine golden thrones will be picked from among you. Let’s all work hard together!”"]},{"number":2141,"title":"Chapter 2141 Purple Afterglow’s Plead for Help!","paragraphs":["2141 Purple Afterglow’s Plead for Help!","This Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting went on for very long and drained Wen Yu of all of her spiritual energy.","Liu Jie had hit it off very well with Wo Lun.","After the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting ended, they continued to talk through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Yin Lin, Bei Xu, and the rest now had clear goals to work towards, which was to grab the chance to fill the remaining nine golden thrones and sit shoulder-to-shoulder with Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan had many things to do.","He had obtained an overwhelming number of opportunities recently but he had not yet had the chance to use them to increase his power.","But before he sorted through his rewards and increased his power, Lin Yuan intended on fulfilling his promise to Jin Qianxun first.","It would also give him the chance to see if there were any opportunities he could net in the Great Lush Federation, albeit the chances were very slim.","Lin Yuan had obtained Fifth Page Truth’s spatial equipment. It was likely that the true treasures were in there.","According to White Speak, the Marsh East Palace was about to become very crowded.","Apparently, the envoys of the Palace of Everything wanted to hold a Banquet of Everything.","Although White Speak had never been to the Marsh East Palace, he had heard of many rumors about it.","The Banquet of Everything was only held once every 300 years in the marsh world and it always involved a mountain of treasures.","Top grade marsh soil would only be the bare minimum of the treasures that would be present.","Lin Yuan was shocked when he heard this but he quickly understood the reason.","Top grade marsh soil was not valued at the Banquet of Everything because marsh soil was very common in the marsh world. But anywhere else, its value would be greatly inflated.","The Banquet of Everything would begin two months later.","But before that, the Storing Ability White Peaches and Deposit Ability Litchi Branches that Lin Yuan nurtured with source-type power would have ripened.","There was no question that the Banquet of Everything was a good opportunity.","It might even catch the eye of Dictator Everything.","Lin Yuan had never encountered a Dictator in the marsh world.","In the past, Lin Yuan had been afraid of meeting a Dictator because it would risk exposing his facade of being a Dictator.","But now that he had Begin Lady with him, he would not panic even if he was exposed for being a fake Dicator.","He would not only be opening the market for the Storing Ability White Peach and Deposit Ability Litchi Branch but Lin Yuan also wanted to obtain some source-type items and sacred source lifeforms at the Banquet of Everything.","After handling the trivial affairs Lin Yuan would be able to concentrate on raising his power to a new level using the resources he had accumulated before heading to the marsh world.","Lin Yuan also had the pile of spirit qi crystals from the white-clothed followers who Sky City had been carefully nurturing to look forward to.","Suddenly, Lin Yuan heard Begin Lady’s voice, “Lin Yuan, I can protect you while asleep because of the Element Well. It will also allow me to try to forge precious instruments at the same time. Do you have any ingredients used for creating precious instruments that I can practice with?”","Begin Lady had agreed to help Lin Yuan to forge precious instruments but it was currently trying to stabilize its spirit fire and Lin Yuan could not bring himself to ask again.","But since Begin Lady had mentioned it, Lin Yuan handed the bodies of the Gorgon Threads, Gorgon Teeth, and Gorgon Clam over to it.","Normally, a main ingredient had to be chosen along with some supplementary ingredients in order to create a precious instrument from the corpse of a sacred source lifeform.","Lin Yuan did not have many supplementary ingredients on hand.","The best supplementary ingredients for creating precious instruments were also parts of sacred source lifeform bodies. The next best would be spiritual ingredients that came from feys.","Using spiritual ingredients from feys was the main reason behind forged precious instruments falling in Stars.","The Gorgon Threads, Gorgon Teeth, and Gorgon Clam had abilities that could work in conjunction with each other. They had come from the Gorgon Apostle which was evolved from the Medusa. Thus, they could actually fuse with each other.","If the Gorgon Threads, Gorgon Teeth, and Gorgon Clam were above 6 Stars, Lin Yuan would never have been willing to part with them as practice materials for Begin Lady.","However, they had all been 4 Stars and their bodies could only be made into 4 Stas precious instruments at best.","They would be perfect for Begin Lady to practice on.","If Begin Lady could produce 4 Stars precious instruments out of the Gorgon Threads, Gorgon Teeth, and Gorgon Clam’s bodies without supplementary ingredients, it would prove its skill.","Lin Yuan had asked the Moon Empress before.","By that time, she had already become a Class 6 Creation Master and could guarantee that she would be able to produce 4 Stars precious instruments out of the three sacred source lifeform corpses.","Begin Lady was always interested in new things.","It had absorbed Su Jian and Bai Dong’s souls but it had never truly encountered the things that Su Jian and Bai Dong had experienced before. But still, it was not curious about them.","Su Jian and Bai Dong had yearned for precious instruments.","After being influenced by Su Jian and Bai Dong, Begin Lady also became very interested in precious instruments.","“Lin Yuan, I should be able to produce the precious instruments in three to five days. I hope the precious instruments I produce will be able to meet your needs so I can be of more help to you in the future!”","While Lin Yuan and Begin Lady were speaking, Purple Afterglow’s frantic voice appeared in his head.","Lin Yuan’s eyes widened.","Purple Afterglow would only be frantically asking for help if something bad had happened in the marsh world.","Genius had been carried out of the marsh world by Lin Yuan last night and had not returned to teach the Hundred Questions Beasts.","Chimey had remained in its nest in the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree to absorb strange flames energy to increase its power.","The only fey that Lin Yuan owned that could travel to and from the marsh world was Purple Afterglow","Purple Afterglow’s favorite activity was spending time with its wife.","Lin Yuan had invested significantly in the marsh world. He could not afford to lose the army of Hundred Questions Beasts or the rare plants that were being grown in his territory.","Lin Yuan immediately went into the Spirit Lock spatial zone with Begin Lady by his side and traveled to the marsh world through Klein Hub.","To his shock, he saw more than 30 terrifying and malevolent birds flapping their wings in the sky. All of them had snake heads.","This was not the first time that Lin Yuan was encountering the Drugged Snake Eagle."]},{"number":2142,"title":"Chapter 2142 I Have a Use For Their Hearts!","paragraphs":["2142 I Have a Use For Their Hearts!","These Drugged Snake Eagles were exactly like the one that Lin Yuan had encountered when he first entered the marsh world.","All of them were Favored Believers.","The Drugged Snake Eagles had managed to get past White Speak and reach this place. This meant that White Speak was also in grave danger now.","However, Lin Yuan could not communicate with his Apostles through his spiritual energy and soul like he could with his feys.","This group of the Drugged Snake Eagles were led by one that was much larger than the rest.","Lin Yuan was too lazy to even use True Data to check on the 30 Drugged Snake Eagles.","The leader of this group was about the same size as the one that Lin Yuan had previously encountered. It was an advanced Class 11 dimensional lifeform.","The other Drugged Snake Eagles were beginner Class 11 dimensional lifeforms.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly was currently trying to fend off the Drugged Snake Eagles.","It was clear that the Drugged Snake Eagles assumed that they had stumbled on a windfall.","No matter which Apostle they served, Favored Believers were always very sensitive to the presence of Apostles.","It went without saying that Favored Believers did all they could to offer up their faith and serve their Apostle.","On the other hand, they saw other Apostles as the best prey. If they encountered an Apostle, they would also find that Apostle’s Favored Believers.","Wendy, Rising Lizard, and White Pavilion had been the first to notice the Drugged Snake Eagles which were skilled at hiding their auras.","Three of them were now laying on the ground, heavily injured.","Only the leader of the Drugged Snake Eagles was focusing on the Kill Food Sky Butterfly. The others were mostly watching the injured Rising Lizard, Wendy, and White Pavilion.","“Hehe, who would have expected that when Lord Prayer Glow ordered us to patrol the south side for resources, we would come across not just a Marsh Crocodile that has become an Apostle but three other weak Apostles gathered together too? I’m sure that Lord Prayer Glow will shower rewards on us when we offer up these three Apostles!”","This group of Drugged Snake Eagles had to be the trusted aides of their Apostle. An Apostle would not send anyone besides its trusted aids to gather resources.","The Drugged Snake Eagles had been traveling for some time gathering resources for their Apostle. But this was the first time that their expected harvest was so large.","“There are not only three Apostles here but also a large amount of marsh soil buried in the ground and many rare plants and lifeforms. I’m sure Lord Prayer Glow will be interested in all of them.”","As he listened to the Drugged Snake Eagles speaking to each other so presumptuously in the language of the marsh world, Lin Yuan was both glad and livid.","He was glad that he had moved the Spirit Craftsmen and regular people behind the large mountain and that the fey breeding bases had also been constructed behind the mountain.","Otherwise, the Drugged Snake Eagles would have seen them first.","The regular people had willingly left their communities and offered up their loyalty for the rest of their life.","Lin Yuan had also made promises to them.","Although Lin Yuan was not the one who had made the promises directly, Sun Ningxiang had only passed on Lin Yuan’s word.","He did not want to let them down.","It would be near-impossible for the regular people and fey breeding bases to survive plundering by the Drugged Snake Eagles.","The Storing Ability White Peaches and Deposit Ability Litchi Branches were already ripe.","If the Drugged Snake Eagles caught sight of them and robbed the entire harvest for the Prayer Glow Apostle, Lin Yuan’s plan would be bust.","Lin Yuan was rarely this furious, nor did he encounter such infuriating situations.","It was clear that the Drugged Snake Eagles saw his territory as a garden they could freely harvest from.","They were so excited that they were close to dancing.","The lead Drugged Snake Eagle was eager to take the Kill Food Sky Butterfly on.","Luckily, Lin Yuan happened to be free when Purple Afterglow came to ask him for help and could immediately head to the marsh world.","Otherwise, the consequences would be calamitous!","The worried Purple Afterglow flashed itself next to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan’s appearance set Purple Afterglow at ease. It had been afraid that Lin Yuan would be too late to save its wife.","Lin Yuan pulled Purple Afterglow over and gently patted its antennae to comfort it.","He turned his angry gaze to the flying group of Drugged Snake Eagles and hissed, “Begin Lady, kill every single one of the Drugged Snake Eagles. If it’s possible, leave their hearts. I have use for them.”","Since the Drugged Snake Eagles thought that Lin Yuan’s territory was free for looting, let them become its fertilizer!","The Drugged Snake Eagles would be the best supplements for Wendy.","The previous Drugged Snake Eagle’s heart had allowed Wendy’s power to skyrocket.","It had not been long since Wendy and White Pavilion became Apostles.","Wendy had been Class 2 while White Pavilion had been Class 3 when they became Apostles.","But because of the Drugged Snake Eagle’s heart, Wendy had not only surpassed White Pavilion’s but now exceeded it by two Classes.","They shared the same environment. Besides the Drugged Snake Eagle’s heart, both of their standards of living were relatively equal.","After Wendy consumed all the hearts of the Drugged Snake Eagles, it would be able to surpass Rising Lizard to reach intermediate Class 9.","Once Lin Yuan appeared, Wendy, Rising Lizard, and White Pavilion noticed him.","The three of them immediately relaxed.","If they were not currently laying on the ground and incapacitated by their injuries, they would have rushed over to him.","Lin Yuan’s appearance also caused the Kill Food Sky Butterfly to let out a big sigh of relief.","Ever since the Kill Food Sky Butterfly joined Lin Yuan and found a partner in Purple Afterglow, Lin Yuan had been very generous to it.","As a result, its power increased at an unprecedented rate.","Nonetheless, it would be a challenge for the Kill Food Sky Butterfly to handle so many of the Drugged Snake Eagles. The weakest Drugged Snake Eagle that was present was not much weaker than the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","The Drugged Snake Eagle that had been about to strike the Kill Food Sky Butterfly blew its top because of what Lin Yuan said."]},{"number":2143,"title":"Chapter 2143 Tragic Wendy, White Pavilion, and Rising Lizard.","paragraphs":["2143 Tragic Wendy, White Pavilion, and Rising Lizard.","It was not because the Drugged Snake Eagles became afraid after hearing what Lin Yuan said but that it did not feel threatened at all by Lin Yuan’s aura.","A full-grown adult would not feel threatened by an infant.","Before the Drugged Snake Eagle could start to mock Lin Yuan derisively, a pink and gold stream of water silenced everything.","Soon, the Drugged Snake Eagles started falling from the sky one after the other.","At the instant that Begin Lady made its move, all of the Drugged Snake Eagles were eliminated.","After eliminating the Drugged Snake Eagles, Begin Lady hesitated.","But Lin Yuan had already made his request. Thus, Begin Lady transformed into a beam of light that soared over to White Speak.","But it was true that it was the only one that could save White Speak.","When it underwent the Heaven’s Trial, Lin Yuan had sent White Speak to sustain two of the attacks.","Although everything that White Speak did was because of Lin Yuan, Begin Lady acknowledged that it owed White Speak a favor.","After it saved White Speak, it would have returned the favor.","Before it left, Begin Lady left a hint of its aura on Lin Yuan.","If Lin Yuan truly encountered danger, the aura it left with Lin Yuan would be able to protect him.","It had almost died during the Heaven’s Trial and never forgot the fear.","It had not allowed itself to become arrogant and think that it was invincible after it absorbed Su Jian and Bai Dong’s souls.","Lin Yuan learned how Begin Lady felt during their conversations.","This made Lin Yuan believe that Begin Lady had the potential to move forward.","Once an expert became arrogant and adopted the belief that he was undefeatable, it would be very difficult for him to continue advancing.","This was why the Moon Empress always emphasized to Lin Yuan that a spirit qi professional needed to remain humble.","After Begin Lady left, Lin Yuan summoned the Jasmine Lily.","Ever since the Endless Gem unlocked the Jasmine Lily, it became increasingly useful to Lin Yuan.","Now that he had full access to the Jasmine Lily’s abilities, Lin Yuan did not need to contract other healing-type feys.","Out of Wendy, Rising Lizard, and White Pavilion, Lin Yuan’s favorite was Lin Yuan. He adored her as he would a daughter.","But now, Wendy’s neck had almost been pecked through fully by the Drugged Snake Eagles.","They only needed to peck a few centimeters deeper and they would have broken Wendy’s spine and killed it. But, they wanted to keep Wendy alive in order to take it back to their Apostle.","However, Wendy was not in the worst state of the three.","White Pavilion’s white scales had been rotted by the venom that the Drugged Snake Eagles spewed and had turned grayish-green.","Underneath its cracked skin should be red flesh. However, its flesh had turned purplish-gray due to the poison and were leaking brownish-green pus.","It could not be in a more wretched state.","After being subjected to a tornado of the Drugged Snake Eagles’ pecks, Rising Lizard now looked like a peeled carrot. Its body was full of bloody holes.","The longer Lin Yuan looked at their miserable states, the more his heart ached.","In the time that White Pavilion, Rising Lizard, and Wendy had joined him, they never had to suffer such injuries.","While the Jasmine Lily was healing Rising Lizard, Wendy, and White Pavilion, the Kill Food Sky Butterfly flew over to Lin Yuan.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly usually guarded the marsh world in its human form.","Previously, the Kill Food Sky Butterfly had represented Lin Yuan’s top combat power. But now, it barely made the cut to be part of his arsenal.","Lin Yuan had summoned Liu Yanshan out of the marsh world to fetch Liu Lan.","After Liu Yanshan fetched Luo Lan, he was abandoned by Red Thorn.","Lin Yuan had numerous bodies of Eternal experts and had no need for Immortal experts. It would be much more beneficial for the Tongue of Relinquish to infest Eternal experts.","Ever since Lin Yuan discovered the Gardener Konjac’s child ramet in Whale Ocean Commerce and gave it to Red Thorn to absorb, Red Thorn transformed from having just one Tongue of Relinquish in each Mouth of Relinquish to having three.","Soon, the tongue tips of those Tongues of Relinquish would also be able to control bodies.","At that time, Lin Yuan’s subordinates would have sufficient experts to help to guard the territory in the marsh world and the burden would not have to rest so heavily on the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","Lin Yuan would not have to push his ‘daughter-in-law’ so hard.","By the time the Kill Food Sky Butterfly came over to Lin Yuan, Purple Afterglow had flown up from Lin Yuan’s palm.","In a flash, it pressed a peck on the Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s lips.","Purple Afterglow’s actions stunned Lin Yuan. To him, it was an inappropriate action.","Lin Yuan felt certain that if Purple Afterglow and the Kill Food Sky Butterfly remained in the marsh world for a few more years, he would be able to see his ‘grandchildren’.","Lin Yuan did not want to stand here and watch the couple’s public display of affection, albeit he was already used to seeing it.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s face flushed after it was kissed and it hurriedly said to Lin Yuan, “Lin Yuan, I’ll go and clear some of the mess. The Drugged Snake Eagles killed some of the Medusa Snake Demons. Wendy and Rising Lizard’s Favored Believers are fine because they went to investigate the mountain at the back. However, White Pavilion’s Favored Believers had remained close to the territory to help the Spirit Craftsmen. Almost all of White Pavilion’s Favored Believers have been wiped out by the Drugged Snake Eagles. White Pavilion has indeed suffered the most.”","Lin Yuan nodded seriously at the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","Dangers were abound in the marsh world and Apostles were often fighting bloody battles with each other.","After White Speak took over the Dark Scorpion’s territory, it had killed any and all dimensional lifeforms that were linked to the Dark Scorpion.","White Speak’s actions allowed Lin Yuan to understand the culture in the dimensional worlds.","After the Kill Food Sky Butterfly left, Lin Yuan focused on healing the three Apostles.","After being healed by the Jasmine Lily, Wendy, Rising Lizard, and White Pavilion’s vitalities were recovered and their broken bodies were healed.","However, there was nothing that the Jasmine Lily could do about poison.","Ever since the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen absorbed the Vicious Poison Law, Lin Yuan gained a strong resistance to poison.","Hence, he had not collected many spiritual ingredients that could counter poison.","The only spiritual ingredient he had that could counter poison was the nectar produced from the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus’ petals.","However, the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus’ nectar would not be able to cure the Drugged Snake Eagle’s venom.","Luckily, Apostles had body qualities that were nothing to scoff at!","Their newly grown flesh and bodies could continuously counter and remove poison.","However, the cost would be continuous bleeding.","Wendy, Rising Lizard, and White Pavilion only fully recovered after 20 minutes."]},{"number":2144,"title":"Chapter 2144 White Speak’s Broken Arm!","paragraphs":["2144 White Speak’s Broken Arm!","After they recovered, Wendy immediately turned into a small snake and climbed up his left leg to reach his arm and started to affectionately nudge his neck.","Wendy had not seen Lin Yuan in some time and missed Lin Yuan terribly.","After Lin Yuan rescued it from a near-dead state, its affection for Lin Yuan became even more uncontrollable.","After Rising Lizard went over to Lin Yuan, it dared not interact with him.","Rising Lizard had turned into a big killing machine.","Apart from the long horns on its head and spikes jutting from its tail, every protrusion on its skin was a dagger in itself that could easily slice Lin Yuan apart.","Although Lin Yuan could not interact with Lin Yuan and express its affection, anyone who owned a pet dog could tell from its eyes that it was looking at Lin Yuan the same way a puppy would gaze at its owner.","Although White Pavilion was White Speak’s son, they had completely different personalities.","White Pavilion always greeted Lin Yuan enthusiastically.","But this time, it did not move after it recovered and continued to stare dazedly at its feet.","Ever since Lin Yuan heard the Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s report, he knew that White Pavilion was injured.","Although it had become an Apostle, it was still a young dimensional lifeform and its mind was not yet mature.","Lin Yuan walked up to it and squatted down. He stroked White Pavilion’s long snout.","“White Pavilion, every dimensional lifeform has to be able to sustain loss during battle. You might have lost a few Favored Believers but the faith power in your totem hasn’t decreased. You will be able to gain more Favored Believers very soon. All you need to do is work a little harder and you’ll be able to recoup your losses.”","Lin Yuan had comforted White Pavilion in such a way because he knew and could tell what it was thinking.","White Pavilion was an Apostle and did not feel much attachment to its Favored Believers. What it missed was the loss in benefits.","The relationship between Apostles and Favored Believers was one where the Favored Believers did all they could to gain their Apostle’s favor.","Thus, the structure of the marsh world was one that centered around the Apostles’ benefits.","White Pavilion felt slightly better after it was comforted by Lin Yuan.","But this was the first time that it had experienced such a loss and it needed time to readjust back to its normal state.","Lin Yuan let out a sigh.","He had neglected Wendy, Rising Lizard, and White Pavilion’s education because he had not been focusing on the marsh world. As a result, the three of them did not even have the courage to face failure.","Lin Yuan said very seriously to the three of them, “As the three of you become stronger, you will encounter increasingly ferocious opponents. Your life has been too comfortable. You don’t know how weak you truly are. The only way you’ll be able to fight back in similar situations in the future is to work hard to become stronger.”","The three of them took in what Lin Yuan said. They fell silent and started to contemplate over his words.","After the Kill Food Sky Butterfly was done noting the damages sustained, it went to Lin Yuan and said, “Lin Yuan, luckily the Drugged Snake Eagles were focused on Wendy and the rest. The losses sustained by the territory aren’t significant. We only lost four of the Medusa Snake Demons who helped to water the Soldier Ration Radishes and around 40 of the Marsh Crocodiles who were being used to transport resources.”","Lin Yuan nodded.","Such losses were acceptable.","The Medusa Snake Demons were the favorite food of the Drugged Snake Eagles and it was impossible for the Drugged Snake Eagles not to kill them.","With Wendy’s mother, Scale Concubine, around, it was easier to train more of the Marsh Crocodiles who were used to transport resources. All that was needed was time and they could have many of the trained Marsh Crocodiles as they wanted.","Lin Yuan used to think that the territory would be secure as long as White Speak was around to guard it. Thus, he had let his guard down.","This incident was a sobering wake-up call for Lin Yuan.","Wen Yu’s fey with the barren bloodline and the Sentient Being Protective Dragon were both in the marsh world. The loss of either would result in damages to Lin Yuan’s foundational power.","Once such strategic-class resources were lost, they could not be recovered.","Lin Yuan was not appeased by the deaths of the Drugged Snake Eagles.","The Drugged Snake Eagles had said that they were loyal to the Prayer Glow Apostle.","He hoped that he would be able to quell his anger by killing the Prayer Glow Apostle and gain a decent sacred source lifeform at the same time.","The Medusa Snake Demons usually liked to move on their own.","But within the territory, they had become a unit.","This was because there was no competition in the territory, allowing friendship to be bred and deepened amongst the Medusa Snake Demons.","Lin Yuan intended on compensating all of the Medusa Snake Demons in the territory by giving them some of the ripe Storing Ability White Peaches and Deposit Ability Litchi Branches.","Most of the daily tasks in the territory were handled by the Medusa Snake Demons.","The Hundred Questions Beasts were also startled.","Lin Yuan instructed Genius to comfort them.","Lin Yuan prioritized White Speak’s situation over meeting with Jin Qianxun.","At first, Lin Yuan only saw White Speak as a tool.","But after time passed, Lin Yuan developed a relationship with White Speak.","White Speak had helped Lin Yuan substantially.","Without White Speak, both he and the Mother of Bloodbath would have been killed by Shark Awn.","...","On a cliff that was more than a thousand meters tall, the water that fell from it could easily generate enough force to break a steel board.","Due to the inconsistencies of the ground height in the marsh world, waterfalls were commonplace.","However, waterfalls that were more than 1000 meters tall were still rare.","At this moment, a man wearing silver armor with a large hole in his neck was hugging his broken arm.","With his face pale, he was looking at a middle-aged man with plain features and wearing green robes who was standing a distance away.","The middle-aged man had long dark-green hair and a rope of vines was tied through the hole in his wrist.","White Speak’s broken arm was resting on this rope.","White Speak did not come from prestige.","Although it had mutated from the White Evil Marsh Crocodile, it did not have much that allowed it to hold its head up high in front of other dimensional lifeforms.","After a lifetime of fighting, White Speak’s mind was toughened and his will was strong.","At this moment, White Speak was beside himself with anxiousness.","Normally, White Speak could roll grades to do battle when it was boosted by Lin Yuan’s faith power.","But without being boosted by Lin Yuan’s faith power, White Speak struggled to match up to the power of Apostles."]},{"number":2145,"title":"Chapter 2145 Hang Them All!","paragraphs":["2145 Hang Them All!","White Speak had heard of the Prayer Glow Apostle before.","Apparently, it had the support of a Dictator.","Although the Prayer Glow Apostle had not received the dictator’s prize, it had received many other benefits.","White Speak believed that it was going to lose its life to the Prayer Glow Apostle today.","Before it lost an arm, it already stood no chance against the Prayer Glow Apostle. But now that it did not have an arm, the likelihood of it beating the Prayer Glow Apostle was even smaller.","White Speak was partially anxious over its circumstances but more so because the 30 Drugged Snake Eagles sent by the Prayer Glow Apostle had broken through its defenses and flown into the territory.","The Drugged Snake Eagles were greedy robbers that plundered resources wherever they went.","Before White Speak met Lin Yuan, it did not even think about setting up any territories but chose to be a freely roaming Apostle instead because it was afraid of encountering robbers like the Prayer Glow Apostle.","In battles for resources between Apostles, the losing side either died or became bankrupt. There were no other paths.","White Speak had already sworn its loyalty to Lin Yuan.","The glowing dot of light in Lin Yuan’s divine kingdom that represented White Speak’s faith power was one of the ten largest ones.","White Speak was not afraid of dying, rather that its death would be worthless.","If it died in a battle against Prayer Glow, it would have done its duty to Lin Yuan.","However, it had allowed the Drugged Snake Eagles to cause damage to Lin Yuan’s territory. In this aspect, it had betrayed Lin Yuan’s trust.","Once dimensional lifeforms reached the level of Apostle, it became important for them to pass down their bloodline.","White Speak was terrified that White Pavilion would be killed by the Drugged Snake Eagles.","Glowing Prayer looked at White Speak mockingly.","Not only was it stronger than White Speak, but its source sacred body could also counter White Speak’s source sacred body.","In a battle between the two of them, there was no question of who the winner would be.","“White Speak, don’t put the blame on me! It’s almost time for the Banquet of Everything. I have been preparing for this centenary event for 60 years. I hope that your territory is filled with enough goodies so I don’t end up wasting my time and energy by coming over here.","“To tell you the truth, I’m very curious. You’re the type of Apostle who trains hard and roams around. What made you willing to start managing a territory? Is it possible that there’s a treasure in this territory? If so, it will soon become mine.”","White Speak had encountered Prayer Glow when it had still been a nomad.","Prayer Glow had been very friendly and had even given it some gifts.","The gifts that Prayer Glow had given it allowed Prayer Glow to tell what kind of circumstances it had.","White Speak did not like to be tied down but placed great importance on kinship and ties. Thus, White Speak found Prayer Glow’s actions to be very despicable.","White Speak knew that it was no match for Prayer Glow and that it was likely going to be killed.","Nonetheless, White Speak still spoke sarcastically. “To my memory, your Dictator isn’t Dictator Everything. But you’re still putting so much effort into the Banquet of Everything. The Banquet of Everything is basically an event for Dictator Everything to gather wealth. Won’t the Dictator you serve be upset by how much time you’ve put into preparing for the Banquet of Everything?”","Prayer Glow’s expression shifted. Its heart skipped a beat.","Dictators usually did not place many restraints on the Apostles that served them.","But once their Apostles made any mistakes, they would have to face severe punishments.","When Prayer Glow went to beg Dictator Return to Ruins, who it served, Dictator Return to Ruins had refused to see it.","There was always stiff competition among the Apostles who served the same Dictator.","When they oppressed other Apostles, they would be able to obtain more benefits from their Dictator.","Prayer Glow suspected that someone had spoken ill of it to Dictator Return to Ruins.","Unlike Dictator Everything, Dictator Return to Ruins had not entered the Turning Wheel Realm and was thus not as reliable.","Moreover, it could trade for resources at the Banquet of Everything, which would help it to increase its power.","Prayer Glow had already offered up its loyalty and faith to Dictator Return to Ruins, so it could not join Dictator Everything’s camp.","Prayer Glow only hoped that it would not displease Dictator Everything by collecting resources for the Banquet of Everything.","Its contributions to Dictator Return to Ruins had always been significant.","White Speak’s words drummed up worry within Prayer Glow, and its look of amusement changed into fury.","“White Speak, you’d better save your concern for yourself! Your arm will probably allow me to trade for useful resources at the Banquet of Everything.”","While it spoke, Prayer Glow decided not to waste time spouting nonsense to White Speak.","White Speak had a forked tongue and knew exactly what Prayer Glow did not want to hear.","Thus, if they continued speaking, Prayer Glow’s anger would only grow.","Prayer Glow raised its left hand and tugged at the vine tied around its wrist as it yelled, “Let’s compare the quality of poison. Hang them all!”","Previously, Prayer Glow’s aim had been White Speak’s arm. But now, it was White Speak’s neck.","Before making its move, the totem of an ancient tree with glowing flaming branches on Prayer Glow’s body started to shake.","The glowing flames caused the totem to appear more vibrant and beautiful.","White Speak was not the type to be a sitting duck.","Despite knowing that the likelihood of it losing was high, White Speak still assumed its battle stance to prepare for the final fight.","At that moment, a stream of pink and gold water appeared next to Prayer Glow.","The water turned into a rope that wrapped around Prayer Glow.","The pink and gold flames that burned all over the rope caused Prayer Glow to lose control over its own strength. As a result, it was unable to release the attack it had intended for White Speak.","The instant that White Speak saw the pink and gold stream of water, it felt a sense of relief and conclusion.","Begin Lady’s figure appeared next to the captured Prayer Glow.","Begin Lady looked at White Speak and said in a monotonous voice, “I’m a little late. I was sent by Lin Yuan.”","Begin Lady seemed to remember something and went on to say, “Your son, White Pavilion, is fine. Although it sustained some injuries, Lin Yuan was able to heal it easily.”","After absorbing the souls of two adults, Begin Lady understood relationships and knew what White Speak was worried about. Thus, there was no need for it to wait for White Speak to pose any questions.","A smile spread across White Speak’s pale face, and it said, “You aren’t late. This is the first time I’m learning how good it feels to receive help during a crisis. I should actually be thanking the idiot you captured. If it had not blathered on for so long, you wouldn’t have been able to reach in time to save me.”"]},{"number":2146,"title":"Chapter 2146 Dictator Return to Ruins?","paragraphs":["2146 Dictator Return to Ruins?","White Speak walked over to Prayer Glow.","In the past, it has been as weak as one of Prayer Glow’s subordinates.","Its source sacred body was completely countered by Prayer Glow. White Speak could not come up with any way to take on Prayer Glow.","But now, the situation had changed.","Prayer Glow was now a trapped fish that White Speak could tear away as it pleased.","White Speak kicked Prayer Glow forcefully to vent some of its rage before it ripped its torn-off arm from Prayer Glow’s vines.","In the past, tearing off its arm would have had a serious impact on White Speak. With the loss of a limb, its combat power would be significantly discounted.","However, White Speak had seen Lin Yuan regrow missing limbs.","Lin Yuan was the Dictator who White Speak had dedicated its life to. In its eyes, there was nothing that Lin Yuan could not do.","If Lin Yuan was willing to be kind, he would help it to re-attach its arm.","Begin Lady’s appearance meant that Lin Yuan had already settled things on the other side and that the 30 Drugged Snake Eagles had not caused much trouble for Lin Yuan at all.","White Speak smirked when it saw Prayer Glow’s look of astonished sadness as it was trapped within the stream of water.","Dictator Return to Ruins was the most well-known Dictator in the Marsh East Circle. However, his power as a Dictator was not considered strong.","Many Dictators liked to keep clean and disliked being associated with too many Apostles.","But the Apostles who they did end up associating with were usually gifted the dictator’s prize.","However, Dictator Return to Ruins did not have any preference and accepted all Apostles that came its way.","Otherwise, given its power, Prayer Glow would never have been able to join the camp of a Dictator.","If Prayer Glow knew that while gathering resources for the Banquet of Everything, it would end up encountering a Dictator like Lin Yuan who had entered the Turning Wheel Realm, it would not have charged in so rashly.","At that moment, Prayer Glow shouted, “No matter who you are, I am an Apostle under Dictator Return to Ruins! How dare you lay a hand on me? Aren’t you afraid of facing Dictator Return to Ruins’ wrath?”","White Speak felt disgusted when it heard Prayer Glow use Dictator Return to Ruins as a desperate threat.","It snapped sardonically, “It doesn’t matter if Dictator Return to Ruins will come after us. A more important question is what Dictator Return to Ruins will do to a piece of trash like you who hasn’t even received the dictator’s prize when he learns that you used his name to make empty threats. Do you really think our Dictator will be afraid of Dictator Return to Ruins?”","White Speak forcefully kicked Prayer Glow a few more times.","Begin Lady smiled and shook its head.","White Speak’s actions indicated that its psychological and physical state had not been greatly affected by the loss of its arm.","“White Speak, go back with me! Lin Yuan will only be put at ease when he sees you.”","White Speak was ashamed that it caused Lin Yuan to worry over it. But at the same time, it was touched.","In Begin Lady’s eyes, Prayer Glow was no different from a corpse.","When Begin Lady was sent over, it could sense how furious Lin Yuan was.","If Prayer Glow did not die, the deaths of the four Medusa Snake Demons would not be compensated.","While Begin Lady and White Speak were rushing back to Lin Yuan, Prayer Glow was frozen and dazed by what Prayer Glow said.","Prayer Glow saw White Speak as an endless source of wealth.","It had set its eyes on White Speak soon after they became acquainted.","Moreover, from what White Speak said, White Speak’s Dictator did not think much of Dictator Return to Ruins. This meant that he had to be stronger than Dictator Return to Ruins.","Oh no! Just who did I piss off?","When it heard what White Speak and the ridiculously strong girl said, Prayer Glow had a feeling that it was about to meet the Dictator who White Speak had sworn its loyalty to.","After this thought, Prayer Glow was so frightened that it almost passed out.","Prayer Glow never wondered if White Speak could be lying.","No Apostle would dare to joke or lie about such a thing.","Soon, Begin Lady and White Speak appeared in front of Lin Yuan.","Rising Lizard, Wendy, and White Pavilion were next to him.","When it spotted White Speak, White Pavilion immediately crawled over to its father.","It slammed its tail on the ground when it saw White Speak’s severed arm.","Luckily, the ground was covered in a layer of the Marsh Ground Sphagna.","The Marsh Ground Sphagna had reached Class 11. Otherwise, White Pavilion’s tail would have opened a hole in the marsh world’s soft ground.","White Pavilion had always been playful but was also fearful of White Speak.","Nonetheless, White Pavilion’s affection for its father was not lacking in the slightest.","Before White Speak greeted him, Lin Yuan stood up and said, “Position your arm on the wound!”","Lin Yuan instructed the Jasmine Lily to release a beam of vitality that healed White Speak’s wounds and severed arm.","With Severed Limbs Growth, White Speak’s severed arm could have been quickly regrown.","But since White Speak had brought its arm back, there was no need to use Severed Limbs Growth, and the Jasmine Lily’s energy could be saved.","It did not take White Speak’s arm to heal and become as good as new.","Lin Yuan’s action had shocked Prayer Glow to the core.","With the Apostles Wendy, Rising Lizard, and White Pavilion next to him, there was no question of Lin Yuan’s status as a Dictator.","Prayer Glow had been traversing the marsh world for a very long time, but this was the first time it was seeing Apostles of such low Class.","It realized that it could not get a sense of Lin Yuan’s aura. It was as though Lin Yuan did not carry any hint of being a dimensional lifeform.","This young man White Speak had addressed as ‘Lord Lin Yuan’, had the exact same features as a Dictator who had entered the legendary Turning Wheel Realm.","While Prayer Glow was observing Lin Yuan, it met his eyes.","His gaze was composed, but there seemed to be a steaming volcano under the calmness.","When it saw Lin Yuan looking at Prayer Glow, White Speak hurriedly said, “Lord Lin Yuan, Prayer Glow is a devious snake! It suddenly led its Favored Believers over in a large group because it had started targeting me over a century ago. Its source sacred body can counter mine. Otherwise, I wouldn’t be as helpless as I was.”","Lin Yuan’s gaze turned cold.","He did not like those who were wicked and devious. But he had no choice but to admit that such people were everywhere in a place like the marsh world where competition was so stiff"]},{"number":2147,"title":"Chapter 2147 A Punch For Your Head!","paragraphs":["2147 A Punch For Your Head!","White Speak had started assuming some time ago that Lin Yuan was a Dictator who had entered the Turning Wheel Realm.","Otherwise, a Dictator like Lin Yuan should not have so little individual power.","When Dictators entered the Turning Wheel Realm, they would have to start over.","While White Speak was speaking to Prayer Glow, its words indicated that it was not concerned by Dictator Return to Ruins.","But White Speak was still afraid that Dictator Return to Ruins would eventually target Lin Yuan because of Prayer Glow.","“Lord Lin Yuan, there is a Dictator behind Apostle Prayer Glow. However, Apostle Prayer Glow hasn’t received the dictator’s prize.”","White Speak dared not say anything else and waited for Lin Yuan to decide on how they would handle Prayer Glow.","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow when he heard that Prayer Glow was part of a Dictator’s camp.","Until now, Lin Yuan had yet to see what a true Dictator looked like or was capable of.","In the past, Lin Yuan would have been envious of a Dictator from the marsh world.","After all, the marsh world was not Lin Yuan’s world but a world of dimensional lifeforms.","But now that he had Begin Lady, he found it hard to believe that a Dictator could be stronger than it.","He could gauge from his discussions with White Speak and Shadow that Dictators were about as powerful as Eternal experts.","Dictators who had entered the Turning Wheel Realm were beyond Eternal.","However, that was not to say that there were no Dictators who were beyond Eternal power but had not entered the Turning Wheel Realm. After all, not every Dictator had the courage to give up everything and start fresh.","Hence, Lin Yuan could confidently take on Dictators with Begin Lady by his side.","Compared to Dictator Return to Ruins, who had yet to show its face, Lin Yuan was more interested in seeing what abilities Prayer Glow’s source sacred body had.","“Since Dictator Return to Ruins was the one who sent its people here to cause trouble, it is the one who owes me an explanation. White Speak, you mentioned that its source sacred body can counter yours. What abilities does it have?”","White Speak’s chest tightened when it thought back to Prayer Glow’s source sacred body’s abilities.","In honesty, Prayer Glow’s abilities countered not only its own but also that of other Apostles.","“Lord Dictator, Prayer Glow’s true body is a rare carnivorous plant called the Firefly Poison Weeping Fig. As its power increases, it will attract more firefly-species poisonous insects to live with it. Together, they will form one living body. The Firefly Poison Weeping Fig isn’t venomous on its own, but as more firefly-species poisonous insects gather around it, it will be affected and become more poisonous. It will then become a carnivorous plant that can kill targets with poison.","“Most dimensional lifeforms don’t produce venom naturally after becoming Apostles. Prayer Glow has never failed to take down any Apostle using its deadly attacks. Otherwise, Prayer Glow wouldn’t be able to take my arm in a physical fight no matter how hard it tried.”","White Speak spoke clearly and allowed Lin Yuan to immediately understand what Prayer Glow was capable of.","After killing Prayer Glow, the sacred source lifeform that came from its body would likely come with lethal poisonous attacks.","Such a sacred source lifeform would only be suited for contraction by lifeforms who possessed strong venom.","It would be useless if such a sacred source lifeform was not used properly. If so, it might be better not to contract it.","But if it could be used properly, it would be able to suppress enemies as well as Prayer Glow had been doing to White Speak.","Dimensional lifeforms were not capable of contracting sacred source lifeforms.","The only people in Lin Yuan’s camp who could fight with poison were Qin Lun and Qin Yu, as both had contracted the extremely venomous Polar Night Blue Sky Scorpions.","The Polar Night Blue Sky Scorpions were not as skilled at wielding venom as they were at dark-type energy.","There was no question that dark-type sacred source lifeforms were more useful for Qin Lun and Qin Yu.","Hence, after killing Prayer Glow, its only use would be increasing Lin Yuan’s store of sacred source lifeforms.","When Prayer Glow heard Lin Yuan ask White Speak about its source sacred body abilities, it was so frightened that its entire body started to tremble.","There could only be one reason for a Dictator to ask about an Apostle’s abilities.","He was likely thinking about how he was going to use Prayer Glow after its death.","Prayer Glow’s biggest hope was that it would be able to save itself and earn the chance to continue living.","A lifeform that spent its entire life scheming after others in order to secure its own profits was far more afraid of death than White Speak, who spent its entire life fighting as hard as it could.","Prayer Glow asked tentatively, “Lord Dictator, I...”","Lin Yuan wanted to obtain more information from Prayer Glow. However, it was unlikely that Prayer Glow knew much about Dictator Return to Ruins.","The crisis of the marsh world was about to be fully resolved.","Before White Speak met Lin Yuan, it brought White Pavilion around with it as they fought their way through life.","After they met Lin Yuan, they started residing in Dark Scorpion’s territory. Thus, they were not updated on the latest information in the marsh world.","Prayer Glow spent its life scheming, and the first condition it needed to fulfill in order to do so was to have sufficient information.","Lin Yuan needed to possess sufficient information before he could attend the Banquet of Everything.","Lin Yuan glanced at White Speak, and White Speak immediately knew what Lin Yuan was planning.","Lin Yuan had asked it a lot about the Marsh East Circle. But there were many questions that","White Speak had been unable to answer.","But now, with Prayer Glow, Lin Yuan could gather more information.","When Lin Yuan saw that White Speak understood what his intentions were, he immediately left the marsh world and returned to the underground palace.","White Speak readied itself for battle and walked over to Prayer Glow. It smiled menacingly and said, “You will answer everything I’m about to ask you! If anything you say is wrong, I will gently punch your head! Whether you’ll be able to survive depends on how you answer.”","Prayer Glow’s lips twitched when it heard what White Speak said.","White Speak was very strong, and even a gentle punch of it would carry 500 kilograms of force.","It had removed White Speak’s arm and almost killed it. One could only imagine how much White Speak hated it.","Was it really going to just give it a gentle punch?","Lin Yuan had not said that he wanted Prayer Glow to be kept alive.","Prayer Glow guessed that White Speak could not make the decision to kill it without its Dictator’s permission.","Thus, Prayer Glow intended to respond honestly to everything that White Speak was about to ask.","Nothing was more important than surviving!"]},{"number":2148,"title":"Chapter 2148 Didn’t Expect You To Live!","paragraphs":["2148 Didn’t Expect You To Live!","However, Prayer Glow did not expect to be questioned by White Speak for hours.","White Speak had started out with normal questions that made Prayer Glow think that White Speak was just having fun.","But once the normal questions were over, White Speak’s questions became increasingly more difficult to stomach.","Each time Prayer Glow hesitated, White Speak would slam its fist down on Prayer Glow’s head.","After multiple painful punches, bumps were now covering Prayer Glow’s head.","Even if White Speak asked extremely sensitive questions, Prayer Glow answered them all.","But once the sensitive questions were over, White Speak started to ask increasingly senseless queries. No matter how hard Prayer Glow racked its brain, it could not come up with the answers.","Even when Prayer Glow had been beaten to the point of dizziness, White Speak continued to pose its questions.","Prayer Glow did not know that from the moment White Speak asked its first question, it had no intention of allowing Prayer Glow to survive.","“Does Dictator Return to Ruins have smelly feces?”","Prayer Glow had been about to lose consciousness, but when it heard this question, it immediately realized what White Speak’s intention was.","Prayer Glow wanted to start hurling insults at White Speak but did not have the strength to do so.","The fist attacks were turning into arm ones.","A splintering sound filled the air when White Speak slammed its forearm down on Prayer Glow’s head.","After killing Prayer Glow, White Speak started to absorb the source-type power from Prayer Glow’s body.","The totem and faith power from Prayer Glow’s body solidified into an amber-colored item.","But before White Speak could clearly see the amber-colored item, it was enveloped in rainbow light.","White Speak gave Prayer Glow’s body, which had turned into a sacred source lifeform to Begin Lady.","At this point, White Speak had accomplished Lin Yuan’s task and was about to return to continue guarding the territory.","This encounter with Prayer Glow caused White Speak to lose almost half of its Favored Believers. This would affect its rate of collection of faith power in the future.","White Speak intended to increase its power before it went with Lin Yuan to the Marsh East Circle to attend the Banquet of Everything.","...","Lin Yuan had been away from the underground palace for a day.","Jin Qianxun had sent many messages today, but Su Yiren had only replied to them and not answered any of Jin Qianxun’s questions because Lin Yuan was not around.","Su Yiren guessed that Jin Qianxun must be in a quagmire of complicated emotions at the moment.","It was likely that he was afraid of being tossed aside by Lin Yuan.","Su Yiren also had no idea what was running through Lin Yuan’s mind.","But given what she had learned about him, she felt that he would have been straightforward if he had no intention of fulfilling his promise to Jin Qianxun. He would not mercilessly leave Jin Qianxun hanging.","Currently, Jin Qianxun did not have an ounce of value.","As Su Yiren waited in Lin Yuan’s room, she saw that a message had come through on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","[Lin Yuan: I’m sorry! I was held back for a day because of one of my people, which caused you to wait for so long. To make it up to you, I’ll give you the chance to pick 50 of the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.]","Su Yiren’s eyes widened when she saw the words on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","It turned out that Jin Qianxun did have value. Lin Yuan even allowed him to earn 50 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","From Lin Yuan’s compensation, it was clear that he intended to value the promise.","Lin Yuan’s attitude toward Jin Qianxun set Su Yiren at ease.","If Lin Yuan fulfilled the promise of someone as insignificant as Jin Qianxun, it went without saying that he would do the same for someone like her who was in his inner circle.","Su Yiren guessed that Jin Qianxun would be holding onto the Thoughts Letter Paper tightly and anxiously as he awaited Lin Yuan’s reply.","The truth was just as Su Yiren guessed.","After a day on edge, Jin Qianxun forcefully suppressed his excitement after seeing Lin Yuan’s response on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Otherwise, he would already have jumped up and started shouting in joy.","Lin Yuan’s compensation caused Jin Qianxun to explode with excitement.","He could pick 50 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls that were all the standard of Class 5 Creation Master resources.","But compared to such compensation, Jin Qianxun was delighted that Lin Yuan had not forgotten his promise.","If Lin Yuan broke the promise, there was nothing that Jin Qianxun could do about it.","Lin Yuan’s message gave Jin Qianxun the courage to consider the sight of himself sitting on the Great Lush Federation’s throne.","He was so excited that he replied to Lin Yuan’s message with a very long response.","When Lin Yuan read Jin Qianxun’s reply, he could sense how Jin Qianxun was feeling.","Lin Yuan decided not to reply to Jin Qianxun. Rather, he led Su Yiren and Liu Jie toward where the Great Lush Federation’s secret aristocratic families were residing.","Su Yiren was silent for a moment before she finally decided to speak. “Young Master, I don’t think Jin Qianxun will be able to hold the fort down if he enters the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court. Not only does he lack power, but more importantly, he also doesn’t have the will for the job.”","Su Yiren had not wanted to say this.","She and Jin Qianxun had dedicated their loyalties to Lin Yuan. By saying this, she was shining the light of suspicion on him.","However, she had always been the bridge of communication between Lin Yuan and Jin Qianxun.","If she did not inform Lin Yuan of the issues she had spotted, it could end up hurting Lin Yuan.","She came from a federation with a Class 5 Creation Master and was also the granddaughter of that Class 5 Creation Master. Thus, she was always able to see the big picture.","Jin Qianxun’s lack of power could be easily made up for. All he needed was an expert to accompany him and secure the situation.","But the key point was that Jin Qianxun did not have the will to hold down the fort.","Will and power were completely different matters.","This was why it was always said that rulers needed to be intimidating and resolute.","Yi Huailong was not strong either, but he had the authoritative air that Jin Qianxun lacked.","Although Yi Huailu was a Class 5 Creation Master, he was too mild-mannered to control the imperial court like Yi Huailong could.","Lin Yuan was also aware of this and had found a partner for Jin Qianxun long ago.","Bai Qinghuan was skilled at strategy and could not contribute much unless there was an ongoing battle.","Even if Bai Qinghuan was able to see the entire world as a chess game, she was still too young.","Without experience, her intelligence and resolution would be limited.","Lin Yuan did not intend to send Bai Qinghuan to Jin Qianxun so she could balance him out but so she could find a good school."]},{"number":2149,"title":"Chapter 2149 One’s Will Can Always be Imposed on Another","paragraphs":["2149 One’s Will Can Always be Imposed on Another","Bai Qinghuan’s way of looking at things would also affect Jin Qianxun to a certain extent. Under her influence, he would handle matters with a firmer hand.","Ever since Lin Yuan suggested that Liu Jie learned from Bai Qinghuan, Liu Jie had improved significantly in terms of managerial skills.","With the Thoughts Letter Paper, Liu Jie could continue to learn from Bai Qinghuan even if they were not physically together.","Bai Qinghuan had sworn her loyalty to Lin Yuan, so there was no reason for him not to trust her.","She still did not have the Thoughts Letter Paper, but it was time that one was made for her.","Lin Yuan could sense that Bai Qinghuan had been working hard to mix in with the other members of Sky City. All she lacked was a chance.","After all, there were not many areas in which she had the opportunity to prove her wealth.","Bai Qinghuan was a smart person.","If he sent her to the Great Lush Federation, she would definitely understand what his plans were.","Once she arrived at the Great Lush Federation, she would not feel as insecure as she was now.","Lin Yuan smiled at Su Yiren.","“I know what you mean. I have already made plans for Jin Qianxun.”","Su Yiren realized she had been concerned for nothing.","Given Lin Yuan’s brain and abilities, there was no way he would not have seen through Jin Qianxun’s flaws.","Liu Jie had yet to communicate directly with Jin Qianxun, but he knew who he was. He felt that Jin Qianxun was a lucky fellow. Technically, he should have been killed by Di Wanmi back in Oak City.","Liu Jie could guess what kind of relationship existed between the Great Lush Federation’s secret aristocratic families.","“The disappearance of the Truth Association has also removed their hold over the Great Lush Federation. Now that the secret aristocratic families are free, all of them will make a grab for power. This will probably be the most chaotic time in the Great Lush Federation. Someone will need to step in to smoothen out the mess.","“Lin Yuan, I think the other families need to be cleared out before Jin Qianxun can take the throne and the Jin family be boosted into the imperial court. Even if you place an expert by his side to bolster his might, he still won’t be acknowledged by the other top secret aristocratic families.”","Lin Yuan saw that Liu Jie had indeed improved after his time with Bai Qinghuan.","Normally, Liu Jie never interjected in his conversations with Su Yiren.","However, Liu Jie’s assessment of the situation was too simplified.","Given the martial force that Lin Yuan possessed, it would not be difficult to eliminate the secret aristocratic families who were stronger than the Jin family. But if he did that, the loss of the Great Lush Federation’s top combat power would be a serious blow to the Great Lush Federation.","Presently, the entire Startling Lines Continent was part of Lin Yuan’s wealth. It would not make sense for him to get rid of the experts who were part of this wealth.","“Due to the death of Fifth Page Truth, there probably aren’t many leaders of the secret aristocratic families left. We can choose the strongest members of the secret aristocratic families and place them as the heads of their families. Then, we’ll have them swear their loyalty to Jin Qianxun.”","Liu Jie was silent for a moment before he said, “Will the leaders of secret aristocratic families who are stronger than Jin Qianxun truly be willing to swear their loyalty to him?”","“Big Brother Liu, have you heard that one’s will can always be imposed on another? As long as pressure is exerted, profits will follow. The people who only just managed to become heads of their secret aristocratic families know what the right choice will be. None of them will be willing to give up the chance they struggled so hard to obtain.","“Every secret aristocratic family has numerous chambers of commerce under them. Lin Yuan wants to control the trade in the entire Startling Lines Continent. To do this, he will need help from the secret aristocratic families,” replied Su Yiren.","Liu Jie clapped his forehead when he heard what Su Yiren said.","He had indeed thought too little about the matter!","Wen Yu, Su Yiren, and Bai Qinghuan all possessed impressive intelligence and capabilities.","However, their specialties were all different.","Liu Jie felt that the changes he had gone through were partly due to his focus on studying and also because these outstanding people around him had influenced him.","Liu Jie and Su Yiren were both family to Lin Yuan. Thus, he would not hide anything from them.","“Big Brother Liu and Yiren, our main objective for going to the Great Lush Federation is to find the Class 5 Creation Master who worked under Fifth Page Truth. I don’t think that the factions of the Great Lush Federation will be in too much of a mess. The Class 5 Creation Master will definitely have taken control after Fifth Page Truth died.”","Liu Jie and Su Yiren’s eyes lit up when they heard what Lin Yuan said. Both of them realized that the situation was more perilous than expected.","Su Yiren had investigated Tower Canon and knew that every member was a Class 5 Creation Master.","Su Yiren had assumed that Fifth Page Truth was behind all of the Truth Association’s Class 5 Creation Master resources. She had not even imagined that there could be another Class 5 Creation Master under Fifth Page Truth.","Sky City now had two Class 5 Creation Masters.","If Lin Yuan could recruit the Class 5 Creation Master who had been under Fifth Page Truth, it would mean that Sky City would have three Class 5 Creation Masters!","With three Class 5 Creation Masters in the same faction, the faction would have the same Creation Master capabilities as top federations like the Radiance Federation, Freedom Federation, and Azure Federation.","Amidst her shock, a thought struck Su Yiren, and she frowned before saying to Lin Yuan urgently, “The Truth Association’s Class 5 Creation Master must have heard of Fifth Page Truth’s death. Will they go into hiding after finally escaping Fifth Page Truth’s clutches? A Class 5 Creation Master is also a powerful expert. If they deliberately try to hide, it’ll be difficult to sniff them out. Fifth Page Truth’s death is a warning to the Class 5 Creation Master that the Truth Association has crossed an enemy they should have left alone.”","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow and replied calmly, “I don’t think that Class 5 Creation Master will do so. Every Class 5 Creation Master is acutely aware of their value. Rather than hiding in the crowd and living each day filled with anxiety, it’ll be better to leverage their value to obtain even more benefits.”","Lin Yuan had encountered his fair share of Class 5 Creation Masters and could understand where their arrogance came from."]},{"number":2150,"title":"Chapter 2150 Master, You’re Unfocused!","paragraphs":["2150 Master, You’re Unfocused!","An expert who did not distinguish themselves could never lay eyes on a Class 5 Creation Master.","Meanwhile, Lin Yuan had met more Class 5 Creation Masters than he could count on one hand.","Aside from the Moon Empress, Chef Supreme, and Bamboo Monarch, Lin Yuan also had Di Wanmi and Yi Huailu as his subordinates.","The Goddess of Mercy and Fifth Page Truth had not had their eyes on Lin Yuan.","One of them had been killed by him.","!!","Lin Yuan was acquainted with enough Class 5 Creation Masters to support seven large federations.","When Lin Yuan killed Fifth Page Truth, he had thought about taking control of Fifth Page Truth’s body using the Tongue of Relinquish.","Alas, Red Thorn made it clear that it could not take control of experts who had unlocked their spirit attribute. Otherwise, Lin Yuan would not have instructed Begin Lady to burn Fifth Page Truth’s body to ashes.","But no matter how many Class 5 Creation Masters Lin Yuan was acquainted with, he would never be able to leverage his personal Class 5 Creation Master power in a critical situation like Fifth Page Truth had done.","In a society where Class 5 Creation Masters were scarce, every Class 5 Creation Master could carry their own arrogance.","Lin Yuan hoped that Fifth Page Truth’s Class 5 Creation Master would not be too puffed up on arrogance.","If they were too full of themselves and had not awakened their birth horoscope, Lin Yuan did not mind bestowing the same existence on the Class 5 Creation Master as the one that Di Wanmi was experiencing.","A puppet with no potential would be more beneficial to Sky City than a recalcitrant living person.","...","Jin Qianxun relaxed when he received Lin Yuan’s response.","Now that he was at ease, Jin Qianxun continued as his old self. He played it safe as he waited for Lin Yuan to come and help.","The Jin family did not have many members, but with Jin Qianxun’s earnest protection, they had more direct and collateral members in total than the other secret aristocratic families who had participated in the scuffle for resources.","Jin Qianding was dead by the time Fifth Page Truth died.","Jin Qianxing had been killed by Jin Qianding when he voiced his opposition.","Jin Qianxun used his seniority and status to seat himself as the head of the Jin family with no competition.","While Jin Qianxun was playing it safe, in a tent far away, a white-haired elderly man with a hunched back was sighing over a failed crystal bottle of spirit fluid.","The elderly man sighed and pushed the crystal bottle into the young man’s arms.","“You sure are daring now to have the courage to try and give me advice! I might not be at peace, but it’s still a Grade 4 spirit fluid. Store it away! When the other side arrives, offer up the spirit fluids on my behalf.”","The young man tugged at his hair distractedly as he reluctantly said, “Master, why are we giving away spirit fluids all of a sudden? You’re a Class 5 Creation Master—”","Before the young man could finish speaking, he was interrupted by the elderly man. “After working all my life, all I want is peace. I don’t want to fight anymore! How can I put on airs as a Class 5 Creation Master in front of someone who managed to kill Fifth Page War?","“Baochuan, I have been teaching you Creation Master skills. Today, let me teach you that true talent recognizes their circumstances. After I offer up my sincerity, I’m sure the other side won’t disappoint me!”","After the last word fell from his lips, the elderly man realized that he felt slightly calmer.","He took out another set of exactly the same spiritual ingredients as before and started the concoction process.","Next to him, the young man looked thoughtful. He seemed to be mulling over what the elderly man had said.","At the same time, he was curious about the kind of person who had managed to kill Fifth Page Truth.","While the young man was ruminating, the elderly man placed the newly concocted potion into the young man’s hands and said, “Look, Baochuan. Haven’t I calmed down now? Go and call over the leaders of the secret aristocratic families. I won’t be able to express my sincerity by just handing out potions. We can prepare another gift before the other side arrives.”","The young man seemed to only partially take in what the elderly man said. But he still left to gather the leaders of the secret aristocratic families.","But he did not feel a hint of embarrassment. Rather, there was a genuine sense of self-importance.","Normally, the leaders of secret aristocratic families would do anything to earn an audience with his master.","The young man did not understand why the leaders of the secret aristocratic families had to be called over when they offered up gifts to the conquerer.","It did not take long for the leaders of the secret aristocratic families, Jin Qianxun included, to arrive nervously at the elderly man’s tent.","Previously, the elderly man had been a legend in the Truth Association. Only the now-dead previous clan leaders had been able to meet with the elderly man.","Given that Jin Qianxun had only taken up his position recently, he had not had the chance to participate in such meetings before.","Before he came, Jin Qianxun sent a message to Lin Yuan.","Frankly, Jin Qianxun did not want to come to the elderly man’s tent.","His hope was that everything would remain calm until Lin Yuan arrived because even the smallest of waves would jeopardize his safety and plans.","Nonetheless, Jin Qianxun dared not ignore the elderly man’s summons.","The elderly man looked at the group of family heads standing in front of him and sighed. “There are so few familiar faces this time. I called you over because I have something that I need you to do.”","The elderly man’s voice was kind and friendly. Yet, his words caused anxiousness to rise within every member of his audience.","All the leaders of the secret aristocratic families had guessed the reason for being called over.","On the one hand, they were afraid that the elderly man would make requests that they could not fulfill yet could not turn down.","The Hou family was currently the strongest secret aristocratic family and the family participating in the internal fight with the most vigor.","The Hou family’s bid for power had already affected the other factions.","The Hou family’s current leader, Hou Meng, had long aimed to enter the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court.","Hou Meng knew that setting an example at such a time would encourage the other family leaders to acknowledge him.","“Elder Weng, what do you want us to do? If it’s something achievable, just say the word, and we will definitely do everything we can!”"]},{"number":2151,"title":"Chapter 2151 If Someone is Acting Out of Character, There Must Be Someone Behind Him!","paragraphs":["2151 If Someone is Acting Out of Character, There Must Be Someone Behind Him!","The elderly man looked at Hou Meng.","At his age, the elderly man had experienced almost everything that life had to offer.","After such a long life, the elderly man now prioritized peace and stability.","Although he never left his tent, he often sent his retainer out to gather information.","When the two retainers outside the tent received any information, they would report it to the elderly man instantly.","Thus, the elderly man knew what Hou Meng’s aim was for being the first to speak out.","Hou Meng’s expression immediately changed to panic when he caught sight of the elderly man’s look. However, he quickly composed himself.","Nonetheless, his expression was now more pleasant and humble than it had been before.","The elderly man ignored Hou Meng and stood up from the chair as he said in a calm voice, “Each of you will be in charge of a direction. You will set out in that direction and inform any tents you see to pack up. Then, return home and do a headcount of all your family members. Finally, go into military formation along with your family members.”","The elderly man gently rapped the table thrice to signal that he was done speaking to them.","All of the heads of families, including Hou Meng and Jin Qianxun, were bewildered by what the elderly man said.","But since the elderly man had knocked on the table thrice, it was clear that he no longer wanted to speak. Thus, none of them dared to ask the elderly man what he meant.","All they could do was treat the elderly man’s words as an imperial order that they had to carry out no matter what.","All of the people present had the status and power to take up the position of the head of their families. Thus, none of them were stupid. All of them knew that one word from the elderly man would be enough to strip them of their position.","Many of them, like Hou Meng, were hoping that they would be able to lead their family into the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court.","But in order to truly secure their seat on the throne, the elderly man’s support was a necessity.","It could be said that regardless of the strength of the family, it could legitimately claim the throne as long as it had the elderly man’s support.","Even if other families were stronger, they would not dare to utter a peep.","As such, all the families did all they could to try and earn the elderly man’s support.","But given their statuses, it would not be easy to make contact with someone of the elderly man’s level.","But now that the elderly man had taken the initiative to make contact with them, many of them saw this as their chance.","Regardless of whether they were afraid of the elderly man or wanted to curry favor with him, the leaders of the secret aristocratic families trampled over each other to carry out the elderly man’s command despite not being certain of the reason behind it.","“Master, all of their intentions are written all over their faces. If Fifth Page Truth was around, none of them would carry such expressions. He would never permit such expressions and ambitions. If the expert who killed Fifth Page Truth is after the Great Lush Federation, there’s no way they will let these people go.”","The elderly man shook his head gently.","“Baochuan, you have been by my side all this time, but you’ve never truly come across someone willing to give up everything for profit and power. Do you really think none of them have guessed the reason behind Fifth Page Truth’s death? We are not the only ones who are aware of the happenings in the Divine Wood Federation. So are they.","“The person who killed Fifth Page Truth also placed Yi Huailong on the throne. This means that they plan to control the federations. These people are just fighting to try and decide who the leader should be. If the person who killed Fifth Page War doesn’t have any strategic plans for the Great Lush Federation, they will recruit the leader who emerged from the fight. The winner of the fight will have proved their power.”","The young man was stunned by what the elderly man said. But he found his master’s words reasonable and hurriedly nodded and said, “Master, they should indeed fight it out. At least they will be able to carve out a future for themselves. My money is on Hou Meng! He is the strongest, and it was clear from just now that he has an authoritative aura even amongst the other heads of the secret aristocratic families. If he’s selected and becomes the king of the Great Lush Federation, we will have to socialize with him often in the future.”","The longer the elderly man listened, the more he felt that his disciple was much too innocent.","He gently patted the young man’s head and said, “Baochuan, you’re too young! It looks like I’ll need to push you to experience more of life apart from just teaching you Creation Master knowledge.","“If you’re trying to conquer a federation, won’t you try to insert your own faction within it? It’s clear that that federation ruined many of the Truth Association’s plans when they clashed. This is why Fifth Page Truth went to confront that faction personally. It might be a coincidence if the plan was only damaged once. But a chain of coincidences indicates that one of our own reports information to the other side.”","The young looked shocked and ashamed at the same time. He agreed that it was time to familiarize himself with human affairs. Otherwise, he’d just appear like a clown before his master.","The young man could not help but sigh, “Master, this faction is hiding so well!”","The elderly man patted the young man’s head with one hand as he rubbed his forehead with the other and said, “Baochuan, the faction that is spying for the other side won’t be too weak. Look at the stronger secret aristocratic families. Which family head looks the most laid back and is more concerned with protecting his own?”","The young man clearly understood the movements and circumstances of the secret aristocratic families well. After thinking for a moment, he blurted, “The Jin family! Is the Jin family the one the other side has taken in?”","The elderly man nodded gently.","“If someone is acting out of character, someone must be behind him! The current leader of the Jin family is Jin Qianxun. To my knowledge, he isn’t such a grounded person.","“Once all the secret aristocratic families are in formation, call Jin Qianxun over. Now that he has become a mole, he must have told whoever is controlling him about the contents of the meeting I called. As long as I’m kind enough to Jin Qianxun, the person behind him will understand my intentions.”","The young man asked with slight confusion, “Master, you are a Class 5 Creation Master. There’s no need for you to put on such a display!”","The elderly man lifted his hand from the young man’s shoulder and patted it forcefully.","“You are now a pinnacle Class 3 Creation Master. I am almost done teaching you all that you need to know. All I want is peace. Are you going to hole up with me forever?”"]},{"number":2152,"title":"Chapter 2152 Class 5 Creation Master Voices His Choice to Submit!","paragraphs":["2152 Class 5 Creation Master Voices His Choice to Submit!","Weng Quejiji was well aware of what kind of personality his disciple had.","Weng Queji never had any children but had long started to care for his disciple, who he had carefully brought up as his grandson.","When Weng Queji was young, he would never have felt anything for a person with whom he did not share any blood relation.","But after all his arrogance had been ground away over time, he started to see Weng Baochuan as his hope for the future. Otherwise, he would never have shared his surname.","Young people needed to carve out their careers.","When he first joined Fifth Page Truth, Weng Queji seriously considered recommending Weng Baochuan to Fifth Page Truth.","But the more he learned of Fifth Page Truth, the more he decided against the idea.","Fifth Page Truth was not an expert who would be a reliable source of support for Weng Baochuan.","If Weng Baochuan followed Fifth Page Truth, he would either lose his life or go down the path of evil.","Weng Queji had been sending his retainers to gather news on the Divine Wood Federation and Iron Hammer Federation.","From the information he received, Weng Queji could be certain that the faction that had killed Fifth Page Truth was a fairly virtuous one.","This was why Weng Queji once again had the idea of sending Weng Baochuan out to make a name for himself. Otherwise, there was indeed no need for Weng Queji to lower himself before Jin Qianxun, given his status as a Class 5 Creation Master.","Even if Jin Qianxun became the king of the Great Lush Federation, he should be the one to try and earn Weng Queji’s favor.","When Weng Baochuan heard what Weng Queji said, he could not help but hug Weng Queji and say passionately, “Master, I don’t want to go anywhere! I want to stay with you!”","Weng Queji rarely saw Weng Baochuan so overcome by emotion, and he could sense strong piety from this display.","Weng Queji coughed and said sternly, “Stop this inappropriate hugging! I still have some years ahead of me. You might not even outlive me!","“Why don’t you take advantage of your youth and go out to train? Do you want to still remain as innocent as you are when all the hair on your head has turned white? With your abilities as a Class 3 Creation Master and your spirit qi professional talent, you will definitely be able to improve at a shocking rate with the right guidance!”","While the teacher and disciple were speaking, Jin Qianxun reported everything that Weng Queji had said to Lin Yuan.","Since Jin Qianxun decided to cling to Lin Yuan, he would instantly report any useful information to Lin Yuan.","Thus, Su Yiren, who was in charge of the correspondence between Lin Yuan and Jin Qianxun, felt that the latter was extremely talkative.","After he was done reporting his news to Lin Yuan, Jin Qianxun took a deep breath.","Jin Qianxun felt that he was going to break if Lin Yuan did not arrive soon.","Hou Meng had approached him more than once to try and force him into a decision.","While Jin Qianxun was sighing to himself, Weng Baochuan’s arrival was announced by the Jin family’s members, who were in formation outside of the tent.","Jin Qianxun had not expected Weng Queji to have more to say to him.","But from what Weng Baochuan said, it was clear that Weng Queji had only extended this invitation to him.","This caused Jin Qianxun to be gripped by anxiousness.","Jin Qianxun suddenly wondered if Weng Queji had noticed that he had sworn his loyalty to Lin Yuan.","Jin Qianxun could not see through Weng Queji at all.","Weng Queji used to be Fifth Page Truth’s subordinate.","Fifth Page Truth’s death was unquestionably related to Jin Qianxun’s spilling of information to Lin Yuan.","Could Weng Queji be planning to kill me to avenge Fifth Page Truth’s death?","Even with this thought in his mind, Jin Qianxun had no choice but to follow Weng Baochuan back to Weng Queji’s tent.","Because he had offered up his loyalty early on, Lin Yuan had already promised a bright future to Jin Qianxun. Thus, Jin Qianxun did not need to seek any benefits from Weng Queji.","Yet, Weng Queji had called him over for a solo meeting at such a junction.","This would immediately raise suspicion in Hou Meng and the rest.","Jin Qianxun had a feeling that even if Weng Queji did not have any important reason for calling him over, Hou Meng and the rest would seek him out once he left Weng Queji’s tent.","But after following Weng Baochuan into Weng Queji’s tent, Jin Qianxun was stupefied by Weng Queji’s statement.","“I’m sure you’ve told whoever you’ve jumped ship to about the meeting I called. I’m very curious to know what you said about me.”","Weng Queji’s statement caused Jin Qianxun to feel as though the air around him had solidified.","Although Weng Queji’s voice was calm, Jin Qianxun felt as though he was completely transparent in front of Weng Queji.","Weng Queji’s aura completely suppressed Jin Qianxun to the point that Jin Qianxun found it difficult to breathe.","Jin Qianxun was temporarily at a loss about how he should respond.","Cold sweat started dripping down Jin Qianxun’s brow and back, soaking through his thin vest.","The elderly man smiled when he saw Jin Qianxun’s expression and said, “You don’t have to be so nervous. If I meant you harm, I would have investigated you when you suddenly started attending the gatherings before the tribes set off on Fifth Page War’s orders. If I had done that, there’s no way you would have survived to this day. I called you over because I want you to pass on a message. I also want to swear my loyalty to the person you’ve joined.”","Jin Qianxun could not remember how he managed to leave Weng Queji’s tent.","When he returned to his tent, he was still in shock.","A Class 5 Creation Master’s loyalty was monumental.","Jin Qianxun immediately gathered his thoughts and sent a message to Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","The moment he sent out the message, Hou Meng and the others arrived.","All of them had been wondering if Weng Queji had called Jin Qianxun over because he had decided to give his support to Jin Qianxun.","But from Jin Qianxun’s dazed demeanor, they erased the thought from their mind.","If Jin Qianxun had gained Weng Queji’s support, he would not be looking like this.","Could it be that Jin Qianxun had affronted Weng Queji? This did not make sense, either!","If Jin Qianxun had truly offended Weng Queji, he would not have been able to leave Weng Queji’s tent alive.","Lin Yuan was riding on Blackie’s back when he received the message from Jin Qianxun.","It seemed that Fifth Page Truth’s Class 5 Creation Master had finally shown himself.","Lin Yuan was about to store the Thoughts Letter Paper away when he saw another message from Jin Qianxun.","This new message caused confusion to spread across Lin Yuan’s face.","Oh? This was interesting!","Apparently, Fifth Page Truth’s Class 5 Creation Master wanted to offer his loyalty to Lin Yuan now that Fifth Page Truth was dead."]},{"number":2153,"title":"Chapter 2153 How Dare You? You Don’t Have the Right!","paragraphs":["2153 How Dare You? You Don’t Have the Right!","Lin Yuan did not know what this Class 5 Creation Master’s intention was, but he knew that he had to be trying to express his friendliness by contacting Lin Yuan through Jin Qianxun before Lin Yuan arrived.","This was similar to how a criminal would turn themselves in before they were arrested.","Lin Yuan was willing to look kindly on a Class 5 Creation Master who was willingly offering up his loyalty. However, he wondered if this Class 5 Creation Master had conditions for offering his loyalty.","Liu Jie and Su Yiren had both noticed the expression on Lin Yuan’s face. They hurriedly craned their heads over to read what was written on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","After reading the message, Su Yiren and Liu Jie both smiled in surprise.","Liu Jie and Su Yiren had never encountered a bigger miracle than a Class 5 Creation Master voluntarily offering his loyalty.","As long as the Class 5 Creation Master was willing to offer his loyalty, they would agree to any request he had.","Lin Yuan was confused about the reason behind the Class 5 Creation Master calling a meeting with the other secret aristocratic families.","But now, it seemed that the Class 5 Creation Master aimed to demonstrate to Lin Yuan that he was friendly.","They still had around six to seven hours of travel time before they arrived at the Great Lush Federation.","At first, Lin Yuan had intended on riding the Kill Food Sky Butterfly to the Great Lush Federation.","But the Kill Food Sky Butterfly had just been through a bloody fight. If he had been slightly later, the Kill Food Sky Butterfly would have been killed by the Drugged Snake Eagles.","Purple Afterglow and the Kill Food Sky Butterfly were comforting each other. Thus, Lin Yuan could not find the heart to summon the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","Blackie had reached Diamond X and could fly extremely quickly.","As a pure flood-dragon-species fey, its bloodline power allowed it to manipulate the winds and clouds.","Blackie was perfectly capable of meeting Lin Yuan’s needs when he was rushing.","Since they still had six to seven hours of traveling, Lin Yuan decided to reward the Class 5 Creation Master in advance.","Lin Yuan sent a message to Jin Qianxun on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","[Lin Yuan: Tell the Class 5 Creation Master to gather all the leaders of secret aristocratic families again. I will be by your side in another six hours.]","Lin Yuan stored the Thoughts Letter Paper away after sending the message.","When Jin Qianxun saw the message from Lin Yuan, he knew that Lin Yuan had decided to accept the Class 5 Creation Master. Otherwise, he would not have issued an order to the Class 5 Creation Master.","Nonetheless, he had no choice.","Jin Qianxun went back to Weng Queji’s tent and relayed Lin Yuan’s instruction.","Weng Queji started to chortle with laughter before he turned to say to Weng Baochuan, “Baochuan, go and call all the leaders of the secret aristocratic families.”","When Weng Baochuan left to gather the leaders of the secret aristocratic families, Weng Queji smiled and said, “You have been hiding and laying low. Because of how you’ve been holding back, most of the members of the Jin family have survived.","“Now that you’re in my tent, there’s no need to continue hiding. When the rest of them arrive, you can stay next to me! With me around, no one will dare to lay a hand on you! It will also give you a chance to see how the other family leaders see you and allow you to make advance preparations!”","Jin Qianxun looked grateful when he heard what Jin Qianxun said.","Jin Qianxun did not have the authoritative aura of a king but was skilled at human relations. He could immediately tell that Weng Queji was being kind to him.","Once he entered the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court and became king, he would have to determine where the other secret aristocratic families stood and kill some of the family leaders to make examples out of them.","Otherwise, he would have no fearsome might to speak of.","It did not take long for the leaders of the secret aristocratic families to gather in Weng Queji’s tent again.","All of them had been shocked when Weng Baochuan called them. They could not come up with a reason for a person like Weng Queqi to need to see them twice.","Could it be that this Class 5 Creation Master wanted to become the king of the Great Lush Federation?","If this was truly what Weng Queji was thinking, there was nothing that Hou Meng could say.","Firstly, he was weaker than Weng Queji. Secondly, all top-secret aristocratic families had benefited from Weng Queji.","If Weng Queji became the king of the Great Lush Federation, the secret aristocratic families would be able to continue receiving Class 5 Creation Master resources from him. This would be advantageous for the entire Great Lush Federation.","But when they arrived at the tent and saw Jin Qianxun standing next to Jin Qianxun, the expressions of all the leaders of secret aristocratic families changed.","All of them would feel resigned if Weng Queji was the one who wanted to become ruler of the Great Lush Federation.","But if Jin Qianxun became the king of the Great Lush Federation, all of them would be confused.","How dare Jin Qianxun? He did not have the right!","Since Weng Queji wanted to show Jin Qianxun that he was a friendly force, he did not mind doing more.","Weng Queji smiled and started chatting with Jin Qianxun in front of the other leaders of the secret aristocratic families.","Weng Queji’s attitude toward Jin Qianxun caused many of the leaders of the secret aristocratic families to erase their expressions of displeasure.","If they showed a sour expression toward Jin Qianxun while Weng Queji was acting so amicable toward him, it would be seen as an insult to Weng Queji.","There were several levels of disappointment that a human was capable of feeling.","The leaders of secret aristocratic families who never stood a chance of being able to enter the imperial court had already given up.","But family leaders like Hou Meng, who had feasible aspirations to take over the imperial court, all of them were feeling uncontrollable indignation.","Although Weng Queji had called all of them over, he had not stated the reason for doing so. All he had done so far was chat idly with Jin Qianxun.","Jin Qianxun’s eyes swept across the faces of the leaders of the secret aristocratic families and noted each individual.","If Weng Queji did not state the reason for calling them over, none of them would dare to ask either.","Time slowly ticked away amidst this strange aura.","Suddenly, Weng Queji’s expression changed as he sensed an aura coming from a distance away.","Weng Queji rose to his feet.","Since he did not know if the person behind Jin Qianxun was willing to expose his identity to the leaders of the secret aristocratic families, Jin Qianxun did not move to open the entrance to the tent.","After Weng Queji stood up, Jin Qianxun and the other leaders of the secret aristocratic families followed suit.","Although they all looked surprised by Weng Queji suddenly standing up, there was no reason for them not to do the same after someone of Weng Queji’s status had done so."]},{"number":2154,"title":"Chapter 2154 You’re Going to Provide Us With Futures?","paragraphs":["2154 You’re Going to Provide Us With Futures?","Weng Queji patted Jin Qianxun’s shoulder and said, “Your luck has come!”","The other leaders of the secret aristocratic families did not understand what Weng Queji meant.","However, Jin Qianxun understood perfectly.","At that moment, Jin Qianxun’s body started to tremble with excitement. His delight was no longer as suppressed as it previously was.","Previously, Jin Qianxun had been afraid that the other leaders of the secret aristocratic families would cause trouble for him.","Although Weng Queji was acting in a friendly manner toward him, Jin Qianxun found it difficult to trust Weng Queji. After all, they had only started to become closer.","But now that Lin Yuan was there, the aura that Jin Qianxun had been suppressing was released.","Weng Queji shook his head at the change in Jin Qianxun.","Even a person who was so conforming to norms could stumble on such luck.","If he did not have someone’s support, Jin Qianxun would not even have the power and capabilities to make a claim to be the second step on the imperial court’s staircase.","While the leaders of the secret aristocratic families were confused, Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, and Su Yiren appeared outside Weng Queji’s tent.","Weng Queji’s two retainers knew what his intentions were. They knew that their master would swear his loyalty to these three people and that they would become these three people’s servants.","The two retainers bowed deeply while pulling the strings of pearls at the entrance of the tent apart for Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, and Su Yiren to enter.","If any leader of a secret aristocratic family saw this, their jaws would instantly drop in shock.","Usually, the two retainers did not even have to nod in greeting or spare a glance at the leaders of the secret aristocratic families.","Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, and Su Yiren’s sudden entrance into the tent caused the leaders of the secret aristocratic families to assume that they were uninvited guests.","The leaders of the secret aristocratic families had never seen the three of them before.","Liu Jie and Lin Yuan had black hair and eyes, which fit with the features of the locals of the Great Lush Federation.","Meanwhile, Su Yiren had purple hair and eyes. It was clear that she was not from the Great Lush Federation.","However, Weng Queji had to have given permission for these three people to appear here. Otherwise, they would not have gotten past the two retainers by the entrance of the tent.","While the leaders of the secret aristocratic families were guessing the identities of these three people, Weng Queji and Jin Qianxun stepped forward toward Lin Yuan.","Jin Qianxun behaved the same way that the two retainers outside the tent had and bowed to Lin Yuan, Su Yiren, and Liu Jie.","Jin Qianxun’s respectful display made his stance clear.","Lin Yuan nodded at Weng Queji before he helped Jin Qianxun upright.","By bowing, Jin Qianxun had made it clear that he was submissive to Lin Yuan.","However, such an attitude made it difficult for him to earn the acknowledgment of the other leaders of the secret aristocratic families.","Nonetheless, this indicated to Lin Yuan that Jin Qianxun intended to cling to him for the foreseeable future.","Jin Qianxun had chosen to show his respect to Lin Yuan, maintaining the intimidating might of a ruler.","Sometimes, Jin Qianxun’s lack of ambition and dominance gave Lin Yuan a headache.","However, he had to admit that Jin Qianxun’s personality made it easier for Lin Yuan to take control of the Great Lush Federation. He did not have to worry about Jin Qianxun developing the courage to try and escape his control.","Weng Queji had already created a comfortable environment for him.","Lin Yuan intended to help Jin Qianxun to bolster his might.","Lin Yuan was not planning on staying in the Great Lush Federation for long.","The Banquet of Everything in the Marsh East Circle was about to start in a month or two. Lin Yuan would rather invest more of his energy into his establishments in the marsh world than in the Great Lush Federation.","Lin Yuan saw the Startling Lines Continent as Sky City’s back garden, which secured Sky City’s source of resources.","But he saw the marsh world as a new world that he needed to venture into and explore.","Lin Yuan needed to spend a large amount of time in the marsh world.","The Freedom Federation had started developing the marsh world.","As Lin Yuan developed the marsh world, there was a chance that he would bump into people from the Freedom Federation.","As Lin Yuan looked into Jin Qianxun’s yearning and excited gaze, he declared, “You probably remember my promise to allow you to stand by my side. With my support, you can do whatever you want.”","Jin Qianxun’s heart skipped a beat.","The meaning behind Lin Yuan’s words was clear.","He was saying that he would be Jin Qianxun’s stable support and that Jin Qianxun could do whatever he felt was necessary to gain the acknowledgment of the secret aristocratic families. He was also saying that he would claim the throne of the Great Lush Federation for Jin Qianxun.","Jin Qianxun understood Lin Yuan’s intentions.","However, he could not muster up his courage in front of the other leaders of the secret aristocratic families who heaped pressure on him on a daily basis.","Although the members of the secret aristocratic families did not know who Lin Yuan was, they could guess his status just from the fact that Weng Queji had bowed to him.","However, Lin Yuan’s words to Jin Qianxun made Hou Meng and the rest extremely uncomforted.","Hou Meng was the first to raise his protest.","Jin Qianxun had already heard many doubtful voices that were aimed at him, and they all added to the pressure weighing down on his chest.","Just like Su Yiren, Liu Jie saw Jin Qianxun as extremely mediocre.","Lin Yuan had presented Jin Qianxun with such a golden opportunity, yet he did not have the courage to reach out to grab it. Was he expecting Lin Yuan to spoon-feed him?","Liu Jie could not help but scoff caustically.","Jin Qianxun had seen Liu Jie in Oak City and knew that he was Lin Yuan’s personal bodyguard.","Liu Jie’s scoff could represent Lin Yuan’s opinion.","Jin Qianxun was the most afraid of Lin Yuan being displeased with him.","Jin Qianxun remembered Lin Yuan saying that he could do whatever he wanted.","Jin Qianxun mustered his courage and looked Hou Meng and the rest in the eye as he started to speak, enunciating each word. “There are almost 300 leaders of secret aristocratic families present. All 300 of you should take the chance to swear your loyalty to me! With this assurance, I will be able to trust and rely on you once I become king of the Great Lush Federation. This will allow you to head toward bright futures!”","Jin Qianxun’s words set off all the secret aristocratic family leaders.","What!? Jin Qianxun, who do you think you are? You’re going to provide us with futures? You aren’t fit to become king of the Great Lush Federation!","Not only do you have the audacity to have such ambition, but you dare to ask us to swear our loyalties to you on our Willpower Runes!? If we do that, our lives will be in your hands!"]},{"number":2155,"title":"Chapter 2155 This is the Undesirable Outcome!","paragraphs":["2155 This is the Undesirable Outcome!","Lin Yuan scrutinized Jin Qianxun as he spoke.","Given Lin Yuan’s understanding of Jin Qianxun’s character, he had not expected to hear such words from him.","By saying such a thing at such a time, it showed that Jin Qianxun, at the very least, did have ambition.","Su Yiren was also momentarily impressed with Jin Qianxun.","If Jin Qianxun was able to gain the sworn loyalties of the leaders of the secret aristocratic families with Lin Yuan’s help, he would be able to control the core of the entire Great Lush Federation through them.","This would be a smart move with lasting effects.","Hou Meng had been suppressing his emotions.","From the way that he was able to distinguish himself from the other leaders of secret aristocratic families and already gain slight acknowledgment from them, it proved that Hou Meng was not an ordinary person.","However, the combination of his disappointment and bitterness toward Jin Qianxun caused Hou Meng to lose control and try to put Jin Qianxun on the spot.","“Jin Qianxun, what gives you the right to ask all of us to swear our loyalty to you?”","Hou Meng was not the only person who had been eyeing the throne of the Great Lush Federation.","The Wei and Gu families had comparable power to the Hou family.","Wei Haodong and Gu Wanting already had high positions in their families before Fifth Page Truth died. They had been in charge of managing their families’ main affairs.","However, it was inevitable that they would face pushback from other members of their families.","Now that they had managed to become their families’ leaders, they wanted to advance their families’ power.","After Hou Meng spoke up, Wei Haodong and Gu Wanting also chimed in. Both of them came in with more force in their demeanors than Hou Meng did.","The few families who had allied with the Hou, Wei, and Gu families also voiced their agreement.","However, they were all quickly silenced by Jin Qianxun’s dominance.","Jin Qianxun could not help but glance at Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan caught Jin Qianxun’s eyes and said, “I already made myself clear. You can do whatever you want.”","Jin Qianxun bit his lip and said something that shocked even himself, “Kill everyone who doubts me! Then, I’ll need to trouble Elder Weng’s beloved disciple to help me to pick out a spokesperson from the families whose heads are killed.”","The moment Jin Qianxun finished speaking, a black shadow shot out from the shadow under Lin Yuan’s feet.","A trail of bloody fallen bodies was left wherever the shadow streaked past.","The sudden deaths caused the leaders of the secret aristocratic families who had been watching from the sidelines to slap their hands over their mouths.","The timid leaders of secret aristocratic families felt their legs go weak, and their bodies start to tremble.","These people had all basked in the comfort of their statuses within their families and had never been in a position like this where they were dispensable and could be killed at any moment.","Hou Meng, Wei Haodong, and Gu Wanting had been larger than life but had died as though they had amounted to nothing.","Now, it made sense that even a Class 5 Creation Master had bowed to this young man and that his presence gave even Jin Qianxun the courage to try and fight for that coveted seat.","The blood spilled from their bodies had not yet turned cold.","It did not take long for the first leader of a secret aristocratic family to step out to swear his loyalty to Jin Qianxun.","After the first one, the second one soon followed.","Under the formidable pressures of confusion and the risk of death, the people present had no backbone to speak of.","Weng Baochuan was slightly displeased with Jin Qianxun ordering him around.","But at the same time, he knew that Jin Qianxun was wielding the might provided by this young man.","Furthermore, his master had also pledged his loyalty to this young man, meaning that he also needed to do the same.","His master had told him to go out and train, and there was a high chance that he meant for Weng Baochuan to accompany this young man.","Hence, leaving a good impression on this young man was imperative.","For this reason, Weng Baochuan became very serious when he left to carry out his task of picking out a spokesperson from each of the families whose leaders had just been killed.","The people who Weng Baochuan picked were all excited but nervous at the same time. They tried to guess why Weng Queji needed to see them and thought, Did I do something to catch the Class 5 Creation Master’s eye? Why else would a Class 5 Creation Master suddenly ask to meet someone as insignificant as me?","The moment they entered the tent, the metallic stench of blood filled their nostrils.","The instant that they glanced at the bodies littering the ground, every single one of them started to quiver.","But before they could make any guesses as to what led to this horrific scene, Jin Qianxun said sternly, “Your original family heads refused to become loyal to me and have paid the price for that decision.","“If you swear your loyalty to me now, you can become the next head of your family. Otherwise, you will meet the same end as they did. I wonder who in your family will be the lucky next candidate to be selected after your death.”","Jin Qianxun’s words were not just meant to frighten them but also laid out the potential gains and losses.","Those who were loyal to him would have the chance to become the leaders of their families and enjoy untold riches and glory.","The only other option was death!","None of the people who had just arrived dared to question the truth of what Jin Qianxun said because the bodies on the ground were proof enough.","It did not take long for all of the leaders of the secret aristocratic families who were present to swear their loyalties to Jin Qianxun.","Although Jin Qianxun had not become the king of the Great Lush Federation, it could be said that he already had a legitimate claim to the throne.","Even Fifth Page Truth had not had such an iron-fisted control over the Great Lush Federation as Jin Qianxun did now.","While the leaders of the secret aristocratic families were taking turns swearing their loyalties to him, Jin Qianxun’s mood was going through a series of changes.","Jin Qianxun enjoyed the feeling of power he now wielded but also felt gratitude and fear for Lin Yuan.","He knew that everything he had came from Lin Yuan.","If Lin Yuan was unwilling to give him these things, anyone from the Great Lush Federation, no matter how low their background was, would be able to take the throne of the Great Lush Federation.","The fear and gratitude pounded into Jin Qianxun that the most important thing he needed to do after taking the throne was to do his best to please Lin Yuan.","After the last leader of a secret aristocratic family had sworn his loyalty to Jin Qianxun, he said, “Go back to your families and lead them back to Clean Brahma City! I trust that you know what to do and say. Once you’re back in Clean Brahma City, I don’t want to hear a peep of discontent at my coronation ceremony. Otherwise, you can expect to meet the same end as these people on the ground!”"]},{"number":2156,"title":"Chapter 2156 Weng Queji’s Offering!","paragraphs":["2156 Weng Queji’s Offering!","While Jin Qianxun was speaking, his gaze swept across the leaders of the secret aristocratic families who were watching.","Anyone who happened to catch his gaze would immediately look away before lowering their heads.","At this instant, Jin Qianxun was struck with the feeling of being a king.","After the leaders of the secret aristocratic families left, Jin Qianxun knelt in front of Lin Yuan and kowtowed to him.","When he lowered his head to the ground, he placed a hand below his head to cushion it and the other hand on his neck.","Lin Yuan knew that this was the sign of the highest reverence in the Great Lush Federation.","Lin Yuan did not stop Jin Qianxun.","After Jin Qianxun was done and rose to his feet, Lin Yuan said, “When you start managing the Great Lush Federation, I will arrange for an assistant for you who will support you but not make any decisions on your behalf. You can send that assistant on any task, no matter how difficult it is.”","At first, Jin Qianxun thought that Lin Yuan was sending someone to watch him.","But Lin Yuan said that the person he assigned would not interfere in Jin Qianxun’s decisions and that he could have the final say in everything regarding the Great Lush Federation.","This filled Jin Qianxun with some doubt. He could not understand what Lin Yuan’s intentions were.","Meanwhile, as Weng Queji watched the dim and confused Jin Qianxun, he could not help but say, “The Lord must have set up this arrangement to train his subordinate!”","When Jin Qianxun heard what Weng Queji said, realization dawned on him, and he hurriedly said, “Lord, rest assured, I will definitely train whoever you send me to the best of my ability.”","Lin Yuan nodded at Jin Qianxun.","Jin Qianxun took the hint and left the tent to Lin Yuan and Weng Queji.","Weng Queji was also willing to become loyal to Lin Yuan. The difference was that Weng Queji was much more valuable than Jin Qianxun.","Although Jin Qianxun could not see what Lin Yuan’s intentions were for now, he was well aware of his position.","Lin Yuan had already found out through Jin Qianxun that the Class 5 Creation Master, who had been under Fifth Page Truth, wanted to join his camp.","Lin Yuan had been in disbelief when he first heard this news.","But Weng Queji had called Lin Yuan ‘Lord’, meaning that he saw himself beneath Lin Yuan.","Just as Lin Yuan was about to say something to Weng Queji, the latter said with utmost formality, “Lord, my name is Weng Queji. This is my disciple, Weng Baochuan. Baochuan, come and greet the Lord!”","Weng Queji hastily greeted Lin Yuan in a timid voice.","Weng Baochuan could tell that Lin Yuan was younger than him. In fact, all three people in front of him were young.","After Weng Queji greeted Lin Yuan and his group, Weng Queji went on to say, “All I want is peace and stability. I joined Fifth Page Truth because he could give me just that. After joining him, I did not ask for much. All I ask from you is a safe life free from troubles, as well as a chance for Baochuan to train properly. If you can meet these needs, I’m willing to work for you from now on.”","When Weng Queji contacted Lin Yuan through Jin Qianxun, Liu Jie and Su Yiren had assumed that Weng Queji had a long list of requests.","After all, it was extremely rare to have a Class 5 Creation Master offer up his services. It was only right that any and all requests and resources he wanted to be met.","However, it turned out that this Class 5 Creation Master wanted so little. It was likely that even Class 1 and 2 Creation Masters in the Radiance Federation would ask for more than he had.","Lin Yuan looked deeply into Weng Queji’s eyes.","With his experience of having lived two lives, Lin Yuan could guess how Weng Queji was currently feeling.","Weng Queji appeared to have already reached nirvana but was actually full of woe and had experienced his fair share of life’s sufferings.","Lin Yuan had no reason not to agree when he only needed to fulfill such simple requests to earn the services of a Class 5 Creation Master.","“From now on, I will provide you with a steady stream of resources. Your disciple should be a Creation Master too. Why don’t you leave him with me from now on? I will arrange for a suitable chance to train him, during which his safety will be assured. This is our first time meeting, and there’s no reason for us to trust each other. So, you need to give me a reason to trust you.”","Even before Lin Yuan could finish speaking, Weng Queji understood what he was getting at.","Fifth Page Truth had not asked Weng Queji to swear his loyalty, but this might not be the same case with Lin Yuan.","As a Class 5 Creation Master, Weng Queji would definitely be placed in an important position in Lin Yuan’s faction.","In such an important position, any change in Weng Queji’s heart could bring untold losses to Lin Yuan.","Rather than a loss of resources, having information leaked would be calamitous.","Lin Yuan had Red Thorn, so it would not make much of a difference to Lin Yuan if Weng Queji was dead or alive.","If Lin Yuan could not rest easy with a living Weng Queji, he would prefer a dead one.","Lin Yuan’s words took Weng Queji by surprise.","Weng Queji had never imagined that he would one day be asked to swear his loyalty to someone.","After pondering for a moment, Weng Queji smiled dryly.","He had just told Weng Baochuan not to be too caught up in the title of being a Class 5 Creation Master. However, he did feel a slight tug of reluctance.","But the fact was that there was not much difference in position between himself and Jin Qianxun in this young man’s eyes. Both of them were dispensable.","Weng Queji was not the type to hesitate. Although he felt disconcerted, he still quickly swore his loyalty to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan sensed that his soul had taken control of Weng Queji’s soul, and he could not help but smile.","Nice! Sky City finally has its third Class 5 Creation Master!","After swearing his loyalty, Weng Queji was now well and truly tamed.","When Weng Queji saw the hostility in Weng Baochuan’s eyes after he was made to swear his loyalty to Lin Yuan, Weng Queji hurriedly coughed and said, “Baochuan, do you remember what I told you to give the Lord? Hurry up and hand it to him!”","Weng Baochuan was stunned and hastily suppressed his hostility toward Lin Yuan.","If he was hostile to someone to who his master had become loyal, it would put him on the opposite side as his master.","Weng Baochuan plastered on a new expression of curiosity and respect as he handed Lin Yuan a piece of spatial equipment."]},{"number":2157,"title":"Chapter 2157 The Floating Island Whale’s Completed Combat System!","paragraphs":["2157 The Floating Island Whale’s Completed Combat System!","Lin Yuan was slightly surprised that Weng Queji had prepared a gift before they met.","Although Weng Queji had sworn his loyalty, it was the contract of a Protector and not a servant.","Lin Yuan would not touch Weng Queji’s finances in spite of the contract between them.","Lin Yuan received the box from Weng Baochuan and looked inside it using his spiritual energy.","Before he could start to carefully look through the box’s contents, he was shocked by the box itself.","Weng Queji had clearly made this seemingly average box.","The box was similar to Lin Yuan’s ring in that it was also considered a piece of spatial equipment. But it was bigger than the spatial ring and could store even more items. The interior of the box was more spacious than Lin Yuan’s ring.","It could be considered a rare treasure.","When Weng Queji noticed Lin Yuan’s interest in the piece of spatial equipment, he hurriedly said, “I killed an expert once in my youth who possessed a 5 Stars spatial-type sacred source lifeform. This box is only made up of a small part of that 5 Stars sacred source lifeform’s body. As long as there are enough spatial metal-type spiritual ingredients, another 500 pieces of spatial equipment can be made from that 5 Stars sacred source lifeform’s body.”","While Weng Queji was speaking, Lin Yuan’s attention was stolen by the shelves of spirit fluids within the box.","It was difficult to estimate how many spirit fluids a Class 5 Creation Master of advanced age could concoct in his lifetime.","Lin Yuan did not know how large of a proportion of his store of spirit fluids Weng Queji had given him.","But in terms of numbers, it already rivaled the total number of spirit fluids that the army of Hundred Questions Beasts had concocted.","There was no question that these spirit fluids were of much better quality than the ones concocted by the army of Hundred Questions Beasts.","Lin Yuan clicked his tongue to himself.","The army of Hundred Questions Beasts was mostly stuck at the level of Class 3 Creation Master and could not concoct Grade 4 spirit fluids.","All of the Grade 4 spirit fluids that Lin Yuan had came from Genius.","The Grade 4 spirit fluids Weng Queji gave him had significantly increased his store of Grade 4 spirit fluids.","The Grade 4 spirit fluids would be perfect for increasing the white-clothed followers’ powers.","Lin Yuan was indeed satisfied with the piece of spatial equipment that Weng Queji had created.","If 500 of these could be made, Lin Yuan would have storage space for as many resources as he wanted.","However, a Class 5 Creation Master’s value was far beyond the ability to create spatial equipment.","One of the Diamond fey storage boxes that came from the Radiance Federation could not match up to this box, but more than ten of them would equate to the same amount of storage space.","Otherwise, it would be difficult for the Spirit Lock spatial zone alone to churn out enough high-class resources that not even Class 6 Creation Masters could produce to meet the white-clothed followers’ needs.","On a fey’s journey of evolution, pure elemental energy and spirit qi were necessities, but not all that was needed.","Weng Queji had given Lin Yuan spirit fluids and a significant number of rare feys.","The feys in the Great Lush Federation were not as clearly categorized by species as those in the Divine Wood Federation and Iron Hammer Federation.","There were all types of geographical environments in the Great Lush Federation.","The sea surrounded a large portion of the Great Lush Federation’s territory. Thus, the Great Lush Federation had an abundance of aquatic feys.","Lin Yuan even saw Island Whale embryos amongst those feys.","This was enough to see how sincere Weng Queji was.","After looking at those feys, Lin Yuan’s attention was not captured by the Island Whale embryos but by a silver-gray flower.","Lin Yuan had never seen such a flower before.","It was only around half a meter tall, but its stem, roots, and petals all had burgeoning sturdiness.","The large flowers resembled carved rocks.","Such feys were not pleasant to look at and would not catch any eyes when they grew by the side of the road.","But it had caught Lin Yuan’s eye because he had used Morbius to check its abilities and exclusive skills.","Previously, Lin Yuan had been thinking about how he should go about creating a combat system on Universe.","Universe’s only method of combat would be to slam into opponents with its body.","Such a method would also cause significant damage to itself and was not truly effective.","Lin Yuan had traded for the Peaceful Calm Air Moss with the Su family in the Divine Wood Federation.","After the Peaceful Calm Air Moss was mutated under the effects of the pure spirit qi, it would increase Universe’s defense system.","However, Lin Yuan did not have many ideas for combat.","But now that he had the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower, Universe would face no issues when it came to combat.","There were nine of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers inside the box. All of their Normal abilities were Explosive Spirit.","Explosive Spirit would cause the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower to spew out all the spirit qi it had absorbed at once as an explosive attack on the enemy.","The Exploding Spirit Rock Flower naturally absorbed spirit qi from the air, but the quality and amount of the spirit qi in the air were lacking. Thus, it was not very useful.","But if Lin Yuan fed the spirit qi crystals to the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower, it could eventually spew out all the spirit qi that had been in the spirit qi crystals as an explosive attack. This was no different from a bomb.","The Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers had different exclusive skills, including Strong Bud, Extremely Long Roots, and more.","Having them was better than nothing but none of them particularly interested Lin Yuan.","Only four of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers were Elite grade. Their Elite abilities were Spirit Rock Flower Body.","Spirit Rock Flower Body was a triggered ability.","It was similar to the Mirror Silver Obsidian Bull’s ability Sacrifice.","When the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower absorbed spirit qi, it could combine its rock attributes with the spirit qi.","The more spirit qi that was absorbed, the stronger the effects of Explosive Spirit would be.","The spirit qi absorbed by the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower would improve the quality of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower’s body. Thus, it did not have to be concerned about its body being unable to handle an over-absorption of spirit qi.","Normally, only feys’ Normal abilities were set.","However, there were some special feys with set Elite abilities, albeit they were very rare."]},{"number":2158,"title":"Chapter 2158 The Special Exploding Spirit Rock Flower!","paragraphs":["2158 The Special Exploding Spirit Rock Flower!","Lin Yuan could not be certain of anything before he started evolving the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers.","After some thinking, Lin Yuan felt assured that the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers’ Elite abilities were set. Otherwise, the coincidence would be too uncanny.","Lu Pinru only contracted the Glowing Silkworm Weavers.","She had spent a lot of money and effort ensuring that all the Glowing Silkworm Weavers had the same Elite abilities.","Even if not all of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers’ Elite abilities were Spirit Rock Flower Body, Lin Yuan could nurture the Elite Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers to try and cultivate Spirit Rock Flower Body in all of them.","Given Lin Yuan’s current abilities, he only needed a few breaths’ worth of time to evolve a Normal fey to Elite.","Moreover, Lin Yuan had the Hundred Questions Beasts and did not need to skimp on Creation Master resources.","Even if the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower was a product of mutation, a few of them were enough.","The Exploding Spirit Rock Flower would allow Lin Yuan to produce an endless stream of bombs as long as he was willing to use up spirit qi crystals.","The attack’s strength depended wholly on the number of spirit qi crystals that were used up.","The number of spirit qi crystals in Lin Yuan’s possession was limited.","If he had too many of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers, Lin Yuan would not have enough supplies for all of them.","Since Weng Queji had sworn his loyalty to him and was now a trusted aide, Lin Yuan took out one of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers from the box and handed it to him.","“Elder Weng, I have never seen this plant-type fey before. Is it a specialty of the Great Lush Federation?”","Weng Queji was surprised that Lin Yuan asked him about something useless. But since the question had been asked, Weng Queji answered honestly, “The Exploding Spirit Rock Flower is not native to the Great Lush Federation. The appearance of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower was an accident. When I was researching a new Grade 5 spirit fluid, an experiment failed. I couldn’t bear to through the product away, so I used it to water these flowers. Eventually, all the precious flowers in the garden died. Only these spotted Rock Orchids survived and mutated.","“I was very curious about this occurrence, so I created more of the failed potions to cultivate a large number of the Rock Orchids, which I started to experiment intensely on. As I started to evolve the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers, I noticed that all of their abilities are the same up till Diamond grade. You should be aware of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower’s Normal and Elite abilities. Its Silver to Diamond abilities are meant to increase Explosive Spirit’s might. However, the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower absorbed spirit qi much too slowly for it to be of any practical use.”","Weng Queji felt that Lin Yuan had to be a Creation Master because he was able to pick out the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower amongst the many feys within the box and notice its special aspects.","Since Lin Yuan was a Creation Master, he had to know how precious pure spirit qi was.","When Creation Masters were concocting spirit fluids, those that contained pure spirit qi were always two to three times more expensive than those with special effects that were of the same grade.","Weng Queji had never thought about canning spirit qi into the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers. Hence, no matter how fanciful Weng Queji’s imaginations were, he could not guess what Lin Yuan was thinking.","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up when he heard what Weng Queji said.","Weng Queji had mentioned how the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower came about.","It turned out that it had mutated after being guided by a failed Grade 5 spirit fluid.","Weng Queji’s second experiment had been successful, meaning that there could be an endless supply of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers.","In terms of price, the Rock Orchids were cheaper than even the Hundred Questions Beasts and Songstress Birds.","Lin Yuan had guessed that the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers might all have the same Diamond abilities.","The Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers’ lack of variety was not a disadvantage to Lin Yuan but a great advantage.","This was because the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower’s Silver to Diamond abilities were all meant to improve the might of Explosive Spirit.","Lin Yuan not only wanted to build up Universe but also wanted to turn the Bug-Consuming Therach Emperor Lizards into moving land fortresses.","If the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers were properly used, they would be extremely beneficial for combat.","However, there were clearly not enough Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers at the moment.","Lin Yuan immediately gave Weng Queji his first order.","“Elder Weng, I am very interested in the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers. I would like you to nurture a batch for me. How long will it take?”","Weng Queji already felt that Lin Yuan’s noticing of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower was ridiculous enough. But now, Lin Yuan even wanted a batch of the useless Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers to be nurtured.","He had clearly said he had produced the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers by chance using failed Grade 5 spirit fluids.","The ingredients used to concoct the Grade 5 spirit fluid did not come cheap. They even included two spiritual ingredients that came from Creation Breed feys.","If he was younger, Weng Queji might ask follow-up questions.","But now, he wanted for nothing and was at peace.","Since all he wanted was stability, he would not mind anything that Lin Yuan asked him to do.","Furthermore, he could tell that Lin Yuan respected him from the way he was addressed.","This put Weng Queji even more at ease.","Although he had been forced to swear his loyalty to Lin Yuan and had lost control of his life, Weng Queji would never have permitted Lin Yuan to disrespect him.","“Lord, it will take almost 12 hours to concoct the failed Grade 5 spirit fluid. It will take close to 36 hours to mutate the Rock Orchids. I will give you a batch of 300 Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers in two days.”","Lin Yuan replied with a smile, “Thank you for your effort! We will be spending a lot of time with each other from now on. You don’t need to call me Lord. You can call me by my name, Lin Yuan.”","Frankly, Weng Queji did not like calling Lin Yuan as ‘Lord’. He was much more comfortable addressing Lin Yuan by name.","“Lin Yuan, if there’s nothing else, I’ll leave Baochuan with you while I stay in my tent to concoct spirit fluids. Let me know when you find a time to send Jin Qianxun and his people back to the Great Lush Federation. I can also concoct spirit fluids while on the Shaking Ground Snow Salamander. It won’t cause a delay in my submission of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers to you.”","While Weng Queji was speaking, Weng Baochuan dutifully went over to stand by Lin Yuan, waiting to begin his training."]},{"number":2159,"title":"Chapter 2159 How Can You Still Be Crying at Your Age?","paragraphs":["2159 How Can You Still Be Crying at Your Age?","Although Weng Baochuan was barely over 20 years old, he had been learning Creation Master skills for a long time.","After being carefully brought up by Weng Queji, his talent, and feys could match that of top geniuses.","But in actuality, Weng Baochuan’s experience of society could not even match up to Lin Yuan’s time in the Xia Region.","Lin Yuan smiled and waved his hand when he heard what Weng Queji said.","“Elder Weng, you don’t need to be in a rush to concoct spirit fluids. You have already been meeting my requirements. I have already gained a lot from you and even discovered something as great as the Exploding Spirit Rock Flower. I think I should give something back to you. Is there anything that you’re wishing for?”","Liu Jie and Su Yiren had not had any special reactions to what Lin Yuan said.","After all the time that they had spent with Lin Yuan, they had long started seeing him as a deity.","Even Class 5 Creation Masters could not easily obtain all of the resources he produced.","Moreover, Lin Yuan already had two Class 5 Creation Masters in his arsenal.","Di Wanmi, who was being controlled by Red Thorn, and Yi Huailu were both extremely modest while they were by Lin Yuan’s side.","Liu Jie and Su Yiren were already used to seeing Di Wanmi and Yi Huailu’s humble demeanors. They felt that all Class 5 Creation Masters should have that same attitude in front of Lin Yuan.","Moreover, Lin Yuan often provided resources to Yi Huailu and Di Wanmi.","Although Su Yiren and Liu Jie did not think much of this, the same did not apply to Weng Queji and Weng Baochuan.","Weng Queji wanted to ask, “Do you know who I am? I am a Class 5 Creation Master! Class 5 Creation Masters are the most revered beings in the world! What resources could exist that could not be created by Class 5 Creation Masters?”","Yet, Lin Yuan had made it seem like he wanted to make one of Weng Queji’s wishes come true.","Normally, it was Weng Queji who fulfilled the wishes of others.","Even Immortal experts only managed to exchange for a pitifully small amount of resources after kneeling and begging him!","Weng Queji found it hard to believe that Lin Yuan would be able to give him anything.","Weng Queji spent all his time in the Startling Lines Continent and had no idea that Class 6 Creation Masters had already emerged in the world and that even they could not hope to compare to Lin Yuan.","But since Lin Yuan had asked, Weng Queji did not try to hide his sincere answer and said, “Lin Yuan, I may seem like nothing matters to me anymore, but I actually crave power as much as I always have. But with lacking manpower, there’s no way I can cross that obstacle. My only wish is to increase my power. If I can increase my power, I will have a reason to exist even longer.”","While he spoke, Weng Queji sighed more than once.","Lin Yuan was silent for a while after listening to Weng Queji’s lament.","He could sense frustration and indignation in Weng Queji’s casual tone.","Weng Queji must have tried umpteen times to cross that obstacle.","It was likely that his current attitude was a result of being beaten down by life and failing repeatedly.","There could only be one reason for an expert to lose hope after failing multiple times while trying to increase their power, which was that something in their body was preventing them from making any further attempts.","“Elder Weng, forgive me for asking, but am I right to say that you are injured in some way?”","Weng Queji’s expression abruptly changed as panic surfaced on his face. But it quickly morphed into frustration.","Weng Queji looked seriously into Lin Yuan’s eyes and tugged his collar open.","Lin Yuan saw a long scar that resembled a centipede crawling on Weng Queji’s chest. The rest of the long robe covered the part where the scar ended and could not be seen.","“I am indeed injured. But I consider myself lucky. I managed to find a mineral vein which I tapped into to save myself. It also gave me the chance to take in Baochuan.”","This was the first time that Lin Yuan was hearing Weng Queji’s story.","It was also the first time for Weng Baochuan, who had been with Weng Queji since he was young.","When Weng Baochuan saw the scar on Weng Queji’s chest, he strode over to Weng Queji and shouted anxiously, “Master, why haven’t I seen you healing yourself even though you’re clearly injured?”","In Weng Baochuan’s eyes, Weng Queji was still a Class 5 Creation Master, and there was nothing he could not do.","Weng Queji gently shook his head and replied, “Baochuan, do you remember me saying that everyone has their limitations, including Class 5 Creation Masters? If I could save myself, do you think that I would be in the state that I’m in now?”","Lin Yuan thought, So I was right.","Given the serious injuries that Weng Queji had sustained, it was likely that his feys were in a critical state as well.","If only Weng Queji was lacking in power, he could continue to stubbornly try to increase his power.","But now that both he and his main feys’ roots were injured, Weng Queji had lost the opportunity to continue growing stronger.","Injuries that could not be healed by even Class 5 Creation Masters likely needed pure spirit qi. Otherwise, Weng Queji could have just produced any resources he needed on his own.","But from Weng Queji’s words and manner, Lin Yuan knew that Weng Queji did not trust his capabilities.","Weng Queji had chosen to swear his loyalty to Lin Yuan because he was under the threat of martial force but also because all he wanted was peace and had no more hopes of increasing his power.","Since Weng Queji did not believe him, Lin Yuan was not going to try to say anything to him,","Lin Yuan took out one of the Spirit-Mouthed Peonies that he had recently harvested from the Spirit Lock spatial zone and placed it on the table before leaving Weng Queji’s tent.","Su Yiren and Liu Jie took one look at the bright red Spirit-Mouthed Peony on the table before following Lin Yuan out of the tent, leaving the worried and concerned Weng Baochuan and Weng Queji.","Weng Queji had not wanted to tell Weng Baochuan about his situation. He had only mentioned it today because Lin Yuan had asked him about his circumstances.","All this time, Weng Queji had been avoiding the matter.","But now that he had revealed it, he found himself slightly more relaxed.","Weng Queji patted Weng Baochuan’s shoulder and said warmly, “Baochuan, how can you still be crying at your age? Hurry up and wipe your tears away! Crying is inauspicious!","“I still have many years ahead of me! When you leave for training with Lin Yuan, try your best to stick close to him. You’ll benefit much more than being by my side! I’ll need you to look after me when I’m really old and disabled!”"]},{"number":2160,"title":"Chapter 2160 Dark Freezing Titan Elephant","paragraphs":["2160 Dark Freezing Titan Elephant","Weng Baochuan forcefully rubbed his eyes. He had always been obedient to Weng Queji.","Weng Baochuan knew what Weng Queji was getting at.","Before Lin Yuan arrived, Weng Baochuan had never imagined that the head of the faction that toppled the Truth Association could be a young boy!","For such a young man to head up a powerful faction, Lin Yuan was unstoppable when it came to power, regardless of his background.","If he could stay by Lin Yuan’s side, he would definitely gain endless benefits while Lin Yuan continued to develop his endeavors.","However, rather than increasing his power and training, Weng Baochuan hoped for the day that he would be able to achieve what Weng Queji could not.","Weng Baochuan made a wish to himself.","I have to cure Master! No matter what!","When Weng Queji saw that Weng Baochuan had stopped crying, he said softly, “Baochuan, go and take your two uncles to see Jin Qianxun. He is seriously lacking manpower, so go and see if he needs help.”","Weng Baochuan nodded earnestly.","Weng Baochuan knew that the main reason for his master saying that was that he wanted some peace.","Weng Baochuan left the space to Weng Queji.","As Weng Queji watched Weng Baochuan walking away, he was dazed for a moment before he sighed softly and said, “After this sigh, I will resign myself! This kind of life isn’t bad!”","If Weng Queji was not frowning deeply, his tone would have been taken as sincere.","After some time, Weng Queji’s gaze finally landed on the Spirit-Mouthed Peony that Lin Yuan had left behind.","The Moon Empress had specially nurtured the Spirit-Mouthed Peony.","Although the Creation Master was a Class 5 Creation Master, there was no way he could have ever seen it before.","Nonetheless, he had the discerning eye of a Class 5 Creation Master.","It did not take long for Weng Queji to figure out what the Spirit-Mouthed Peony was.","At that moment, Weng Queji understood Lin Yuan’s good intentions.","But at the same time, he felt that Lin Yuan was naive.","At first, Weng Queji had refused to accept his reality.","But Weng Queji noticed that the concentration of pure spirit qi he concocted with his Class 5 Creation Master powers was far from being able to meet his needs.","It was at that moment that he decided to give up.","But when Weng Queji casually pulled open the Spirit-Mouthed Peony, his jaw dropped in silent surprised delight.","The ever-steady Weng Queji hurriedly summoned his main fey as his body started to tremble.","For almost a century, Weng Queji had never been so full of burning passion and hope.","The fey that Weng Queji had summoned changed into human form. It had blue hair and white eyes and looked as though it had cataracts. Its sturdy body was full of solid power.","However, its hands were in different stages of decay.","A malady like this that only appeared on the weak and sickly made this stocky man seem like a paper tiger.","This man initially had the same expression as Weng Queji, akin to a bottle suddenly being smashed.","After sensing such pure spirit qi, the man now had the same expression as Weng Queji.","But in spite of his shock, the man hurriedly circulated his spiritual power and was afraid of wasting even the smallest trace of the pure spirit qi.","Weng Queji was spiritually linked to his main feys.","When Weng Queji sensed his main fey starting to recover after absorbing the pure spirit qi within the Spirit-Mouthed Peony, he forcefully waved his hand and screamed fervently, “Old friend, the heavens are so generous to us! We now have a chance to try again!”","While Weng Queji’s main fey was absorbing pure spirit qi, snow started to fall around it.","The man started to let out a buzzing noise.","This was the man’s way of responding to Weng Queji while it was absorbing pure spirit qi.","With renewed hope, the zen expression that used to hang off Weng Queji’s face vanished completely.","A few minutes ago, all Weng Queji had wanted was peace.","But now, his previously withered heart started to beat again.","Although it was just an instant, Weng Queji rediscovered his youthful courage to overcome problems and scale obstacles.","After two full hours, the man who had been sitting crossed-legged next to Weng Queji stood up.","Weng Queji had not shown any affection to his feys after contracting them.","But now, this man with blue hair and white eyes suddenly embraced Weng Queji.","Weng Queji let out a shocked gasp when he was hugged. But when he sensed his fey’s flaming heart, Weng Queji said, “Old friend, we were never able to cross that wall because we lacked spirit qi that was pure enough to help your bloodline to evolve. You won’t be stuck at Eternal V if your bloodline evolves!”","Weng Queji had not only found his motivation but was also able to see the light in his future again.","Weng Queji had not led an easy life and had not received many blessings along the way.","This was the first time that Weng Queji felt that he owed someone not just a favor but an enormous one.","After the blue-haired and white-eyed man was done with his exhibition of joy, he set Weng Queji back down on the ground.","The blue-haired and white-eyed man was silent for a moment before he said self-reproachfully, “If my bloodline wasn’t so special, we wouldn’t have wasted decades. It’s all my fault!”","While he spoke, he let his head and hand drop as an apologetic expression spread across his face.","Weng Queji placed a hand on the blue-haired and white-eyed man’s shoulder.","“Freezing Elephant, what are you saying? When I was young, I was a roaming orphan who was raised by a farmer couple. I always saw it as my biggest opportunity to have been able to form a contract with you. Without you, I would never have been able to become a spirit qi professional, much less have access to Creation Mastery. Do you remember how many times you’ve saved me during our journey together? I’ll feel hurt if you apologize to me!”","A look of reminiscence appeared on Weng Queji’s face.","When he saw that the blue-haired and white-eyed man lifted his head, Weng Queji looked into his eyes and smiled as he said, “Your bloodline might be special but isn’t weak at all. If your bloodline evolves from the Freezing Curse Sacred Elephant to the Dark Freezing Titan Elephant, your future will be boundless! So, there’s no need for you to be down on yourself!”"]},{"number":2161,"title":"Chapter 2161 The Gift From Lin Yuan!","paragraphs":["2161 The Gift From Lin Yuan!","Weng Queji had never been a man of many words. He had been quiet since he was young.","He had not even said much to Freezing Elephant over the years. Both of them quietly stayed by each other’s side.","But after spilling so many words that came from the heart, Weng Queji suddenly felt that he had been too quiet all these years and neglected to show care for his feys.","Weng Queji waved his hand and summoned the rest of his feys.","Warmth and hope started to fill the tent.","Weng Queji only returned his feys to his spiritual spatial zone after the moon had been hanging in the sky for many hours.","Weng Queji was in no rush to ask Lin Yuan for more pure spirit qi. He assumed that such pure spirit qi was hard to come by.","Weng Queji decided to focus on the tasks that Lin Yuan gave him before he asked Lin Yuan for more rewards.","After all, he had not made any significant contributions yet. His skin was not thick enough to ask for unfounded rewards.","Thus, Weng Queji started to concoct spirit fluids that Lin Yuan could use to nurture the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers.","After Lin Yuan left Weng Queji’s tent, he went to see Jin Qianxun.","When Lin Yuan was speaking with Jin Qianxun, Weng Baochuan walked in with Weng Queji’s two retainers.","As the retainers of a Class 5 Creation Master, it was very likely that their main feys had reached pinnacle Immortal.","With Weng Baochuan and Weng Queji’s two retainers helping Jin Qianxun, Lin Yuan would not have to put in so much effort.","Ever since Jin Qianxun obtained the loyalty of the leaders of the secret aristocratic families, he no longer had any nerves holding him back.","After communicating with all the leaders of the secret aristocratic families, Jin Qianxun came up with a secret hit list.","The names on the list were all troublemakers who were thorns in the sides of the leaders of the secret aristocratic families as well as the naysayers against Jin Qianxun and the Jin family.","Jin Qianxun handed the compiled list to Weng Baochuan. He hoped that Weng Baochuan and Weng Queji’s two retainers would be able to kill the people on the list in secret.","Although Jin Qianxun had gained a shade of the authoritative nature of a king, he still did not have the courage to order Weng Queji’s two retainers around.","Weng Baochuan did not find anything wrong with Jin Qianxun’s request.","Bloodshed and assassinations were common when the Truth Association was in charge of the Great Lush Federation. Weng Baochuan had personally witnessed such events countless times.","Since it was assassinations, they could not be done out in the open.","On the way to the capital of the Great Lush Federation, Clean Brahma City, Weng Queji had managed to send over 90 of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers to Lin Yuan.","He also asked Lin Yuan if the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers needed to be evolved to Diamond X/Legend.","Lin Yuan immediately stored the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers in the Spirit Lock spatial zone and did not tell Weng Queji to further evolve their power and quality.","It would be much more efficient to task the army of Hundred Questions Beasts to evolve the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers rather than using up the time of a Class 5 Creation Master.","When Lin Yuan did not tell Weng Queji to continue evolving the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers, Weng Queji was about to ask Lin Yuan if there were any other tasks for him when he received a Diamond Item-Storing Walnut from Lin Yuan.","“Elder Weng, you have given me so many spirit fluids. The Grade 4 and 5 spirit fluids will be very useful to me. They will be perfect for nurturing some of my subordinates. The contents of the Item-Storing Walnut are my gift to you. I hope that you will be happy in the coming days as a member of Sky City’s family.","“If you have the time and energy, I would appreciate it if you could concoct different Grade 5 spirit fluids. If you need any ingredients, don’t hesitate to ask Su Yiren.”","Lin Yuan’s gesture moved Weng Queji.","Lin Yuan had already given him one of the Spirit-Mouthed Peonies. This meant that Lin Yuan had guessed that Weng Queji needed pure spirit qi.","Could there be more of the Spirit-Mouthed Peonies inside the Item-Storing Walnut?","Weng Queji could not bring himself to ask for them and preferred Lin Yuan to voluntarily hand them over. After all, Weng Queji usually only delivered resources and had never asked anyone for resources.","Weng Queji received the Item-Storing Walnut courteously and did not immediately look inside.","But once he returned to his tent, he tipped out all of the items within the Item-Storing Walnut.","Three beautifully crafted brocade boxes were revealed.","Weng Queji immediately recognized the threads as having come from the Glowing Silkworm Weaver.","When he opened the first brocade box, Weng Queji saw almost 20 of the Spirit-Mouthed Peonies lying within it.","The first Spirit-Mouthed Peony that Lin Yuan had given Weng Queji had already been immensely encouraging to him. He would never have dared to dream that he could receive 20 of the Spirit-Mouthed Peonies.","The 20 Spirit-Mouthed Peonies were the best present that Weng Queji could have ever hoped for.","Although there were not enough of the Spirit-Mouthed Peonies to fully transform Freezing Elephant’s bloodline, there were enough to heal its roots.","With Lin Yuan’s generosity, Weng Queji’s gratitude toward him multiplied.","Previously, Weng Queji was still slightly sore about having to swear his loyalty to Lin Yuan. But now he could not be gladder.","The contents of this one brocade box were already more than what Weng Queji could have hoped for.","But he was still very curious to find out what was in the other two boxes.","Weng Queji opened the second brocade box and was almost blinded by the light that flooded out of it.","It was not difficult for Class 5 Creation Masters to produce heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","Almost half of the Great Lush Federation was surrounded by the sea, so there was no lack of Elemental Shellfish in the Great Lush Federation.","But despite being a Class 5 Creation Master, Weng Queji had only managed to produce a few of the Over the Rail Coral elemental pearls.","It was almost just as difficult for Class 5 Creation Masters to nurture the Over the Rail Coral elemental pearls as it was for Class 4 Creation Masters to nurture the Cloud Dream Lake elemental pearls.","Yet, in this brocade box which contained hundreds of the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, the lowest quality of the lot was Over the Rail Coral. There were even a few of the Heavenly Maiden Sleet elemental pearls.","Weng Queji had never had the chance to lay eyes on heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls of such high quality, much less own them!"]},{"number":2162,"title":"Chapter 2162 Dead Masters and Servants!","paragraphs":["2162 Dead Masters and Servants!","The contents of the first brocade box had allowed Lin Yuan to win Weng Queji’s sincerity.","But this second box allowed Weng Queji to see the benefit of submitting to Lin Yuan as well as the warmth of being part of Sky City.","Weng Queji remembered Lin Yuan saying that he was going to use the Grade 4 and 5 spirit fluids to nurture his subordinates.","The way that Lin Yuan was willing to use Grade 4 and 5 spirit fluids on his subordinates showed how generous he was to those under him.","Weng Queji reached out and took hold of the third brocade box. It was clearly larger than the second brocade box.","When Weng Queji opened the third brocade box, he was greeted by a small crystal bottle that was about half the size of a palm.","The crystal bottle was full of an amber fluid that resembled honey.","Weng Queji opened the cap of the crystal bottle and examined it closely. Soon, his jaw dropped again.","It could be said that he had been shocked more times after meeting Lin Yuan than he had been in his entire career as a Class 5 Creation Master.","Weng Queji was not aware of the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia, of which there were only two in the world. However, he could sense the effectiveness of the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","Very few items in the world could cleanse a body of all its impurities.","The Moon Empress was the only one in the Radiance Federation with such an item.","Although Chef Supreme and the Bamboo Monarch were also Class 5 Creation Masters, they still had to seek the Moon Empress out when they wanted to cleanse the impurities from their disciples’ bodies.","Since this was the case for the Class 5 Creation Masters in one of the three major federations, the nomad Weng Queji did not even need to be mentioned.","The crystal bottle was filled to the brim with the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar. There was enough to thoroughly cleanse the bodies of two people.","It was clear that Lin Yuan had taken Weng Baochuan into consideration.","Parents were always more grateful to those who were kind to their children than if they were to be on the receiving end themselves.","This was exactly how Weng Queji was feeling.","After a person’s body was cleansed of impurities, they would be able to contract most source-type items.","There were many source-type items that had strict conditions for the quality of their contractors’ bodies.","Weng Baochuan would have his pick of source-type items and could perfectly make up for his lacking combat abilities.","Weng Queji was speechless at the contents of the three brocade boxes.","It seemed that all he could do to repay Lin Yuan was work to the best of his abilities.","They were currently on the way to Clean Brahma City so healing Freezing Elephant’s roots now would attract a lot of attention.","It would be better to wait until they settled into Clean Brahma City.","When they arrived at Clean Brahma City, Jin Qianxun immediately asserted his status as king and took over the imperial court, which the Truth Association had previously occupied.","The Jin family had over 300 direct descendants and more than 10,000 collateral descendants. More than 300,000 guards and servants attended to the Jin family.","With so many collateral descendants, guards, and servants, the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court quickly became spick and span.","All of the secret aristocratic families had been forbidden from entering the Truth Association’s territory. Not even Jin Qianding had ever entered.","Jin Qianxun was very curious about this place.","When he pushed open the bronze gates and stepped into the area that had been exclusive to the Truth Association, Jin Qianxun was greeted by a peculiar bronze tower.","There were 37 people lying by the tower’s feet.","From the way that the 37 corpses were positioned, one could tell that the leader had been standing while the other 36 had been kneeling.","There was blood seeping out of all of their orifices.","This was clearly the case of dead masters and servants.","Jin Qianxun did not know that Fifth Page Truth had been the leader of the Truth Association, nor was he aware of the existence of Tower Canon.","However, Jin Qianxun knew that all of these dead people had sworn their loyalty to the head of the tower, just like his first brother had.","Jin Qianxun did not know if he should get this place cleaned up.","He might end up damaging or losing something that Lin Yuan needed.","Jin Qianxun immediately sent a message to Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","When Lin Yuan received the message, he immediately took Liu Jie and Su Yiren with him to the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court.","Lin Yuan had heard the Moon Empress and Purple Love mention that Tower Canon had gotten its name from the bronze towers that each of the Eight Pages presided over.","Lin Yuan believed that Fifth Page Truth’s light bronze tower had to contain at least one of Tower Canon’s secrets.","He had already looked inside Fifth Page Truth’s spatial equipment. There were at least three times the number of resources within it than there were in the Divine Wood Federation’s imperial court.","It was likely that there was also a fair amount of resources within Fifth Page Truth’s subordinates’ spatial equipment.","Lin Yuan was very enthusiastic when it came to gathering resources.","If he was not as active as he was, he would not be able to support Sky City.","It was difficult to raise a family! All the required resources had to be gathered!","Everything that Jin Qianxun had came from Lin Yuan. He respected and felt more affection for Lin Yuan than he did for his dead parents.","Despite being the ruler of the Great Lush Federation, Jin Qianxun personally greeted Lin Yuan at the entrance of the imperial court.","Although many of the Jin family’s collateral descendants and servants stared at him confusedly, Jin Qianxun did not care.","Since he had led the Jin family into the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court, Jin Qianxun was now the most venerated individual in the Jin family’s history.","But Jin Qianxun cared more about how Lin Yuan saw him than maintaining his reputation in front of others.","Jin Qianxun had brought with him all of the resources that he had prepared and immediately handed them over to Lin Yuan when they met.","When Lin Yuan looked through them, he saw that Jin Qianxun had gathered more resources than the Yang family had when they were in charge of the Divine Wood Federation’s imperial court.","This was unsurprising.","A likely explanation was that Fifth Page Truth’s envoys had taken most of the Yang family’s resources back to the Truth Association.","Jin Qianxun had been increasingly feeling like he was of no use to Lin Yuan. As a result, he felt increasingly less confident standing by Lin Yuan’s side.","Jin Qianxun had come up with an idea while he was on the way to Clean Brahma City.","He felt that it was time for him to tell Lin Yuan about that idea.","This was the best chance for him to demonstrate his loyalty.","Jin Qianxun gnashed his teeth and said, “Lord Lin Yuan, I intend to gather the resources from all of the Great Lush Federation’s families’ treasure vaults and give them to you!","“You spoke with me about the Great Lush Federation’s development issue. All of the Great Lush Federation’s families are now under my control and have no authority of their own. They might end up undisciplined again like they were under the Truth Association’s rule.”"]},{"number":2163,"title":"Chapter 2163 20 Island Whales!","paragraphs":["2163 20 Island Whales!","As Jin Qianxun spoke, he carefully observed Lin Yuan’s expression.","Alas, he was unable to pick out any out-of-the-ordinary expressions on Lin Yuan’s face.","Jin Qianxun mustered his courage and said, “I intend to rule with an iron fist and keep all of the secret aristocratic families in order using force. This way, they won’t be able to become undisciplined.”","Su Yiren and Liu Jie frowned when they heard what Jin Qianxun said.","If a family or faction could not even keep a hold of its resources, it would lose all of its vigor.","Not even Fifth Page Truth had done such a thing when he ruled over the Great Lush Federation.","But now, Jin Qianxun would use this method to control all of the Great Lush Federation’s secret aristocratic families.","Although this method would undoubtedly rake in large profits for Lin Yuan, it would be disastrous for the Great Lush Federation in the long run.","Jin Qianxun could rule with an iron fist without taking all of the secret aristocratic families’ resources.","Given Liu Jie and Su Yiren’s backgrounds and statuses, they scorned the method that Jin Qianxun chose to try and curry favor with Lin Yuan.","They also knew Lin Yuan intended to properly develop the Startling Lines Continent.","Jin Qianxun’s actions went against Lin Yuan’s intention.","Lin Yuan looked deeply into Jin Qianxun’s eyes. He felt that it was necessary for him to make some things clear to Jin Qianxun.","He knew that Jin Qianxun was doing this to try and gain favor with him.","Jin Qianxun had to be lacking a sense of security.","Lin Yuan intended to give Jin Qianxun this sense of security with what he was about to say.","If Jin Qianxun still decided not to prioritize the Great Lush Federation’s welfare, he would not be fit to continue occupying its throne.","When Lin Yuan did not respond immediately to what Jin Qianxun said, the latter immediately became nervous.","At that moment, Lin Yuan said sternly and solemnly, “Before Yi Huailong took the throne of the Divine Wood Federation, I told him what I expected of him. I want him to rebuild the Divine Wood Hundred Sequence and make it so that five Divine Wood Envoys are able to attend the Major Federation Meeting a few decades later and fight for glory on the Divine Wood Federation’s behalf.","“I have the same hopes for the Great Lush Federation. Do you understand what I’m saying?”","Lin Yuan looked straight into Jin Qianxun’s eyes when he spoke.","Instinctively, Jin Qianxun wanted to avert his gaze.","But Lin Yuan’s words ended up lighting a spark within Jin Qianxun that he had been trying to suppress for a long time.","After being lost for so long, Jin Qianxun finally knew what he had to do.","As long as he could bring glory to and strengthen the Great Lush Federation, he would be able to meet Lin Yuan’s expectations.","At that time, he would no longer lack a sense of security.","Jin Qianxun would rather be worshiped in the Great Lush Federation than just in the Jin family. He wanted to be cemented into the Great Lush Federation’s history books and be remembered for generations to come.","Jin Qianxun balled his fists and said loudly, “I understand! I know what to do! I heard that you want to rebuild the harbor. I should be able to help!","“Many of the secret aristocratic families have spirit qi professionals who are skilled at working underwater. I can gather them together. Since the Great Lush Federation is so close to the sea, there are many canals. These spirit qi professionals who are skilled at working underwater are definitely capable.","“In the future, I intend to center the Great Lush Federation around academics. We will go to the Divine Wood Federation and Iron Hammer Federation to teach and set up schools.”","When Jin Qianxun was done speaking, he looked to Lin Yuan to see if he approved his plan.","Su Yiren started looking at Jin Qianxun in a slightly different way after listening to him.","While the Great Lush Federation’s aristocratic families were on the way to Clean Brahma City, Lin Yuan had told Jin Qianxun about how he wanted to take control of all the trading activities within the Startling Lines Continent.","It could be said that Lin Yuan’s decision changed the Great Lush Federation’s previously indolent nature.","But now, apart from trading, Jin Qianxun found a more suitable way to develop the Great Lush Federation.","Jin Qianxun had pinpointed the Great Lush Federation’s strength.","There were many Scholars, Spiritual Ingredient Analysts, and Fey Observers in the Great Lush Federation. They had several times the number that the Divine Wood Federation and Iron Hammer Federation had.","The education level in the Divine Wood Federation and Iron Hammer Federation was much lower than that of the Great Lush Federation.","In the Great Lush Federation, every child underwent 15 years of education as long as they could afford the school fees.","Many of the Great Lush Federation’s secret aristocratic families had previously formed chambers of commerce to make their living. As a result, they had accumulated a mountain of experience.","Now, they could export their Scholars, Spiritual Ingredient Analysts, and Fey Observers to the Divine Wood Federation and Iron Hammer Federation.","There was a lot of revenue to be earned from investing in chambers of commerce, but the cost of operations was also not low.","But to set up the schools, all they needed was to send over their Scholars, Fey Observers, and Spiritual Ingredient Analysts. This would not cost much at all.","If an academic was willing to settle down in one of the Divine Wood Federation’s smaller cities or tribes, the locals would be more than willing to provide a tent or tree castle.","Lin Yuan smiled assuredly at Jin Qianxun.","“That isn’t a bad idea! I will let Yi Huailong and Luo Lan know. They will ensure the safety of the Scholars while they’re in the Divine Wood Federation and Iron Hammer Federation.","“I do need some spirit qi professionals who are skilled at working underwater for the new harbor project. While I want to take control of the Great Lush Federation’s trading, I also want to compensate the Great Lush Federation.","“You thought of the Great Lush Federations’ new development direction all on your own. After the harbor’s construction, I will arrange for at least 20 mature Island Whales. At that time, you can send some of your trusted men to ride the Island Whales to trade with the other federations. Given the Great Lush Federation’s advantageous geographical position, long-distance trading is the best option.”","Lin Yuan’s words instantly broadened Jin Qianxun’s horizons.","He had been solely focused on the Startling Lines Continent and had never considered crossing the ocean.","But Lin Yuan had casually said that he would place 20 Island Whales in the harbor.","Being a native of the Great Lush Federation, Jin Qianxun had seen less than 20 Island Whales in his life so far.","Since there were no Class 5 Creation Masters in the Great Lush Federation, it did not even have one Island Whale.","However, with his background as a member of one of the Great Lush Federation’s secret aristocratic families, Jin Qianxun had seen the Island Whales from other federations that had come to trade with the Great Lush Federation.","The Great Lush Federation was finally about to have Island Whales of its own, and 20 at them!"]},{"number":2164,"title":"Chapter 2164 Crimson Spirit Bronze!","paragraphs":["2164 Crimson Spirit Bronze!","Jin Qianxun had discovered long ago that Yi Huailong was under Lin Yuan’s control and that the entire Divine Wood Federation was Lin Yuan’s back garden.","But he did not know that Lin Yuan also had control over the Iron Hammer Federation.","This meant that with Jin Qianxun as the king of the Great Lush Federation, Lin Yuan’s name would be branded on the entire Startling Lines Continent!","It was likely that Luo Lan and Yi Huailong cared as much about the tasks that Lin Yuan gave them as he did.","When the Scholars, Fey Observers, and Spiritual Ingredient Analysts went to the Divine Wood Federation and Iron Hammer Federation to set up schools, it was unlikely that they would face obstruction from the ministerial officials.","Lin Yuan’s words had already given Jin Qianxun a sense of security. But now, he had laid all of his worries well and truly at rest.","Lin Yuan had to trust him deeply to let him take charge of such an important project as the harbor that would have 20 Island Whales servicing it.","Lin Yuan had no idea that he had left such a mental impact on Jin Qianxun by leaving the harbor in his hands.","Lin Yuan also had his own considerations.","Lin Yuan would struggle to leave one of his close companions on the Island Whales to manage the trading.","After all, Sky City did not have many members.","The lowest-ranked members were the white-clothed followers.","Even after the expansion, there were still only less than 400 white-clothed followers.","An adult Island Whale grew by more than 10,000 meters per year. It was much larger than any floating sea fortress that humans could build.","A human-built ship needed hundreds of people to keep it functioning, while the Island Whale needed more than 2,000 people.","Lin Yuan did not have 40,000 people to spare in Sky City that he could leave on the 20 Island Whales.","Since the harbor was in the Startling Lines Continent, Jin Qianxun was the best person to manage it.","Since he had taken control of the trades that the Great Lush Federation had spent hundreds of years establishing, it was only right for him to compensate them.","There were enough members of the Great Lush Federation’s secret aristocratic families to service the 20 Island Whales.","Although not even Class 6 Creation Masters could produce the resources that Lin Yuan could, and the Spirit Lock spatial zone produced elemental pearls in an endless stream, he had only been a spirit qi professional for a year.","There was no way that a year would be enough for him to produce enough resources to meet the needs of 20 Island Whales.","Lin Yuan had promised to give Jin Qianxun 20 Island Whales because of the resources that Fifth Page Truth had accumulated.","The 20 Island Whales had been stored in a precious instrument that Fifth Page Truth had made from the body of a water-type sacred source lifeform.","It turned out that one could get rich so easily by killing and stealing!","This was why Lin Yuan had immediately rushed over when he received Jin Qianxun’s message.","Fifth Page Truth had to take the Truth Association’s most precious resources everywhere with him. But the less important resources had to be stored in the Truth Association.","While they headed into the depths of the imperial court, Jin Qianxun conversed with Lin Yuan.","The more they talked, the more ambition bloomed within Jin Qianxun.","It could be said that Jin Qianxun had found his main direction for the imperial court.","When they reached a giant door, Jin Qianxun did not follow Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, and Su Yiren in. Rather, he stayed outside and gazed at the large door as he absorbed the contents of his conversation with Lin Yuan.","The center of the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court had already undergone special remodeling as it had served as the Truth Association’s main camp.","A somewhat unique space had been constructed out of a large amount of spatial spiritual ingredients.","Su Yiren looked at the bronze tower with intense hatred.","“Young Master, Seventh Page War also brought along a similar tower when she invaded the Dark Continent. My grandmother never managed to leave the tower after her fight with Seventh Page War.”","Lin Yuan patted Su Yiren’s shoulder to comfort her.","At that moment, Morbius’ voice appeared in Lin Yuan’s mind, “Partner, this tower is made from the Crimson Spirit Bronze! I can try to refine the Crimson Spirit Bronze using my root power. This tower might be your biggest prize for killing Fifth Page War!”","Shock immediately spread across Lin Yuan’s face.","The profits he had gained since killing Fifth Page Truth were unquantifiable.","Apart from the 20 Island Whales, Lin Yuan had also gained the body of a 10 Stars sacred source lifeform.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen could increase the rate at which it raised its Stars through the Law Staff.","But Morbius believed that none of these could match up to this tower. Was it because of the Crimson Spirit Bronze?","Lin Yuan had never heard of the Crimson Spirit Bronze.","When Morbius sensed Lin Yuan’s shock, it said, “Partner, the Crimson Spirit Bronze is a metal spiritual ingredient that has surpassed Sovereign.","Lin Yuan’s mind immediately started to wonder if the Crimson Spirit Bronze could be fed to the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","However, this would mean that the Sovereign metal spiritual ingredient that the Perfect Touch Wisteria had just absorbed would go to waste before the Perfect Touch Wisteria had the chance to use it.","Lin Yuan would find it a big waste to replace the Coiling Dragon Blood Gold without even using it once, much less a Sovereign metal spiritual ingredient.","Morbius sensed how Lin Yuan felt and hurriedly said, “Partner, it would be a true waste to allow the Perfect Touch Wisteria to use the Crimson Spirit Bronze!","“The Crimson Spirit Bronze’s effects are to protect souls and hide auras. Infuse your soul power into the Crimson Spirit Bronze to brand your soul on it. When your soul is attacked, the Crimson Spirit Bronze will help sustain some damage. When the Crimson Spirit Bronze is on your person, no external entities will be able to sense your aura!","“If a top assassin carries the Crimson Spirit Bronze, their combat power will be multiplied. Tower Canon did not choose the Crimson Spirit Bronze to create their towers just to show off their status. They’re likely hiding something. Otherwise, there’s no need to mix in so much of the Sovereign Ever-Changing Temper Gold into the Crimson Spirit Bronze to mold its shape.”","Morbius’ explanation caused Lin Yuan to narrow his eyes.","The Crimson Spirit Bronze was truly a treasure!","While Morbius was talking about the Crimson Spirit Bronze’s effects, Lin Yuan was wondering how many hanging pieces could be made out of this tower."]},{"number":2165,"title":"Chapter 2165 Crux of Tower Canon?","paragraphs":["2165 Crux of Tower Canon?","Now, Lin Yuan knew that this tower was made of a mixture of the Crimson Spirit Bronze and Ever-Changing Temper Gold.","Given how precious the Crimson Spirit Bronze was, its proportion should not be large.","When Lin Yuan saw how excited Morbius was getting, he knew that there had to be more than what met the eye to whatever was hidden within this tower.","It was possible that whatever was hidden within the tower could be more outstanding than the Crimson Spirit Bronze.","Lin Yuan told Liu Jie and Su Yiren, “Big Brother Liu and Su Yiren, help me collect all of the resources from Fifth Page Truth’s servants. I’m going to take a look inside the tower!”","Liu Jie instinctively wanted to speak up.","He was Lin Yuan’s retainer, so Lin Yuan’s safety was always his top priority.","Fifth Page Truth’s tower was unknown territory. Who knew what was hidden within?","But eventually, Liu Jie stopped himself from saying anything.","Lin Yuan had even managed to kill Fifth Page Truth. Was there anything that he could not handle?","Even if there was anything dangerous inside this tower that belonged to a dead person, it was likely that Lin Yuan would be able to handle it with ease.","Thus, Liu Jie led Su Yiren to gather all the resources outside the tower.","Lin Yuan entered the tower.","Begin Lady was right on Lin Yuan’s face.","He was aware that the tower was not safe but was still unafraid.","There were many levels in the tower.","The first level was a large hall. A long table made of bone was at the back of the hall.","It was likely that Fifth Page Truth’s throne of bones used to sit next to the long table.","After checking on it with True Data, Lin Yuan realized that this large table made of bones was made fully of the bones of Creation Breed and above feys.","Lin Yuan was not interested in furniture made from the bones of feys. Thus, he decided to take this table apart and divide the bones among Weng Queji, Yi Huailu, and Di Wanmi to be used in concocting Grade 5 spirit fluids.","Many Grade 5 spirit fluids required the bones of Creation Breed feys.","When Lin Yuan reached the second level, he looked at the scene before him with shock.","It fully resembled a theme park.","Fifth Page Truth had had the appearance of a young boy. Could this have been his playground?","Lin Yuan found it difficult to believe that Fifth Page Truth, at his age, had such a secret interest!","After looking through the second level, Lin Yuan noticed that the materials used to make the toys were all valuable.","Lin Yuan did not even have a girlfriend, so being a father was impossible.","Chu Ci was already 16 years old and had no need for such toys.","Hence, Lin Yuan decided to take apart these toys as well.","On his way to the third level, Lin Yuan could not help but wonder to himself if the entire tower was filled with such bizarre artifacts.","It would take Lin Yuan a week or two to take apart the toys from the second floor and turn them into usable spiritual ingredients.","But when he reached the third level, he saw that it was almost ten times the size of the first and second levels.","Yet, the tower had a uniform shape when viewed from the outside.","This phenomenon was most likely because Fifth Page Truth had used a method to shrink and stabilize the space.","There were ten shelves on the third floor, each filled with bottle-shaped spatial equipment.","Lin Yuan picked up one of the bottles and looked inside. He saw that it was filled with many resources.","The resources were categorized neatly and padded up Sky Creation’s store of resources well.","Many of the resources in the bottle could be classified as resources meant for war.","Lin Yuan was curious about why Fifth Page Truth had stored away so many resources meant for war.","As Lin Yuan traveled from the fourth to the fifth, to the sixth, seventh, and finally, the 12th floor, there was not once that he was disappointed by what he found.","Lin Yuan had truly emptied out Fifth Page Truth’s pockets and used them to feed Sky City.","From just the resources that Fifth Page Truth had accumulated, Lin Yuan could easily nurture all of the white-clothed followers to B-rank. There was no need for him to worry about earning resources.","Lin Yuan was secretly pumped up.","Of the over 400 white-clothed followers, none of their main feys had reached Fantasy Breed. Lin Yuan had left all of them at Diamond X/Fantasy V.","The white-clothed followers must go through at least three World Cleansings before their feys evolved to Creation Breed.","If Lin Yuan absorbed a small part of every World Grace that descended, he could gain countless spirit qi crystals.","Resources were much more useful when they were turned into power rather than being left in storage.","Lin Yuan intended to spend most of Fifth Page Truth’s resources quickly to arm the white-clothed followers and strengthen the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","Lin Yuan had not let down his guard for a second while he was looking through the resources in the Tower of Truth.","Lin Yuan remembered Morbius mentioning that there could be something trapped inside the tower.","When he first arrived on the 13th floor, Lin Yuan suddenly felt his soul being strongly pulled. The sensation was dizzying.","Lin Yuan could hear a faint and beautifully melancholic wail.","He activated the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen and used it to suppress the dizziness.","Lin Yuan looked up ahead, and the sight caused his back to break out in cold sweat.","He saw a partially see-through girl wearing a red pleated dress and staring at him unblinkingly.","She was holding a book, and the sorrowful wail was coming from within the book.","Begin Lady materialized next to Lin Yuan and used a pink and gold stream of water to shield him. Nonetheless, it could not fend off the tugging on Lin Yuan’s soul.","But the stream of water did block the effects of the sobbing. He no longer had the feeling of wanting to draw his sword and end his life.","After Begin Lady appeared, it carefully inspected the situation.","After a few seconds of silence, it said, “Lin Yuan, this girl isn’t alive! That book is interesting! Even my soul is slightly affected! Wait here while I go and get that book for you!”","Lin Yuan’s brain kicked into high gear when he heard that it was a book.","Tower Canon... Tower Canon...","There was a tome hidden in each of the Eight Pages’ towers.","Were the books the crux of Tower Canon?"]},{"number":2166,"title":"Chapter 2166 Secret of the Dead, Volume 5, Sinking Song!","paragraphs":["2166 Secret of the Dead, Volume 5, Sinking Song!","The book was dead.","Even without being activated, it could affect Begin Lady, who had already set its spirit fire alight.","Just what was this book?","Begin Lady did not use its body to touch the purple and gray-bound tome. Instead, it used a stream of water to deliver the book to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan instinctively used True Data to check on the book.","The instant that he found out that the book was called ‘Secret of the Dead, Volume 5, Sinking Song’, the book sensed the fresh vitality of a living creature and entered Lin Yuan’s body.","At that moment, just like when he had awakened Morbius back in Xia Region, the darkness captured Lin Yuan and he lost consciousness.","...","The monsoon season in the Great Lush Federation lasted from April to May.","Hurricanes swept through Clean Brahma City every one or two weeks.","No matter how efficient the water drainage system was in Clean Brahma City, the streets were rarely dry during this period.","But today, when the citizens of Clean Brahma City woke up, they realized with shock that the sun was hanging proudly in the cloudless sky.","Many residents in Clean Brahma City started to take pictures of this unusual but welcome weather.","The Great Lush Federation had undergone a big change in the past two weeks.","Usually, even the smallest of changes affected ordinary people the most.","But this change did not affect ordinary people at all.","Rather, Jin Qianxun had invested many funds into repairing the city. This greatly lifted the standards of living for the citizens of Clean Brahma City.","It was not just the capital city that was undergoing repairs but the smaller towns as well.","Jin Qianxun used this method to obtain a large wave of support from the citizens.","In two weeks, Jin Qianxun’s organization of affairs had smoothened into a well-oiled machine, and he could sit soundly on the throne of the Great Lush Federation.","However, Jin Qianxun did not feel relaxed in the slightest. In fact, he had been steeped in worry for the past two weeks.","Lin Yuan had gone to collect the Truth Association’s resources after receiving notice from Jin Qianxun. Yet, he had ended up losing consciousness and had yet to open his eyes.","Jin Qianxun was worried about the condition of Lin Yuan’s body but also about whether he could continue to occupy the throne without Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan’s comatose state left Jin Qianxun no different from a blade of grass floating in the wind.","Jin Qianxun’s main concern was for himself, but this was not the case for Su Yiren, Liu Jie, and Begin Lady.","At that moment, in one of the rooms in the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court, a man and two women were staring at a young man sleeping on the bed with distress written all over their faces.","The young man’s shadow was moving erratically.","When Su Yiren noticed the movement of the shadow, she said, “Shadow, if you’re worried about Lin Yuan, come out and watch him with us.”","She turned to Liu Jie and said, “Big Brother Liu, it won’t do you any good to sit here forever. We don’t know when Lin Yuan is going to wake up. You haven’t rested in 15 days and are only making do with your spiritual power now. This might impact your brain. Lin Yuan won’t want to see you like this when he wakes up.”","When Liu Jie heard what Su Yiren said, he shook his head austerely","Begin Lady had told him about what had happened to Lin Yuan inside the tower.","Liu Jie pinned all the blame onto himself.","If only he had gone with Lin Yuan, he might have been able to shield him and prevent that strange book from entering Lin Yuan’s body.","However, the one feeling the most self-reproachful was not Liu Jie.","Begin Lady was feeling more blame than Liu Jie did.","It was the one who had brought the strange book to Lin Yuan.","When Liu Jie did not respond, Begin Lady grabbed his hand and pointed at Lin Yuan, saying, “This bed is three-meters-wide. Go and lie down there to get some rest. That way, you won’t have to leave Lin Yuan’s side. He isn’t in critical condition, and his signs of life haven’t diminished in the slightest.","“This is why I told Jin Qianxun to put a lockdown on the news. Not even Weng Queji knows that Lin Yuan is in a coma. If Lin Yuan doesn’t wake up soon, we will have to take him out of the Great Lush Federation!”","Su Yiren looked at Begin Lady.","Liu Jie had seen Begin Lady, but Su Yiren had not.","But once Begin Lady dashed out of Fifth Page Truth’s tower with Lin Yuan, she immediately placed it as an expert that was protecting Lin Yuan.","Su Yiren nodded when it heard what Begin Lady said.","If Lin Yuan did not wake up soon, the news should no longer be sealed.","Begin Lady had carefully examined Lin Yuan 15 days ago but could not find out the reason behind Lin Yuan’s coma.","Begin Lady had heard Lin Yuan say before that the Moon Empress was a Class 6 Creation Master.","If Lin Yuan did not wake up soon, Begin Lady would seek Lin Yuan’s master out and let her study Lin Yuan’s condition.","Just as Begin Lady was about to speak, it sensed Lin Yuan’s breathing had changed.","Delight immediately bloomed on its face, and its gaze locked on Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan’s eyelashes started to flutter.","Begin Lady knew that Lin Yuan was finally about to wake up!","Su Yiren and Liu Jie were not strong enough to sense the change in Lin Yuan’s breathing. But both of their minds were fully focused on Lin Yuan and had noticed the movement in his eyelashes.","Liu Jie and Su Yiren immediately jumped to their feet with joy.","When Lin Yuan groggily opened his eyes, he was instantly starving. It was as though he desperately needed to replenish his blood sugar.","Lin Yuan could sense how badly his body was craving nutrients.","The cause of all this was the strange book that had taken root in the divine kingdom. It was the book that was pushing his desire for replenishment.","All of the nutrients in Lin Yuan’s body had been sucked dry by the book known as ‘Secret of the Dead, Volume 5, Sinking Song’.","Liu Jie, Su Yiren, and Begin Lady were waiting for Lin Yuan to fully open his eyes so they could check on his condition.","When Lin Yuan finally opened his eyes, he said feebly, “Get me something to eat.”","Liu Jie immediately brought out food from his Diamond fey storage box and piled them on the table next to the bed so Lin Yuan could pick what he wanted himself."]},{"number":2167,"title":"Chapter 2167 Lin Yuan’s Large Appetite!","paragraphs":["2167 Lin Yuan’s Large Appetite!","Liu Jie’s Diamond fey storage box had been custom-ordered by Night Leaning Moon from Ostrich Logistics.","Liu Jie’s Diamond fey storage box had a much larger storage space than regular Diamond fey storage boxes and much better preservation effects.","When Liu Jie had time, he liked to fill the Diamond fey storage box with cooked dishes so he and Lin Yuan could enjoy delicacies even if they were not in an ideal place for cooking.","A mouth-watering fragrance permeated the air when Liu Jie laid out the food he had carefully cooked on the table.","In spite of their worry and elation, Su Yiren and Begin Lady began to salivate.","Naturally, the same went for Lin Yuan.","Due to the strange book, Lin Yuan was now absolutely starving.","When he caught a whiff of the food, Lin Yuan could not help but want to stuff them into his mouth.","However, Lin Yuan was in much too weak of a state to move himself to the table to eat.","He struggled to lift his hand and pointed at the table as he said weakly, “Big Brother Liu, I can’t get up now. Please move the food closer to me!”","While Liu Jie was laying out the food, he froze.","As he picked out some of the food that Lin Yuan liked best and moved them to Lin Yuan’s face, Su Yiren picked up a plate of roasted meat and peeled a jackfruit to reveal the soft flesh underneath. She wrapped the meat in the fruit and placed it in Lin Yuan’s mouth.","A spirit qi professional’s body was much stronger than a regular person’s.","Lin Yuan was a B-rank spirit qi professional and had already cleansed his body of impurities.","Although he had been comatose for 15 days, there was no need to stick to a light diet.","If a regular person consumed such rich food after 15 days of not eating, their stomach would immediately be in turmoil.","Su Yiren had already been with Lin Yuan for a considerable amount of time. To her memory, he did not eat much and rarely went for seconds.","But now, his appetite was astonishing. It was as though his body had turned into a bottomless well.","No matter how much food Su Yiren fed him, Lin Yuan would eat it.","His craving for food had reached an almost insane point!","At that moment, Lin Yuan seemed to be hungrier than the members of the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribes had been when they were stuck in the sea of flowers.","Lin Yuan’s state increasingly perturbed Su Yiren.","After Lin Yuan had consumed a plate of roasted meat, roasted fish, and four jackfruits, he finally regained some of his strength.","The dishes Liu Jie had taken out were all Lin Yuan’s favorites.","There was enough food on the table to feed 30 full-grown men.","However, all of the food ended up in Lin Yuan’s stomach.","After eating all of the food that Liu Jie had taken out, Lin Yuan wiped his mouth absentmindedly with a tissue.","At that moment, Lin Yuan was wondering how many nutrients the book would drain from his body each day.","If he wanted to live normally, he would have to eat a similar meal to this every day.","Oh no! I’m about to become a bottomless well for food!","Liu Jie and Su Yiren shared a look.","Su Yiren was only shocked while Liu Jie wondered whether Zhao Xiaochun possessed Lin Yuan!","The sight of Zhao Xiaochun eating buffet restaurants to ruin was similar to Lin Yuan’s current state.","Liu Jie was afraid that Lin Yuan might eat himself sick.","Zhao Xiaochun ingested food like a maniac and often felt starved because she had contracted a very special and strong sacred source lifeform.","The change in Lin Yuan’s demeanor was likely linked to that book from the bronze tower.","When Begin Lady carried Lin Yuan out of the bronze tower, it had mentioned that Lin Yuan falling into a coma might be due to an opportunity he was taking in.","Now that Lin Yuan was awake, it indicated that what Begin Lady had said was true.","If he had not received an opportunity, there was no way that Lin Yuan could have woken up. After all, the book had even been able to affect Begin Lady.","When Lin Yuan looked dissatisfied, Liu Jie took out a few more dishes and two more that he had learned from Zong Ze.","While Lin Yuan was eating, he started to calculate how many nutrients the book required.","After eating for some time, Lin Yuan still had a strong urge to eat even after consuming his required amount of resources.","Lin Yuan had suppressed the urge but was instinctively tempted by the new food that Liu Jie took out.","In frustration, he waved his hands at Liu Jie and said, “Big Brother Liu, keep the food away! Otherwise, I won’t be able to resist!”","While he spoke, Lin Yuan noticed the eyebags around Liu Jie and Su Yiren’s eyes.","“Big Brother Liu and Yiren, both of you must have had a hard time watching over me all this time with Begin Lady! Go back and rest! You don’t have to worry about me. I haven’t fully investigated the function of the book. Let me study it, and I’ll let you know if there are any problems!”","Su Yiren and Liu Jie had not left Lin Yuan’s side for the past 15 days.","Su Yiren rested for a few hours while communicating with Jin Qianxun, but Liu Jie had been holding on all this time through sheer willpower.","Now that they were certain that Lin Yuan was fine, it was high time for Liu Jie and Su Yiren to catch up on rest.","This sleep was not going to be a short one for either of them.","After sending off Liu Jie and Su Yiren, Lin Yuan heard Begin Lady say, “Lin Yuan, I’m sorry! I...”","Begin Lady knew that the book was an opportunity for Lin Yuan. But it had been careless and let him fall into danger.","When Lin Yuan heard Begin Lady’s apology, he immediately guessed what Begin Lady was thinking.","He looked at Begin Lady and said seriously, “Begin Lady, you don’t have to apologize to me. I would not have received this opportunity if you hadn’t brought the book to me. With my capabilities, I wouldn’t have been able to walk up to the book. You helped me!”","Begin Lady gently shook its head. It was the type to stubbornly stick to its principles.","Begin Lady did not agree with what Lin Yuan said but did not respond. Instead, it buried its feelings of apology deep in its heart.","It remembered how the book had been able to affect it even without being activated and said solemnly, “Lin Yuan, this book’s background is definitely extraordinary! You shouldn’t use this book unless you’re certain that you won’t get hurt!”"]},{"number":2168,"title":"Chapter 2168 Chu Ci’s First Precious Instrument!","paragraphs":["2168 Chu Ci’s First Precious Instrument!","Lin Yuan knew that Begin Lady said this out of his best interests. Thus, he nodded seriously at Begin Lady.","But he sensed that the book called Secret of the Dead, Volume 5, Sinking Song that had fused with the fountain of faith in the shrine now belonged to him.","After the time that Fifth Page Truth’s spirit attribute had entered Lin Yuan’s divine kingdom and created a holy spirit, this was the second time that something external had entered Lin Yuan’s divine kingdom.","The foundation of the divine kingdom was faith power.","The book could perfectly fuse with faith power and had been imprinted by faith power.","Thus, it likely came from the dimensional world.","Secret of the Dead! Could it come from the same dimensional world from which the Pilgrimage Corpse Bird came?","If there was truly such a secret in that dimensional world, could there be a similar secret in the marsh world?","Currently, the Secret of the Dead, Volume 5, Sinking Song was still absorbing his faith power. Once it had its fill, it would truly belong to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan could guess what the book’s ability was.","Begin Lady smiled radiantly when Lin Yuan nodded.","If Little Peach could see Begin Lady at that moment, she would notice that Begin Lady’s smile was completely and only meant for Lin Yuan.","“Lin Yuan, do you remember that you gave me three sacred source lifeform bodies to practice creating precious instruments? I’m done! Take a look to see if they’ll be useful!”","Begin Lady took out a strangely-shaped ring and handed it to Lin Yuan.","There was a beautiful but also sinister female face on the ring.","There were insects crawling all over the face, forming a thick net.","The ring mount looked like a half-open clamshell. It was as though it was about to close shut over the woman’s face at any time.","It was always the case that the smaller the precious instrument made from sacred source lifeform bodies, the more valuable it would be.","It was also rare for the small precious instruments to be presented as accessories.","A spirit qi professional could use multiple precious instruments during combat.","But if the precious instrument was too large or its usage clashed with that of other precious instruments, the spirit qi professional would not be able to use many of them at once.","When Lin Yuan had fought against Han Qi, the latter had used the Demon Lizard Tooth Blade.","Given that it was a dagger-type precious instrument, Han Qi could only hold one in each of his hands. Even if he had a third one that he wanted to use, he would not be able to bring it out.","But an accessory-type precious instrument such as a ring could be worn on a finger at all times, making it very convenient to use.","The precious instrument that Begin Lady had made from the Gorgon Threads, Gorgon Teeth, and Gorgon Clam was not only a rare accessory-type precious instrument but was also beginner 4 Stars.","Cai Huo’s Gorgon Threads had only been 3 Stars.","The fact that Begin Lady could create a 4 Stars precious instrument out of two 4 Stars sacred source lifeforms and one 3 Stars sacred source lifeform proved how strong its forging abilities were.","Lin Yuan did not have to worry and could leave the body of the pinnacle 10 Stars Law Staff to Begin Lady.","Lin Yuan studied the ring’s shape while checking on it using True Data.","This was when he found out that the ring was called the Ring of Gorgon Loop.","It could link up with a target and become connected to its life.","Every time the target sustained an attack that used up vitality, a decaying gu imprint would be placed on the culprit.","Once there were a certain number of decaying gu imprints, the culprit’s heart would explode.","The Ring of Gorgon Loop was basically a weaker combination of the Gorgon Threads, Gorgon Teeth, and Gorgon Clam’s abilities.","Nonetheless, it was enough to serve as a 4 Stars precious instrument.","The Ring of Gorgon Loop’s ability was similar to that of Sacrifice. Both could save one’s teammates while protecting oneself.","Every time one sustained damage, a decaying gu imprint would be placed on the one that caused damage.","This would turn the user into a thorny rose that ensured that the enemy took damage along with them.","The Ring of Gorgon Loop could produce stronger effects when someone with strong defensive abilities used it.","Chu Ci immediately came to Lin Yuan’s mind.","She had been training with Cold Moon of late, so he had not had the chance to carry out his 4.0 plan to turn his sister into an iron bucket.","If he gave the Ring of Gorgon Loop to Chu Ci, she would immediately turn into a thorny bucket.","Lin Yuan already had an 8 Stars precious instrument and would soon have a 10 Stars precious instrument. Thus, no matter how strong the abilities of the Ring of Gorgon Loop were, it would not be of much help to Lin Yuan.","It was undoubtedly more suitable for Chu Ci.","The new season of the S Tournament had started in the Radiance Federation.","Zhang Xiaobai, Xin Ying, Lu Pinru, and Tan Ran were working hard as reserve members.","In the past, not many disciples of top factions participated in the S Tournament.","But this year, perhaps due to the influence of the fight between the Radiance Hundred Sequence and the Freedom Federation envoy group, many of them had formed teams with members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence to throw their hats into the ring of the S Tournament.","There were so many strong competitors that Zhang Xiaobai’s team dared not voice their confidence in victory.","Soon, Chu Ci would return from her training with Cold Moon to join the team to participate in the S Tournament.","Chu Ci’s feys had all been evolved by Cold Moon.","Cold Moon was a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master. It was easy for her to evolve Chu Ci’s feys and establish the best nurturing path for Chu Ci.","Today, Chu Ci was far from who she used to be.","With the 4 Stars Ring of Gorgon Loop, the Dome Guild Club would stand a better chance.","The more Lin Yuan looked at the Ring of Gorgon Loop, the more satisfied he became, and he gave the Begin Lady a thumbs up.","Delight instantly appeared on Begin Lady’s face.","It reached out to Lin Yuan and said, “You can give me any bodies of sacred source lifeforms that you have! I’ll temper them all!”","When the Goddess of Mercy mass-killed the Truth Association’s experts, they had summoned all of their sacred source lifeforms out in a desperate attempt to fend her off.","Alas, the gap between their power and that of the Goddess of Mercy was colossal.","Under attack from such special power, the members of the Truth Association and their sacred source lifeforms had all been slaughtered."]},{"number":2169,"title":"Chapter 2169 Begin Lady Likes to Breed!","paragraphs":["2169 Begin Lady Likes to Breed!","Purple Love had organized all of the sacred source lifeform bodies.","Lin Yuan gave all the 6 Stars and below sacred source lifeforms and Fifth Page Truth’s fully preserved pinnacle 10 Stars Divine Order Evil Fetus’ bodies all to Begin Lady.","“Begin Lady, go and temper these sacred source lifeforms. I left Fifth Page Truth’s spatial equipment in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. You can take whatever resources you need from there. Don’t rush to temper the Divine Order Evil Fetus first. Wait for Purple Love and Blue Lotus to bring back the spiritual ingredients meant to complement sacred source lifeform bodies before you start to temper it. It should make the product stronger!”","The Heavenly Family Cottage was a faction that had existed for thousands of years. There was no way that human federations could hope to match up to the resources that they had accumulated.","Lin Yuan understood the intentions of Purple Love and the other Heavenly Family Feys.","Blue Lotus would give him any and all spiritual ingredients that could complement the bodies of the Divine Order Evil Fetus and Law Staff.","Lin Yuan was looking forward to seeing what the precious instruments made from the Divine Order Evil Fetus and Law Staff eventually looked like.","“I’m very interested in forging precious instruments! When I feel how the sacred source bodies are combining and changing in my body, it makes me feel like I’m breeding new life!”","Begin Lady paused before saying seriously, “Lin Yuan, you asked for my help to give some of my bloodline to nurture a batch of feys. You said that it’d allow the Divine Wood Federation to quickly increase its power.","“I can work a bit harder and lend my bloodline to more feys. The feys don’t just have to come from the Divine Wood Federation. I can give some to the Iron Hammer Federation and Great Lush Federation too!","“The Sacred Wood Mystic Realm was in the Divine Wood Federation, but it’s not unique to the Divine Wood Federation. If not for you, I wouldn’t be able to give my bloodline to feys from the Divine Wood Federation.”","Lin Yuan had made this request to Begin Lady some time ago.","At that time, he had not yet taken control of the Iron Hammer Federation and Great Lush Federation.","Begin Lady had agreed.","But now he had the entire Startling Lines Continent in the palm of his hand.","Rather than just increasing the Divine Wood Federation’s power, it would also help to increase the power of the Iron Hammer Federation and Great Lush Federation.","Before the finances of the three federations were combined and flowing smoothly, one faction suddenly being more powerful than the other two would cause some problems to emerge, even if Yi Huailong, Luo Lan, and Jin Qianxun were all under Lin Yuan’s control.","Begin Lady knew the benefits and disadvantages of infecting other feys with its bloodline.","The feys that it infected with its bloodline would undergo a mutation. They would become stronger and be able to increase their power faster.","Otherwise, the feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline would have been fought over so fervently by the Divine Wood Federation’s elite and placed on such a high pedestal.","But there were two sides to every coin. Although the benefits were great, there were inevitable downsides as well.","The Holy Lady was able to reach Immortal because Begin Lady had injected a large amount of its bloodline into the Holy Lady.","The feys that had only been slightly infected by the Sacred Wood bloodline did not have high of a concentration in their blood as the Holy Lady did.","However, to people from the Startling Lines Continent, they were content to just have their feys be able to reach Creation Breed.","In a continent that did not even have Class 5 Creation Masters, thearch-class experts were considered the ceiling.","It could be said that delivering feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline to all three federations was the only way to rapidly increase the power of the experts from the Startling Lines Continent.","While it spoke, Begin Lady’s eyes did not leave Lin Yuan’s face.","Begin Lady remembered Lin Yuan mentioning that he wanted the white-clothed followers to form contracts with the feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline.","Begin Lady had told him about the disadvantages of feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline then.","Lin Yuan immediately gave up on the idea.","Instead, Lin Yuan decided to invest more of his resources so that the geniuses who chose to believe in him would one day have the chance to fight against the heavens. This way, they would not be limited by a predetermined ceiling.","A leader like Lin Yuan glittered majestically in Begin Lady’s eyes.","It had absorbed Su Jian and Bai Dong’s souls but had never truly encountered the things that Su Jian and Bai Dong had experienced before. But still, it was not curious about them.","Both had been the leaders of their respective families. However, neither of them had such foresight and generosity.","All they wanted was for their subordinates to increase their power as quickly as possible, even if it cost them their lives.","There were many experts who were guards in the Su and Bai families that had their growth rushed in such a way.","Lin Yuan did not immediately agree with what Begin Lady said.","He had heard that feys infected with Begin Lady’s bloodline had limitations.","In the past, Begin Lady had done so because it wanted to exchange for high-class Creation Master resources.","Moreover, Begin Lady needed three to five times the amount of bloodline to infect animal-type feys than it did plant-type feys.","Clearly, feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline were invaluable in the Divine Wood Federation.","The Su family had only been willing to give some of the Peaceful Calm Air Moss to Lin Yuan because they wanted to take over the imperial court.","Lin Yuan had been seducing the veteran elite families in the Sacred Forest City for so long with his Class 5 Creation Master resources, but he had yet to receive a second plant-type fey with the Sacred Wood bloodline.","Lin Yuan was afraid that Begin Lady would suffer if he agreed to its suggestion of delivering feys infected with its bloodline to the entire Startling Lines Continent.","Before Lin Yuan could open his mouth to ask, he saw Begin Lady’s expression and immediately knew what Lin Yuan was thinking.","Begin Lady had made its stance clear.","It was a faerie born from nature. So, even after absorbing the souls of two humans, it did not feel shy.","“I exist because of you! I’m willing to do anything for you! Moreover, with the Element Well, I can give away much more of my bloodline than I used to. I will be able to infect around 100 plant-type feys or 20 to 35 animal-type feys daily. As long as this range isn’t exceeded, I won’t be affected to a great extent.”","Lin Yuan was happy to hear what Begin Lady said.","It was great news that Begin Lady would not be affected!","With so many feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline entering the Startling Lines Continent’s three federations daily, the Startling Lines Continent would be transformed in less than a year.","Although Begin Lady could produce so many feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline every day, the feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline were still rare.","There were many experts in the Startling Lines Continent!","Perhaps only 1% of them would be able to obtain a fey with the Sacred Wood bloodline.","Rather than using more of its bloodline to infect animal-type feys, it would be much more valuable to use the bloodline on plant-type feys."]},{"number":2170,"title":"Chapter 2170 Not Worried at All?","paragraphs":["2170 Not Worried at All?","There were spirit qi professionals who were affiliated with plant-type feys in the Iron Hammer, Great Lush, and Divine Wood Federations.","Specifically, the ratio of the total number of spirit qi professionals from all three federations affiliated with plant-type feys to the number of feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline would be about 30 to 1.","After all, the proportion of spirit qi professionals affiliated with plant-type feys was very large.","In order to preserve the quality-to-price ratio, this gift could only be given to the spirit qi professionals who were extremely especially affiliated with plant-type feys.","If Begin Lady infected 100 plant-type feys with its bloodline daily, it could deliver 36,000 plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline to the three federations. This meant that each federation could receive 12,000 plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline.","After more than ten years, every spirit qi professional who possessed a plant-type fey with the Sacred Wood bloodline could become an emperor-class expert.","Frankly, this was just a safe estimate.","If these plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline landed in the factions with Class 4 Creation Masters, these factions would definitely be willing to invest their Class 4 Creation Master resources into these plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline.","After high-class Creation Master resources were invested, the improvement that would have taken more than ten years would take place within five years.","It could be said that the Startling Lines Continent was about to reach its prime.","Begin Lady’s suggestion fueled Lin Yuan’s ambition and put some schemes in his mind.","These spirit qi professionals who contracted the plant-type feys did not belong to Sky City.","Thus, they had to be controlled.","It was difficult to predict the human heart. Lin Yuan did not want to end up developing a new batch of enemies that emerged in ten years’ time.","There were many ways to control them, so Lin Yuan was not overly worried.","The job could be accomplished well, whether it was in the hands of Su Yiren or Wen Yu.","At that time, they would have to take note of the spirit qi professionals whose feys were about to break through to Myth Breed so they could be gathered together to undergo the evolution simultaneously.","This would make it easier for Lin Yuan to collect the spirit qi crystals.","As long as this plan could come to fruition, Lin Yuan could use spirit qi crystals freely in the future.","Once he gained many spirit qi crystals, he could use them in more ways than just nurturing the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","Lin Yuan still had many things to do.","With this thought, Lin Yuan said, “Begin Lady, use your bloodline to only infect plant-type feys! You’ll have to use your bloodline to infect feys, forge precious instruments, and protect me at the same time. It’s going to be tough on you!”","Begin Lady gently waved its hands and said nonchalantly, “I can easily accomplish these. It won’t be difficult at all! Additionally, doing these things will be very new experiences for me. I welcome them! I am a faerie transformed from an underground river. It’s natural for me to love to breed new life!","“There is an endless list of things to do in the Great Lush Federation. I’m sure you’ll want to go and see Jin Qianxun! He has been running over here often to ask about your condition. Each time, he only leaves after a few hours. Regardless of whether his worry is genuine, he’s very smart! At first, Liu Jie and Su Yiren weren’t fond of him. but now, they’ve both accepted him.”","Lin Yuan nodded.","He was well aware of the reason behind Jin Qianxun needing to see him.","Rather than being worried about himself, he was more so worried about his position.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan was fine with Jin Qianxun’s attitude.","Lin Yuan had never been the type to be expressive or change his mind easily.","Since he had decided that Jin Qianxun would be the one to sit on that throne, he would not drag Jin Qianxun down from that seat until he committed a grievous error.","It was likely that Jin Qianxun dared not make the decisions on the many things that had to be done in the Great Lush Federation on his own accord.","It was time for Lin Yuan to give him a set of instructions.","After settling matters in the Great Lush Federation, it would be time for Lin Yuan to use the Law Staff to increase the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Stars.","Some time had passed since Fifth Page Truth died.","The Law Staff that Begin Lady had captured was still alive, but its life force had already begun to weaken due to Fifth Page Truth’s death.","If Lin Yuan did not use the Law Staff to increase the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Stars soon, it would go to waste.","When Begin Lady changed into a pink and gold crystal and landed on the corner of Lin Yuan’s eye, he took out a Thoughts Letter Paper and recounted the past few days’ events.","Luo Lan had sent him many messages while he had been in a coma.","During this time, she had led the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribes to the capital of the Iron Hammer Federation, Freezing Hammer Tribe.","The Freezing Hammer Tribe was on the mountain where the snow celestial resided.","The terrain of the snow-capped mountain was perilous. At the same time, nothing in the Iron Hammer Federation imperial court could provide substantial support.","The servants close to Luo Cai had abandoned him after the order he gave.","Without any support, Luo Cai was now a shadow of a man.","Most of the members of Freezing Hammer Tribe were the Luo family’s direct and collateral descendants.","Many of the collateral descendants were relatives with prominent statuses.","All of them had been suspicious when Luo Cai took the throne. All of them preferred Luo Lan.","However, none of them had dared to speak up because of the power that Luo Cai wielded, and they had been forced to become Luo Cai’s lapdogs.","Now that Luo Cai had lost all of his power, many of these distant relatives had noticed that his footing was becoming increasingly unstable.","When they found out that Luo Lan was bringing the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribes to the foot of the snow-capped mountain, they immediately went into the imperial court and killed all the servants who were still loyal to Luo Cai. This was their way of expressing their loyalty to Luo Lan.","All of these distant relatives had schemes of their own.","Many of them had participated in helping Luo Cai to hunt Luo Lan.","Now, they were all afraid that she would nurse the grudge and seek revenge on them.","Their action now was their way of compensating for what they did.","They believed that their support was necessary if Luo Lan wanted to secure the Iron Hammer Federation’s throne.","If the Freezing Hammer Tribe’s power was cut down, Luo Lan’s power as a direct descendant would also be diminished.","At that time, why would the Black Gold and Platinum tribes bother to listen to this young upstart who barely knew anything about the world?","It could be said that all the distant relatives from the Freezing Hammer Tribe shared the same thought.","Thus, none of them felt panicked at all!"]},{"number":2171,"title":"Chapter 2171 Kill!","paragraphs":["2171 Kill!","Luo Lan reported everything that happened on the journey back to the Iron Hammer Federation to Lin Yuan.","The last message from Luo Lan had come half an hour ago.","The message left an amused expression on Lin Yuan’s face.","[Luo Lan: Young Master, what do you think I should do about these distant relatives?]","Luo Lan’s message told Lin Yuan that she was ready to eliminate these distant relatives from the Freezing Hammer Tribe.","Luo Lan was the leader of the Imperial court and the head of the Freezing Hammer Tribe. How she decided to deal with her relatives was a personal family matter.","Lin Yuan did not want to interfere.","No matter what her decision was, it would not affect Lin Yuan’s plan.","Thus, Lin Yuan replied.","[Lin Yuan: Congratulations on saving so many hidden tribe members. The amount of Soldier Ration Radishes that Su Yiren delivered to you should be enough. Things over there in the Iron Hammer Federation are going more smoothly than I expected. That is proof of your capabilities.","[By the time you’ve eaten through all of the Soldier Ration Radishes, winter should be over too. At that time, the trading route between the Divine Wood and Iron Hammer Federations will be finished, and the Iron Hammer Federation will have the same access to food as the Divine Wood Federation. As for the matter regarding your distant relatives, you don’t have to ask me. You can deal with it in your own way!]","Lin Yuan was in a good mood after reading the reports from Luo Lan.","It was a good thing that she had managed to save so many tribe members.","The Startling Lines Continent was about the usher in an era of peace and prosperity.","Lin Yuan hoped that with what he wanted to build and establish, more lifeforms would be blessed and be able to lead better lives.","Luo Lan had reported almost everything that happened on her journey to Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Yet, she had not received any replies from him.","This filled Luo Lan with disappointment.","Unlike Jin Qianxun, who needed to rely fully on Lin Yuan in order to secure his seat on the Great Lush Federation’s throne, Luo Lan had already gained the loyalty of most of the tribes.","She was like a savior in the eyes of the tribes.","She hoped that Lin Yuan could witness her wins and successes. This was because, to her, he was her savior.","It could be said that Luo Lan had never felt more conflicted.","She clearly felt the urge but could not steel her heart enough to do so.","After she sent her long message to Lin Yuan, Luo Lan sighed gently and prepared to return the Thoughts Letter Paper to the spatial equipment that Lin Yuan had given her.","It was at that moment that she saw Lin Yuan’s reply.","All this time, she had been like a warrior goddess and assumed that her heart had already turned as tough as stone.","But when she saw the message from Lin Yuan, Luo Lan felt warmth and a sense of security.","Her eyes pricked with tears.","Lin Yuan’s congratulations was the biggest affirmation for Luo Lan.","She knew that he was very busy.","He had not replied to her messages for so long and had not held the scheduled Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meetings either.","Thus, she assumed that the Great Lush Federation had fully captured his focus.","But in spite of how busy he was, Lin Yuan still remembered his promise to her and had used action to fulfill it.","At first, all Luo Lan hoped for was for none of the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members to go hungry during winter.","But now, Lin Yuan was going to provide the Iron Hammer Federation with as much food as there was in the Divine Wood Federation.","This was not only something that Luo Lan had not dared to hope for but also something that the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members dared to dream of.","Lin Yuan said that she had proved her capabilities, but Luo Lan knew that he was the one who had given her these capabilities and the respect of the tribes.","If not for the Soldier Ration Radishes that Lin Yuan had given her and set her up as a goddess back in the sea of flowers, there was no way she could wield the might and power she possessed today.","Lin Yuan told her to make the decision regarding her family matter herself.","This led Luo Lan to cement her resolve.","The distant relatives were only trying to safeguard their profits.","Even her father had received pushback from these relatives against some of his policies.","When she took the throne, she would meet with the same obstacles from these relatives.","It was possible that these relatives would end up affecting her initial promise to Lin Yuan.","If she wanted the Iron Hammer Federation’s development to improve, the federation would have to change.","These distant relatives were no different from tumors.","There was no reason not to cut away these tumors during the Iron Hammer Federation’s transformation.","Luo Lan stored the Thoughts Letter Paper away.","As she stood in front of the sea of troops, she raised her sword in front of the snow-capped mountain and roared into the icy wind, “Kill!”","The troops that traveled with Luo Lan from the border to the Freezing Hammer Tribe rescued the fleeing tribe members while eliminating bandits they met along the way.","Aside from winter, bandits were always the biggest threat to the Iron Hammer Federation.","This journey could be considered the Iron Hammer Federation’s biggest retaliation against the robbers in history.","The bandits usually only ran wild in winter.","Even Black Gold tribes did not have the energy to take on these bandits during winter due to food scarcity.","But on this expedition, all of the Iron Hammer Federation’s Black Gold, Platinum, Yellow Gold, White Silver, Light Bronze, and Black Iron tribes worked together to eliminate the bandits.","The wave of troops outnumbered the bandits by ten to one. Thus, they stood no chance of fighting back.","The journey filled Luo Lan with fervent passion.","She led the troops to the base of the snow-capped mountain.","The heads of the Black Gold tribes and Class 4 Creation Masters were standing next to Luo Lan as they awaited her command.","None of them expected her to come to such a decision.","This decision not only did not cause the leaders of the Black Gold tribes and Class 4 Creation Masters to see her as cold-blooded, but rather, they were shocked and happy with her growth.","The fact that she was able to make such a decision proved that she was fit to be the head of the Iron Hammer Federation.","Luo Lan’s choice also steeled her resolve for change.","This caused everyone in the tribes to have even more faith that she would be able to make good on her promise.","After Luo Lan’s shout, a noise erupted from behind her akin to that of a tsunami.","At that moment, the tribe members all assumed that an avalanche had been triggered."]},{"number":2172,"title":"Chapter 2172 The Secret That was Recorded!","paragraphs":["2172 The Secret That was Recorded!","The distant relatives from the Freezing Hammer Tribe were still sitting soundly in their homes.","Although people were dying from hunger and cold on the streets of the Iron Hammer Federation, even the servants of distant relatives could drink steaming bowls of lamb soup and fresh fruits every day.","The collateral descendants who took advantage of their status as being part of the Luo family and the distant relatives who held a certain amount of power never had to worry about going hungry.","After every meal, the leftovers would not be given to the starving and poor people, nor would they be gifted to the servants. Rather, the leftovers were all tossed out.","The wastage of precious resources has always been a way of demonstrating one’s status.","Luo Cai had been able to take the throne because of the power of the Truth Association.","This had resulted in the distant relatives suffering greatly.","After all, there had been a powerful martial force supporting Luo Cai that these distant relatives could never hope to match up to.","After suffering at the hands of Luo Cai, the distant relatives did not want to go through the same experience a second time.","The distant relatives believed that capturing Luo Cai and delivering him to Luo Lan when she took over the throne would be the best way of gaining her favor.","But at the same time, these distant relatives also wanted to control Luo Lan.","All of them had watched Luo Lan grow up. In their eyes, she was nothing more than an insecure kitten who they would be able to puppeteer at will once she was on the throne.","They would be able to use her to suck the Iron Hammer Federation dry.","Even if they had started out with pure hearts, spending a prolonged period under the smog of riches and debauchery had caused their principles to decay generations ago.","When Luo Lan’s father had been the Iron Hammer Federation’s king, his pressure forced the distant relatives to suppress such ideas.","But now that the young Luo Lan was there, these distant relatives saw their chance.","Right before the sound of a roaring tsunami arose, the distant relatives had been huddled together, enjoying a feast as they discussed their plans for Luo Lan.","During the talks, the distant relatives all ended up on the same page.","They even assigned all the roles they were going to play and how the profits would be distributed.","Those who would not be of much help would receive fewer profits, while those who contributed more would gain more.","The friendly banquet soon turned ugly as many of them were willing to contribute more and were unwilling to do less and thereby receive less.","Luo Lan’s shout traveled up and down the mountain, frightening the distant relatives.","However, Luo Lan’s intention and resolve to kill did not involve giving these distant relatives the chance to fight back.","At first, Luo Lan was like any other regular person and had been blinded by hate.","She had insisted on taking Luo Cai’s head as revenge for her father.","But now, it did not matter to her if she was the one who ended up killing Luo Cai.","She knew that Luo Cai had either been captured by the distant relatives or was hiding somewhere in the Freezing Hammer Tribe.","Regardless of which case it was, he would eventually end up as a corpse.","Luo Lan remembered how her strict father had nurtured her.","She had been doing her best to continue going down this path.","Now that she had joined the Astronomical Parliament and received help from Lin Yuan, the Iron Hammer Federation was about to walk down a path more glorious than even her father could have ever dreamed of.","The best way she could keep the memory of her father alive was to do her best as the ruler of the Iron Hammer Federation and help the federation to climb to even greater heights.","This would also be the best way for her to repay Lin Yuan’s help.","The sound of horseshoes rattled throughout the Freezing Hammer Tribe.","This was an impending disaster for both the distant relatives and Luo Cai.","However, to the members of Freezing Hammer Tribe, this sound was music to their ears during winter.","A large amount of Soldier Ration Radishes was distributed.","Within the short span of a day, none of the citizens of the Iron Hammer Federation continued to go hungry.","Such a feat had never been accomplished in the history of the Iron Hammer Federation.","The first instruction that Luo Lan gave as the ruler of the Iron Hammer Federation’s imperial court was to the servants as she ordered them to reconstruct the statue of the god that all the tribes worshiped.","At first, Luo Lan worshipped that celestial on the snow-capped mountain as well.","But now, she had redirected the object of her faith.","When she had been in danger, she had thought about praying to the celestial for protection. But, she had received no reply.","The person who had truly ended up protecting her was Lin Yuan.","Luo Lan had picked her servants from amongst the Black Gold and Platinum tribes.","All of these servants had seen Lin Yuan in the sea of flowers.","Thus, when they received the order from Luo Lan to construct a statue of Lin Yuan, none of them had voiced any objection. Rather, they felt touched and were in agreement.","She knew that this first order she gave seemed ridiculous and unorthodox. However, she would not hear of any objection.","Since Lin Yuan needed faith power, Luo Lan would do her best to create the best conditions for him to receive what he needed.","The celestial on the mountain was preceded by the legends surrounding it. Luo Lan had never actually laid eyes on it before.","If there truly was a celestial being on the mountain protecting the Iron Hammer Federation, it would be angered by all of the citizen’s redirection of their faith.","However, Luo Lan did not care in the slightest.","It did not matter whether there truly was a celestial being.","If one did exist, Luo Lan hoped that it would be angry. At least then, she would be able to ask directly why it acted like a coward during a true crisis and allowed so many to die after receiving centuries of worship from the citizens of the Iron Hammer Federation.","Luo Lan had always been a materialist.","Demons and celestial beings were all powerful lifeforms.","Lin Yuan had mentioned that he was very interested in the celestial being. This had to be because of the legend.","If she could lure the celestial being out, it would also be a form of helping Lin Yuan.","Luo Lan did not know that Lin Yuan was not just interested in the celestial being on the mountain.","Before falling into a coma, Lin Yuan had a habit of flipping through the Annal of Monster Information.","The contents of the Annal of Monster Information were mystical. It was difficult for Lin Yuan to understand them immediately; some were too ineffable. Thus, Lin Yuan did not have the chance to test them out.","He had already read 1/3 of the Annal of Monster Information.","One of the parts that Lin Yuan had been able to understand was the one about the Snow Celestial Mountain.","There had to be a secret hidden in the Snow Celestial Mountain for it to be mentioned in the Annal of Monster Information.","This was why Lin Yuan had promised Luo Lan that he would head to the Iron Hammer Federation one more time before leaving for the marsh world."]},{"number":2173,"title":"Chapter 2173 Brown Willow Coral and Demon Pattern Light Oxygen Fish!","paragraphs":["2173 Brown Willow Coral and Demon Pattern Light Oxygen Fish!","While Luo Lan was dealing with her distant relatives, Lin Yuan went to see Jin Qianxun.","As Jin Qianxun looked at the smiling Lin Yuan, he felt as though all his burdens were lifted.","He had been in a coma for two weeks and only came to see Jin Qianxun after waking up.","Now, he realized that Jin Qianxun’s aura had changed significantly from two weeks ago.","Two weeks ago, he seemed more like the head of a family.","But now, he had the faint aura of a king around him.","Lin Yuan did not waste time on pleasantries and immediately said, “I heard from Yiren that you have started preparations for the construction of the harbor.”","Jin Qianxun hurriedly replied, “I held my first imperial meeting 13 days ago. During the meeting, I told all the secret aristocratic families to offer up their spirit qi professionals who are skilled at working underwater. With these 150,000 spirit qi professionals cleaning and building the harbor, it should be fully cleaned in about a month.”","Jin Qianxun’s reason for investing so much effort into the harbor was not just to get in Lin Yuan’s good books.","The harbor would involve 20 Island Whales that Lin Yuan would provide. It was a gargantuan project that would affect the Great Lush Federation’s foundation.","Once the project was underway, Lin Yuan would only gain a harbor where 20 of the Island Whales could congregate, but to the Great Lush Federation, the doors to long-distance trading would be opened.","When Lin Yuan heard what Jin Qianxun said, he looked at Jin Qianxun with approval.","Although Jin Qianxun’s aura of a king was not as robust as it should be, he was still capable at managing and carrying out tasks.","Previously, Jin Qianxun had not fully understood the harbor project.","Lin Yuan did not obtain any useful information from Jin Qianxun on the way to Clean Brahma City.","But while Jin Qianxun had been confused, the same did not apply to Weng Queji.","Fifth Page Truth had seen the power of the entire Startling Lines Continent as an offering to him. Thus, it was only natural that he had not put any effort into the harbor.","However, Weng Queji had noticed the special features of the harbor and acknowledged its value.","When he had been a Class 5 Creation Master under Fifth Page Truth, he had enjoyed great freedom and tried to explore the harbor numerous times. Thus, the information regarding the harbor that he had prepared for Lin Yuan was extremely comprehensive.","It would not be difficult to develop the harbor.","The Island Whales would not be docked in the harbor the same way that boats were.","As long as the water in the harbor was deep enough and there was sufficient oxygen, the Island Whales would be able to move around freely.","However, a giant floating island like the Island Whale had a terrifyingly large amount of needs.","It did not have to be said that the same went for the Island Whales.","Moreover, they were different from the goldfish in that the goldfish breathed in the oxygen within the water while the Island Whales were unable to breathe underwater. They could only take in air through their blowholes.","It could take up to half an hour for the Island Whale to take a breath. Each breath would drain the surroundings of at least a square kilometer of oxygen.","If a harbor did not come with special setups, there was no guarantee that the Island Whales could breathe.","But luckily, it was not difficult to increase the oxygen concentration in the harbor and enable the Island Whales to breathe.","There was a large amount of the Brown Willow Coral at the bottom of the harbor. Unlike other corals, the Brown Willow Coral did not protect weak fish. Instead, it consumed these weak fish and was slightly poisonous.","The Brown Willow Coral was one of the corals that used up the most oxygen.","The spirit qi professionals skilled at working underwater only needed to clean all of the Brown Willow Corals at the bottom of the harbor before placing a layer of energy ores on top of them.","Next, aquatic plants like the Oxygen Sea Anemone could be planted at the bottom of the harbor, where they would produce oxygen continuously.","Even if multiple of the Island Whales breathed simultaneously, there would be no worry of lacking oxygen.","The Oxygen Sea Anemone lived at the bottom of the sea and was not picky with food. It could prey on small fish or even absorb the feces of larger aquatic lifeforms.","The Island Whales’ existence would attract many sea lifeforms to live in and around them.","Each time the Island Whale relieved itself, the ocean was blessed.","The Oxygen Sea Anemone did not need to be high-grade. It would be enough for them to just be Silver grade.","A year later, the Oxygen Sea Anemone would be able to reach Diamond grade at the very least just by living off the feces of the Island Whale and not hunting for any food itself. There was a possibility that it would even be able to evolve to Myth Breed.","There were numerous feys like the Oxygen Sea Anemone on the shores of the Great Lush Federation.","Besides the Oxygen Sea Anemone, some fish-species feys could release oxygen.","The small fish was known as the Demon Pattern Light Oxygen Fish and could only be found in the Great Lush Federation.","The oxygen released by a school of the Demon Pattern Light Oxygen Fish would provide more oxygen than the Oxygen Sea Anemone.","“You did well. Bai Qinghuan has been sent over. I’m sure you’ve met her. Let Bai Qinghuan and Weng Baichuan stay by your side and train for some time. I will fetch them later. I’m sure you’ll also be able to learn from Bai Qinghuan.”","Sky City had not halted its operations while Lin Yuan had been unconscious.","While Liu Jie and Su Yiren had been worried about him, they still ensured that everything continued smoothly.","At first, Lin Yuan planned to keep Weng Baochuan by his side and personally nurture him.","But on the road to the Great Lush Federation, Lin Yuan realized that Weng Baochuan was a genius at strategy, just like Bai Qinghuan.","Rather than sending him away, it would be better to allow him to interact with Bai Qinghuan so they could help each other grow.","Before he met Bai Qinghuan, Jin Qianxun would have silently underestimated whatever young girl Lin Yuan sent to tail him.","But when he finally met Bai Qinghuan and interacted with her, he realized that she was hiding an astonishing eye for strategy.","After speaking casually to her for a few hours, Jin Qianxun felt that he had learned a fair amount.","Jin Qianxun had never dreamed that he would be able to reach such heights.","He knew that he had always lacked a mind for strategy.","Although Jin Qianxun knew that with Bai Qinghuan around, he would never be able to make decisions on his own and would always seek out her counsel, Jin Qianxun still hoped that Lin Yuan would call her away later rather than sooner.","The longer that Bai Qinghuan remained in the Great Lush Federation, the more he would be able to learn from her."]},{"number":2174,"title":"Chapter 2174 Gift and Favor!","paragraphs":["2174 Gift and Favor!","Previously, Bai Qinghuan had felt increasingly lost by Lin Yuan’s side.","She knew what her strengths and weaknesses were and that compared to Su Yiren and Wen Yu’s talent for management, her eye for management could not be of much help to Lin Yuan.","She had been afraid of being abandoned by him.","When he sent her to the Great Lush Federation to help Jin Qianxun, she finally felt she was useful to him.","No matter how skilled at strategy she was, her background was just so.","The Great Lush Federation was on the same level as the Divine Wood Federation.","She could even influence his policies when she was by Jin Qianxun’s side.","Despite being the adopted daughter of the Bai family, a veteran elite family from the Divine Wood Federation, this made her feel as though her worth had been inflated.","With Bai Qinghuan training by Jin Qianxun’s side, Lin Yuan did not have to worry about any trouble cropping up in the Great Lush Federation.","In the Divine Wood Federation, the Bai, Su, and Yang families had been erased from existence. Of the four veteran elite families, the Yi family was the only one left.","Thus, the Divine Wood Federation was lacking in combat power.","But now, it seemed that the Great Lush Federation’s combat power did not exceed that of the Divine Wood Federation by much.","After all, many of the Great Lush Federation’s experts had died due to their contracts.","Otherwise, a beginner thearch-class expert like Jin Qianxun would never have had the chance to make a bid for the throne.","Although Jin Qianxun never asked for his help when it came to power, Lin Yuan could sense how frantic Jin Qianxun was.","Jin Qianxun knew that the Great Lush Federation could not bring the trading empire involving 20 Island Whales to life with their current power.","Without experts who were strong enough to hold down the fort, they would be losing their resources wherever they went when they were meant to be trading them.","Lin Yuan was certain that given Jin Qianxun’s character, he would not utter a word even if his situation was hopeless by his own means.","Since Jin Qianxun could not make the first move, Lin Yuan would do so.","“Jin Qianxun, our previous correspondences have only surrounded the development of the Great Lush Federation. You have no more questions about the direction of the Great Lush Federation’s development, but have you thought about how you’re going to keep the Great Lush Federation safe from external influences? Trading using the Island Whales is a double-edged sword endeavor. If not done properly, it will lead to problems instead.”","Lin Yuan’s words had hit the nail on the head of Jin Qianxun’s heart and touched on the Great Lush Federation’s most pressing issue.","Jin Qianxun was not a Creation Master and did not possess a large amount of Creation Master resources.","Jin Qianxun dared not say that the entire Great Lush Federation needed to rely on Lin Yuan. But that was the truth.","But once he uttered those words, he would come off as worthless.","Weng Queji was currently stationed in the Great Lush Federation, but the person he was loyal to was Lin Yuan and not Jin Qianxun.","It was likely that he would be leaving the Great Lush Federation soon.","Given Jin Qianxun’s status, he had no right to order Weng Queji to stay.","As he looked at the stumped Jin Qianxun, Lin Yuan picked up the teacup from the table and took a small sip. Next, he asked with an unchanged expression, “I’m sure you’ve heard of the Divine Wood Federation’s feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline.”","Jin Qianxun was stunned when he heard this, and he could not understand why Lin Yuan was suddenly bringing up the plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline.","When the Truth Association had been in charge, the Great Lush Federation and Divine Wood Federation had been collaborators and rivals at the same time.","Jin Qianxun was one of the main members of a top-secret aristocratic family and so was not unfamiliar with the feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline.","It could be said that the Divine Wood Federation’s strength was largely related to the plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline.","Suddenly, Jin Qianxun’s eyes lit up.","For Lin Yuan to mention the plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline that were unique to the Divine Wood Federation at such a time, could he mean that he wanted to give some of the plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline to the Great Lush Federation?","Lin Yuan was also controlling the Divine Wood Federation. As such, there was a high chance that his guess was right.","Jin Qianxun’s heart was beating wildly as he said, “Lord, the feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline are famous. If not for them, the Divine Wood Federation would never have been able to stand toe-to-toe against the Iron Hammer Federation for so many years.”","Lin Yuan nodded.","He had only seen eight of the Iron Hammer Federation’s Black Gold tribes.","Although all of them were weaker than the Divine Wood Federation’s four veteran elite families, the difference was not large.","The Iron Hammer Federation’s top combat power was indeed greater than that of the Divine Wood Federation.","If Jin Qianxun did not know what plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline were, Lin Yuan would have had to use up some time explaining them to him.","But since he knew, everything was now simpler.","“For the next four months, I will provide 12,000 plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline to the Great Lush Federation. Go and pick out some talents from the secret aristocratic families who are affiliated with plant-type feys. The condition is that each of them has to have comprehended at least one Willpower Rune.”","The moment Lin Yuan was done speaking, Jin Qianxun could not help but gasp.","In front of Lin Yuan, Jin Qianxun appeared solemn and composed. He was afraid of being discourteous to Lin Yuan and angering him.","Jin Qianxun had lost control and gasped because Lin Yuan’s words were too mind-bending.","He had promised 12,000 plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline!","It was likely that the Divine Wood Federation had stored up less than 500 feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline in the past few centuries.","Lin Yuan was never one to boast. Otherwise, Jin Qianxun would not have made it to the throne of the Great Lush Federation.","It seemed that Lin Yuan had taken full control of the Sacred Wood Mystic Realm in the Divine Wood Federation. This was the only way he could obtain so many plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline.","With all those plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline, he would not have to worry about the Great Lush Federation’s foundation being shaky.","At that moment, Jin Qianxun was just as excited and surprised as he was thankful and respectful towards Lin Yuan.","Jin Qianxun fell to his knees to prepare to express his gratitude to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan pulled Jin Qianxun up and said, “If you want to thank me, do your best to make the Great Lush Federation as strong as possible. I will also need the faith of the citizens of the Great Lush Federation. I will leave this matter to you. I have a keen sense for faith. I will become aware the moment you take a step down the wrong path.”"]},{"number":2175,"title":"Chapter 2175 Let Me Sleep a While More!","paragraphs":["2175 Let Me Sleep a While More!","Lin Yuan did not explain to Jin Qianxun what faith power was, nor did he tell Jin Qianxun what he should do to obtain the faith of the Great Lush Federation’s citizens.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan believed that Jin Qianxun would be able to do well.","If he could not even accomplish such a simple task, he would not deserve to sit on the throne of the Great Lush Federation.","When he heard what Lin Yuan said, Jin Qianxun immediately gave his word to Lin Yuan.","Jin Qianxun did not think that it would be difficult to obtain the Great Lush Federation’s citizens’ faith for Lin Yuan. This was because their lives were about to become much better.","Furthermore, Lin Yuan was going to send 12,000 plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline to the Great Lush Federation very soon.","All the secret aristocratic families of the Great Lush Federation would be able to benefit from Lin Yuan’s blessing.","With such a blessing, the secret aristocratic families would know what to do.","Jin Qianxun was confident that in the next six months, he would be able to obtain the faith of at least half of the citizens for Lin Yuan.","As for whether they became devotees, that would depend on what Jin Qianxun did for the next six months.","This was the first request that Lin Yuan had made of him. Jin Qianxun was going to do it well, no matter what.","After giving his instructions to Jin Qianxun, Lin Yuan continued heading to the Tower of Truth.","Previously, due to the Secret of the Dead, Volume 5, Sinking Song, Lin Yuan had no time to instruct Morbius to refine the Crimson Spirit Bronze that was in the Tower of Truth.","But now, it was time for Lin Yuan to instruct Morbius to analyze the Tower of Truth and store the treasure that was the Crimson Spirit Truth away.","Sky City’s main members were not using any techniques to shield their souls.","Lin Yuan decided to turn the Crimson Spirit Bronze into pendants and distribute them. In a way, this would give each of Sky City’s main members a shield.","Lin Yuan’s promise to Jin Qianxun meant that he would first provide resources to the Great Lush Federation.","This could be seen as him being biased, but he had no choice but to do so.","The Great Lush Federation needed to rise up quickly in order to handle the harbor and 20 Island Whales.","After all, Yi Huailong and Luo Lan would be able to obtain just as many plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline four months later. Thus, there would be nothing for them to complain about.","“In order to maximize the amount of Crimson Spirit Bronze obtained, a significant amount of the Ever-Changing Temper Gold will be wasted. However, the Ever-Changing Temper Gold is still a Sovereign metal spiritual ingredient. So, a small amount will still be saved.”","Lin Yuan placed his hand on the tower while excitement coursed through his veins.","No matter how many treasures Lin Yuan obtained, Sovereign metal spiritual ingredients were still extremely rare.","Unlike the previous Sovereign metal spiritual ingredients that Lin Yuan encountered in the past, the Ever-Changing Temper Gold was not meant for combat.","The Ever-Changing Temper Gold had strong malleability and plasticity. It could be combined with any metal spiritual ingredient while ensuring that the metal spiritual ingredient retained its original attributes. As a result of this, many tough metal spiritual ingredients could change their shape and structure.","If he could obtain enough of the Ever-Changing Temper Gold, they could be used in the construction of Sky City.","When Lin Yuan placed his hand on the surface of the Tower of Truth, he felt the Morbius bracelet on his wrist grow hot.","The monstrous Tower of Truth turned into putty and slowly entered Lin Yuan’s palm.","If anyone saw this, they would think that Lin Yuan’s palm was swallowing the Tower of Truth.","After the Tower of Truth had completely disappeared, Lin Yuan heard Morbius’ tired voice say, “Partner, there was more of the Crimson Spirit Bronze and Ever-Changing Temper Gold in Fifth Page Truth’s tower than I expected.","“All of the Crimson Spirit Bronze and Ever-Changing Temper Gold that I refined is in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. I will go and rest now. I will wake up about a day later.”","Lin Yuan hurriedly asked, “Morbius, haven’t you accumulated a fair amount of root power? Why are you going to sleep again?”","Morbius had used its root power to save Lin Yuan multiple times.","Many of Lin Yuan’s opportunities came from Morbius using up some of its root power.","Lin Yuan did not want Morbius to use too much of its root power to refine the Crimson Spirit Bronze and Ever-Changing Temper Gold.","Although the Crimson Spirit Bronze and Ever-Changing Temper Gold were very valuable, they were still only two types of spiritual metal ingredients. They would never be able to save Lin Yuan’s life in a crisis.","If any issues cropped up, Morbius would fall into a deep and long slumber again after overly exerting its root power.","Lin Yuan did not want Morbius to fall asleep again. He much preferred for Morbius to remain awake so they could talk often.","Lin Yuan discussed many development plans and ideas with Morbius.","Morbius’ tired voice became slightly lighter when it heard what Lin Yuan said.","“Partner, I didn’t touch the root power that I accumulated. Otherwise, I wouldn’t be as tired as I am now. While you’ve evolved me from Normal grade to where I am now, I became stronger too.”","Once it was done speaking, Morbius fell asleep.","Meanwhile, Lin Yuan returned to where he had been resting in the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court.","When Jin Qianxun received Lin Yuan’s promise, he received 100 plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline on that day itself.","By now, his loyalty and faith toward Lin Yuan far exceeded that of a regular devotee.","Lin Yuan could sense that the amount of faith in the faith fountain in the divine kingdom that came from Jin Qianxun could be ranked as one of the 100 strongest sources.","The more subordinates Lin Yuan gained, the more faith he could garner.","Lin Yuan and Jin Qianxun had not been acquainted for long.","Given that Jin Qianxun was able to provide Lin Yuan with so much faith power, he would never do anything to betray Lin Yuan, even without being bound by a contract.","Over the next two days, Lin Yuan and Su Yiren did a final organization of the Great Lush Federation’s resources.","Jin Qianxun was surprised that Lin Yuan did not end up deciding to take the resources with him but left them to Jin Qianxun instead so he could use them on the harbor and Great Lush Federation.","No matter how capable one was, one would not be able to accomplish anything meaningful without the right conditions.","The Great Lush Federation needed resources to develop.","Resources were no different from money.","Without resources, Jin Qianxun would never be able to realize his dreams.","In the past two days, Lin Yuan had organized the resources and met up with Bai Qinghuan.","Both of them chatted for an afternoon.","After their talk, Lin Yuan was even more satisfied with her."]},{"number":2176,"title":"Chapter 2176 Selfish Desire to be Admired!","paragraphs":["2176 Selfish Desire to be Admired!","Bai Qinghuan not only had an eye for strategy but was also a very intelligent person.","There were many things that Bai Qinghuan was able to do even without Lin Yuan giving her explicit instructions.","Bai Qinghuan could understand what Lin Yuan was thinking.","She was also well aware of why Lin Yuan placed her by Jin Qianxun’s side.","When Bai Qinghuan found out that Jin Qianxun had sworn his loyalty to Lin Yuan, she knew that her task at the Great Lush Federation was not to take a look at Jin Qianxun. Lin Yuan wanted her to expand her horizons and raise her ambitions.","!!","Bai Qinghuan’s background was not outstanding, and she could only get ahead of others when it came to strategic thinking.","Bai Qinghuan treasured this opportunity greatly and longed to gain more experience.","If she could expand her horizons, Lin Yuan would not have to give her too many instructions.","An intelligent person like Bai Qinghuan did not need to be boosted by Lin Yuan in order to grow.","Lin Yuan was almost done with all of his business in the Great Lush Federation.","Weng Queji had given Lin Yuan the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers long ago.","There were already more than 30 of the Exploding Spirit Rock Flowers that the Hundred Questions Beasts had evolved to Diamond grade.","Lin Yuan felt that it was time for him to improve himself.","He was currently a B-rank spirit qi professional. When compared to people of his age, he was already extremely outstanding.","Zong Ze, Gu Lang, and Liu Jie were a few years older than Lin Yuan but were only A-rank spirit qi professionals.","Once one became an A-rank spirit qi professional, one would be considered a king-class spirit qi professional as long as he had a Fantasy Breed fey.","There was a large division of rank amongst A-rank spirit qi professionals.","Due to his body condition, Lin Yuan needed to evolve feys until they could absorb the spirit qi from him.","No matter how busy he was, Lin Yuan did not relax when he came to increasing his power.","He was well aware that everything came down to power.","By now, he was not far away from becoming an A-rank spirit qi professional.","He sensed that his body’s spiritual power was starting to coalesce.","In order for B-rank spirit qi professionals to evolve to A-rank, all of the spiritual power in their bodies had to be solidified to form a core.","Lin Yuan estimated that as long as he continued to increase his power at the current rate, he would be able to reach A-rank in about five months.","At that time, he would only be 19 years old.","At that age, there were no A-rank spirit qi professionals in the Radiance Federation or even the world.","For the past few months, Lin Yuan’s mind had been fully focused on taking on the Freedom Federation envoy group and conquering the Startling Lines Continent.","Thus, he spent less than ten hours evolving feys each day.","But now, Lin Yuan was much freer.","From now on, Lin Yuan intended to spend more than 12 hours each day evolving feys.","This way, he would be able to become an A-rank spirit qi professional in just another three months.","At that time, all of Lin Yuan’s Diamond/Fantasy V feys would be able to break through to Suzerain/Fantasy.","There was an enormous gap between Normal and Fantasy Breed feys.","The same went for the gap between Fantasy Breed and Myth Breed feys.","With another exclusive skill, a fey’s power could be increased by an unimaginable degree.","Before being promoted to A-rank spirit qi professional and evolving all his feys, he wanted to first evolve the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen and Perfect Touch Wisteria.","Liu Jie had summoned the white-clothed followers while Lin Yuan was on the way to the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court.","In the 15 days Lin Yuan had been unconscious, the white-clothed followers reached Clean Brahma City.","While the white-clothed followers were out training, they wore Sky City’s uniform.","Jin Qianxun was well aware that the white-clothed followers were subordinates who Lin Yuan put a lot of effort into nurturing.","Hence, Jin Qianxun ensured that all of the white-clothed followers were fed and serviced well in Clean Brahma City.","It was time for many of the white-clothed followers’ feys to be evolved.","Due to Lin Yuan, all of the feys’ strength was halted at Diamond X/Fantasy V.","Now, it was time to promote the white-clothed followers from king-class to emperor-class.","The white-clothed followers who were recruited first all had at least three feys. Amongst the three feys, at least two of them had reached Diamond X/Fantasy V.","It could be said that Lin Yuan could receive at least 100 portions of the World Graces.","He could evolve the Perfect Touch Wisteria to Fantasy Breed with such a large amount of spirit qi crystals.","At that time, Lin Yuan would possess thearch-class combat power without any external help despite only being a B-rank spirit qi professional.","If anyone else found out about this, they would not believe it.","Furthermore, with the dark gold snake, other Creation Breed feys would be no match for the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","Liu Jie had been on edge for 15 days.","After resting for two days, he finally regained his spirits.","Liu Jie was currently experimenting with the spiritual resistance of insect-species carcinoma feys with Su Yiren.","Lin Yuan sought Liu Jie out and instructed him to gather the white-clothed followers together.","Liu Jie was the member of Sky City who was in charge of the white-clothed followers.","Lin Yuan was the City Lord of Sky City and did not directly insert himself into the management of the white-clothed followers.","Liu Jie had just built up an authoritative force within the white-clothed followers.","If Lin Yuan went over Liu Jie’s head and gave orders to the white-clothed followers, he would cut away at Liu Jie’s authoritative aura.","Once a superior’s authoritative aura was lost, the consequences could be disastrous.","This especially applied to the white-clothed followers who were abruptly promoted from king-class to emperor-class in a short span of time and believed that they could overpower Liu Jie.","Liu Jie was the one who gave the order for the white-clothed followers to gather in Clean Brahma City.","Liu Jie knew that Lin Yuan was preparing to increase the power of the white-clothed followers.","When the power of the white-clothed followers increased, so did Sky City’s overall power.","Liu Jie had also put a lot of effort into nurturing the white-clothed followers.","After Lin Yuan collected all the resources he needed, Jin Qianxun cleaned out the area within the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court that used to belong to Fifth Page Truth.","He was planning to build a martial arts hall there.","With the large amount of plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline that came from Lin Yuan and Lin Yuan’s permission to distribute these plant-type feys, Jin Qianxun intended to give them to some of his more loyal imperial guards first.","Naturally, these people would be chosen from amongst the Jin family’s direct descendants and collateral descendants.","It could be said that Jin Qianxun had his own selfish desires.","But Lin Yuan did not oppose them. Rather, he admired Jin Qianxun’s actions."]},{"number":2177,"title":"Chapter 2177 Help Me!","paragraphs":["2177 Help Me!","Lin Yuan knew that Jin Qianxun had been aiming to cling to him and do whatever he asked.","But in spite of this aim, Jin Qianxun was still the head of a federation and needed to have the necessary aura that came with it.","The best way to increase his foundational power was to nurture a batch of subordinates who were loyal to him to increase the amount of power at his disposal.","Liu Jie went to see Jin Qianxun first to borrow the use of the martial arts hall.","Since Liu Jie had asked, there was no way that Jin Qianxun would dare to turn him down and immediately cleared the space for him.","Next, Liu Jie contacted some of the stronger white-clothed followers and led them to the martial arts hall in the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court.","Lin Yuan, the City Lord of Sky City, was a mystery to the white-clothed followers.","Although those present were the first few joiners of the white-clothed followers, only Zhou Luo and a few more of them had spoken to Lin Yuan before.","Besides the first few joiners, the rest of the white-clothed followers had all been recruited by Liu Jie.","Nonetheless, they all knew that any changes in their fate depended on Lin Yuan and Liu Jie.","The first few joiners were all citizens of the Radiance Federation.","At first, they did not know who Liu Jie and Lin Yuan were.","But when Lin Yuan and Liu Jie revealed their identities during the fight against the Freedom Federation envoy group, every citizen of the Radiance Federation found out that Lin Yuan was the Moon Empress’ disciple while Liu Jie was Night Leaning Moon’s disciple.","All of the white-clothed followers felt honored to be able to be part of a faction that both of them had established.","Now, they were in unfamiliar territory, but it was a territory that Sky City had conquered.","The white-clothed followers could never have dreamed of anything like this happening.","Now, they saw Lin Yuan and Liu Jie as no different from gods.","Half a year ago, all of them had only contracted mediocre feys and were part of the pits of society.","But now, their arsenal of feys had exceeded even that of other king-class experts.","More importantly, their feys had evolved to Fantasy Breed when they were Bronze or Silver grade. This allowed them to have much greater potential than their peers.","While the white-clothed followers were looking at Lin Yuan and Liu Jie with high esteem, Lin Yuan was also gazing back at them.","As Lin Yuan looked at these people’s confident and energized expressions, he felt a sense of accomplishment.","After treading on a path laden with thorns in the past six months, he finally saw some results.","Lin Yuan looked at Liu Jie.","Liu Jie shouted to the 47 white-clothed followers who were in the martial arts hall, “All of you are A-rank spirit qi professionals. Some of you have even reached S-rank. Previously, you were made to keep your feys’ powers stuck at Diamond X/Fantasy V. Now is the time to evolve your feys and transform yourselves into emperor-class experts. You should have heard of how dangerous the World Cleansing is. But with us around, we can guarantee that you will be safe during the World Cleansing.”","In the past, the white-clothed followers would have caused an uproar if they had heard what Liu Jie said.","But after training for so long, all of the white-clothed followers could remain composed even in the face of delight.","Lin Yuan instructed Shadow to leave his shadow and said, “Later, Shadow will help you to overcome your World Cleansing. Your safety is assured by gathering all of you together and having your feys evolve at once. Additionally, I hope that you can help me with something.”","Morbius could use the Pure Land of Bliss to absorb the World Graces without the feys feeling anything.","The Pure Land of Bliss would only take about around 2% of each of the World Graces.","Normally, it was very difficult for a spirit qi professional to help their fey overcome the World Cleansing.","When feys were injured, it would be impossible for them to absorb 98% of their World Grace.","This was why so many spirit qi professionals were willing to respond to Lin Yuan’s trade message on Star Web even if it would cost them a portion of the World Grace.","Thus, there was actually no need for Lin Yuan to tell the white-clothed followers about this condition.","But as the City Lord of Sky City, Lin Yuan did not want to lie to his subordinates for the sake of his own profits.","As such, there were some things that still had to be said.","The moment Lin Yuan was done speaking, almost all of the white-clothed followers bowed with their fists cupped and said, “City Lord, if you need us to do anything, all you need to do is say the word! We would never dare to claim that we were helping you!”","The white-clothed followers’ voices were bright and deafening. Anyone who heard them could tell that they were sincere.","It could be said that it was human to be selfish.","When Jin Qianxun swore his loyalty to Lin Yuan, he had selfishly wanted to nurture a group of experts who were only loyal to him.","Although the white-clothed followers had joined Sky City and had dedicated their loyalty, they still needed to look out for themselves.","This was because many of them had parents, wives, and children back home who they needed to support.","They needed to think about their families even if they did not look out for themselves.","But in front of Lin Yuan, all of the white-clothed followers tossed all selfish thoughts out of their minds.","One had to plunge into the murky abyss before understanding how dark this world was.","When the value of the resources was more significant than the talent, a lack of Creation Master resources led to factions preferring to nurture those who were sincere rather than talented.","Thus, even a spirit qi professional who had comprehended multiple Willpower Runes did not have much chance to prove their abilities.","In this world, it was difficult for there to be instances of the main character catching the eye of a bigshot with his outstanding talent, like in the books that Lin Yuan had read in his previous life.","When the Moon Empress was picking her disciples, she had looked out for Creation Master talent rather than spirit qi professional talent.","Since the white-clothed followers had such experiences in the past, all of them were even more grateful and respectful of Lin Yuan after joining Sky City and having their fates changed.","After receiving top resources, a spirit qi professional’s standard of living would not only be improved, but they would even be able to obtain a higher status in society.","In this world ruled by martial force, power was a more formidable strength than riches."]},{"number":2178,"title":"Chapter 2178 A Group of World Cleansings!","paragraphs":["2178 A Group of World Cleansings!","When Liu Jie heard what the white-clothed followers said, he nodded in satisfaction while thinking about how intelligent the white-clothed followers were.","Lin Yuan did not put on any airs in front of his Sky City subordinates. But this did not mean that he was a tolerant person.","He placed a high premium on the loyalty of the faction members.","The benefits received by the Spirit Craftsmen who were willing to leave society and relocate to the marsh world were the best examples.","If the white-clothed followers were willing to do the same, there was no question that they would definitely receive more resources from Lin Yuan.","At first, Lin Yuan wanted to provide an explanation. But after hearing what the white-clothed followers said, he kept his words to himself.","He pointed at Zhou Luo, who was standing at the right side of the front of the crowd, and said, “Zhou Luo, let’s start with you!”","It could be said that Zhou Luo was the member of the white-clothed followers closest to Lin Yuan.","Not only had Lin Yuan personally recruited Zhou Luo as the first member of the white-clothed followers, but Zhou Luo had even survived the water world dimensional rift alongside Lin Yuan and Liu Jie.","If Zhou Luo had not used the Lava Dragon Lizard to block the Blade Worms, Lin Yuan and Liu Jie would have died under the assault of Tower Canon’s Ashes Team.","If Lin Yuan had used the secret weapon the Moon Empress had given him against the Blade Worms, he would have stood no chance against the Ashes Team and the dimensional hub in the evolving dimensional rift.","Zhou Luo’s sacrifice had created a chain reaction that led all the way to the result.","Liu Jie’s Insect Queen had mutated after absorbing the Blade Queen Bee’s venom while Lin Yuan had obtained the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen.","Zhou Luo had started out as a regular white-clothed follower.","But after the brush with death he shared with Liu Jie and Lin Yuan, both of them decided to make him the deputy leader of the white-clothed followers.","There were no issues with Zhou Luo’s capabilities, and he had been helping Liu Jie to manage the white-clothed followers all along.","Among the white-clothed followers, Zhou Luo’s talent was average.","But there were times that a spirit qi professional who started out as average ended up surpassing all the rest.","Since Zhou Luo was the deputy leader of the white-clothed followers, he had to have the power to back it up.","With Lin Yuan’s favor, Zhou Luo’s third fey ended up being the Sea King Cretaceous Dragon that came from Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","The Sea King Cretaceous Dragon had been the main fey of Coiling Dragon’s Valley’s Young Leader, Long Tao. This was enough to show that its terrifying-dragon-species bloodline was strong.","There was a legend that the Sea King Cretaceous Dragon had the bloodline of the top terrifying-dragon-species, the Overflowing Sea Extreme Cold Dragon.","Long Tao’s Sea King Cretaceous Dragon was only Silver/Fantasy, while Zhou Luo’s one had already evolved to Fantasy Breed when it was Bronze grade.","In terms of talent, Zhou Luo’s Sea King Cretaceous Dragon was more powerful than Long Tao’s.","With just the Sea King Cretaceous Dragon, the rest of the white-clothed followers dared not disrespect Zhou Luo regardless of whether they were more talented than him.","This was because the Sea King Cretaceous Dragon raised Zhou Luo’s overall power and because it was proof of how important Zhou Luo was to Lin Yuan.","Ever since Zhou Luo became the deputy leader of the white-clothed followers, he rarely went out on missions. Instead, he spent more time planning and strategizing alongside Liu Jie.","Liu Jie wanted to stay with Lin Yuan as much as possible. Thus, Zhou Luo’s job was not easy in the slightest.","Zhou Luo had not seen Lin Yuan in more than two months.","Now, he took a few steps forward toward the smiling Lin Yuan, who was pointing at him, and summoned his three feys.","Every single one of the white-clothed followers’ feys was personally evolved by Lin Yuan.","Zhou Luo’s Dark Snake Dragon Lizard and Sea King Cretaceous Dragon were both very fond of Lin Yuan. But the fey that had the closest bond to Lin Yuan was the Lava Dragon Lizard that had transformed from the Iron Bone Tearing Lizard.","The Lava Dragon Lizard had been this way ever since Lin Yuan changed Zhou Luo’s life.","Lin Yuan had helped to evolve the Lava Dragon Lizard’s bloodline when it was Diamond II.","By that time, the Lava Dragon Lizard already had very high intelligence. Hence, it had more memories of Lin Yuan than the Dark Snake Dragon Lizard and Sea King Cretaceous Dragon did.","Zhou Luo was the only white-clothed follower who was aware of Shadow’s existence.","Besides him, there were 46 other white-clothed followers whose feys needed to undergo World Cleansings.","If the feys underwent the World Cleansings one by one, they would still be here many hours later.","As such, Zhou Luo asked, “City Lord, should my feys undergo the World Cleansings one after the other, or all at once?”","Lin Yuan immediately replied, “Have all three start their World Cleansings together!”","Lin Yuan turned his gaze to the rest of the white-clothed followers and said, “Most of you have three main feys. A few have four. When it’s your turn, summon all of them out and have them start their World Cleansings simultaneously!”","The moment Lin Yuan was done speaking, three large holes appeared in the sky above the martial arts hall.","One of the holes was full of lava, while the other two crackled with lightning.","The might and aura from the World Cleansings drained the blood from the faces of the white-clothed followers.","Normally, it would be very unlikely that the white-clothed followers would be able to take on even one of the World Cleansings with their three feys.","This was the reason so many emperor-class experts were plagued by their inability to evolve their feys.","If the wall that was the World Cleansing was not this difficult to scale, most emperor-class experts would not have joined factions but remained free agents like Duan He had been.","Not every faction was as kind to its members like Sky City was.","Even top factions needed their members to provide contributions and produce results in exchange for resources.","Emperor-class and thearch-class experts joined factions so that they would have an easier time taking on the World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation.","Regular people and weak spirit qi professionals did not get to hear what was said in emperor-class and thearch-class expert circles. Even king-class experts were not privy to much knowledge. After all, there was a threshold of power to cross.","Before one reached that level, they found out almost nothing about it.","It was often heard in emperor-class and thearch-class experts circles about how some had failed in their World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation.","Although they were shocked by the aura of the World Cleansings, the white-clothed followers were not afraid because they knew that Lin Yuan and Liu Jie were there with them.","Since Lin Yuan and Liu Jie had told them to undergo the World Cleansings in such a way, they would definitely keep all of them safe."]},{"number":2179,"title":"Chapter 2179 The Perfect Touch Wisteria Begins its Evolution!","paragraphs":["2179 The Perfect Touch Wisteria Begins its Evolution!","This was not the first time that Shadow was helping spirit qi professionals overcome their World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation. It was well aware of how strong they were.","Presently, Shadow had reached Immortal. With its power, it could take on the Trials of World Creation without breaking too much of a sweat, much less the World Cleansings that Fantasy Breed feys needed to face to evolve to Myth Breed.","Lava and lightning relentlessly flew down toward the Lava Dragon Lizard, Sea King Cretaceous Dragon, and Dark Snake Dragon Lizard.","All three feys were gripped with anxiety, and Zhou Luo was frozen as well.","But rather than being immobilized by fear, he was excited for his feys to increase their power.","Zhou Luo knew that Lin Yuan had been paying more attention to nurturing the white-clothed followers of late.","He had been promoted to S-rank spirit qi professional not long ago.","S-rank spirit qi professionals could use their spiritual power to produce spirit qi vortexes and absorb the spiritual energy of their surroundings to protect themselves and increase their stamina during combat.","Due to this, S-rank spirit qi professionals had no restrictions in the grade of feys they could contract.","Zhou Luo knew how much Liu Jie and Lin Yuan favored him.","Although he was only a king-class expert, he believed that Lin Yuan would provide him with many resources once he reached emperor-class.","Soon, his main feys would evolve from Myth I to Myth II, then to Myth III, until they finally reached Creation Breed.","Zhou Luo badly wanted to increase his power. This went for the other white-clothed followers as well.","The white-clothed followers hoped to increase their power and that their feys would transform into human form.","There was something that Liu Jie had not told Lin Yuan yet.","For some reason, Sky City’s white-clothed followers now all shared the same proclivity as Duan He.","There were some that started treating their feys as their wives once they ascertained that they were female.","There was no difference between them hoping for their feys to transform into human form and them waiting for their wives to arrive.","At that moment, the white-clothed followers froze.","A black shadow cleaved two bolts of lightning and a stream of lava into half.","The shadow that was attacking the World Cleansings reminded the white-clothed followers of the shadow that had cut down the Miao family’s veteran thearch-class experts on the ultimate fighting ground.","The earliest members of the white-clothed followers had been there during Sky City’s blood pact ultimate fight against Connected Beast Park.","The Miao family had been a top faction with a Creation Master role. They had maintained their place amongst the top factions for decades.","None of the white-clothed followers were worried about Sky City’s future.","It was the black shadow that had killed Liu Yanshan and Han Tianhe that made the white-clothed followers aware of how powerful the faction they had sworn their loyalty to was. It also filled them with firm confidence.","The white-clothed followers had all been looking up to the black shadow. Now, they were getting to see it in the flesh, and it was helping them to overcome their World Cleansings.","With Shadow’s help, the three World Cleansings were quickly defeated.","While Zhou Luo’s three main feys were absorbing the World Graces, the Pure Land of Bliss was also absorbing its part of the World Graces.","A pile of spirit qi crystals appeared on the Pure Land of Bliss.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was rushing to use the wind elements to gather the spirit qi crystals.","There were so many spirit qi crystals that it was difficult for the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope to quickly clear the Pure Land of Bliss.","When Gray saw what was happening, it went to help and transformed into a puff of cloud covering the Pure Land of Bliss.","Next, it sensed where the spirit qi crystals were and relayed the information to the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope so it could quickly dig them out.","The two of them worked together swimmingly.","As the spirit qi professionals’ took turns sending their feys to undergo their World Cleansings, two large wooden chests in the Spirit Lock spatial zone were soon filled with spirit qi crystals.","Gray ended up having to stack the spirit qi crystals next to the two wooden chests.","Lin Yuan had always been short on spirit qi crystals.","But now, there were clearly more of the spirit qi crystals than there were heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","By the time the last white-clothed follower’s three main feys were done with their World Cleansings, more than four hours had passed.","After these four hours, Sky City gained another 47 emperor-class experts who could stand proudly as the linchpins of any faction they were in.","It was unlikely that even a faction like Tower Canon would be willing to invest so many resources into nurturing their subordinates.","The white-clothed followers were always busy.","Before Sky City started making any big waves, all of them had been focusing on training and did their best every day.","Thus, Lin Yuan did not interfere much with them.","After the 47 white-clothed followers left, Lin Yuan and Liu Jie prepared to leave to have dinner.","Liu Jie had already conquered the stomachs of countless people with his culinary skills.","The first few stomachs to submit to him belonged to Lin Yuan, Wen Yu, and the Mother of Bloodbath. Later came Su Yiren and Ta Lei.","Now, even Begin Lady, who was not picky with food, asked to eat the food he cooked daily.","That night, Liu Jie picked a few fish-species feys native to the Great Lush Federation and cooked up a feast.","After filling his belly, Lin Yuan retired to his room and went into the Spirit Lock spatial zone with Begin Lady.","Once he entered, Lin Yuan saw the pile of spirit qi crystals that was akin to a miniature mountain.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope and Gray were currently counting the spirit qi crystals.","When they spotted Lin Yuan, Chimey, Gray, and the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope rushed to greet him.","Lin Yuan soothed and played with them for a short while.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was about to return to counting the spirit qi crystals when it was stopped by Lin Yuan.","This was because the number of spirit qi crystals was unimportant to Lin Yuan.","He would soon use all of them to evolve the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","Lin Yuan looked forward to the Perfect Touch Wisteria increasing its power.","Since the Perfect Touch Wisteria was spirit locked by Morbius, it would not gain any new abilities when it evolved.","However, as it continued to increase its quality and grade, it could gain more exclusive skills.","Exclusive skills were always stronger than abilities."]},{"number":2180,"title":"Chapter 2180 Explosive Expansion!","paragraphs":["2180 Explosive Expansion!","Lin Yuan had wanted to evolve the Perfect Touch Wisteria for a long time.","It was a fey that he had spirit locked, meaning that it was part of his power.","Lin Yuan was always enthusiastic when it came to increasing his power.","The Spirit Lock spatial zone was 480 square meters and was far from the cramped space it used to be.","There were numerous large appetites for spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The spirit pool produced spirit qi at around the same rate that the feys within it used up spirit qi.","The Spirit Lock spatial zone had always produced a large stream of resources.","There was enough space for Lin Yuan to decorate and fill up the area as he liked.","He had set aside 20 square meters of space for the Perfect Touch Wisteria to ensure that it had enough space to move.","When the Perfect Touch Wisteria used Swallow Same Source to absorb the dark gold snake scale, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope and Chimey both became terrified of the dark gold flames and dared not go near the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","Although Gray would not show obvious fear of the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s dark gold flames, it was still unwilling to spend too much time around the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria was a plant-type fey. Thus, its intelligence was very low.","It only became active and lively when Lin Yuan was around, almost like a child that wanted to be loved by their parent and was doing everything to get in their parent’s good books.","Lin Yuan went over to the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","The few of the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s vines that had not consumed anything yet immediately wrapped around Lin Yuan and started to gently massage his chest and hand.","At first, Chimey was perched on Lin Yuan’s shoulder.","But after Lin Yuan walked nearer to the Perfect Touch Wisteria until he was only ten meters away, Chimey flew off from his shoulder and back to its nest on the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree.","It was clear that Lin Yuan’s existence was not enough to overpower Chimey’s trepidation of the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s dark gold flames.","Once it was back in its nest, Chimey started to observe the close interaction between Lin Yuan and the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","Chimey thought, If Red Thorn was here, it would be green with envy over the Perfect Touch Wisteria!","Red Thorn was the most openly possessive out of all of Lin Yuan’s feys.","Genius, Chimey, Blackie, Purple Afterglow, and the rest of Lin Yuan’s feys had sensed this long ago.","Even Begin Lady, who had set its spirit fire alight, felt uncomfortable around that aura.","This situation allowed Lin Yuan to confirm that he had indeed stumbled on a treasure. The dark gold snake scale was definitely extraordinary.","Lin Yuan instructed the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope to bring 1,000 spirit qi crystals to him.","Currently, Morbius was at Gold grade.","Each spirit qi crystal contained a startlingly large amount of spirit qi.","Lin Yuan fed all 1,000 of the spirit qi crystals to the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","He would be able to tell from the increase in the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s power how much vitality and spirit qi was needed for the Perfect Touch Wisteria to use its Elite ability Peak Sturdiness to raise its sturdiness and durability.","Next, Lin Yuan took out a large number of the Soldier Ration Radishes from the Diamond fey storage box.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria needed not only pure spirit qi but also vitality to increase its power.","There was no better source of vitality than the Soldier Ration Radish.","In the past, Lin Yuan always crushed the spirit qi crystals in his hand. But this time, there were too many spirit qi crystals, so he used the Source Sand to create a large hand that was three square meters wide and slammed it down on the 1,000 spirit qi crystals.","When the 1,000 spirit qi crystals were crushed, a strong gust of wind was kicked up.","Before Lin Yuan crushed the spirit qi crystals with the large hand made of sand, he had already instructed the Perfect Touch Wisteria to begin absorbing the spirit qi from the spirit qi crystals.","As the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s three wildly dancing vines that had already consumed entities rapidly absorbed the spirit qi, the other vines started to suck up the Soldier Ration Radish’s sap.","Lin Yuan instructed the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope to gather up the Soldier Ration Radishes that had been sucked dry while continuing to take more of the fresh Soldier Ration Radishes out from Diamond fey storage box.","When the dry Soldier Ration Radishes were moved to the marsh world, they would serve as excellent fertilizers.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria’s aura skyrocketed as it absorbed the spirit qi and vitality. It did not take long for the Perfect Touch Wisteria to reach Platinum grade.","Previously, one of the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s vines was only around six to seven meters long and not even as thick as Lin Yuan’s forearm.","But now, one of its vines was 20 meters long and much thicker than his waist.","The increase in the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s size not only caused the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope and Chimey to panic, but even Gray was perturbed.","When Lin Yuan noticed this, he hurriedly soothed the three of them.","Following this, he immediately left the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Four pairs of enormous black wings appeared on his back. He flapped the wings and sped off in the direction of the martial arts hall.","After the white-clothed followers left the martial arts hall, Jin Qianxun instructed numerous Spirit Craftsmen to survey the area.","Jin Qianxun wanted the Spirit Craftsmen to draw up some designs so he could pick the best ones out of them and combine them as the final blueprint for the martial arts hall.","Ever since his conversation with Lin Yuan, Jin Qianxun felt extremely excited.","He was currently on the ground at the martial arts hall and conversing with the Spirit Craftsmen.","This was the first time that Jin Qianxun was seeing Lin Yuan with four pairs of black wings on his back.","When he saw Lin Yuan speeding over, Jin Qianxun had the sharp sense to send the Spirit Craftsmen away.","Lin Yuan said, “You can leave too. I need absolute silence. No one is to disturb me! Otherwise, they’ll have to bear the consequences themselves!”","Jin Qianxun was stunned momentarily before he hastily left.","After Jin Qianxun left and closed the door of the martial arts hall behind him, Lin Yuan immediately let the Perfect Touch Wisteria out.","It would not be appropriate to evolve large feys in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope and Chimey had their ways of communicating with him.","After the Perfect Touch Wisteria reached Platinum grade, just its aura terrified the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope and Chimey.","It was only natural that the Wood-Building Winged Sandflies and Dark Crystal Armored Insects being raised in captivity were scared out of their wits too.","If the Perfect Touch Wisteria evolved to Suzerain in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, the Wood-Building Winged Sandflies and Dark Crystal Armored Insects might end up dying of fright!"]},{"number":2181,"title":"Chapter 2181 Personally Nurtured to Myth Breed!","paragraphs":["2181 Personally Nurtured to Myth Breed!","Lin Yuan could not afford to lose such feys that could produce pure elemental energy.","The martial arts hall was large enough to hold several feys undergoing World Cleansings simultaneously. It went without saying that there was enough space.","It was perfect for Lin Yuan to evolve the Perfect Touch Wisteria here.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria’s increase in power and size was definitely a good thing.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria mainly used its body during combat. The stronger and larger its body was, the more combat power would come from it.","Lin Yuan did not rush to take out another batch of spirit qi crystals. Rather, he told Begin Lady, “Begin Lady, help me watch over this space. If you discover anyone spying nearby, eliminate them immediately.”","Both the spirit qi crystals and the Perfect Touch Wisteria were Lin Yuan’s secret weapons and secrets.","There was no way he would allow them to be discovered by anyone.","When Begin Lady heard what he said, it appeared next to him and said with a smile, “Don’t worry, Lin Yuan. I won’t let your trust down. I’ll definitely help you to keep this secret!”","With Begin Lady’s assurance, Lin Yuan summoned all of the spirit qi crystals out of the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The 1,000 spirit qi crystals allowed the Perfect Touch Wisteria to evolve from Silver grade to Diamond X and finally to Fantasy III.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria was a true Fantasy Breed fey at that moment.","Each of its vines was 40 meters long and had a diameter of one meter.","When it had been Bronze grade, the Perfect Touch Wisteria could have been considered a potted plant.","But now, it had fully transformed into a ferocious beast.","Because of Forbidden Growth, the Perfect Touch Wisteria could automatically comprehend a Willpower Rune after absorbing enough energy. There was no need for Lin Yuan to provide it with a Willpower Rune.","When feys automatically comprehended Willpower Runes, the Willpower Runes were always compatible with their bodies.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the Perfect Touch Wisteria and saw that its new exclusive skill was called Broken Vine Replacement.","It would allow the Perfect Touch Wisteria to transfer the damage suffered by one vine onto another vine so that the first vine could be preserved.","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up when he saw this exclusive skill.","It was not a rare exclusive skill as many vine-species plant-type feys had similar exclusive skills.","Broken Vine Replacement was criticized by many spirit qi professionals who possessed plant-type Fantasy Breed feys.","Moreover, Fantasy Breed feys did not have multiple options for exclusive skills like Bronze grade feys did.","But while this exclusive skill was useless to other vine-species plant-type feys, it was a reward in this case.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria currently had three vines that had absorbed entities using Swallow Same Source. One had absorbed the dark gold snake scale, the other had absorbed the Forever Frozen Frost Iron, and the third had absorbed Begin Lady’s intermediate faerie bloodline.","Lin Yuan had decided to let the Perfect Touch Wisteria absorb the Sovereign metal spiritual ingredient Forever Frozen Frost Iron because he wanted to create an elemental reaction with the vine that had absorbed the dark gold snake scale and produce higher level damage.","If the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s vines were destroyed, they could be regrown.","However, after the special entities that had been absorbed were destroyed, the regrown vine would be no different from a regular vine.","It could be said that Lin Yuan had been terrified that the vines that had absorbed special entities would be damaged.","The sting would not be as painful if the vine that had absorbed the Forever Frozen Frost Iron and Begin Lady’s bloodline were destroyed.","It would not be difficult to obtain more of Begin Lady’s bloodline. Thus, even if the vine that had absorbed it was destroyed, it could easily be made up for.","Although Lin Yuan no longer had any of the Forever Frozen Frost Iron, he did have other Sovereign metal spiritual ingredients.","But if there were any issues with the vine that had absorbed the dark gold snake scale, Lin Yuan had no idea where he would go to find another one that the regrown vine could absorb.","Once the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s vine absorbed a certain object, it could no longer absorb anything else.","But now, with the new exclusive skill Broken Vine Replacement, Lin Yuan no longer had to worry about this.","Unless the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s other seven vines were destroyed as well, the vine that had absorbed the dark gold snake scale would always be preserved.","Broken Vine Replacement increased the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s margin for error during combat.","From a certain angle, it could be said that the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s defensive abilities had also been raised.","Lin Yuan was not disappointed by the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s new exclusive skill.","Although the Diamond X/Fantasy III Perfect Touch Wisteria was a plant-type fey, it already had a certain level of intelligence.","Although Lin Yuan could not communicate simply with the Perfect Touch Wisteria through spiritual energy, he could guess what the Perfect Touch Wisteria was thinking.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria badly yearned to evolve once again.","Lin Yuan smiled when he sensed what the Perfect Touch Wisteria was thinking.","He took out two Diamond fey storage boxes filled with the Soldier Ration Radishes and dumped them all out.","Next, he took out half the spirit qi crystals from the pile and crushed them using the hand of sand that the Source Sand had created.","This slam crushed at least 14,000 spirit qi crystals.","When the gust of spirit qi appeared, the Perfect Touch Wisteria wasted no time repeating what it had done before and started to absorb the pure spirit qi and Soldier Ration Radish sap at the same time.","With such a boisterous injection of resources, the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s power skyrocketed.","Suddenly, when the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s aura reached a certain threshold, an obsidian hole appeared in the sky.","When Lin Yuan saw the obsidian hole, he knew that the Perfect Touch Wisteria had used the ability Forbidden Growth to evolve the Myth Breed.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria was not Lin Yuan’s first Myth Breed fey.","Lin Yuan’s first Myth Breed fey was Merciful Soul that he had obtained through special means.","However, the Perfect Touch Wisteria was the first fey Lin Yuan contracted, who he had personally nurtured to Myth Breed.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria had evolved using concentrated spirit qi that not even Class 6 Creation Masters could produce.","Since its appearance did not change much when it reached Fantasy Breed, it would transform wholly when it reached Myth Breed.","Lin Yuan was greatly looking forward to this transformation."]},{"number":2182,"title":"Chapter 2182 Four Hearts For You!","paragraphs":["2182 Four Hearts For You!","With the three treasures that the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s vines had already absorbed and the top-tier nurturing it received, it should be able to take on the World Cleansing on its own!","With this thought, Lin Yuan summoned Shadow.","But, he did not instruct it to help the Perfect Touch Wisteria with its World Cleansing like it did for the white-clothed followers’ feys.","When feys experienced the World Cleansing, they mostly evoked flames, ice, and lightning.","This was a rule that Creation Masters had discovered while they were nurturing feys.","The black hole above the Perfect Touch Wisteria was brewing a snowstorm.","Gray wind blew out from the black hole and was soon accompanied by clusters of frost.","Because of the icy snow in the black hole, the temperature around the martial arts hall dropped.","Lin Yuan looked at the swaying Perfect Touch Wisteria and said seriously, “Perfect Touch Wisteria, try to handle the World Cleansing on your own. If you can’t handle it, hit the ground with the vine that absorbed Begin Lady’s bloodline, and I’ll immediately send Shadow over to help you.”","The Perfect Touch Wisteria could not communicate with Lin Yuan but could sense the meaning behind Lin Yuan’s words.","In all the time that it had been nurtured by Lin Yuan, the Perfect Touch Wisteria had never experienced combat.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria wanted to try its hand at combat so it could prove itself.","At the instant that the white snow descended, the Perfect Touch Wisteria swung its vine that had absorbed the dark gold snake scale at the snow.","This was because the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s only method of attacking and defending was to use the vines.","Secondly, the Perfect Touch Wisteria had sensed the threat that the World Cleansing posed.","Eventually, a scene that Lin Yuan had not predicted appeared before his eyes.","When the Perfect Touch Wisteria attacked, solid vitality spurred the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s vines to extend.","The vine that had a dark gold snake scale already had the form of a snake.","As the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s power grew, the image of the snake became clearer.","The snake scales on the snake-shaped vine were roused into action as dark gold flames shot into the sky and evaporated the white snow.","None of the snow managed to touch the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s vines.","When this scene unfolded, Lin Yuan had no idea if the World Cleansing was testing the Perfect Touch Wisteria or if it was the other way around.","There was no chance for Shadow to step in at all.","This scene shocked even Begin Lady.","Begin Lady was a faerie who had experienced the Heaven’s Trial. It understood how tough the tests from nature were for feys.","Moreover, Begin Lady had absorbed Su Jian and Bai Dong’s souls. As such, it was afraid of the tribulations feys had to face when they evolved from Fantasy Breed to Myth Breed.","Su Jian and Bai Dong had also thought about sending their feys to experience the World Cleansings and prove their feys’ powers.","As long as one was a direct descendant from a veteran family, there would be stiff competition amongst those who were close in age.","Bai Dong and Su Jian had been so anxious to prove themselves that their feys had almost died at the hands of the World Cleansings.","Begin Lady sighed.","What kind of fey had Lin Yuan nurtured?","After passing the World Cleansing so easily, the Perfect Touch Wisteria raised its eight vines and intertwined them, forming four hearts for Lin Yuan in the sky.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria occasionally spent time in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","When it saw Gray, Chimey, and the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope playing together and molding the clouds into hearts, the Perfect Touch Wisteria picked up the trick too.","After the World Cleansing came the World Grace.","While the Perfect Touch Wisteria was forming hearts in the sky, the World Grace descended.","Lin Yuan hurriedly said, “Perfect Touch Wisteria, your chance to transform has come. Focus on absorbing the World Grace. This is the turning point of your life.”","Lin Yuan not only looked forward to the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s transformation but also hoped that its power could increase rapidly.","Plant-type feys did not have high intelligence when they were Fantasy Breed.","Once they reached Myth Breed, their intelligence would shoot upwards.","Although plant-type feys only changed into human form when they reached Myth III, they would have comparable intelligence to animal-type feys once they reached Myth Breed.","The sound of Morbius chuckling appeared in Lin Yuan’s head. “Partner, rather than hoping for the Perfect Touch Wisteria to gain intelligence, you should be looking forward to what it’ll look like when it changes into human form. You have so many spirit qi crystals, and you’ve already used at least 14,000 of them. The Perfect Touch Wisteria will easily be able to evolve to Myth III.”","Lin Yuan was slightly stunned when he heard what Morbius said.","But it did not take long for his lips to stretch into a wry smile.","He had indeed been getting ahead of himself.","Morbius checked on the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s condition before it said, “Partner, a fey like the Perfect Touch Wisteria with a tough exterior and long vines doesn’t have a gender. When it changes into human form, it will pick a gender according to its subconscious and personal wishes. I wonder what the Perfect Touch Wisteria will end up choosing! Do you want to pick on its behalf?”","Lin Yuan shook his head gently.","When it came to evolving his feys and increasing his power, Lin Yuan always did everything he could to provide his feys with the best so they could have an easier time on their journeys.","This was Lin Yuan’s way of being responsible to his feys but also to himself.","But when it came to matters such as picking genders, Lin Yuan was willing to leave the freedom of choice to his feys. He would not interfere with this aspect of his feys’ growth.","Even if Lin Yuan truly had a choice that he was leaning toward, he would not enforce his proclivities on the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","When it heard what Lin Yuan said, the Perfect Touch Wisteria started to focus on absorbing the World Grace.","Because of the World Grace, the Perfect Touch Wisteria started to expand wildly.","In the blink of an eye, each one of the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s vines reached a length of 800 meters.","It was considered a giant plant-type fey.","However, the Perfect Touch Wisteria was a vine-species plant-type fey."]},{"number":2183,"title":"Chapter 2183 The Perfect Touch Wisteria in Human Form!","paragraphs":["2183 The Perfect Touch Wisteria in Human Form!","If the Perfect Touch Wisteria slammed any of its vines down on the ground, it would leave a deep crater and produce powerful quakes.","The change in its size was only the beginning of the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s transformation.","A large bundle of plants appeared at the center of the eight vines.","As the vines continuously absorbed the spirit qi and Soldier Ration Radish sap, it started to grow rapidly.","The appearance of the bundle of plants appeared to be covered by a thick wooden-textured skin.","The bundle seemed to be an added base for the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","As a vine-species plant-type fey, the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s roots were not long.","But with the appearance of this bundle of plants, the Perfect Touch Wisteria could remain securely nailed to the ground.","Numerous long wispy roots sprouted from the bundle of plants and pierced the ground.","Several bitter gourd-shaped fruits appeared around where the wispy roots sprouted.","The fruits were where the Perfect Touch Wisteria stored its energy.","It could absorb the fruits through the wispy roots to last longer during combat.","This change fully made up for the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s weakness during terrestrial combat.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria’s eight vines were also covered with a tough wooden exterior.","There were pleats on the surface of the vine that were unique to the exterior of vine-species plants.","These pleats were all lethal weapons during combat.","Although the pleats did not appear large, one touch would be enough to realize that they were half a meter thick.","While the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s vines were moving about, the pleats were no different from study cleavers.","When Lin Yuan thought that the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s transformation was complete and prepared to test out its new exclusive skill, a soft and coiled stem grew out from the strange bundle of plants.","The stem was only around two to three meters tall and was fully eclipsed by the eight vines.","If Lin Yuan was not the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s contractor, he would not be able to tell anything special from its appearance.","After the stem grew out, the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s transformation was complete.","When he heard the Perfect Touch Wisteria communicating with him using spiritual energy, Lin Yuan smiled and replied, “Perfect Touch Wisteria, continue absorbing the rest of the spirit qi! I will provide you with more of the Soldier Ration Radishes. Once you reach Myth III, you’ll be able to change into human form and communicate with me using your natural ornaments.”","After a few squeals of joy from the Perfect Touch Wisteria, it went back to absorbing the spirit qi.","Meanwhile, Lin Yuan examined the new exclusive skill that the Perfect Touch Wisteria gained when it evolved to Myth Breed.","The exclusive skill by the name of Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn caused Lin Yuan to purse his lips.","But, his pursed lips were also slightly upturned, an indication of his uncontrollable delight.","The exclusive skill Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn would allow the energy within the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s vines to gather at a certain spot in the vines.","An illusionary spike consisting of energy would grow out from the spot where the energy was gathered.","This exclusive skill gave the Perfect Touch Wisteria a technique to explosively use its energy.","There was no question that the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s nurturing direction involved allowing it to absorb the best entities through Swallow Same Source.","With such a method of nurturing, it was only natural that the Perfect Touch Wisteria would be able to roll grades to fight.","But the Perfect Touch Wisteria could already roll grades to fight. But with Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn, it had gained an even stronger combat technique.","Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn broke the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s obstacle of only being able to use Normal abilities.","Lin Yuan found it difficult to imagine how powerful the Perfect Touch Wisteria would become when it used the vine that had absorbed the dark gold snake scale to shoot out the illusionary spikes.","The advantages of Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn did not only come from it being able to release energy explosively but more so that the spikes were undetectable and could escape sensing. This meant that they would be difficult to dodge.","In a battle between feys, energy-exploding techniques had their drawbacks. After all, the amount of energy within a fey’s body was limited.","The biggest fear that feys had when using exploding energy techniques was that they would miss their target.","Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn had a high possibility of hitting its mark.","While Lin Yuan was in the throes of happiness, the Perfect Touch Wisteria went through two more World Cleansings and absorbed two more World Graces.","After absorbing two of the World Graces, the Perfect Touch Wisteria expanded again.","However, the stem that grew at the center of the Perfect Touch Wisteria did not change visibly even after absorbing two World Graces.","Lin Yuan thought, It looks like this stem will only grow again once the Perfect Touch Wisteria evolves to Creation Breed.","There were very few flowering vine-species plants.","However, the flowers of flowering vine-species feys were always the core of that vine-species plant-type fey.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria was about to undergo the Myth III World Cleansing.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria continued to use the vine that had absorbed the dark gold snake scale to defend against the snow falling from the sky.","After the Perfect Touch Wisteria absorbed the last World Grace, its enormous body shimmered and turned illusionary.","The burgeoning vitality sounded like rushing water.","When the dark green wood-elemental energy transpired, the bitter scent of vine-species feys permeated the entire martial arts hall.","Finally, the massive Perfect Touch Wisteria turned into a girl who was around 1.75 meters tall and wearing a dark green dress.","The human who the Perfect Touch Wisteria transformed into was not considered beautiful amongst the feys in human form who Lin Yuan had encountered in the past.","Still, she had a charming and languid aura hanging off of her.","With its aura, the Perfect Touch Wisteria had a certain elegance in human form.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria gently lifted its hand, dipped its slender green nail polish-tipped fingers into the illusionary figure, and pulled out a long dark green whip.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria gently twisted the long whip around its waist.","With the long whip pulling at its dress, the Perfect Touch Wisteria appeared even more charming than before.","It could be said that the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s human form was that of a beautiful and charming mature lady.","Its features were not overly dainty, and its aura raised its beauty even higher.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria was not done absorbing all of the spirit qi in the surroundings.","Since the Perfect Touch Wisteria still needed to absorb the spirit qi, the losses would be incalculable if the spirit qi dissipated."]},{"number":2184,"title":"Chapter 2184 Am I Pretty?","paragraphs":["2184 Am I Pretty?","Lin Yuan was able to obtain a large amount of spirit qi crystals when he nurtured the white-clothed followers.","However, spirit qi crystals were still very precious, and it would not do to waste any of them.","Hence, even after changing into human form, the Perfect Touch Wisteria could only wave at Lin Yuan from a distance.","Lin Yuan once again heard the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s excited voice, “Yuan, am I pretty?”","Lin Yuan could not help but slap his forehead when he heard this.","Oh God! The Perfect Touch Wisteria’s image and voice are worlds apart!","The creature in front of him appeared to be a charming lady, but the way it spoke did not match its exterior in the slightest.","If the Perfect Touch Wisteria said such a thing to the enemy during combat, the jarring juxtaposition could end up distracting the enemy.","If an expert even blinked during combat, they could end up having the tables turned on them.","Lin Yuan came to understand this during the fight between the Goddess of Mercy and Fifth Page Truth.","If Fifth Page Truth had used the Divine Order Evil Fetus from the beginning, the Goddess of Mercy and Begin Lady’s joint attacks would not have crushed him to such a degree.","Under the barrage of attacks from the Goddess of Mercy, Fifth Page Truth had absolutely no opportunity to use the Divine Order Evil Fetus.","If Fifth Page Truth could have found a way to distract the Goddess of Mercy, the ending could have been different.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria continued to absorb spirit qi as it extended a tentacle out from beneath its dress to drain the Soldier Ration Radishes’ sap as well.","It could be said that Lin Yuan had raised the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","It could receive as many resources as it wanted from him. All it needed to do was concentrate on absorbing them all.","As a result, the Perfect Touch Wisteria was now very reliant on him.","At that moment, the Perfect Touch Wisteria was dying for Lin Yuan’s response.","Lin Yuan looked into the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s expectant eyes and said with a smile, “You look good. But the most important thing for you to do is to concentrate on absorbing spirit qi. I will provide you with more spirit qi crystals. As for how far you’ll make it, that is all on you!”","Lin Yuan set aside around 2,000 spirit qi crystals before crushing the rest.","He could not use all of the spirit qi crystals on the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","He had to keep some of them for emergencies.","Given that they were to be the gunpowder for Universe’s combat system, it went without saying that there could not be a lack of spirit qi crystals.","A thought entered the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s mind when it sensed the sea of pure spirit qi.","Yuan is much too nice to me!","While the Perfect Touch Wisteria absorbed pure spirit qi and prepared to make a bid for Creation Breed, Lin Yuan sensed a pang of urgency from the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen.","Ever since Lin Yuan instructed Begin Lady to capture the pinnacle 10 Stars Law Staff, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had been yearning to absorb the energy within the Law Staff.","Lin Yuan had been unconscious for 15 days. The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had long felt starved.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had the biggest appetite out of all of Lin Yuan’s feys, source-type lifeforms, and sacred source lifeforms.","After days of being tempted by the Law Staff and being unable to get its hands on it, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was miserable.","Now, not even Immortal bodies appealed to it.","Lin Yuan hurriedly started to soothe the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen, “Once the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s evolution is complete, it’ll be your turn! There’s no need to rush.”","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen muttered, “I’m not really in a rush. It’s just that by increasing my Stars, I’ll be able to absorb World Crystals and Immortal bodies quicker. Previously, I did not dare to try to absorb the Eternal Heart because I was afraid that I would not be done with it even after half a year had passed.","“Once I reach 6 Stars, I can start trying to absorb the Eternal Heart! Master, do you know how powerful the Sword Skills can be once they’ve been boosted by the illusionary Immortal bodies in my storage?”","Lin Yuan could not help but smile crookedly.","That brat was afraid that he was not on the ball and tried to use its abilities to tempt him.","Ever since the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen evolved to 4 Stars, the Queen and Sacred Sword Forms both gained new abilities.","Lin Yuan had not used any of the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s new abilities during his clash against the Freedom Federation envoy group.","This was because there had been no illusionary Immortal bodies in the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s storage at the time, and he would definitely have attracted attention from the Freedom Federation’s royalty if he had used them.","If he still had other means of defeating his enemies, Lin Yuan did not want to raise suspicion about Morbius because he had exposed how special the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was.","If he had used the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s new abilities, he would not have had to use as much effort to defeat Qian Yu or Lu Ou.","“Enough. The Perfect Touch Wisteria’s evolution will be complete in another three hours. At that time, I’ll return to the Spirit Lock spatial zone immediately so you can begin absorbing the Law Staff’s energy.”","While Lin Yuan was speaking with the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen in his mind, the Trial of World Creation had started to form.","Lin Yuan had personally witnessed how helpless Endless Summer had been in the face of the Trial of World Creation.","When it came to plant-type feys, Endless Summer’s talent and foundation were definitely not considered weak.","Even the uncontracted feys in the wild knew to huddle together or seek help from stronger feys in order to overcome the Trial of World Creation.","Lin Yuan once heard the Moon Empress remark that only 1/10 of the Myth III feys in the world could survive the Trial of World Creation.","The number was only this high when human help was taken into consideration.","Since Lin Yuan had gotten a head start in life, he always viewed this world with a survivorship bias.","The real world of spirit qi professionals could absolutely be described as bloody and merciless.","Amongst the 1/10 who were lucky enough to survive the Trial of World Creation, only one out of 10,000 managed the feat on its own.","A fey like that could easily reach Immortal.","Presently, Lin Yuan did not require the Perfect Touch Wisteria to prove itself by overcoming the Trial of World Creation.","This was because the Perfect Touch Wisteria would need some time to recover if it ended up injured.","Furthermore, the Perfect Touch Wisteria was different from regular feys as it only needed pure spirit qi and vitality.","Lin Yuan did not even need to provide it with world crystals and law crystals.","Hence, technically, as long as Lin Yuan was willing to nurture the Perfect Touch Wisteria, he could increase its power to indefinite levels.","With the ability Forbidden Growth, there was no concern of it being blocked by a limit.","Lin Yuan said, “Shadow, go and help the Perfect Touch Wisteria take on the Trial of World Creation so it can absorb the Creation World Ley Lines without worries.”","Shadow made a noise of agreement before transforming into a black shadow attached to the Perfect Touch Wisteria."]},{"number":2185,"title":"Chapter 2185 Tactile Vine Wood World","paragraphs":["2185 Tactile Vine Wood World","With Shadow’s help, everything would go smoothly.","Soon, the Perfect Touch Wisteria evolved from Myth Breed to Creation Breed.","The vine-shaped Law Rune that was overflowing with vitality that had previously been in the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s body transformed into a law world.","The Creation World Ley Line fell into the world of laws next to the Perfect Touch Wisteria. As a result of this, the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s law world slowly became more solid and complete.","Five Creation World Ley Lines entered the world next to the Perfect Touch Wisteria.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria had absorbed all of the pure spirit qi.","While the Perfect Touch Wisteria was increasing its power, the dried Soldier Ration Radishes eventually piled up to three 50-meter-tall mounds.","When the Perfect Touch Wisteria was done absorbing the spirit qi, Lin Yuan used True Data to check on it.","[Fey Name]: Perfect Touch Wisteria","[Fey Species]: Strong armor wisteria species/long wisteria species","[Fey Grade]: Sovereign (2/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Creation V","Abilities:","[Forbidden Growth]: After contracting any lifeform, it can break the limit that comes with the contract. As long as it has sufficient energy, it would be able to continuously increase its power. When it has absorbed the maximum amount of energy, it will be able to comprehend a required Willpower Rune.","Exclusive Skill:","[Swallow Same Source]: Every vine will have the same grade and quality, but they can be separated to act as individual entities. Every vine can consume something and take control of its attributes. The swallowed entity cannot be spat out, but an even higher-level item can replace it. (Once it gains attributes, the vine cannot be separated again.)","[Broken Vine Replacement]: When a vine is destroyed during combat, another vine can be picked to take on the damage instead to save the first vine.","[Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn]: The energy within the vines can be gathered at a certain spot. An illusionary thorn composed of energy will sprout from this spot. The illusionary thorn will be undetectable.","[Tactile Vine Wood World]: All of the wood-type energy and vitality stored within the vines will be released. The wood-type energy and vitality will transform into a large number of vines. The vines will intertwine and form a world of vines. The main body will fuse with this world to attack targets. Before the wooden world is broken, all the damage sustained by the main body will be reduced and shouldered by the wooden world.","Lin Yuan saw that the Perfect Touch Wisteria had gained a new exclusive skill named Tactile Vine Wood World when it evolved to Creation Breed.","Tactile Vine Wood World would cause the Perfect Touch Wisteria to use up all of the wood-type energy in its body to create a world of vines.","Furthermore, the Perfect Touch Wisteria could even fuse itself with the vine world and attack the target as it pleased.","Since it could move as it pleased and attack however it wanted, it would be even more difficult to sense the attacks of Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn.","More importantly, the vine world could reduce the damage the Perfect Touch Wisteria sustained.","If the Perfect Touch Wisteria was sustaining too much damage, the vine world shouldered the damage.","Before the wooden world broke, the Perfect Touch Wisteria would not have to worry about suffering a deadly attack.","Tactile Vine Wood World increased the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s defensive abilities.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria would be Lin Yuan’s strongest soldier. Whether it was attack or defense, the Perfect Touch Wisteria was outstanding.","As he looked at the Perfect Touch Wisteria grinning at him, Lin Yuan thought, If the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s Elite ability Peak Sturdiness did not use up so much spirit qi and vitality, it might even be able to reach Immortal.","However, Lin Yuan cared more about the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s real power rather than its grade.","Thus, Lin Yuan felt that using up all that spirit qi and vitality was worth it.","Lin Yuan looked at the Perfect Touch Wisteria and said, “I’m going to call you Green Vine from now on! You only just transformed into human form and have yet to leave the Spirit Lock spatial zone. Let me introduce you to a few friends and get a taste of human delicacies!”","Lin Yuan remembered how complimentary Endless Summer had been about Liu Jie’s food.","When Endless Summer was in human form, it ate daintily but had just as big of an appetite as the Mother of Bloodbath.","When Green Vine heard what Lin Yuan said, it patted its back and said happily, “Wow, I can finally leave that place! I want to stay with you from now on. Don’t worry. I’ll adapt to the human world very soon.”","Lin Yuan looked at the innocent expression on Green Vine’s elegant face and thought darkly, The human world is very complicated. You better not become infected and start to rot!","It was fine to have a greedy monster like the Mother of Bloodbath.","If Green Vine turned itself into a Christmas tree like Endless Summer had done, Lin Yuan would not be able to keep it by his side at all times, no matter how kind he was.","Not only would Lin Yuan be unable to keep Green Vine by his side, but he would also be unwilling to let it out of the Spirit Lock spatial zone too often.","After all, Lin Yuan could not be too outlandish when he did most of his tasks.","If Green Vine dressed itself to the nines and ended up looking like a Christmas tree, it would immediately attract eyes no matter where it went.","At first, Lin Yuan had more to say to Green Vine. But he heard the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen rushing him, and he knew that it could not wait any longer.","If he made it wait any longer, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen would start to throw a tantrum like an unruly child.","Not many people were in the martial arts hall, and Jin Qianxun had forbidden anyone from entering.","Thus, Lin Yuan decided to return to the Spirit Lock spatial zone from the martial arts hall to increase the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Stars.","Begin Lady gazed at Green Vine for some time.","Green Vine was not a plant-type fey with the Sacred Wood bloodline, but it had absorbed Begin Lady’s bloodline power.","Thus, Begin Lady felt a certain closeness to Green Vine.","“Lin Yuan, Green Vine’s future is boundless! If you need more spirit qi crystals, it will be easy for Green Vine to awaken its birth horoscope and start walking down heaven’s path. Green Vine’s direction involves continuously accumulating energy. This direction can be carried out anywhere!”","In its words, Begin Lady’s feelings for Green Vine leaked out."]},{"number":2186,"title":"Chapter 2186 Bai Qinghuan’s Cruelty!","paragraphs":["2186 Bai Qinghuan’s Cruelty!","Begin Lady had only managed to pass the Heaven’s Trial with Lin Yuan’s help.","But in the hundreds to thousands of years before that, Begin Lady only had itself to rely on.","It had created Little Peach to communicate with the outside world.","If it had met someone as gentle as Lin Yuan from the beginning, its path would not have been as difficult as it had been!","After Begin Lady was done lamenting, it remembered what Lin Yuan had asked it to do.","Its eyes glinted.","“Lin Yuan, two people tried to use special means to spy on the martial arts hall from the outside. I crushed their heads using my spiritual energy.”","Lin Yuan’s eyes narrowed, and he thought, Luckily, I told Begin Lady to keep watch. Otherwise, outsiders would have discovered the existence of Green Vine and the spirit qi crystals.","For there to still be spies even after his warning to Jin Qianxun, there could only be two possibilities.","The first possibility was that Jin Qianxun’s scheming side had gotten the better of him.","There was no way that Jin Qianxun would betray Lin Yuan because of their contract.","But Lin Yuan did not like his subordinates to be overly scheming.","The second possibility was that Jin Qianxun had not taken full control of the imperial court and that those under him were extremely curious about Lin Yuan.","Regardless of the reason, Lin Yuan intended to get an explanation from Jin Qianxun after he was done increasing the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Stars.","This martial arts hall was inside the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court.","After spotting the two crushed heads and putting the pieces together, Jin Qianxun had to be beside himself with anxiousness.","Lin Yuan’s guess was right.","After receiving the report that two imperial guards’ heads had been crushed for some unknown reason, Jin Qianxun jumped up from the throne and erupted with panic.","There were a total of 30 king-class experts and five emperor-class experts standing guard outside the martial arts hall.","The heads that were crushed belonged to two emperor-class experts.","Currently, the Great Lush Federation’s imperial court was lacking in strong defensive power.","Lin Yuan was the only person who could have killed the two emperor-class experts without so much as rustling a leaf.","For him to have attacked, it meant that the two emperor-class experts had tried to spy on what was happening within the martial arts hall.","Jin Qianxun had instructed with emphasis before he left that these people were only to guard the area and not try to peek into what was happening within the martial arts hall.","Jin Qianxun had been trying to strengthen his connection to Lin Yuan.","However, Lin Yuan’s attitude toward him was not overly warm.","Compared to Jin Qianxun, Lin Yuan was more invested in the development of the entire Great Lush Federation.","Jin Qianxun did not know what he would do if Lin Yuan became displeased with him over this matter!","With that thought, a bead of cold sweat dripped down Jin Qianxun’s brow and slid down his chin.","His fear and panic soon morphed into fury.","He slammed his hand down on the table and bellowed at the servant who had reported the situation to him, “Go and investigate! Find out which aristocratic families those two imperial guards came from!","“Just how ignorant and evil do they have to be? How dare they play such dishonest tricks after swearing their loyalties to me? If that’s the case, let me show you how fearsome I can be!”","Jin Qianxun had essentially been cheated by the people who had sworn their loyalties to him.","There was no way he could take such an affront lying down.","Although the leaders of the secret aristocratic families had sworn their loyalties to him under duress, they had been procrastinating severely in all the tasks he had assigned.","That in itself had already displeased Jin Qianxun greatly.","Everything that had happened was like a sparked piece of kindle that set off the flames of Jin Qianxun’s anger.","All of the servants in the imperial court had been chosen from amongst the Jin family’s direct descendants.","Jin Qianxun subscribed to nepotism. After all, it would always be easier to make use of and interact with one’s own family members.","The servant who had reported the situation could be considered Jin Qianxun’s nephew.","This servant had always seen Jin Qianxun as kind and mild-mannered. He had never seen Jin Qianxun get this angry.","This servant immediately realized the severity of the matter and hurriedly said, “Your Majesty, I’ll go and investigate immediately! Once I’m done, I’ll tell the heads of their factions to come and see you!”","Jin Qianxun sniffed angrily.","“Scatter lighted coals all over the imperial court’s steps and make the two of them walk over it! Remember to use Silver Bamboo Charcoal!”","Jin Che sucked in a cold breath.","There were a total of 365 stairs to reach the imperial court.","Even if one was an emperor-class, one would definitely end up seriously injured by the time one got to the main palace unless spirit qi was employed for protection.","Moreover, it would not be regular charcoal that would be scattered on the stairs but the Silver Bamboo Charcoal.","The aristocrats used Silver Bamboo Charcoal to obtain warmth during winter.","Many districts in the Great Lush Federation were close to the sea. The marine cities were not any warmer than the Iron Hammer Federation during winter.","Silver Bamboo Charcoal was the pick of the aristocrats because it did not produce smoke when it burned and could also be burned for a long time. Additionally, it could reach extremely high temperatures.","Even a thearch-class expert would end up with all the flesh below their knees burnt to a wreck by the time they reached the main palace.","When Jin Qianxun saw that the servant did not immediately leave to do what he had commanded, he roared, “Jin Che, do you not want to work anymore?”","Jin Che was instantly startled back to his senses. He hastily apologized and scurried off to do what Jin Qianxun had ordered.","Jin Qianxun was being this strict because he wanted to establish his might as well as express his loyalty to Lin Yuan.","Since he had not done well in the task that Lin Yuan had given him, he needed to put on the right attitude at the very least.","Just as the servant was about to walk out of the main palace, a bright and pleasant female voice said, “Wait. Uncle Jin, if you’re just trying to explain to Lord Lin Yuan, you’re right to do this. But if you want to establish your might, you’re lacking in strength a little.","“Currently, more than 80% of the secret aristocratic families are unwilling to submit to you. Why don’t you have the two family leaders bring everyone in their families besides their servants to the main palace so they can all receive your punishment? Once these two aristocratic families are punished, I’m sure the others will learn their place.”","Bai Qinghuan’s words shocked everyone within the palace.","The servants did not know Bai Qinghuan well, but they knew that Jin Qianxun was very amicable toward her. To a certain extent, she had the power to influence his decisions.","After a few days of interacting with her, Jin Qianxun and Weng Baochuan realized that she had a very good eye for strategy and spoke with feminine slyness that often rendered one speechless.","However, neither of them had expected her to be so cruel in her actions."]},{"number":2187,"title":"Chapter 2187 Change in the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Skirt!","paragraphs":["2187 Change in the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Skirt!","Bai Qinghuan’s heartlessness had exceeded both Weng Baochuan and Jin Qianxun’s expectations.","It would be a struggle for even thearch-class experts to make it up the stairs covered by the Silver Bamboo Charcoal.","Even a thearch-class expert would be reduced to a pile of ashes before he reached the main palace.","However, Weng Baochuan and Jin Qianxun thought about it from a different angle.","It was true that one needed to be made of stone in order to express one’s might.","The best way to secure control of the Great Lush Federation would be to be merciless at times like this.","Jin Qianxun said to Jin Che in a low voice, “Go and send 50 imperial servants to carry this out. Don’t forget that all of them have to come from different aristocratic families.”","Jin Che’s body trembled as he left to carry out Jin Qianxun’s order.","Bai Qinghuan’s smile had not left her face at all. In fact, her smile became broader after she made her suggestion.","Jin Qianxun had not been the only one who was holding back these past few days. Bai Qinghuan had also been stewing in anger.","The Great Lush Federation appeared to be calm, and Jin Qianxun’s claim to the throne was secure.","However, the members of the secret aristocratic families always procrastinated when it came to doing the tasks that Jin Qianxun had given them.","Although Lin Yuan had acknowledged Bai Qinghuan, she still had not made any significant contributions.","But now, her chance was finally here.","...","After Lin Yuan returned to the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Green Vine immediately started to look around the area as though it was a tourist at an attraction.","It did not take long for it to start playing with Universe, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope, Gray, and Chimey.","Green Vine had been growing in the Spirit Lock spatial zone previously and was well-acquainted with Universe, Chimey, Gray, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope, Genius, and Purple Afterglow.","Previously, Chimey and the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope had avoided Green Vine because it was unable to retract its dark gold flames.","Now that Green Vine was in human form, it could retract its aura and would not affect anyone around it.","At that moment, Morbius’ figure appeared next to Lin Yuan.","Besides Lin Yuan, not even Begin Lady could see Morbius.","Lin Yuan was slightly stunned for a moment before he shook his head gently.","“So far, the only healing-type fey I’ve contracted is the Jasmine Lily. When it comes to attack, defense, healing, and control, the one I lack the most is healing. Thus, even if I were to make a choice now, I would still go with the Jasmine Lily and not Green Vine.","“As long as Green Vine’s grade can be raised, it can make up for its lack of abilities by gaining more exclusive skills.","“Previously, I assumed that the stem would start to grow quickly once Green Vine reached Creation Breed. Yet, the stem still looks the same as when Green Vine was Myth Breed. Flowers will only grow from the stem when Green Vine reaches Immortal!”","Morbius nodded in agreement.","Once Green Vine produced flowers, it would truly become the cream of the crop of vine-species feys.","After Begin Lady entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone, it picked up the 10 Stars Law Staff again.","The Law Staff had always been under Begin Lady’s care.","Although the Law Staff was almost no different from dead now that Fifth Page Truth had died, it would not be easy for the 4 Stars Sacred Sword Wielding Queen to absorb the energy within it.","Begin Lady needed to keep the Law Staff fully restrained and puncture a hole at the core of its energy. This would make it convenient for the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen to absorb the energy within it.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen looked exactly like a homeless vagrant who had been starving for seven to eight days.","Meanwhile, Begin Lady was a chef who took its own sweet time.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was already drooling within Lin Yuan’s soul.","He hurriedly summoned it out for fear of his soul ending up drenched in the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s saliva.","After the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen evolved to 4 Stars, its appearance had changed completely.","There were two main reasons for the change.","The first reason was that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had absorbed Shark Awn’s Immortal body.","Shark Awn had been a pinnacle Immortal fey that was both water- and blood-type. Thus, it greatly impacted the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s type.","Previously, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had absorbed more water-type Law and World Crystals. Hence, its main type was water.","There was an immeasurable amount of willpowers, laws, and energy within an Immortal body.","Although the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had not absorbed many blood-type Law and World Crystals, the second-most dominant type in the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s body was blood-type.","There was an ocean on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt. But instead of being blue, it was a stretch of blood instead.","When the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s blood-colored skirt billowed in the wind, the figures of various ferocious sea beasts could be seen within the ocean of blood.","There was a giant whale swimming about in the ocean of blood that occasionally spurted out a pillar of blood from the surface of the ocean. It added a terrifying and wild aura to the ocean of blood.","If one took a closer look at the ocean of blood, one would see the eerie outline of a shark below the whale.","The whale was only about the size of this shark’s fin.","The shark seemed to be releasing unending malice and terror.","There was a light green snow pine on the shore of the ocean. It was as though it had shrunk and was very short after being exposed to water.","A black crow was resting on the bows of the snow pine as it dispersed fear throughout the other lifeforms.","The giant rainbow-colored python had long given up on taking on the black crow and had been chased to the grassland in the distance.","A giant silver turtle that resembled a small mountain was resting on the shore.","This giant silver turtle had no earthly desires and had become a playground for many of the lifeforms.","A giant pegasus in the sky was flapping its wings repeatedly. The image of a warrior goddess could occasionally be seen on the pegasus’ back.","When one took a closer look, one would notice that the warrior goddess’ image changed into 13 different forms.","There was a large bat with nine thorns behind the pegasus.","The bat was hunting the pegasus down.","The nine spikes on its tail created gusts of wind that boosted its speed.","There was a smaller bat with an aura of death and dreams behind the large bat. It stuck close to the large bat as though it was an obedient puppy.","A yellow land dragon was slamming its tail on the ground. It had the opposite temperament to the giant turtle. No lifeforms dared to get close to the violent dragon.","It could be said that from all angles, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt appeared to be a detailed and intricate painting of mystery."]},{"number":2188,"title":"Chapter 2188 The Queen’s Treasure Vault and the Sacred Sword’s Hilt","paragraphs":["2188 The Queen’s Treasure Vault and the Sacred Sword’s Hilt","Besides the changes to the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt, a glass display case also appeared behind the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s body.","The display case was crafted to perfection.","The same patterns on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt appeared on the display case.","A figurine lined up on the display case seemed to be in an illusionary state.","The figurine did not have a human form. Rather, it had the form of an Immortal fey that had activated its Immortal bodies.","Lin Yuan knew that the only figurine in the display case came from Shark Awn’s Immortal body after the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen absorbed it.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen spent most of its time consuming Shark Awn’s Immortal body.","During the time that Lin Yuan was unconscious, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was finally done with absorbing Shark Awn’s Immortal body.","Lin Yuan took a look at the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s True Data.","[Sacred Source Name]: Sacred Sword Wielding Queen","[Sacred Source Species]: Source genus/Sacred Source species","[Sacred Source Star Grade]: 6 Stars","[Sacred Source Type]: Water (Main)/Mixed","Abilities:","[Queen Form]:","1. Queen’s Skirt Hem: Able to absorb the Willpower Runes from the bodies of dead feys or source-type items. The Willpower Runes or Law Runes from Myth Breed feys’ Law Crystals will be carved on the queen’s skirt. The Law Crystals which have their laws absorbed will become Law Crystals that possess pure law power.","2. Queen’s Treasure Vault: The energy core of lifeforms, such as Immortal bodies and Eternal Hearts, will become the energy will be stored in the queen’s treasure vault. The treasure vault will distill the energy within the energy cores into illusionary Immortal bodies that contain the fey’s abilities when it was still alive and unclean materials. The illusionary Immortal bodies can become sword spirits that can be applied to Sword Skills.","Illusionary Immortal Body (Emperor Spike Demon Shark): An illusionary body of both blood- and water-type. It is affiliated with blood- and water-type Sword Skills. When it is applied to a Sword Skill as a sword spirit, ‘inverse blood’ effects will be produced.","[Sacred Sword Form]:","1. Blade of Sacred Sword: When the spirit qi in the body is depleted, the blade will pierce the skirt hem to unleash all the laws and willpower stored within.","Sword Skill (Dark Death World): Night Crow Wither Attack.","Sword Skill (Vast Water World): Attack of the Sea Leaping Whale.","...","2. Sacred Sword’s Hilt: When the sword hilt is knocked against the crown, spirit qi can be used up to choose a Sword Skill. The other Sword Skills, willpowers, and laws can be sacrificed to fuse with the chosen Sword Skill. After the fusion, the sacrificed Sword Skills, willpowers, and laws, will be gone.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had transformed from the child stage to the adolescent stage.","The Grace Queen had gained the ability called Queen’s Treasure Vault.","Apparently, the illusionary Immortal Bodies were the collectibles that were to be stored within the Queen’s Treasure Vault.","The ability to clean the Immortal bodies was similar to that of purifying the Law and World Crystals.","They could be given to Immortal Breed feys to help them break through their power.","The Queen’s Treasure Vault allowed Lin Yuan to understand the fundamentals of the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Queen Form.","The Grace Queen was a production-type sacred source lifeform, and its abilities had been perfectly preserved.","Before the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had evolved from 3 Stars to 4 Stars, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen could not absorb Law Crystals, World Crystals, Law Source Crystals, and World Source Crystals while it was absorbing an Immortal body.","But, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen could use more than just its skirt to absorb the Immortal bodies and Eternal Hearts.","The Queen’s Treasure Vault and Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt were both unique entities. Both of them could commence absorption simultaneously.","This had fundamentally increased the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s production quantity.","Furthermore, the illusionary Immortal bodies could turn into sword spirits that boosted Sword Skills.","In order to use the illusionary Immortal bodies to boost Sword Skills, they both had to share the same type. Otherwise, there could be negative impacts instead.","The illusionary Immortal bodies were the energy cores of Immortal feys.","When Lin Yuan activated or boosted the Sword Skills, he could even pose a threat to Creation Breed feys.","This was enough to push Lin Yuan up and out of the league of the younger generation. He was now at a level that the younger generation could only aspire to reach.","However, using an illusionary Immortal body came with a price as well. Each time Lin Yuan used one, he would have to use up all of the energy within it.","It would take the illusionary Immortal body at least three months to recover.","In the past, Lin Yuan would have been disappointed if he saw this ability that needed such a long recovery time after every use.","After all, Lin Yuan had gained multiple Immortal bodies on this trip to the Startling Lines Continent. He had even gained a few of the Eternal Hearts.","Lin Yuan intended to store all of the Immortal bodies and Eternal Hearts in the Queen’s Treasure Vault, where the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen could slowly absorb them.","Once a sizable number of the illusionary Immortal bodies and Eternal Heart figurines had been accumulated, it would be easier for Lin Yuan to use the sword spirits to boost the Sword Skills. There was less that he would have to worry about.","Many of Lin Yuan’s friends in his previous life had the hobby of collecting figurines.","Lin Yuan had envied those friends.","But now, he had a display case for his own collectibles.","However, it was not plastic models that would be lined up in the display case but items that came from the energy cores of top lifeforms.","Lin Yuan was very satisfied with the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Queen’s Form’s ability.","However, the Sword Form’s ability caused Lin Yuan to grimace.","After the ability Blade of Sacred Sword, another skill named Sacred Sword’s Hilt had appeared.","The ability Sacred Sword’s Hilt would allow Lin Yuan to pick a Sword Skill and sacrifice other Sword Skills, willpowers, and laws in order to boost the chosen Sword Skill.","This would essentially combine two or more Sword Skills.","The sword spirits could also boost the combined Sword Skills.","This further raised Lin Yuan’s combat capabilities.","However, the price of this combat technique was much too heavy.","The Sword Skills, willpowers, and laws would all become the currency that was paid in order to activate the ability.","Lin Yuan had never imagined that such an overpowering ability could exist in this world.","The ability was now the final safety net that Lin Yuan put in place for himself. There was no way he would make use of t unless he was in real danger of dying.","If he truly ended up on the precipice of death, any cost would be worth it in order to save his life.","Every Sword Skill had its own unique ability.","After many Sword Skills were combined, a stacked effect would be produced.","The choice of World Crystals and Immortal bodies that Lin Yuan had the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen absorb was random.","But from now on, he was going to change this."]},{"number":2189,"title":"Chapter 2189 The 6 Stars Sacred Sword Wielding Queen","paragraphs":["2189 The 6 Stars Sacred Sword Wielding Queen","Even if Lin Yuan did not use the Sword Form’s second skill Sacred Sword’s Hilt, he needed to consider matching the Sword Skills with the sword spirits.","For example, Lin Yuan had obtained Shark Awn’s illusionary Immortal body.","Shark Awn’s illusionary Immortal body was both water- and blood-type.","When Lin Yuan combined water- and blood-type laws, the sword spirit from Shark Awn’s illusionary Immortal body would definitely be able to make a big splash.","From now on, Lin Yuan intended to properly match the Sword Skills with illusionary Immortal bodies to prepare for any situation that called for them.","Lin Yuan had just finished checking on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s data and was lamenting how difficult it was to raise when Begin Lady said in a stern voice, “I have already used the power of the spirit fire to completely shackle the Law Staff.","“The Law Staff is currently struggling with all its might. The shackles will only be able to last 15 minutes at the most. After that, the already weak Law Staff will be burned to death by the spirit fire. Try your best to have your sacred source lifeform absorb the Law Staff’s source power before that happens!”","Begin Lady pointed at the upper part of the staff that was half-skeletonized. The center of the bone shattered.","The 10 Stars Law Staff immediately started to retaliate violently against the attack.","However, all of its struggles were futile.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had been craving the Law Staff for a long time.","Since Begin Lady was guaranteeing its safety and that it only had 15 minutes to absorb the Law Staff’s energy, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen bent over and attached its mouth over the center of the Law Staff before it started to drink with delight.","When Lin Yuan saw what the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen did, the word ‘zombie’ popped into his head.","As happy as the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was, the Law Staff was in ruins.","Lin Yuan could clearly sense that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s aura was slowly becoming stronger.","A short five minutes later, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen evolved from 4 Stars to 5 Stars.","God knew how much effort Lin Yuan had put into nurturing the 4 Stars sacred source lifeform.","The past few months of selfless contributions did not help the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen as much as sucking the Law Staff’s energy for five minutes did.","But this was just the beginning.","The 5 Stars Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s aura started to climb again.","Seven minutes later, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen skyrocketed to 6 Stars.","Lin Yuan clenched his fist tightly.","If the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had not absorbed all of the Law Staff’s energy, it would be lucky to reach 5 Stars or even 6 Stars by the time the Major Federation Meeting rolled around.","But now, Lin Yuan only needed to put in a little more effort, and the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen would definitely be able to reach 7 Stars within the next two years and gain a new ability as well.","This would allow Lin Yuan to have more secret weapons at hand at the Major Federation Meeting.","Although there were still three minutes left before the Law Staff was killed by the spirit fire, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was done draining all of the Law Staff’s vitality after only another minute.","As such, the Law Staff was reduced to a dead body.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had a dissatisfied expression as it put down the Law Staff’s body and said happily, “Master, I can now gobble down treats much quicker than in the past!”","While the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen spoke, it did some careful calculations. A moment later, it reached out its hand and held up four fingers to Lin Yuan, saying, “I’m at least 40% faster now!”","Lin Yuan thought, It looks like the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen is able to absorb Law Crystals, World Crystals, Law Source Crystals, World Source Crystals, Immortal bodies, Eternal Hearts, and the like 20% faster each time it gains a Star.","This speed had clearly exceeded Lin Yuan’s expectations.","He was more than satisfied.","Now that Lin Yuan was done evolving the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen, he did some thinking.","He took out Eternal Aurora Broken Night Fox’s Eternal Heart that he had obtained from killing the Truth Association’s envoy.","The Aurora Broken Night Fox was one of the rare healing-type Eternal Breed feys that had both light- and dark-type.","After the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen absorbed the Sacred Cure White Deer’s World Crystal, it gained the Sword Skill Attack of the Forest Turned Deer that was both light- and wood-type.","Although the light-type was much weaker than the wood-type, it could be boosted by the sword spirit from the Aurora Broken Night Fox’s Eternal Heart.","Lin Yuan had unlocked the Jasmine Lily’s abilities but was still comparatively weak when it came to healing.","Presently, Lin Yuan wanted to gain a secret weapon that could boost healing abilities.","When Begin Lady saw the Aurora Broken Night Fox’s Eternal Heart, it said, “Lin Yuan, do you remember the Blood Claw Charging Wolf that I took control of? You wanted the Blood Claw Charging Wolf to become the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s puppet.","“I think that it would be a better choice to extract the Blood Claw Charging Wolf’s Immortal body. The Blood Claw Charging Wolf is one of the rare feys with four types. Dark, blood, gold, and wind are all types with extremely strong combat connotations. It is much more precious than the Immortal bodies of other feys.”","Begin Lady was not a Creation Master but had set its spirit fire alight. Thus, it could still sense the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s abilities to a certain extent.","Since Lin Yuan had brought Begin Lady into the Spirit Lock spatial zone, it meant that he had no intention of hiding anything from it apart from Morbius.","Begin Lady’s words caused Lin Yuan’s eyes to light up.","It was true that the Blood Claw Charging Wolf was an outstanding choice.","Firstly, the Blood Claw Charging Wolf was Sovereign X/Immortal VIII. At this level, its Immortal body could provide almost as much of a boost as an Immortal IX fey.","Moreover, out of the Sword Skills that Lin Yuan currently had, there were three that could match up with the Blood Claw Charging Wolf’s types.","Thus, Lin Yuan would have many choices of Sword Skills to pick from to use the Blood Claw Charging Wolf’s sword spirit on.","The more Sword Skills were combined, the stronger the effect would be.","Previously, when Lin Yuan instructed the source-type power to evolve the law power, there was even the chance to transform the law power into law worlds.","Lin Yuan was not going to do this in the future because it would not be difficult to obtain World Crystals.","There was no need for Lin Yuan to use up the source-type power.","But now, Lin Yuan could use source-type power to further evolve the level of the Blood Claw Charging Wolf’s Immortal body.","Since he meant for it to be his secret weapon, he could accept spending a little more.","Lin Yuan said, “Begin Lady, you mentioned that the Blood Claw Charging Wolf was feral and that it has been making so much noise in its prison of water that you haven’t been able to rest properly. Why don’t we put an end to its misery now?”"]},{"number":2190,"title":"Chapter 2190 Here to Apologize!","paragraphs":["2190 Here to Apologize!","After Lin Yuan placed the Blood Claw Charging Wolf’s Immortal body inside the Queen’s Treasure Vault, he had reached a checkpoint with the evolving of his feys’ powers.","Lin Yuan’s power had already transformed completely in the short span of a few tens of minutes.","Begin Lady picked up the Law Staff’s body with the intention of turning it into a precious instrument once Purple Love brought over the spiritual ingredients.","Lin Yuan returned to the martial arts hall on his own.","After leaving the Spirit Lock spatial zone, he was surrounded by green vines.","The Perfect Touch Wisteria liked the name Green Vine.","When it was in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, it had mentioned its name to Chimey, Gray, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope, and Universe more than once.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope had not thought much of it, but Universe had been floored and insisted that Lin Yuan name it as well.","After ruminating for a moment, Lin Yuan decided to give another name to Universe, ‘Sky Sea’.","Universe was born to live in both the sky and sea.","In his previous life, Lin Yuan heard the legend of the Kraken, which was unimaginably gigantic.","Lin Yuan hoped that when Universe took to the sky and started to increase its power, a rumor in the main world would spread about how astonishingly colossal it was.","Even when Green Vine was not speaking, its aura was concentrated to the point that it was almost tangible.","Lin Yuan prepared to take Green Vine out of the martial arts hall.","Meanwhile, Jin Qianxun was waiting by the martial arts hall door alongside two men whose calves were burnt to smithereens.","These two men were dressed lavishly but were in such a story state. They were curled up on the ground but dared not even let out a whimper of pain.","Bai Qinghuan and Weng Baochuan were standing next to Jin Qianxun. Both of them had witnessed what had happened.","They were looking at the two men who were prone on the ground with scorn.","Weng Baochuan felt that given the wrecked state of these two direct descendants, it would be better for them to take their own lives rather than continue suffering humiliation at the hands of Jin Qianxun.","Although Bai Qinghuan and Weng Baochuan were both looking at the two men with derision, completely different thoughts were running through their minds.","As Bai Qinghuan gazed at the two pathetic family leaders, all she could think about was how stupid and blind they were.","They were incapable of even keeping their own family members in order.","The matter had been handled by 50 imperial guards who came from various secret aristocratic families.","It was likely that the news had already spread amongst the secret aristocratic families.","It was unlikely that there would be no more instances of ignorant and blatant disobedience of Jin Qianxun’s orders.","This meant that the construction of the harbor could be sped up.","Bai Qinghuan beamed internally when she thought about how her suggestion had been of help to Lin Yuan.","She had been raised in Sacred Forest City by the Bai family to be the wife of the Bai family’s Young Leader.","She had seen way too many families being destroyed over a slip of the tongue.","Although the occurrence was uncommon, she had seen her fair share.","Thus, Bai Qinghuan did not find the actions to be cruel at all.","Rather, if the Great Lush Federation could seize this chance to speed up its operations, it would be beneficial for all the citizens of the Great Lush Federation.","Sometimes, progress could be made by eliminating some of the bad seeds. There was no question that this trade was worth it.","If Jin Qianxun was not trying to prove to Lin Yuan that the spying in the martial arts hall had nothing to do with him, he would have kicked the two men on the ground to death.","Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan were the leaders of the secret aristocratic families, the Fang family and Du family, respectively.","Although these two families did not have as high of a position as the Jin family, they were still considered above average.","The previous leaders of the Fang family and Du family had been Fang Weijie’s father and Du Yaoshan’s oldest brother. Both of them had been well aware of their duties.","But when the yoke was handed over to Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan, both families started on a downward trajectory.","Jin Qianxun had noticed the hatred in Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan’s eyes long ago.","But every time he caught their glares, his heart twitched.","He did not know what he was going to say to Lin Yuan.","He had been dragged down by these two fools on the ground.","If Lin Yuan did not want to hear what he had to say and continued to be upset with him, Jin Qianxun did not know what he would do.","While Jin Qianxun was shaking with terror, the doors of the martial arts hall opened, and Lin Yuan strode out.","Green Vine swaggered behind Lin Yuan.","Although its appearance and voice did not match its personality at all, it was still timid in front of unfamiliar people.","Thus, there was no way it would make the first move to speak to someone it did not know.","Green Vine stared curiously at Jin Qianxun, Bai Qinghuan, Weng Baochuan, and the two men on the ground.","It did not have much experience and had only just changed into human form. Thus, every person and thing attracted Green Vine’s interest.","Jin Qianxun immediately walked up to Lin Yuan. He first bowed to Lin Yuan before he bowed to Green Vine.","Jin Qianxun had never seen Green Vine, but he knew that he needed to try and gain favor with everyone who managed to appear by Lin Yuan’s side.","Given Green Vine’s appearance, Jin Qianxun could easily tell that it was a fey in human form rather than a true human.","Jin Qianxun had an idea of how old Lin Yuan was. Thus, he never bothered to think that the women next to Lin Yuan could be his feys.","“Lord, there were two imperial guards who took it upon themselves to investigate what was happening within the martial arts hall. They came from the Fan family and Du family. These two are the heads of those two families. I have brought them here to apologize to you!”","From the moment that Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan saw Lin Yuan, their bodies started to quiver uncontrollably.","Both of them had seen Lin Yuan before.","It was Lin Yuan who had placed Jin Qianxun on the throne of the Great Lush Federation and used shocking methods to kill all those who dared to oppose and force the leaders of the secret aristocratic families to swear their loyalty to Jin Qianxun.","Previously, Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan had some grudges against Jin Qianxun.","Although they knew that the imperial guards from their families had erred, they saw it as Jin Qianxun putting them in a spot because of their past grudges.","But now, it seemed that this was not the case. It turned out that the imperial guards who came from their families had offended this Lord!","Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan would never dare to make a move on Lin Yuan.","Given their statuses as the leaders of aristocratic families, it went without saying that power was an invincible force that no one could deny.","At that moment, Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan understood that it was not Jin Qianxun who wanted to make things difficult for them but that they had been ruined by those two imperial guards they had personally chosen.","Jin Qianxun hated Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan as much as Du Yaoshan and Fang Weijie currently resented those two dead imperial guards."]},{"number":2191,"title":"Chapter 2191 To Make Amends!","paragraphs":["2191 To Make Amends!","Lin Yuan looked deeply into Jin Qianxun’s eyes.","Jin Qianxun’s demeanor and expression told him that Jin Qianxun was indeed uninvolved with the matter.","If unsavory ideas had entered his mind, Bai Qinghuan would have informed Lin Yuan long ago.","“Oh? You said that they’re here to apologize to me. What is the error that they need to apologize for?”","Jin Qianxun hurriedly explained the entire situation to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan was silently shocked. He had not expected Bai Qinghuan to come up with such a callous idea.","Jin Qianxun had even managed to carry out such a callous idea.","This event showed that Jin Qianxun and Bai Qinghuan could cooperate with each other.","He had arrived at the martial arts hall suddenly, and not even Jin Qianxun was aware of it. Thus, it went without saying that the aristocratic families’ leaders were also unaware.","This meant that the two imperial guards had acted on their own accord.","The leader of the Du family and Fang family were innocent parties who had been dragged into this.","With this, Jin Qianxun had established the necessary might and formidable authority.","Currently, the Great Lush Federation was lacking in top combat power.","Lin Yuan felt that it would be better to let Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan live.","If the Fang family and Du family’s members were all reduced to ashes, the two of them would no longer be able to continue as the leaders of the Du family and Fang family.","Lin Yuan decided that he would have them make up for the two empty imperial guard spots.","There were times when it would be better to keep the sinners alive rather than kill them in order to make an example out of them.","With every additional day that Du Yaoshan and Fang Weijie lived, the other secret aristocratic families would continue to remember what Jin Qianxun had done.","Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan had sworn their loyalty to Jin Qianxun. Hence, no matter how much they hated him, they could only swallow their loathing.","When Lin Yuan did not respond, Jin Qianxun immediately started to panic as he assumed that Lin Yuan was begrudging him.","This caused the hatred that Jin Qianxun felt for Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan to reach a peak.","“Lord, why don’t you kill the two of them now? Since the imperial guards who committed the crime came from their families, they have to be involved!”","Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan were begging for mercy from Lin Yuan now because this was their only chance to save their lives and because they knew that Jin Qianxun would not use the contract to torture them while Lin Yuan was here.","Ever since they overcame the Silver Bamboo Charcoal on the 365 stairs to arrive at the main palace, Jin Qianxun had already used the contract to torture them countless times.","As such, both of them detested Jin Qianxun.","They could never forgive him for exterminating their families.","However, both of their lives were in Jin Qianxun’s hands, so they would never have the chance to get their revenge.","It would be better for them to continue living rather than die like this.","They were in the prime of their lives and could have more progeny. But if they died, their bloodline would die with them. The Fang family and Du family would end with them.","When he heard Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan say that they were wronged, Jin Qianxun’s jaw clenched tightly.","If they were wronged, what about him?","At that moment, Jin Qianxun, Fang Weijie, and Du Yaoshan heard Lin Yuan say calmly, “Since you know that the imperial guards who came from your families have made a mistake, I’ll give you the chance to make amends! Go and fill up the two empty imperial guard spots tomorrow morning.”","After Lin Yuan spoke, Jin Qianxun dared not add anything after.","It was clear that Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan were elated.","Both of them had made their pleas as a final desperate attempt. Neither of them thought that it would truly work.","But how were they going to become imperial guards in their current state? If they became wheelchair-bound imperial guards, they would never be able to keep up.","Jin Qianxun would then use the excuse to get rid of them.","Despite being lost in their thoughts, neither of them forgot to thank Lin Yuan profusely.","Bai Qinghuan grinned in amazement to herself.","Lin Yuan’s action had not only preserved the Great Lush Federation’s top combat power but had also left Jin Qianxun’s authority intact.","Bai Qinghuan had not thought of that method.","The way that Weng Baochuan looked at Lin Yuan had clearly changed.","In Weng Baochuan’s heart, Lin Yuan was a faction leader who had managed to kill Fifth Page Truth. He was someone incomprehensible and all-powerful.","Yet, it turned out that Lin Yuan also had a merciful side of him.","This trait only elevated Lin Yuan’s character.","Because of his action, Weng Baochuan felt that he would be able to grow.","At that moment, Weng Baochuan understood why his grandfather had told him to stay by Lin Yuan’s side to train.","Now that Lin Yuan was done with what he needed to do, he wanted to head to the Iron Hammer Federation to take a look at the Snow Celestial Mountain.","Lin Yuan had already explored all the contents of the Annal of Monster Information that he had access to.","For the Snow Celestial Mountain to be written in the book, there had to be something extraordinary about it.","Lin Yuan raised his hand, and two green beams of light landed on Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan.","Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan, who were in agony, suddenly felt all of their pain disappear. This was followed by a numb feeling in their legs.","From their angle, they could not see the changes that were happening to them, but Jin Qianxun, Bai Qinghuan, and Weng Baochuan watched as new bones, muscles, and skin grew on Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan’s decimated legs.","Jin Qianxun’s oldest brother, Jin Qianding, had been a healing-type spirit qi professional.","People from other secret aristocratic families always came to seek treatment from Jin Qianding.","However, Jin Qianding had never been able to regrow bones and flesh like Lin Yuan was able to do.","Lin Yuan’s actions had exceeded the comprehension of Jin Qianxun, Bai Qinghuan, and the rest.","Lin Yuan ignored their reactions.","After treating Fang Weijie and Du Yaoshan, he left and returned to his room.","He intended to send word to Liu Jie and Su Yiren and leave for the Iron Hammer Federation in two days.","Within another two days, Lin Yuan would be able to settle all the matters in the Great Lush Federation.","Now, the Divine Wood Federation, Iron Hammer Federation, and Great Lush Federation were all at peace, and the biggest issues related to their development had all been resolved. It would only be a matter of time before the three federations started thriving."]},{"number":2192,"title":"Chapter 2192 Improvement of the Astronomical Parliament’s Members!","paragraphs":["2192 Improvement of the Astronomical Parliament’s Members!","With Lin Yuan continuously supplying plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline, this timeline could be shortened with no limit.","Two years later, with two Class 5 Creation Masters, the Startling Lines Continent or maybe even each federation would be able to send five envoys each to participate in the Major Federation Meeting.","With the plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline and Class 5 Creation Master resources, all of this was possible.","Liu Jie and Su Yiren had been accompanying Lin Yuan all this time.","Liu Jie was Lin Yuan’s retainer knight and was in charge of his safety.","Su Yiren had been in charge of contacting Jin Qianxun and relaying all information about the Great Lush Federation’s development to Lin Yuan.","Su Yiren and Luo Lan were on good terms. Their similar past experiences led Su Yiren to see herself in Luo Lan.","Moreover, Su Yiren had helped Luo Lan significantly.","Thus, the two of them were already as close as sisters.","Luo Lan had been bred to be the First Princess. As such, her capabilities were definitely nothing to scoff at.","But there were a million things to do in the Iron Hammer Federation, and Luo Lan could not handle all of them on her own.","Luo Lan rose early and slept late. In fact, she slept less than three hours each day.","As a result, she had lost a significant amount of hair.","Nonetheless, Luo Lan was not worried about her physical appearance being affected by her loss of hair. Even if she went bald, she could still put on a wig that the crown could sit on.","Luo Lan was more worried about not being able to finish all that needed to be done, even after losing so much sleep.","As the ruler of the Iron Hammer Federation, Luo Lan could now show a hint of weakness.","As a result, Luo Lan covered herself with a hard exterior in order to hide her vulnerability.","She only poured out all her troubles in front of Su Yiren.","Su Yiren had offered more than once to help Luo Lan.","Su Yiren wanted to help out Luo Lan once she arrived at the Iron Hammer Federation with Lin Yuan.","This was because of her kinship with Luo Lan and because she hoped Lin Yuan would help Luo Lan while helping her to recover the Seven States of Darkness.","For the Iron Hammer Federation to prosper and rebuild the Seven States of Darkness, a large amount of metal spiritual ingredients was necessary.","Su Yiren knew that by the time she started to recover the Seven States of Darkness, the construction of the harbor in the Great Lush Federation would be completed, and the 20 Island Whales would have conducted numerous trades.","Because of Lin Yuan, the Startling Lines Continent’s three federations could be seen as one entity.","At that time, she could obtain the metal spiritual ingredients from Luo Lan through the 20 Island Whales.","Su Yiren felt that she still had some sway when it came to Jin Qianxun.","Jin Qianxun arranged for the Island Whales to do long-distance sea trades in order to obtain more finances.","The Dark Continent was rich in unique products, especially dark- and poison-type feys.","Dark- and poison-type feys could usually fetch higher prices.","Jin Qianxun would not be at a disadvantage if he helped her.","Thus, when she heard that Lin Yuan was preparing to head to the Iron Hammer Federation two days later, Su Yiren was overjoyed","In the 15 days that Lin Yuan had been in a coma, the scheduled Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meetings had not taken place.","Thankfully, with the Thoughts Letter Paper, the other members of the Astronomical Parliament did not have to drive themselves insane with curiosity and anxiousness.","With the two days that he had, Lin Yuan went into the marsh world and fetched Wen Yu out so they could hold the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting.","During this meeting, Lin Yuan realized that every member had grown substantially.","Bei Xu’s faction now had over 200 members. After countless brushes with death, every member had been honed into an elite. Many of them had formed contracts with source-type items that they found in dimensional rifts on expeditions led by Bei Xu.","Bei Xu had encountered a large human camp of more than 5,000 people.","A corrupt faction was controlling them.","Besides a few people who were free agents, most of them were just tools that the faction was taking advantage of to make money.","Bei Xu had managed to use his powers to kill the corrupt oppressors and saved the people in the camp who had cursed imprints on them.","Next, he took control of the camp.","From this, he caught a whiff of a lead and slowly gained an understanding of what the Grotto Continent truly was.","Lin Yuan felt that Bei Xu had a quality and significant improvement.","Yin Lin had been focused on evolving the king sea demon who she had contracted, as well as strengthening her bond with her feys through using various spiritual ingredients and refining her beast patterns.","While she was increasing her power, she used the large amount of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls that she obtained from Lin Yuan to build up her faction.","The rare coral-species feys that Yin Lin nurtured in her territory were already sold throughout the capital of the Azure Federation, Azure Water City. She was still continuing to expand the reach of her business to the other large cities.","Yin Lin used her status, background, and the riches she had accumulated to increase the power of a batch of her chosen subordinates.","On Bu Po’s end, nothing much had changed. However, his attitude had changed completely.","All of his fright and terror had been tamped down.","He was able to become one of the Spirit Mother’s reserve disciples because of his talent.","The more he made his talent shine, the better it would be for him.","Bu Po did all he could to demonstrate his Class 3 Creation Master talent and made sure his actions were as high-profile as possible.","He had received hate from many other of the Spirit Mother’s reserve disciples.","Additionally, he had also gained the opportunity to be taught by the Spirit Mother daily, albeit from behind a curtain. Previously, he only received such lessons on the weekends.","There were three people, including Bu Po who received such treatment.","Bu Po slowly started to focus his attention on these two other people.","The special treatment from the Spirit Mother was a signal to Bu Po that he had distinguished himself from the other reserve disciples and that these two people were his true rivals.","In reality, Su Yiren, Ta Lei, and Luo Lan had all seen Lin Yuan. Lin Yuan had witnessed all of their growth personally.","Wo Lun communicated with Lin Yuan often because of the Great Lush Federation’s construction of the harbor.","Recently, Wo Lun had been trying to recruit people to join him.","He even sold some collectibles that he knew were beloved by the elite and used the money to try and attract more help. This was in spite of his own adoration for those collectibles.","Recently, Wo Lun had been wanting to go on a long sea journey. His destination would be the Great Lush Federation’s harbor!"]},{"number":2193,"title":"Chapter 2193 Truth Above Power!","paragraphs":["2193 Truth Above Power!","Wo Lun came to this decision after a discussion with Lin Yuan.","As a sailor who liked to go on adventures, Wo Lun did not like to stay in one place. He could only find happiness and bliss when he was out exploring.","The adrenaline that coursed through his veins when he was one instant away from dying made him feel even more alive than in any underground bar.","Wo Lun yearned to go on a cross-ocean adventure.","Lin Yuan needed to build up confidence for Jin Qianxun and the entire Great Lush Federation.","Lin Yuan could sense from his conversation with Jin Qianxun that Jin Qianxun was delighted by his offering of the 20 Island Whales.","But he did not have much confidence when it came to cross-ocean trading.","Lin Yuan found this understandable. After all, the entire Great Lush Federation did not have much experience with cross-ocean trading.","Thus, Lin Yuan decided to find a batch of people with experience to help them.","The entire Great Lush Federation would see from Wo Lun and his trading how much money there was to be made in cross-ocean trading.","Lin Yuan also had to bear costs when he invested in the Great Lush Federation.","He requested that Jin Qianxun produce two baby Island Whales every year.","In ten years, the Great Lush Federation’s fleet of Island Whales would grow to 40 strong.","Jin Qianxun dared not oppose Lin Yuan’s request. All he could do was grit his teeth and agree.","Lin Yuan could sense that Jin Qianxun had been strained to agree.","After he put an end to the Great Lush Federation’s chamber of commerce role, it would be easy to free up the Great Lush Federation’s resources to nurture the Island Whales.","Without Class 5 Creation Masters, it would take almost 1/5 of the imperial court’s revenue to nurture two Island Whales and breed two baby Island Whales.","Jin Qianxun would never be naive enough to believe that he had the authority to order Elder Weng around.","Lin Yuan never liked to force others.","Jin Qianxun would understand once he saw the appeal of cross-ocean trading.","It would be difficult to hatch five baby Island Whales each year, much less two.","Lin Yuan truly believed that the Great Lush Federation would be able to obtain more than enough resources from cross-ocean trading.","It was likely that Jin Qianxun would be willing to take out more money to breed even more Island Whales.","When Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, and Wen Yu were included, there were a total of 11 members of the Astronomical Parliament.","Out of all of them, the one who had changed the most in the shortest amount of time was Peace.","Peace had settled into Green Continent City and was living the life of a celestial being.","The Tide Rain Mantis allowed Green Continent City to achieve freedom of rain.","The Tide Rain Mantis’ ability came from itself and used a very small amount of spiritual power.","Ever since Peace started living in Green Continent City’s City Lord’s residence, there was constant light rain in a one-kilometer radius around the City Lord’s residence.","In a place like the Broiling Rock Continent, where finding even a mouthful of water during the drought season was a bona fide miracle, everyone in Green Continent City now had deep respect for Peace.","This was because power was not the truth in the Broiling Rock Continent—water was!","After Lin Yuan learned about the Broiling Rock Continent and Green Continent City’s situations from Peace, he came up with a custom nurturing plan for her.","The Broiling Rock Continent was full of peril. It was especially dangerous during the drought and monsoon seasons.","Thus, Peace was not suited to travel too far and take the risk of setting up her own private faction to increase her power.","It would be a better choice to develop Green Continent City from within Green Continent City.","Peace had already gained stable footing in Green Continent City.","But if she wanted to gain more faith and respect, she needed to strengthen her ability to create water.","There was someone next to Peace named Pang Luo, and he was the City Lord of Green Continent City.","Pang Luo was very friendly and enthusiastic. He was focused on developing Green Continent City and turning it into a megacity.","But no matter how big Pang Luo’s dreams were, a megacity would need even more water in order to sustain it.","Given Peace’s current ability, she could not achieve it.","Thus, Lin Yuan’s direction for Peace would be to help her produce as much water as possible.","There were many feys that could produce water. However, very few of them were insect-species feys which Peace was affiliated with.","The last time Lin Yuan returned to the Radiance Federation and met the Moon Empress, he sent Master Hong Shen to represent him on a visit to the Cage of Brahma Insects.","The Cage of Brahma Insects’ specialty was nurturing insect-species feys. It could be said that no place nurtured more insect-species feys than the Cage of Brahma Insects.","Moreover, in large-scale production of insect-species feys, there was a high chance of producing mutated feys.","There were many mutation variations. All of them were stronger than the original in some way.","If Master Hong Shen personally visited the Cage of Brahma Insects, he would definitely receive decent treatment. After all, he was a quality Class 4 Creation Master.","However, there was no way that Master Hong Shen would get to meet the Cage of Brahma Insects’ main members.","In a top faction like the Cage of Brahma Insects, Class 4 Creation Masters did not have much of a presence unless they wanted to join.","However, Master Hong Shen represented Lin Yuan in his visit to the Cage of Brahma Insects.","The leaders of the Cage of Brahma Insects, Fan Jianyi and Fan Hansheng, and the other direct descendants and main members of the Cage of Brahma Insects all turned up to greet Master Hong Shen warmly.","The Return from Faraway Mansion and the Cage of Brahma Insects had been working together for some time.","In the past, Lin Yuan had sought a fair amount of help from the Cage of Brahma Insects.","The Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls allowed the Cage of Brahma Insects’ production to fundamentally increase.","If not for Lin Yuan, the Cage of Brahma Insects would never have received help and support from the Moon Empress.","Everyone in the Cage of Brahma Insects was exceptionally grateful to Lin Yuan.","After learning of Lin Yuan’s request from Master Hong Shen, the Cage of Brahma Insects picked their best and did not hold anything back.","They provided Lin Yuan with two insect-species feys skilled at producing water.","Master Hong Shen gave the two feys to Lin Yuan when he returned.","Both of these feys were extremely rare and had never even appeared on Star Web before.","The first fey was called the Spring Mouth Drill Pupa. It was an insect-species fey that would never emerge from its pupa and was adept at both attack and defense.","When the Spring Mouth Drill Pupa started to spin and drill, it could easily cause damage to feys of the same grade.","However, the Spring Mouth Drill Pupa’s method of creating water was to search out water sources and drill a well there.","Rather than producing water, a more accurate saying was that it sought out water.","No matter how dry the Broiling Rock Continent was, the rainwater from the monsoon season would still end up seeping into the underground rivers.","There might be very few spring mouths, but they did exist.","If the Broiling Rock Continent had a fey like the Spring Mouth Drill Pupa, it would not be in the state that it was in.","It could be said that the Spring Mouth Drill Pupa would definitely be a blessing to the Broiling Rock Continent."]},{"number":2194,"title":"Chapter 2194 Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly","paragraphs":["2194 Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly","However, Lin Yuan did not intend to give Peace the Spring Mouth Drill Pupa.","Peace had had a difficult life and thus had a stronger will than her peers.","Nonetheless, the will of one’s character was different from experience in society.","Peace had not interacted with many people. Thus, she lacked societal experience.","If the Spring Mouth Drill Pupa was given to Peace, she might not be able to utilize it well.","Once Peace used the Spring Mouth Drill Pupa to produce a few reliable sources of water, the Tide Rain Mantis’ ability to create water would pale in comparison.","As a result of this, Peace’s importance in Green Continent City would diminish.","If Peace lost her position in Green Continent City and could not build a faction, Lin Yuan was the one who would suffer the loss.","The second insect-species fey was very suitable for fey as well as the Broiling Rock Continent’s current situation.","The Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly had mutated from the Acid-Dissolving Roly Poly. There was only one in the entire Cage of Brahma Insects.","This mutation was a coincidence, and no one could be certain if it would happen again.","The Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly could draw in heat from the surroundings and turn it into clean water in its body.","In some areas, the roly poly was known as the ‘tide insect’.","Fan Hansheng had called Lin Yuan especially to emphasize the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly’s ability to create water.","In a place like the Royal Capital that had a temperate climate, the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly’s ability to create water did not stand out.","When it was placed in a water tank, it could only produce enough water to fill the tank in about half an hour.","The average interior temperatures would fall by about three to four degrees because of the heat that the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly had absorbed.","But when the people from the Cage of Brahma Insects experimented on the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly in Bronze Furnace City, they noticed that it was like a mobile spring in the over 50-degree environment of Bronze Furnace City.","The Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly was currently only Bronze grade.","When he heard what Fan Hansheng said, Lin Yuan knew that Peace’s position as the ‘Goddess of the Green Continent’ would only become more secure.","Lin Yuan had personally visited the lava zone in Bronze Furnace City in the past. Thus, he was well-acquainted with the environment there.","From Peace’s description, the weather of the Broiling Rock Continent was even more severe than that of Bronze Furnace City.","Thus, the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly could definitely produce even better effects than when it was in Bronze Furnace City.","After Peace obtained the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly and evolved it to Platinum grade using the spirit fluids that Lin Yuan delivered to her, she would easily be able to fix the water scarcity problems of a large federation.","The Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly was like a man-made lake in the Broiling Rock Continent.","Most importantly, the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly could even lower temperature.","There was no way that ice-type feys could survive in an environment like the Broiling Rock Continent.","The Broiling Rock Continent not only lacked water, but the heat was deadly as well.","Even during the monsoon season, the temperatures were as high as during the drought season. The rain that fell was around 40 to 50 degrees.","It could be said that no one in the Broiling Rock Continent knew what it felt like to be refreshed.","Given that the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly absorbed heat to turn it into water, it could act like an air-conditioner in a home.","It could also lower the temperature of Green Continent City.","It went without saying that the area around the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly was the coolest.","Peace had not comprehended any Willpower Runes yet.","However, there was no need for a fey like the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly that did not have much combat power to evolve to Fantasy Breed while it was only Bronze grade.","As long as Peace eventually comprehended a Willpower Rune suitable for the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly, it would eventually be able to evolve to Fantasy Breed and Myth Breed.","The more heat the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly absorbed, the more water it would produce.","The Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly could transform a small portion of the heat it absorbed into its own power.","As a result, Lin Yuan did not need to worry much about Peace’s nurturing of the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly in the future.","Lin Yuan had sent the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly to Peace long ago.","After Peace formed a contract with the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly, she immediately updated Pang Luo.","She asked Pang Luo to set aside a large area of land outside the City Lord’s residence and to dig a hole for a lake there. She stated that the lake had to be wide and deep.","Pang Luo respected Peace and, after their days of interaction, now felt a special kinship toward her.","Thus, Pang Luo trusted Peace wholeheartedly.","However, Pang Luo did not understand why Peace wanted him to dig a large man-made lake outside of the City Lord’s residence.","A man-made lake could only be called so when it was filled with water. Without water, it would just be a giant hole.","Peace could indeed summon rain, but it was far from enough from being able to fill the lake.","Due to the weather and temperature, the water in the lake would evaporate quickly.","Some of the water would even seep into the ground.","Thus, Pang Luo intended on asking Peace for the reason.","Peace did not say much. All she did was reveal a small smile to indicate that she would be able to fill up the lake with water.","Pang Luo was shocked but soon started to beam broadly.","Given Pang Luo’s understanding of Peace, she was not the type to boast without having the means to back it up.","A person who was full of hot air would never consider the fact that Green Continent City’s current water supply was insufficient to hold up a large city.","Pang Luo immediately instructed his subordinates to begin digging the hole.","In just 13 days, a giant hole meant to be a lake was dug.","In order to prevent too much water from seeping underground, Pang Luo instructed his subordinates to cover the bottom of the lake with many rocks. He also asked spirit qi professionals with earth-type feys to ensure that the rocks were packed tightly together.","If Peace could fill the man-made lake immediately, Green Continent City would truly gain freedom of water.","The citizens in Green Continent City could not only drink as much water as they wanted but could even start enjoying luxuries such as bathing with water.","Whether it was because she was after a certain image or status, or if she just wanted to gain the faith of the citizens of Green Continent City, Pang Luo called all of the citizens of Green Continent City to come to the lake after Peace gave her repeated assurance that she would be able to fill the man-made lake.","This way, all the citizens would be able to witness this noble act.","Peace liked some of the ways that Pang Luo did things. She also knew that he would be able to help her to meet her goals.","Peace was wearing a watery blue dress.","In the Broiling Rock Continent, only those who were truly respected were deserving to wear blue. This was because blue was the color of water.","Those who were verified Rain Masters added blue elements to their clothing and accessories.","However, none of the Rain Masters dared to wear all blue.","Pang Luo was the one who had given this set of clothes to Peace.","Peace had put it on without hesitation.","The people in the city were very accepting of Peace’s attire. All of them had been blessed by her to some extent.","However, the other Rain Masters in Green Continent City all had some private words for Peace."]},{"number":2195,"title":"Chapter 2195 Refreshing Feeling!","paragraphs":["2195 Refreshing Feeling!","Once a person decidedly saw another as a rival, it was easy for feelings of hostility to bubble up.","Ever since Peace entered Green Continent City, the other Rain Masters had received decreasing respect as all of the respect had been transferred onto Peace.","If not for the support from Pang Luo and the fact that they could not compete with her ability to create water, some of the Rain Masters would have publicly expressed their displeasure.","Peace had been staying in the City Lord’s residence but had also selected a few girls with similar power and started to nurture them.","Peace knew that she needed more than individual combat power to build a faction. She also needed to have a group of people to act as her eyes and hands.","Thus, Peace had a good grasp of the happenings within Green Continent City.","Peace decided to take the chance to shut the mouths of all the Rain Masters in Green Continent City, who were indignant about her.","Green Continent City would not lack water as long as she was around.","As long as the Rain Masters were intelligent, they would not gossip and spit acid about her in private.","Otherwise, Pang Luo would kick them out immediately.","These Rain Masters could not leave Green Continent City either. There were too many instances of Rain Masters who died after leaving Green Continent City.","In the future, Green Continent City was going to be developed into a megacity.","All of the Rain Masters knew how beneficial it would be to live in a megacity.","When they received the call from Pang Luo, all of the residents of Green Continent City gathered at the man-made lake and looked at Peace with hope.","Even the Rain Masters, who felt hostile toward Peace, hoped that she would be able to fill up the lake with water.","In the Broiling Rock Continent, as long as one had the ability to create water, one could receive the title of ‘Rain Master’.","But there were many Rain Masters who did not even produce enough water in a day to meet their family’s needs and still needed to buy water from external vendors.","If Peace improved the water issue of the entire Green Continent City, the less-powerful Rain Masters would also benefit significantly.","The Rain Masters who had contracted the Duck-Mouthed Lungfish produced water with a thick and foul taste. It was even more difficult to ingest than some of the by-products produced by humans.","Peace sensed the hopeful looks all around her, but all she could think about was Lin Yuan and the large family that was Sky City.","She softly said a word of thanks to Lin Yuan before she raised her hand and summoned the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly.","After the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly evolved to Platinum grade, its body had grown to four meters wide. It was even larger than the cars from Lin Yuan’s previous life.","But in the face of this giant man-made lake, the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly looked tiny.","Peace could feel its delight and uncontrollable emotions when she summoned the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly. The Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly loved this environment and temperature.","Peace did not immediately instruct the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly to begin absorbing the heat and creating water.","Rather, she brought it to the center of the man-made lake.","The Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly crawled extremely slowly.","By the time the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly made it to the center of the man-made lake, it had captured the gazes of every person present.","However, the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly did not sense any of these gazes. Or rather, it ignored all of them","The Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly only had one thought, which was to get to the center of the man-made lake as quickly as possible. This was because Peace would only allow it to start absorbing as much heat as it wanted when it reached the center of the man-made lake.","When the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly reached the center of the man-made lake, Peace said with soft determination, “From now on, no one in Green Continent City will need to worry about the lack of water.”","When Peace spoke, even those who had confidence in her could not help but purse their lips. Her words were just too unbelievable.","Not having to worry about access to drinking water and not worrying about the lack of water were completely different issues.","Green Continent City already technically did not have to worry about access to water.","Ever since Peace arrived, no one in the city had to die of thirst again.","But not having to worry about access to water included water for cleaning, cooking, and even watering plants. This was an unimaginable amount of water.","However, what the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly did next dispelled all of the distrust of the crowd.","After Peace was done speaking, she immediately instructed the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly to begin absorbing heat.","The Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly was now like a surging spring mouth. With it at the center, a pillar of water that was more than 16 square meters wide and seven to eight meters tall shot out.","Since the bottom of the man-made lake had been fortified, the amount of water that seeped underground decreased significantly.","The lake started filling up at a visible rate.","The people of Green Continent City felt that if gods truly existed, Peace and the pillar of water would be the evidence.","The water level continued to rise. In just half an hour, the enormous lake was already 20% filled.","Although Peace was the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly’s contractor, she was also silently shocked by its abilities.","Before she instructed the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly to begin unleashing its power, she never expected it to have such capabilities.","Peace immediately said to Pang Luo, who was standing next to her, “Pang Luo, the man-made lake will be filled in another two hours. Get people to dig canals out from the man-made lake so the residents of Green Continent City will have an easier time obtaining water. Next, pick some districts that are suitable and dig seven more man-made lakes of a similar size. I think I’ll be able to keep all eight lakes filled.”","The Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly could increase its power by absorbing heat.","From the amount of water that the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly produced in three hours, it seemed that it would not be difficult to keep eight man-made lakes filled.","Peace wanted to take the chance to elevate her status even more so that she would have an irreplaceably high position in the hearts of every person in Green Continent City.","Peace added a last remark to Pang Luo, “Remember to keep all eight man-made lakes sufficiently far apart from each other.”","Peace had a reason for saying this.","After Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly had absorbed all the heat from an area, the area would need some time to replenish its heat.","The man-made lakes needed to be sufficiently far apart from each other to ensure that there was enough heat for the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly to absorb. This would also ensure that the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly’s water production rate did not drop.","Pang Luo was about to nod excitedly when he suddenly felt an indescribably pleasant refreshingness.","He was not the only one who felt this. Every resident of Green Continent City, including Peace, felt the same.","When these people who were used to having high temperatures as an old friend felt this rush of refreshingness, they felt as though they had died and gone to heaven."]},{"number":2196,"title":"Chapter 2196 Guaranteed Power!","paragraphs":["2196 Guaranteed Power!","If a person never had a certain item of feeling, they would never yearn for it because they did not know what it could do for them.","Although many Rain Masters in the Broiling Rock Continent could not even keep themselves afloat, there were still experts who emerged from the Broiling Rock Continent.","Green Continent City had received aid from an expert 30 years ago.","He had ascertained the positions of all the Rain Masters within Green Continent City and told them to gather together to address the water scarcity issue.","By forbidding people outside of the city walls from entering, it ensured that the water that the city did have could be used to preserve the lives of the city’s residents.","This would give the people outside the city hope and the goal of working toward becoming a Rain Master so they could eventually live within the city.","Furthermore, Green Continent City was also a checkpoint in the Broiling Rock Continent that linked multiple cities. It was a hub for many citizens of the Broiling Rock Continent to gather.","Once a large city disappeared, it could cause a break in the link.","This was a situation that regular people could not understand but that experts took into consideration.","30 years ago, the Rain Master expert had used a certain technique to help Green Continent City to overcome the drought season.","After that expert left, a group of people who had experienced what he had done seemed spellbound. From then on, they often found themselves still marveling and thinking back to that feeling.","In the Broiling Rock Continent, people were considered elderly once they reached 20 years old and above. A person would be considered extremely lucky if they made it to 30 years old.","After all, the yearly switches between the drought and monsoon seasons caused resources to dry up extremely quickly.","The people who had lived through what that Rain Master had done had long left this world, and that mystical feeling had faded into a legend.","It could be said that this refreshingness and comfort resulted in shivers that emanated from their soul outwards.","Many of them finally realized why their predecessors never forgot that feeling even after decades had passed.","While bathing in such refreshment, even their outlook on life had changed.","Although the sunlight was as scorching as ever, the lowered temperature caused the burning rays to seem more like a crimson veil. It no longer felt like roasting torture.","Would they be able to handle it if they never got to experience this feeling ever again?","Amidst the refreshment, Peace was dazed momentarily before she placed her hand on her chest and mumbled, “Mr. Leo.”","Next, she patted the shoulder of Pang Luo, who was standing next to her, and said, “Snap out of your daze. If you don’t send people to dig the man-made lakes soon, all the water will go to waste! Hurry up and send all of them into action! Once the eight man-made lakes have been dug out, we can begin expanding Green Continent City.”","Peace spoke loudly and with confidence.","Pang Luo was extremely respectful toward Rain Masters. He was even gentle and kind toward the Rain Masters, who had only contracted the Duck-Mouthed Lungfishes.","But even the most powerful Rain Master felt at least a hint of fear toward Pang Luo.","But in front of Peace, Pang Luo did not care at all that she had robbed him of his speaking authority as the City Lord.","This was because she had created a miracle.","Previously, Peace had intended to position her as the goddess of Green Continent City and capture the residents’ hearts through her ability to summon rain.","But now, he had scrapped that plan because she could already live up to that title without his help.","But expanding Green Continent City was not a simple task.","With eight reservoirs, Green Continent City would become the most unique city in the entire Broiling Rock Continent. It could even become a kingdom with more than billions of citizens.","Moreover, Pang Luo felt an increasingly uncontrollable warmth as he looked at the confident Peace, who was walking through the rain while wearing blue.","Pang Luo took a deep breath and immediately started giving out orders.","He mobilized every citizen of Green Continent City. Even children who were only seven or eight years old were tasked with collecting stones from the side of the man-made lake.","Pang Luo even sent out 200 of his personal guards.","The guards’ job was not to build the man-made lake but to fetch the homeless who were sheltered under rocks in the wilderness.","At first, Green Continent City had forbidden these homeless people from entering the city because they had no means of helping them. If too many homeless entered Green Continent City, the water scarcity would worsen, and even the original residents of the city would end up dying of dehydration.","This would definitely throw a wrench into the lives of Green Continent City’s residents.","But now that the water scarcity issue had been resolved and there was more than enough water to go around, Green Continent City had the means of gathering all the homeless in a 50-kilometer radius of the city.","After solving the water scarcity issue, more people meant more labor.","The current number of citizens was insufficient to expand the city and turn Green Continent City into a megacity. More people needed to come to live in the city to help with the building process.","Peace stood by the edge of the lake like a goddess while the Water-Drawing Heat Roly Poly gobbled up as much power as it wanted while spreading that refreshing feeling in all directions.","This event was unprecedented in Green Continent City, where it was hot all year round.","Before the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting began, three man-made lakes had been filled.","Lin Yuan sat on the Leo throne and marveled at Peace’s achievements over the past two weeks.","Although Peace could not match up to Yin Lin’s background, nor did she have the attention of the Spirit Mother like Bu Po did and was a reserve disciple, she also had her own advantage by remaining in Green Continent City, which was that she had the authority for the final say.","Right before the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting ended, Lin Yuan fell silent.","He realized that the plans he had laid out had benefited Ta Lei and Su Yiren. With his advice, they had managed to increase their power.","But Yin Lin, Wo Lun, and Bei Xu focused more on expanding their factions than increasing their own power.","This would be beneficial for the Astronomical Parliament’s long-term development.","“Everyone, pay attention! You must guarantee that you are still increasing your own power before you move on to expanding your factions. If you aren’t strong enough, developing your factions won’t be any point!”","Lin Yuan had contemplated deeply before saying that.","Lin Yuan was the City Lord of Sky City, but his power was not considered strong among its members.","However, this strength did not take into account his secret weapons.","Lin Yuan’s current limitation was his spirit qi professional rank.","But this was not his fault.","If others heard of the speed that Lin Yuan increased his spirit qi professional power, their jaws would drop.","In just a year, his spirit qi professional rank had jumped by two ranks.","He had achieved what would have taken others ten years to do.","But despite all that, Lin Yuan felt it was not enough."]},{"number":2197,"title":"Chapter 2197 Too Stuffed!","paragraphs":["2197 Too Stuffed!","Lin Yuan’s combat power could only reach a new level when he was promoted to A-rank spirit qi professional.","Others first raised their spirit qi professional rank before they nurtured their feys.","But Lin Yuan did the opposite now—he was the one who was standing in the way of his feys’ evolution.","Chimey nagged every day about wanting to meet with its fans.","But Lin Yuan’s spirit qi professional rank had not reached A-rank. Thus, it did not matter no matter how hard Chimey worked.","No matter how busy Lin Yuan was, he still squeezed out ten hours each day to evolve feys.","Moreover, all of the feys that Lin Yuan nurtured were pinnacle Silver feys that Listen had specially gathered.","Lin Yuan worked this hard because he was well aware of the importance of a faction leader’s individual power.","But when the members of the Astronomical Parliament heard what Lin Yuan said, Liu Jie, Su Yiren, and Ta Lei, who spent a lot of time by Lin Yuan’s side, quickly understood his intentions.","After thinking for a moment, Yin Lin also understood why Lin Yuan said this.","After some deep contemplation, Bei Xu and Wo Lun realized that they had done things in an upside-down manner.","Lin Yuan’s reminder came at a good time. It was not too late to change directions.","Before the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting ended, Luo Lan and Lin Yuan reconfirmed their plans to meet in the Iron Hammer Federation.","When Lin Yuan saw how anxious Luo Lan was, he knew that she was in great need of resources.","Luo Lan had managed to win the hearts of the people with just her might.","But when it came to a period of stable development, the tribes could still be respectful of her but would not work for her as diligently for her as they did before.","Lin Yuan intended to send numerous plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline to the Iron Hammer Federation to help with its development.","Although Lin Yuan was sincere in his treatment of Luo Lan, she was still technically his puppet.","If his puppet could not maintain 100% of the speaking authority, investing resources into her would be a waste.","Lin Yuan never liked to do things that ended in waste.","Lin Yuan had boosted Jin Qianxun all the way to the throne of the Great Lush Federation and had used astonishing means to cement Jin Qianxun’s might.","Lin Yuan was heading to the Iron Hammer Federation to investigate the Snow Celestial Mountain.","He did not want to spend too much time in the Iron Hammer Federation.","Thus, for Lin Yuan to put an end to the matter quickly, he had to employ astonishing methods again.","This status was tied to the imperial court’s throne and absolute authority.","Lin Yuan was the one who supplied the Soldier Ration Radishes that saved the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members.","Lin Yuan hoped that the people he saved were not the ungrateful type.","If there were truly such people, Lin Yuan would have no choice but to reclaim the lives he had saved.","Lin Yuan knew that Luo Lan’s heart was fully focused on the Iron Hammer Federation’s development.","Luo Lan transformed what was meant as the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribes’ welfare into the path she was going to go down from now on.","Thus, after Luo Lan seized absolute authority, Lin Yuan did not need to worry that Luo Lan would stray without any restrictions in place.","Currently, the Iron Hammer Federation’s foundation was shaky.","But with more investment of resources, there was the possibility of the Iron Hammer Federation making a comeback and suppressing the Great Lush Federation and Divine Wood Federation.","This was because Lin Yuan had noticed a difference in the faith and character of the people from the Iron Hammer Federation when compared to the Divine Wood Federation and Great Lush Federation.","After the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting ended, Lin Yuan headed to the Freezing Hammer Tribe as quickly as he could.","Luo Lan had already lost count of the last time that she had proper rest.","After such a prolonged period of exhaustion, Luo Lan’s head ached just looking at words on a page.","Luo Lan’s female attendants were direct descendants of Black Gold tribes who had distinguished themselves. They were both capable and sensible and could be called truly talented elites.","There had to be less than 30 such talented elites in the entire Iron Hammer Federation.","They were capable and had the background to back it up. It went without saying that they were arrogant.","Although they had close contact with Luo Lan and were well aware of Luo Lan’s status and how she had saved the tribes, they did not see much difference between her and them.","But in the past two weeks, the six chosen direct descendants of Black Gold tribes had fully submitted to her. All of them were now trying to show off their own talents and help bear Luo Lan’s burdens.","When they saw Luo Lan massaging her temples again, a short-haired girl could not help but say, “Your Majesty, go and rest! There are so many things to do. The list is endless. You don’t have to burn the midnight oil every day to solve every issue.","“The Black Gold tribes are all on your side. But the battles between the Platinum tribes is becoming more and more serious. A lot of Platinum tribes have lost control because of their battles! There is new information coming in daily. If you continue to go without sleep, your body won’t be able to handle it!”","Luo Lan waved her hand dismissively.","The issue was not whether or not her body would be able to handle it.","When a spirit qi professional washed his body with spirit qi, they would not feel the same exhaustion that regular people did, nor would their spirits be damaged by prolonged sleep loss.","All they needed was some spiritual ingredients that could nourish their spirits, and they would be replenished.","Luo Lan had already contracted the Vitality Sloth and only needed to sleep two to three hours each day.","She had already done all she could to solve the issues but to no avail.","Luo Lan did not know if the issue lay in her lack of ability or if it was an aftereffect of the Platinum tribes having eaten their fill.","Shockingly, conflict of such scale could arise during the winter season.","Luo Lan waved her hand, and a short girl with dark blue hair and bare feet who had upturned her collar said with a pained voice, “Your Majesty, Sha Sha is right! It will be difficult to fix the issue of the fighting between the Platinum tribes with just an order.","“Every tribe in the Iron Hammer Federation, even the Black Gold tribes, has lost a large portion of its members. It only goes without saying that the Platinum tribes and smaller tribes have suffered significant losses. The Yellow Gold and White Silver tribes wanted to seek protection from the Platinum tribes. After absorbing the manpower from the White Silver and Yellow Tribes, it’s only natural that the Platinum tribes have become more ambitious.","“But there is a limit to the resources, so conflict is inevitable. Sometimes I think it might not be a good thing to be too stuffed during the winter season.”","Luo Lan clenched her fist tightly.","During the summer season, many tribes wanted to accumulate resources to tide themselves over the winter season."]},{"number":2198,"title":"Chapter 2198 Call Ice Bite out!","paragraphs":["2198 Call Ice Bite out!","Previously, every tribe was silent during winter.","The tribe members went into a state akin to hibernation and did all they could to reduce their energy loss.","The current situation was largely related to the Soldier Ration Radishes that had been distributed.","But Luo Lan did not agree with what her female attendant Ni Xing said.","No matter how intense the fighting became, stomachs still had to be filled. If stomachs could not even be filled, the Iron Hammer Federation could not hope to develop.","Frankly, Luo Lan knew that the issue with the Platinum tribes was not the only one. The Black Iron, Light Bronze, White Silver, and Yellow Gold tribes were all also butting heads constantly.","It was only that the fighting between the lower-ranked tribes was not as intense and, therefore, eye-catching as that of the Platinum tribes.","If the Black Gold tribes had not already divided up the territory, none of them would have backed down in a clash of profits. All of them wanted to be able to boast that they came out as the winner of the conflict.","Luo Lan’s tightly clenched fist relaxed, and she went back to massaging her forehead. But this time, it was not because she was dizzy from a lack of rest but because she did not want to spend any more time addressing the fights between the Platinum tribes.","Since she knew that she would not be able to solve the issue, she decided to leave it in the hands of someone who could.","Currently, the people of the Iron Hammer Federation were filled with happiness, but none of the tribes were focused on development. Rather, all they could see were potential profits.","Since this was the case, it was time for a painful wake-up call for all the factions.","Luo Lan stood up and unfurrowed her brow as she said, “I’m going to get some sleep. I’ll sleep until I naturally wake. There’s no need for you to wake me up. The six of you, send the message down that six days later, I will be holding an imperial meeting with tribes that are Platinum and above.”","Luo Lan left immediately after she was done speaking.","When she left, her six female attendants were left looking at each other. They did not understand the reason behind Luo Lan saying such a thing.","Currently, the Platinum tribes were in the thick of fighting. It was clear that they had gained momentum.","The tribe leaders would never stop what they were doing and travel thousands of miles to come to attend an imperial meeting.","When the previous king was still alive, he never held an imperial meeting during the winter season, no matter what happened.","Although they could not figure out a reason, the six of them immediately went to carry out Luo Lan’s order.","While Luo Lan was lying on the bed, she took out a piece of light gold paper and looked through the conversations she had with Lin Yuan on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Lin Yuan, I’ll have to depend on you again!","At that moment, Lin Yuan had no idea what Luo Lan was thinking. If he knew, he would definitely feel glad.","There were times when dignity did not come from stubbornness. Rather, there were times when problems could be better solved by relying on each other.","This meant that Luo Lan trusted him.","Each piece of snow on the rivers of the Iron Hammer Federation was around the size of half a palm. The snow that fell added heavy weight to the people they fell on.","The icy wind was like knives that slashed through the flesh of lifeforms.","Even the beasts that were made to live in such a climate were unwilling to leave their homes in such weather, even at the risk of starvation.","In such weather, even the streets of the Freezing Hammer Tribe were quiet.","The only sounds were during mealtimes when the food vendors would call out to attract customers. But in the midst of the snow and wind, it was difficult to hear their voices beyond two meters.","In such terrible weather, the fights between the tribes were in full swing, and every bloody clash ended in blood and death.","During these fights, many snow beasts decided to break their fast. Even the bear-species feys that hated to be awoken decided to halt their hibernation.","While on Blackie’s back, Lin Yuan witnessed many of these fights but did not stop any of them.","When Su Yiren saw the expression on Lin Yuan’s face, she immediately knew that Lin Yuan might start an even larger operation for the Great Lush Federation once he met up with Luo Lan.","After being by Lin Yuan’s side for so long, Su Yiren could clearly sense his bias toward the Iron Hammer Federation.","But as an observer, Su Yiren knew that fights had broken out amongst the Platinum tribes because they wanted to develop themselves.","Now that they were warm and fed, their ambitions would flare up rapidly.","If the fights were allowed to go on, the winning Platinum tribe would not be able to catch up with the Black Gold tribes even after ten years of development.","“Young Master, Luo Lan must be out of ideas now. You said that you wanted to investigate Snow Celestial Mountain. During that time, I’ll stay to help Luo Lan. I want to push back the recovery of the Dark Continent. It can begin after everything is settled in the Iron Hammer Federation.”","Lin Yuan immediately understood what Su Yiren meant.","It could be said that Su Yiren’s greatest wish was to recover the Dark Continent and bring light back into the Seven States of Darkness. Ever since Lin Yuan promised her that he would fulfill her wish, Su Yiren’s wishes only became more evident.","For Su Yiren to be willing to push back on achieving her dream in order to help Luo Lan, it meant that she and Luo Lan shared a deep kinship.","Su Yiren would need help from Luo Lan when she was trying to recover the Seven States of Darkness.","Lin Yuan was not in disagreement with this.","The Astronomical Parliament was a large family, but each member was an individual.","If any two members became close enough that they were even willing to help each other out, it proved that the members of the Astronomical Parliament were close.","“I only need Big Brother Liu with me when I head to Snow Celestial Mountain. With you helping Luo Lan, she’ll have a much easier time. Luo Lan is soft-hearted. With you around, she’ll be able to make firmer decisions.”","Su Yiren nodded gently when she heard what Lin Yuan said.","But given Su Yiren’s understanding of Luo Lan, the latter had to have undergone a transformation for her to decide to eliminate all of her relatives from the Freezing Hammer Tribe.","Now that Luo Lan had experienced giving out a death sentence, she would not be overly soft-hearted.","A quick decision was the best solution in a complex situation.","What the Iron Hammer Federation needed now was that quick decision to fix its complex situation.","Luo Lan had urgently invited Lin Yuan to the Iron Hammer Federation because she was aware of this. She wanted to borrow his strength to cut off the Iron Hammer Federation’s rotting parts.","Liu Jie listened to the wind whistling in his ear as he silently stood by Lin Yuan’s side.","In the past few days, Liu Jie had turned two insect-species carcinoma feys in succession into fairies. As such, his combat power was completely different from what it used to be.","As he looked at the endless snowy landscape in front of him, Liu Jie raised his hand, and the chubby Dimensional Light Moth appeared next to him.","Liu Jie immediately ordered the Dimensional Light Moth, “Fat Dimension, call Ice Bite out!”"]},{"number":2199,"title":"Chapter 2199 Polar Region Jade Silkworm","paragraphs":["2199 Polar Region Jade Silkworm","The Dimensional Light Moth’s fairy form appeared dazed and vapid. It was also the fattest fairy that Lin Yuan had ever seen.","But in spite of the Dimensional Light Moth’s short arms and legs, its face was still exceptionally beautiful.","The silver glow of the spatial energy was like a spotlight on the Dimensional Light Moth’s face.","“Liu Jie, call me Dimension. Don’t call me Fat Dimension! I am a girl, after all!”","While it huffed its response out, the Dimensional Light Moth placed its arms over its stomach.","After a violent spatial fluctuation, a fairy with two pairs of wings, white hair and eyes, and a half-elementalized body appeared next to the Dimensional Light Moth. The half of the fairy that was not elementalized had slender arms.","The Dimensional Light Moth pouted sulkily.","Liu Jie drily scooped the Dimensional Light Moth into his arms and said soothingly, “Fat Dimension, you’re getting increasingly temperamental!”","At first, the Dimensional Light Moth had a delighted expression. But when it heard what Liu Jie said, its expression crumpled again.","The Dimensional Light Moth’s dazed and vapid expression caused Su Yiren to see stars.","Su Yiren had contracted the Absolute Love Poppy, which had the natural ability of seduction. As such, she conducted herself in a promiscuous and sometimes unprincipled manner. She liked to use the Absolute Love Poppy to settle troublesome issues.","But after spending some time with Su Yiren, Lin Yuan noticed that she could never resist the temptation of cute things.","Su Yiren loved adorable lifeforms.","However, fairies were arrogant and did not like interacting with people besides their contractors.","Thus, Su Yiren had been brushed off numerous times in her attempts to reach out to Liu Jie’s fairies.","Su Yiren knew that this seemingly innocuous and vapid fairy was hiding thousands of troops within its abdomen.","If the Insect Queen was the producer of insect-species feys and was in charge of sending out Liu Jie’s troops, the Dimensional Light Moth was the door to disasters.","Although they were both fairies controlled by Liu Jie through the Insect Queen and they had both been evolved through insect-species carcinoma feys, the Dimensional Light Moth was clearly timid or even fearful of the four-winged Ice Bite.","Evidently, Ice Bite’s fairy bloodline was superior to the Dimensional Light Moth.","The Dimensional Light Moth had been combined with the Firefly Demon Fetus and transformed into a fairy earlier.","But ever since Ice Bite transformed into a fairy, its bloodline was advanced four wings.","The concentration of a fey’s bloodline could demonstrate its potential.","Due to the limited quantity of Firefly Demon Fetuses, Liu Jie was very careful when he picked his insect-species carcinoma feys even though he had already decided to center his development around the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle.","Ice Bite’s original form was the Polar Region Jade Silkworm.","Liu Jie had decided to transform the Polar Region Jade Silkworm into a fairy because he had no powerful weapons to handle the polar region.","Insects usually preferred to live in warmer climates. The combat of an army of insects fell precipitously in a polar region.","Liu Jie had specially nurtured Ice Bite in consideration of his limitation.","Given the concentration of the Polar Region Jade Silkworm’s bloodline when it transformed, it proved that Liu Jie had made the right decision.","Ice Bite flapped its four wings and had a cold expression.","But in fact, it was extremely timid and flew up Liu Jie’s sleeve soon after appearing without so much as peeking its head out.","Liu Jie said in frustration, “Ice Bite, use frost and snow to create your team!”","Liu Jie used to only have one contracted fey, the Insect Queen.","Now that he had numerous insect-species carcinoma feys that had transformed into fairies, Liu Jie finally understood the joys of having numerous feys and communicating with them.","Ice Bite was shy and timid, but when it received a task from Liu Jie, it was never careless.","Ice Bite flapped its wings and entered the wind and snow.","All of the fairies were under the Insect Queen’s control. After being boosted by the Emperor Core of All Insects, the Insect Queen’s spiritual energy exceeded that of other spiritual-type feys of the same grade. Thus, Liu Jie’s spirit qi professional rank did not limit the fairies.","Night Leaning Moon had given Liu Jie a treasure that would help him comprehend Willpower Runes.","Ice Bite had worn this treasure for a few days.","Coincidentally, Ice Bite comprehended a Willpower Rune and evolved to Myth Breed when Lin Yuan was unconscious.","Although it was in fairy form, it was still a Myth Breed insect-species carcinoma fey.","Aside from instances where some groups and individuals did all they could to nurture themselves, there were no cases of carcinoma feys in the wild that had evolved to Myth Breed on their own.","When a fey evolved to Fantasy Breed and then Myth Breed, it underwent two transformations.","Ice Bite had just finished undergoing the second transformation.","Lin Yuan had been shocked by the powers that Ice Bite had demonstrated.","He looked at the rushing white snow beneath his feet. The movement of the snow was akin to an avalanche.","But when Lin Yuan used True Data to carefully check on Ice Bite, he saw that it was not white snow beneath his feet but minuscule child Polar Region Jade Silkworms.","After the Polar Region Jade Silkworms hatched, they consumed the snow continuously to nourish themselves. They also used the snow to increase and complete their powers.","At the moment, Lin Yuan found it difficult to do the calculations.","When Ice Bite received the order to create its own team, it produced thousands of child insects at once.","But now, the number of child insects had crossed the millions.","If Ice Bite was given sufficient time, it could produce enough child insects to cover the Iron Hammer Federation’s ground in white.","After evolving to Myth Breed, Ice Bite was now demonstrating its might as a carcinoma fey to the world.","Liu Jie had been feeling that he was weak.","But after his first insect-species carcinoma fey evolved to Myth Breed, Liu Jie stopped belittling himself.","“Lin Yuan, snow won’t benefit the Iron Hammer Federation in any way. Without all that white snow, mining could still be carried out during the winter season. The three federations would then be able to transfer resources to each other rather than just having the Divine Wood Federation deliver food aid to the Iron Hammer Federation.","“The Iron Hammer Federation also needs to contribute! The Divine Wood Federation is most lacking in metal resources. If the Iron Hammer Federation stops supplying spiritual ingredients during winter, I’m sure Yi Huailong will eventually become bothered!”"]},{"number":2200,"title":"Chapter 2200 Polar Region Frost Pupa","paragraphs":["2200 Polar Region Frost Pupa","After spending time with Bai Qinghuan, Liu Jie not only improved in terms of his military leadership abilities but also started to think more deeply when it came to matters of human nature.","He thought so deeply that he was even willing to waste time trying to figure out a person’s thought process through his character and experiences.","Yi Huailong was the family leader of a veteran elite family who had been promoted to the ruler of a federation. But when it came to foresight and thought processing, they were still at the level of the leader of a veteran elite family.","Yi Huailong could listen to everything that Lin Yuan said and unconditionally provide all that was asked of him.","But Luo Lan and the Iron Hammer Federation were his rivals. There was no way that Yi Huailong could be generous with them.","Liu Jie summoned Ice Bite now because he wanted to bring the Iron Hammer Federation out of its winter season with the help of Ice Bite’s power.","This method would also bring the Divine Wood Federation and Iron Hammer Federation closer together and prevent any feelings of discord from rising within Yi Huailong.","But the most important factor was Lin Yuan’s interest in the Snow Celestial Mountain.","It snowed all year in the Snow Celestial Mountain.","The weather was still acceptable at the bottom of the mountain. But once one reached the middle of the mountain, the snow became more than three meters deep, and even ice formed at some parts, making the terrain utterly unscalable by regular means.","Liu Jie felt that it would be a good idea to allow Ice Bite to consume all of the snow on Snow Celestial Mountain. This way, the white snow could hide nothing on the mountain.","Liu Jie told Lin Yuan about his idea, to which Lin Yuan smiled and nodded.","Even if Liu Jie did not bring it up, Lin Yuan would ask Liu Jie to do so.","The Iron Hammer Federation did not have any Class 5 Creation Masters. It had absolutely no means of fighting back against the Truth Association.","There was a legend that there was a being on Snow Celestial Mountain that often received offerings from the Iron Hammer Federation. The legend also stated that the being had made an appearance in the past.","Offerings would lead to faith power. The lifeform on Snow Celestial Mountain had to have a great thirst for faith power.","Lin Yuan felt that it was likely that Snow Celestial Mountain was mentioned in the Annal of Monster Information because of faith power.","After interacting with Begin Lady, Lin Yuan learned that faith power was not only useful to dimensional lifeforms.","Begin Lady had also absorbed faith power before it set its spirit fire alight. In fact, the faith power produced better effects for Begin Lady than pure spirit qi did.","This was one of the main reasons Begin Lady had infected so many plant-type feys with its bloodline back when it resided in the Sacred Wood Mystic Realm.","Thus, faith power could not only be linked to the dimensional worlds.","Even if he did not manage to find out the secret of the Snow Celestial Mountain on this trip, he definitely needed to find the lifeform that needed faith power.","In the past, Lin Yuan would have been extremely cautious. But now that he had Begin Lady, he could be more daring in his actions.","If Lin Yuan wanted to gather faith power from the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members, he would clash with the goal of this creature on Snow Celestial Mountain.","Even if Lin Yuan did not want to make an enemy of the lifeform on Snow Celestial Mountain, the lifeform would definitely cause trouble for Luo Lan once it stopped receiving offerings and faith power.","Since that was the case, he would be better to strike first and with a heavy hand.","With Ice Bite around, it was time to change Snow Celestial Mountain’s name.","Blackie flew at breakneck speed, but the child insects that Ice Bite produced were almost able to catch up with Blackie’s flying speed.","If someone was following Blackie at that moment, they would notice that surging river of white left bare rocks in its wake.","Lin Yuan traveled from a warm climate to a cold climate. As the snow thickened, the temperature dropped further.","The child insects that Ice Bite produced could keep up with Blackie’s flying speed because after they consumed sufficient snow and matured, the matured insects would be able to lay around 20 to 45 eggs.","During the birthing process, the Polar Region Jade Silkworm would excrete a special organ and mutate, thus evolving into the Polar Region Frost Pupa.","Once this happened, the Polar Region Frost Pupa would no longer consume snow. Rather, it would burn up the energy within its body that it had obtained from the snow and attack with its body.","The Polar Region Jade Silkworm had appeared in the polar region before.","The Gold Polar Region Jade Silkworm led 100,000 of the Polar Region Frost Pupas and caused a blizzard that leveled 20 to 30 northern provinces. It went without saying that a building 50 to 60 meters tall stood no chance and was quickly ground into granules.","Even before they reached Freezing Hammer Tribe, Ice Bite’s troops would be complete.","Liu Jie gave Ice Bite the order to restrain any tribes it came across that were fighting.","Liu Jie knew how much effort Lin Yuan had put into the Startling Lines Continent.","He had not helped much with the previous establishments of the Divine Wood Federation and Great Lush Federation. Thus, Liu Jie wanted to take it upon himself to handle everything in the Iron Hammer Federation.","Although the Polar Region Jade Silkworms were individual, it was coded into their genes to do their best to carry out Ice Bite’s orders.","Luo Lan’s appearance in the sea of bone lotus flowers had been nothing short of a miracle.","Now, the Iron Hammer Federation’s tribe members were about to witness another miracle.","Luo Lan could not obtain the most updated information because Lin Yuan was still riding Blackie on his way to the Freezing Hammer Tribe.","After all, under Ice Bite’s control, any action could be seen by Ice Bite as a hostile act and lead to slaughter.","Luo Lan slept soundly. After she laid down all her burdens and decided to leave it all to Lin Yuan, her sleep was deep and restful.","After she woke up, she found that all of her exhaustion had melted away.","Ni Xing and Sha Sha were heads of Luo Lan’s six female attendants and so stood by the door of her bedroom the entire night.","Both of them were aware of Luo Lan’s temper and disposition.","When Luo Lan walked out of her bedroom, they handed her a thick stack of information and said, “Your Majesty, this is the current state of the wounded in the fights between the tribes. According to the most recent reports, four of the Platinum tribes have almost been completely slaughtered!”","Luo Lan took a breath when she heard what Sha Sha and Ni Xing said.","She pushed the stack of information back to Sha Sha and Ni Xing.","“I slept for almost an entire day. It must have been hard for you to put together such comprehensive reports! I won’t be looking through the information, and you don’t have to collect any more from now on. All you need to do is sit tight and be prepared to hold an imperial meeting at any time.”","When Luo Lan finished speaking, she grasped Sha Sha and Ni Xing’s hands and said, “There isn’t much to do, and there’s no rush to set up the imperial meeting. Why don’t you accompany me for a walk around the garden?”"]}]);
